 created. 0.1.96 is the nearest published\nrelease and reports no new errors in-tree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328750\n", "files": ["python/sites/lint.txt", "python/sites/python-test.txt"], "git_node": "76e75a3f3d4625c8be486865c01525c6cc453df7", "git_parents": ["bef095e5bd845deaa6e32fb673d7cfe03ce92c82"], "node": "af8b8aa55589c88c08c37646b8e8c5236928dd1f", "parents": ["2ee3853d50d64a94b3a64a1d814433cc84edde16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074262 - Use the netperf-tc wrapper for network throttling, r=aerickson,perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328557\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/browsertime/support-scripts/network_bench.py"], "git_node": "c1eeffd6a6d0e816fa262c5ce360a53feddba415", "git_parents": ["76e75a3f3d4625c8be486865c01525c6cc453df7"], "node": "2983fb349f695b906f271ab513e67a3b07a96f9d", "parents": ["af8b8aa55589c88c08c37646b8e8c5236928dd1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1909810 - Add try presets for DOM workers and storage components. r=ArnaudBienner\n\nBased on presets courtesy of Jan Varga.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327891\n", "files": ["dom/quota/test/README.md", "dom/tests/browser/browser.toml", "tools/tryselect/try_presets.yml"], "git_node": "e72b50632fb7695a34a081f8840f5f435806d5b3", "git_parents": ["c1eeffd6a6d0e816fa262c5ce360a53feddba415"], "node": "9c9206b78074bdb3d103b8e3c6be878a0e12452b", "parents": ["2983fb349f695b906f271ab513e67a3b07a96f9d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Turner \u003cdavid.turner@raspberrypi.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071471 - Remove mAcceleratedFormats from V4L2 code r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nInitV4L2Decoder() had copied some logic from VAAPI code to cache a list\nof which hardware codecs are supported.  However, an error in the code\nmeant it could only cache one codec, causing issues when multiple V4L2\ncodecs are present.\n\nRemove this caching entirely from the V4L2 codepath.  In the case where\nthe codec is present/working, it provided no speed-up.  glxtest already\nworks out which codecs are present so we'll never hit this codepath for\ncodecs without a hardware decoder present.  The only case where this\ncaching could have helped was codecs which are present and supported but\nbroken somehow, which seems very niche and I've never seen in practice.\n\nI think the Vulkan decoder has the same bug but I've limited this patch\nto the V4L2 decoder because I'm unfamiliar with the Vulkan code and\ndon't have the ability to test it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328167\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "0703d99400af50cfbbe94a9688b69a9157dc4faf", "git_parents": ["e72b50632fb7695a34a081f8840f5f435806d5b3"], "node": "6d42feccfa834e47950083803b44d82b01151310", "parents": ["9c9206b78074bdb3d103b8e3c6be878a0e12452b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074387 - Type the event and observer entry points in SessionStore.sys.mjs. r=sthompson,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nThe cast back to nsISupports at notifyObservers is there because the generated DOM element typings declare no QueryInterface, so a typed browser fails the observer service's weak-type check.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328091\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "426c779d57e8f822cd4233159c9ff24cc5553921", "git_parents": ["0703d99400af50cfbbe94a9688b69a9157dc4faf"], "node": "b47fce3dae28ad14267c1603637f39a2f42e7a47", "parents": ["6d42feccfa834e47950083803b44d82b01151310"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069784 - Document the options parameters in SessionStore.sys.mjs. r=sthompson,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nTypeScript rejects `aOptions.foo` rows under a `@param {Window|object} aOptions`, so the bags become typedefs, shared with the private helpers that read them. The documented default of `private` changes from false to the source window's privateness, which is what `#prepareClosedTabOptions` does.\n\nThe API page shows the typedef names where the per-property rows were, since sphinx-js renders no entry for a typedef.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328073\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "7a155d6be9ee5ad5cde7764f946021acf9a71ff2", "git_parents": ["426c779d57e8f822cd4233159c9ff24cc5553921"], "node": "fad9c807b0902fe1e8aae6178ccca846b96a22c3", "parents": ["b47fce3dae28ad14267c1603637f39a2f42e7a47"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074358 - Remove the unused isRemotenessUpdate flag from tab restore. r=sthompson,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328069\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/StartupPerformance.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "433fb36fac429ed075cdd337aabb63348b1760c8", "git_parents": ["7a155d6be9ee5ad5cde7764f946021acf9a71ff2"], "node": "6eaed252a298b24f3056d657cad58318e4adeac8", "parents": ["fad9c807b0902fe1e8aae6178ccca846b96a22c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2014934 - make net::Dashboard::ConnectionData hold strong ref to Dashboard r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328590\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/Dashboard.cpp"], "git_node": "dabbb9117c0ad721b52d8704354145a3db2c2bb6", "git_parents": ["433fb36fac429ed075cdd337aabb63348b1760c8"], "node": "7aa17c715e2674c4edae30025427923afcba4015", "parents": ["6eaed252a298b24f3056d657cad58318e4adeac8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jolie Huang \u003cjohuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074496 - Label the selection shortcut AI action button \"Ask about this text\" instead of the provider name r=fluent-reviewers,flod,Mardak\n\nThe `#ai-action-button` in the selection shortcut panel used `genai-shortcut-button-2` (\"Ask { $provider }\"). This made it show \"Ask ChatGPT\" in Smart Window too. As requested in comment 2, replace it with a single string that doesn't name a provider, `genai-shortcut-button-3` (\"Ask about this text\"). There is no Smart Window variant. The provider-name label code, including the per-popup refresh when the provider changes, is no longer needed and is removed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328672\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/genai.ftl"], "git_node": "21d0c037f2d4752ed9361fd8535aab6b3dcade7a", "git_parents": ["dabbb9117c0ad721b52d8704354145a3db2c2bb6"], "node": "e082defaa9c2422680665e6aac3b9b08af3749bd", "parents": ["7aa17c715e2674c4edae30025427923afcba4015"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074830 - Stop reporting partitioned tracker cookie reads as allowed tracker cookies. r=emz,cookie-reviewers,valentin\n\nThis patch changes the cookie service to pass the partition reason to the\naccepted-cookie notification, and changes NotifyBlockingDecision to treat\nan allow decision carrying STATE_COOKIES_PARTITIONED_TRACKER as partitioned\naccess, so it no longer emits STATE_COOKIES_LOADED_TRACKER.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328548\n", "files": ["netwerk/cookie/CookieService.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieService.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/ContentBlockingNotifier.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_partitioned_cookies.js"], "git_node": "96b92d51b1a1155a0606057cee6e746d264c2661", "git_parents": ["21d0c037f2d4752ed9361fd8535aab6b3dcade7a"], "node": "a65ceb68db9682749fdb79aecadb3e7095d730b9", "parents": ["e082defaa9c2422680665e6aac3b9b08af3749bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Jakobi \u003cajakobi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033958 - Drop a zero-delta pan-end that would synthesize a pan gesture block r=botond\n\nOn Wayland, GTK reports the end of a touchpad pan as a scroll-stop event, which\nnsWindow turns into a zero-delta pan-end. With no active block,\nInputQueue::ReceivePanGestureInput turns it into a pan-start plus a synthetic\npan-end), and the resulting block cancels animations in OnPanBegin and OnPan.\nNothing then restarts them, since the zero displacement sends the\nAPZC straight back to NOTHING and OnPanEnd early-returns in that state --\nleaving a scroll-snap container stranded between two snap points.\n\nSuch a pan-end has no displacement to apply and stands for a gesture that is\nalready over, so drop it instead of synthesizing a block. A pan-end that does\ncarry a displacement is unaffected.\n\nAdd a gtest, StrayPanEndPreservesSmoothMsdScroll_Bug2033958, checking that a\nstray zero-delta pan-end leaves a running main-thread driven SmoothMsd animation\nalone.\n\nAlso add StrayPanEndSnapsBackOverscroll_Bug1931090, where an interrupted\nblock's zero-delta pan-end is the only thing left to snap back overscroll.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324262\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.h", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestPanning.cpp"], "git_node": "2ed080eb558ec064c50844b34dad2a70bd98ce60", "git_parents": ["96b92d51b1a1155a0606057cee6e746d264c2661"], "node": "ed8cefc4a0a8b67fd046b277bbfbc84f247b1bcc", "parents": ["a65ceb68db9682749fdb79aecadb3e7095d730b9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070853 - P1. Vendor application-services 5825bcac for db-crypto and fxcontainers r=joschmidt,bdk\n\nThis comes from these commands:\n\n```\n./mach vendor third_party/application-services/moz.yaml -r 5825bcac7d22a24f335ca82fb419c901844c46d7\n./mach vendor rust\n./mach uniffi generate\n```\n\ndb_crypto and fxcontainers are new namespaces, so config.toml gains their\nasync_wrappers sections and the crypto entries move out of logins.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324941\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-static/browser_all_files_referenced.js", "docs/rust-components/api/js/db_crypto.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/fxcontainers.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/logins.md", "third_party/application-services/.buildconfig-android.yml", "third_party/application-services/automation/build_against_all.py", "third_party/application-services/automation/build_against_desktop.py", "third_party/application-services/automation/build_against_hnt.py", "third_party/application-services/automation/swift-components-docs/generate-static-docs-website.sh", "third_party/application-services/components/ads-client/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/components/ads-client/integration-tests/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/components/ads-client/integration-tests/tests/http_cache.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/ads-client/src/client.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/ads-client/src/client/config.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/ads-client/src/ffi.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/ads-client/src/ffi/telemetry.rs", "third_party/application-ser