   Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48495}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/peer_connection_tracer_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_tracer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc"], "git_node": "f51e63f02f5994c58e154cc1da2ce999d2f074f0", "git_parents": ["6a61000af3cb002b20375087a2d44a521bf15ffd"], "node": "2311a145d42ae637de9a9082186c62bfeffff569", "parents": ["3620c972ecb7b5426d753f5085b4aa6fb7fb4d9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 247e438680\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/247e4386801b9e2d9ded0674ace472ac770fb4e1\n    Remove sending rtcp TargetBitrate for screencast by default\n\n    Change defaults not to send any bitrate allocation instead.\n    TargetBitrate is a non-standard RTCP message that is obsolete in favor\n    or the VideoLayersAllocation RTP Header extension.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222127\n    Change-Id: I013dad92389e46394b0a73f91e1c6d0173fff342\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/499780\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48496}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0067.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0101.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0130.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/end_to_end_tests/extended_reports_tests.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_send_stream_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "9ea8553deb78d6f188de1aa0d263a348fcb922bb", "git_parents": ["f51e63f02f5994c58e154cc1da2ce999d2f074f0"], "node": "1f9a5c59eadcb32963a5c340a893e815841122ff", "parents": ["2311a145d42ae637de9a9082186c62bfeffff569"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 32618d80f5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/32618d80f57b515055121f5761ae7b78e715f590\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-05T04:09:05).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Iec29236c1ee6820ba91bf5cf35e3903345370158\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/499940\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48497}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "99f727ae17ab527380c7e1b9a6bec567246f48e3", "git_parents": ["9ea8553deb78d6f188de1aa0d263a348fcb922bb"], "node": "682a6da91340769c5b8676aa144502b31e25786d", "parents": ["1f9a5c59eadcb32963a5c340a893e815841122ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from fee771a146\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/fee771a1463048fe76547fe3cbb9e66b26ace20f\n    Add SocketReceiveTimeCalculator\n\n    Extracts socket arrival time calculation into\n    SocketReceiveTimeCalculator and introduces the field trial\n    WebRTC-Socket-NonMonotonicClockFix.\n\n    When enabled, this resolves issues where packet receive timestamps\n    latch into the past or become stale due to non-monotonic socket clocks,\n    backward clock adjustments, or clock drift.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:555794212\n    Change-Id: I77621b4c7fa8b7e284f64725ec526f7f75422b10\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/499200\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48498}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/experiments/field_trials.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/async_udp_socket.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/async_udp_socket.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/async_udp_socket_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/clock_aligner.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/clock_aligner.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/clock_aligner_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "677d5403dcad0d9ac82419acff90d935360f26a3", "git_parents": ["99f727ae17ab527380c7e1b9a6bec567246f48e3"], "node": "34ce20a00ec19e788640d539500b442904743b0c", "parents": ["682a6da91340769c5b8676aa144502b31e25786d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 09385480af\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/09385480af77e5fc9529349d6d49b56ffd63e5c1\n    SCReAM: Only calculate delay metrics on packets in recent burst window\n\n    Previously, ParseScreamFeedback calculated min and max one-way delay\n    across all packets reported in a feedback message. When feedback was\n    sent infrequently (e.g. 100-250ms at low bitrates or during sparse\n    periods), natural transit jitter across the long interval caused\n    latency difference to remain high (\u003e 10ms). This falsely throttled\n    the reference window increase scale factor down to 0.1, severely\n    delaying BWE rampup.\n\n    This change restricts the min/max one-way delay calculation in\n    ParseScreamFeedback to packets sent within a recent tail burst window:\n    - BurstWindowMin (default 25ms) from the last sent packet\n    - Extendable up to BurstWindowMax (default 50ms) as long as consecutive\n      packets have send time gap \u003c= BurstWindowMaxGap (default 3ms)\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: Ib955ed0aa1506a0405f5c24d4c62b2b53ecd0cac\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/499043\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48499}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/delay_based_congestion_control.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/delay_based_congestion_control_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/g3doc/implementation_diff.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_feedback.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_feedback.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_feedback_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/scream_test.cc"], "git_node": "5ca13ff617f862e9d53c16b07e82327e29f75a93", "git_parents": ["677d5403dcad0d9ac82419acff90d935360f26a3"], "node": "b3c17add0c9fd2a670a56ad8d736ba88ccbc365a", "parents": ["34ce20a00ec19e788640d539500b442904743b0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from a15ee918a3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a15ee918a3be67705ce9da2cea38051491828218\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-06T04:07:53).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I774fde67246a279a708180653f7a2895a44a457a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500280\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48500}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "1b5431784e16bf3c8407a0a567b4bdcec966bd63", "git_parents": ["5ca13ff617f862e9d53c16b07e82327e29f75a93"], "node": "eb155381a29734c273dd1beb888c99f8f0190bf0", "parents": ["b3c17add0c9fd2a670a56ad8d736ba88ccbc365a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6efdb1d4e9\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6efdb1d4e974a8594e1263d8f7e432dc22a5c7dd\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-07T04:05:43).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I585d7666a564aba4567d30d67abfa8e786a70d37\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500540\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48501}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "0be47e831215a1f21578aa70105493286bede7c0", "git_parents": ["1b5431784e16bf3c8407a0a567b4bdcec966bd63"], "node": "abb336128577024ef9ee6ce72aef0ef8d3b62460", "parents": ["eb155381a29734c273dd1beb888c99f8f0190bf0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 5155d4b0a9\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5155d4b0a9bb8bb630d4e70b22516641cd460731\n    Decouple transport packet delivery from network thread in CallTest\n\n    Run PacketTransport and FakeNetworkPipe on a dedicated transport thread\n    in CallTest, decoupling packet transport delivery from Call's internal\n    network thread.\n\n    Introduce TransportToNetworkPacketBridge and\n    SendingTransportToNetworkPacketBridge to marshal received packets and\n    OnSentPacket notifications across to Call's network thread\n    asynchronously.\n\n    This models production behavior where transport delivery occurs outside\n    the Call queue and prevents reentrancy and deadlock between media\n    encoding/pacing and packet delivery that can happen in some tests when\n    Call is configured with a single thread for network and worker:\n\n    https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/webrtc/builders/try/mac_rel/95229/overview\n\n    Bug: webrtc:11993\n    Change-Id: I8b9da782fb0266942f55283b0afcb4f12b1eb1ab\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500460\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48502}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/call_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/call_test.h"], "git_node": "ad88d5b8c2f04f6c85840686925b7db6e446bf8c", "git_parents": ["0be47e831215a1f21578aa70105493286bede7c0"], "node": "d89e7788b8993978c5af207e85a505cccc1339b2", "parents": ["abb336128577024ef9ee6ce72aef0ef8d3b62460"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9bc0124a0a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9bc0124a0a16b3c3e94ed6dee12c3589f5ac0b5d\n    Introduce EncodedAudioFrameInjectorInterface.\n\n    Intended to support a new Web API to inject encoded media in a\n    peerconnection. It uses a placeholder AudioEncoder and AudioTrack to\n    simulate normal audio processing.\n\n    Bug: chromium:532190488\n    Change-Id: I4d69a377412623f5c73fc659e83493a737725113\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497100\n    Reviewed-by: Jakob Ivarsson\u200e \u003cjakobi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48503}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/encoded_audio_frame_injector_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/rtp_sender_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/audio_send_stream.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/media_channel.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0029.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/encoded_audio_frame_injector.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/encoded_audio_frame_injector.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_proxy.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_receiver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "615b152967de3e8b371a478eee078a6a489d632c", "git_parents": ["ad88d5b8c2f04f6c85840686925b7db6e446bf8c"], "node": "800ec432b8222843e3f1808026ec7e0ad5138d4e", "parents": ["d89e7788b8993978c5af207e85a505cccc1339b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 5fd97c10d5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5fd97c10d592a2efc522e0e5b12f436cfe5bc11e\n    Roll chromium_revision 57ed38e9f7..dca9c4468e (1682199:1690475)\n\n    Manually fix the roll by adding the same fix as https://chromium-review.git.corp.google.com/c/chromium/src/+/8259432 in WebRTC (clang: consume clang-android-runtime-library on Linux too).\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/57ed38e9f7..dca9c4468e\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/57ed38e9f7..dca9c4468e\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * android_ndk_version: 2@30.0.15729638..2@30.0.16138531\n    * fuchsia_version: version:33.20260814.3.1..version:33.20260824.1.1\n    * siso_version: git_revision:bc45e8f67ae0f37d337190ad64aa8bb440c791eb..git_revision:efbbe7f1892211b5e9512576843a3c247b6a6d7c\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/8a8d38839a..8ca8a372ca\n    * sr