d_party/androidx/cipd: SaKviZDdUK6w34Z7aU4SvE5FZBeke5TuFOXWm5JCWEkC..jFoeHemr4FrlCYCfvynepL61nbKzpKGLtfT7eFuU-YQC\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/69a652ea05..c924a7c537\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/d58e50d914..806a40c4f6\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/0f6077afa1..e1ab7df93f\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/12cc78a34e..89fd0aa10a/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: I2cca000d6295a7ff7bf6d5c678df50672f931d38\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501020\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48522}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "839e3b112b757bfc4438c5a2536df0ff88664d73", "git_parents": ["69d2b9aadb28ab0acd2d96d3529f41f238f8310a"], "node": "d101e19a812086379a758e7234e07c7bfb99bc8a", "parents": ["cfc9a19012cc2998565d866dbc9657572d9f3112"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 23b0662fd1\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/23b0662fd11100856b001714262988d140555062\n    Fix race in TooManyDataChannelsOpenedBeforeConnecting\n\n    The test checked caller and callee MaxChannels() immediately after\n    WaitForConnection(). However, WaitForConnection() only checks for ICE\n    connection. SCTP association establishment over DTLS runs\n    asynchronously and completes after ICE connection, causing MaxChannels()\n    to intermittently return std::nullopt and fail assertions.\n\n    - Wait for caller and callee SCTP MaxChannels() to match expected values\n      asynchronously using WaitUntil.\n    - Add using ::testing::NotNull and assert non-null transport pointers.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Ia63c0a78bad07db8faff998d8e2924b3c4619755\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500742\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48523}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_end_to_end_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "ba5bfa9cf3f7a97cb519e204c9ffd02380be1c34", "git_parents": ["839e3b112b757bfc4438c5a2536df0ff88664d73"], "node": "b50c8d5c104508738d695fdf1742060168bf1c68", "parents": ["d101e19a812086379a758e7234e07c7bfb99bc8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 52e450c947\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/52e450c947f51d30b6edce94b7051aac510b6001\n    Add CBR rate control tests for V2 VideoEncoderInterface validation.\n\n    These tests are meant to validate some baseline behavior, and are not\n    intended to be used for continuous performance benchmarking.\n\n    Several test scenarios are left as follow-ups.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:496266459\n    Change-Id: I36d3d5cb072074bc3ee88d21b09d8854811cefed\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/499721\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48524}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_encoder_rate_control_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "da942e4c02370070ae980035ca75f7b40ef8f5b8", "git_parents": ["ba5bfa9cf3f7a97cb519e204c9ffd02380be1c34"], "node": "b3788822f46c09451ed4309c683ff04d2f7fab0b", "parents": ["b50c8d5c104508738d695fdf1742060168bf1c68"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 83c2ab9ac6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/83c2ab9ac62dbfb96cf58d66622ed645c6f50215\n    pc: fix premature ICE candidate signaling in CallTransferredForCaller\n\n    In PeerConnectionIntegrationTest.CallTransferredForCaller, connecting\n    fake signaling before creating and setting the remote offer on the new\n    callee allowed in-flight ICE candidates from the caller to be relayed\n    prematurely. Because the new callee had not yet received the remote\n    offer, AddIceCandidate rejected the candidate, causing an assertion\n    failure.\n\n    Signal SDP only during initial re-negotiation with the new callee, and\n    re-enable ICE candidate signaling after the offer is set.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ia87da3366c7ee7878d1728940653c7482974999e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500940\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48525}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/slow_peer_connection_integration_test.cc"], "git_node": "80131b1c59c60315abb37adb85ac77ab89ae0624", "git_parents": ["da942e4c02370070ae980035ca75f7b40ef8f5b8"], "node": "7eac95a60aba5d06c42a979384082a0455176275", "parents": ["b3788822f46c09451ed4309c683ff04d2f7fab0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from b7f122dfe6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b7f122dfe63da9b984bee1e0debd0bc7257f0ff5\n    Migrate standalone tools and loopback tests to LoggingConfig\n\n    Update standalone command-line tools, loopback test runners, and fuzzer\n    defaults to initialize logging via webrtc::InitializeLogging instead of\n    legacy LogMessage::LogToDebug and SetLogToStderr:\n    - video_loopback\n    - sv_loopback\n    - screenshare_loopback\n    - rtc_event_log_visualizer\n    - rtc_event_log_to_text\n    - video_encoder\n    - data_channel_benchmark\n    - audio_processing_simulator\n    - rnn_vad_tool\n    - webrtc_fuzzer_main\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42234107\n    Change-Id: I52a531176a5d2ba09c460a9afecb55c05085b4ee\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500741\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48526}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/rnn_vad/rnn_vad_tool.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/audio_processing_simulator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/data_channel_benchmark/data_channel_benchmark.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/rtc_event_log_to_text/main.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/rtc_event_log_visualizer/main.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/video_encoder/video_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/webrtc_fuzzer_main.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/screenshare_loopback.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/sv_loopback.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_loopback.cc"], "git_node": "647b35694b86847f97d3cf77b363c730bb7db849", "git_parents": ["80131b1c59c60315abb37adb85ac77ab89ae0624"], "node": "49261017e27b0335f01a5adeeb46675b7a6dd3be", "parents": ["7eac95a60aba5d06c42a979384082a0455176275"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 88fae9df4f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/88fae9df4f35ffe4df089ab9ee3bc8bc99a208ae\n    Roll chromium_revision 89fd0aa10a..0739e1d2d9 (1693561:1693673)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/89fd0aa10a..0739e1d2d9\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/89fd0aa10a..0739e1d2d9\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/fead248f7b..55629f64f1\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/c585383919..aea45ffee0\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/96f27f9615..b138532971\n    * src/third_party/androidx/cipd: jFoeHemr4FrlCYCfvynepL61nbKzpKGLtfT7eFuU-YQC..lOPALhnO3FBbFRzb8lMkPO7jYNDPJnH1wm52Z95oKyIC\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/c924a7c537..5ac00be14b\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/e1ab7df93f..e25373a588\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/89fd0aa10a..0739e1d2d9/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: I7096bcf50f07d1d4100576ab60df5959bd37b5ae\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501060\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48527}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "e02bbb2873e4b1a770b83041786dfc124afb8d81", "git_parents": ["647b35694b86847f97d3cf77b363c730bb7db849"], "node": "972a314cbaa7cd7a02b505295bf1ce793718a309", "parents": ["49261017e27b0335f01a5adeeb46675b7a6dd3be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 05e27f1265\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/05e27f126511a4c853ab73102233897ca09d6ddb\n    Propagate DTLS-SRTP writable state changes after activation\n\n    When SRTP is already active, MaybeSetupDtlsSrtp returns without\n    notifying writable-state subscribers. A media channel attached while\n    the transport is not writable can consequently miss the recovery edge\n    and never satisfy its first-writable send condition.\n\n    Update the cached writable state after attempting SRTP setup. This\n    propagates both loss and recovery while retaining readiness checks and\n    deduplicating notifications already emitted during SRTP activation.\n\n    Add regression coverage for a subscriber attached during an outage\n    and separate RTP/RTCP recovery with RTCP mux disabled.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Test: rtc_pc_unittests (613 passed; new tests fail without fix)\n    Test: Native Chrome P2P outage/recovery reproduction and media interop\n    Change-Id: Ia6c1b1397895508924e630026742517485221b06\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500980\n    Commit-Queue: simon \u003cxiaoshumin@agora.io\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48528}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_srtp_transport.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_srtp_transport_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "c0f4c2ecc8f2afebb6a175061e808b8d288dc2c1", "git_parents": ["e02bbb2873e4b1a770b83041786dfc124afb8d81"], "node": "24ebbae02055626a035a2d1ff5d3885c6bc07447", "parents": ["972a314cbaa7cd7a02b505295bf1ce793718a309"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 8a9a929a80\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/8a9a929a801b0ef53ae60fd10a672c589e608a59\n    Prevent delayed FrameDecoded from advancing RTP cleanup epoch\n\n    FrameDecoded() unwraps a stored uint16_t RTP sequence number relative\n    to the current receive state. If the frame is decoded only after the\n    receive sequence advances by more than half the 16-bit range, the old\n    value can unwrap into the next epoch. PacketBuffer::ClearTo() then\n    advances the cleanup boundary into that future epoch, and subsequent\n    packets from the current epoch are dropped.\n\n    Use PeekUnwrap() so delayed decode feedback cannot modify the receive\n    unwrapper. If the resulting cleanup boundary is ahead of\n    newest_media_seq_num_, remove only that frame's history entries and\n    skip both PacketBuffer and RtpFrameReferenceFinder cleanup.\n\n    Track the newest-media watermark on the H.264/H.265 receive path as\n    well, so the same validation applies on every codec path.\n\n    Add focused RtpVideoStreamReceiver2 coverage and an end-to-end VP9\n    flexible-mode regression test.\n\n    R=asapersson@webrtc.org\n\n    Bug: webrtc:556950523\n    Change-Id: I673ccb0397cb9df891cc4882503c0df5c926d632\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/499540\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48529}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0030.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0035.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0037.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0041.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0056.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0058.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0059.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0138.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "e54ab930888f6dd803588ad4594e1ee886f94f1f", "git_parents": ["c0f4c2ecc8f2afebb6a175061e808b8d288dc2c1"], "node": "9a06a67d44e8a79d1d837bc66d2a5496c8469584", "parents": ["24ebbae02055626a035a2d1ff5d3885c6bc07447"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 08a639c57a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/08a639c57a841b16d7d5a98962c220cd7aa7217d\n    Protect PeerConnection lifecycle and JNI invocations with ReadWriteLock.\n\n    Add a ReentrantReadWriteLock in PeerConnection to prevent use-after-free\n    race conditions between JNI method invocations and dispose().\n    Concurrent calls to JNI methods while dispose() is executing could lead\n    to native memory corruption when freeOwnedPeerConnection is executed\n    while another thread is accessing the C++ PeerConnection instance.\n\n    Changes:\n    * Introduce lifecycleLock (ReentrantReadWriteLock) and wrap JNI-calling\n      methods with callWithNative/runWithNative under readLock.\n    * Throw IllegalStateException(\"PeerConnection has been disposed.\") when\n      invoking methods on a disposed instance.\n    * In dispose(), execute close() and child disposals prior to acquiring\n      writeLock to avoid deadlocks with signaling thread observer callbacks.\n    * Guard freeOwnedPeerConnection and zeroing nativePeerConnection under\n      writeLock.\n    * Make dispose() idempotent so duplicate or concurrent calls complete\n      safely.\n\n    Bug: b/533453798\n    Change-Id: If848b8dd7652c9810256414db890ec206cb8c996\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500801\n    Commit-Queue: Linus Nilsson \u003clnilsson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48530}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "1dc3cacc3a9dc115c7a242b555d1970cdd978d28", "git_parents": ["e54ab930888f6dd803588ad4594e1ee886f94f1f"], "node": "9397b9940c62dfddfa1c9544ae5fdb62b5171b4c", "parents": ["9a06a67d44e8a79d1d837bc66d2a5496c8469584"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from c39a2fc679\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c39a2fc679bc66d69ef5fee86d58549fda863459\n    Add simulated time support to CallTest\n\n    Allow CallTest subclasses to run under simulated time by providing\n    constructors that accept a TimeController pointer or unique_ptr ownership.\n    When a TimeController is configured, CallTest passes it to\n    CreateTestEnvironment and creates network and transport threads via\n    TimeController::CreateThread instead of using physical threads.\n\n    In RtpRtcpObserver, add Wait(TimeController*) to allow waiting under\n    simulated time without blocking real-time execution.\n\n    Migrate CodecEndToEndTest and EndToEndTestH264 to run with\n    GlobalSimulatedTimeController, resolving long runtimes and timeouts on trybots.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ia33271bdf6262fd85461c9284048cd3b6bc00c3b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500822\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48531}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/call_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/call_test.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/rtp_rtcp_observer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/end_to_end_tests/codec_tests.cc"], "git_node": "e9b776eafaa6960786ebd7a847b326dadf3ada63", "git_parents": ["1dc3cacc3a9dc115c7a242b555d1970cdd978d28"], "node": "8807992e38116a6a80bd4ac9306b3df9c16a7fb4", "parents": ["9397b9940c62dfddfa1c9544ae5fdb62b5171b4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from d4443ab23f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d4443ab23f953e12d3d7edefbd74dfc1b941ba08\n    Remove legacy logging calls\n\n    - Remove legacy LogMessage::LogToDebug calls from\n      common_video/h264/sps_vui_rewriter_unittest.cc.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42234107\n    Change-Id: I0ceea2eae5ccb900919e695a1b90dc5a92c7a349\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500821\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48532}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/h264/sps_vui_rewriter_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "8d4d98ffa5100d0663f7b587e9043f57298989b6", "git_parents": ["e9b776eafaa6960786ebd7a847b326dadf3ada63"], "node": "ad67d77e73d942d48984ef6b3eb447dacb4294c9", "parents": ["8807992e38116a6a80bd4ac9306b3df9c16a7fb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 683588cc3a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/683588cc3aa5ba47f3d7635178317241e466d50c\n    Roll chromium_revision 0739e1d2d9..1a5eaa35af (1693673:1693924)\n\n    