\n    Change-Id: I726397c4099603790c7f881817d25bafa6aa1021\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501040\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48538}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_packet_processor.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_packet_processor.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/packet_processor.h"], "git_node": "b8bb7f7e09e1f1cfbb0df65064af2630e7244325", "git_parents": ["ffc970219ce402a59233458309167c5c588af2fe"], "node": "40f390ec3a53947dd5715eafd4accc38de6a4548", "parents": ["8c90de5ba77bb3f44fde46b90668556bd97f21d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 21c61a76d6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/21c61a76d62b3f1aee87c6cc6da57559456518f9\n    Validate NALU length and SPS dimensions in H.264 RTP depacketizer\n\n    Add bounds validation in VideoRtpDepacketizerH264:\n    - In ProcessStapAOrSingleNalu, verify that the rewritten SPS NALU size\n      does not exceed uint16_t max before writing it into the 16-bit\n      STAP-A length header. Packets with rewritten NALUs exceeding 65535\n      bytes are rejected rather than having their length truncated.\n    - Validate that parsed SPS picture dimensions are non-zero and fit\n      within uint16_t range before populating RTP video header dimensions.\n\n    Bug: b/522976033\n    Change-Id: I34218f123521509235236a2afe7efcddfe6ca106\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500602\n    Auto-Submit: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48539}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/video_rtp_depacketizer_h264.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/video_rtp_depacketizer_h264_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "1b6ab5b8d72eb5cd8d41aa9064d3866c95fe7e53", "git_parents": ["b8bb7f7e09e1f1cfbb0df65064af2630e7244325"], "node": "6c89a2a66edcfd395a025c76a205ec14c10e49a4", "parents": ["40f390ec3a53947dd5715eafd4accc38de6a4548"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0605df5be8\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0605df5be8068d1b9524cf60988ee007f0967b02\n    dtls-in-stun: remove invalid dashes from ice-option\n\n    which are not ice-char. Also DCHECK for such names in\n    the ice option setter (not used by SetRemoteDescription)\n\n    Bug: chromium:556773246\n    Change-Id: I2494bb8c6f14c20f4e869522d52a0bc21a4e81c3\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500041\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48540}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/transport_description.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/transport_description.h"], "git_node": "a9bf4340c74c2f7f3fa570de03e881242a9a6de1", "git_parents": ["1b6ab5b8d72eb5cd8d41aa9064d3866c95fe7e53"], "node": "ddbc717d84e91257ae9dbadb87abf4d6715c6b55", "parents": ["6c89a2a66edcfd395a025c76a205ec14c10e49a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1e381bc89f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1e381bc89fda030af68de7e071eccfe7af6f58ee\n    Reenable AudioPacketLoss test\n\n    The test no longer looks flaky\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225249\n    Change-Id: Ia80c346a2f0dcbc45338b04da32dc406f2c2d5a4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500042\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48541}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "585c0b292480c7b4dc731024c6ebe838354eeda8", "git_parents": ["a9bf4340c74c2f7f3fa570de03e881242a9a6de1"], "node": "1c6ee54295a11ee22f349b982aa653f985ad515d", "parents": ["ddbc717d84e91257ae9dbadb87abf4d6715c6b55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 8354b7c19d\n\nEssentially a no-op since we're going to see this change\nreverted when we vendor in 348e5ff724.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/8354b7c19d32a3dbe7268319af6085e6ec9ec099\n    RtpSender: Create the Sframe encryptor and hand out a worker proxy\n\n    Implements `RtpSenderBase::CreateSframeEncryptorOrError`\n\n    When called, it creates a `SframeEncryptor` on the worker thread and \u2014\n    if an SSRC is already assigned \u2014 immediately pushes it to the media\n    channel via `SetSframeEncryptor`. If the SSRC is not yet known,\n    `SetSsrc` is updated to push the encryptor to the channel once an SSRC\n    is assigned.\n\n    The returned `SframeEncryptorInterface` is wrapped in a new\n    `SframeEncryptorProxy` that marshals `SetEncryptionKey` calls to the\n    worker thread, so callers can safely invoke it from any other thread.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: Ic647c4658fa672c820d09a13c34ee0b158f3ae89\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/493780\n    Commit-Queue: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48542}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/348e5ff724.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch"], "git_node": "aa0499bd997072fcb34358cc9d7027ccd6865dcd", "git_parents": ["585c0b292480c7b4dc731024c6ebe838354eeda8"], "node": "2e1478a3cd8c9e5e02d3eedaf386aebc99147cbb", "parents": ["1c6ee54295a11ee22f349b982aa653f985ad515d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0520f29091\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0520f29091f6c2e4848076e3ad13dfd51d1a3cff\n    Update protobuf version to fix perf bots\n\n    https://ci.chromium.org/p/webrtc/g/perf/console\n\n    Change-Id: I145b6b155d086d74c1aab02921bb131876370f9a\n    Bug: None\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501460\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48543}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/.vpython3", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "e3913f2f75cc85921803c390d2c1b47cafb265ea", "git_parents": ["aa0499bd997072fcb34358cc9d7027ccd6865dcd"], "node": "8568942f7844885b42c0f22c72db372feed41466", "parents": ["2e1478a3cd8c9e5e02d3eedaf386aebc99147cbb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 348e5ff724\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored 8354b7c19d.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/348e5ff7247ceffe58d8fa3daf8fb917d74f68c9\n    Revert \"RtpSender: Create the Sframe encryptor and hand out a worker proxy\"\n\n    This reverts commit 8354b7c19d32a3dbe7268319af6085e6ec9ec099.\n\n    Reason for revert: breaks webrtc-internal bot. Compile error in sframe\n\n    Failure Link: https://fusion2.corp.google.com/invocations/e9a2a344-3234-4d69-a6e9-b95f8700b396/targets/%2F%2Fthird_party%2Fwebrtc:webrtc_all_cc/log?q=label:session_id%3Dbtbs-224212c0-8627-4ddc-9137-60e85c0d9b6c\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e RtpSender: Create the Sframe encryptor and hand out a worker proxy\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Implements `RtpSenderBase::CreateSframeEncryptorOrError`\n    \u003e\n    \u003e When called, it creates a `SframeEncryptor` on the worker thread and \u2014\n    \u003e if an SSRC is already assigned \u2014 immediately pushes it to the media\n    \u003e channel via `SetSframeEncryptor`. If the SSRC is not yet known,\n    \u003e `SetSsrc` is updated to push the encryptor to the channel once an SSRC\n    \u003e is assigned.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e The returned `SframeEncryptorInterface` is wrapped in a new\n    \u003e `SframeEncryptorProxy` that marshals `SetEncryptionKey` calls to the\n    \u003e worker thread, so callers can safely invoke it from any other thread.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    \u003e Change-Id: Ic647c4658fa672c820d09a13c34ee0b158f3ae89\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/493780\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48542}\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    No-Presubmit: true\n    No-Tree-Checks: true\n    No-Try: true\n    Change-Id: I7e24587bf67f8f4a5f85a29c672fbccc22a566b8\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501520\n    Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Owners-Override: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48544}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/348e5ff724.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch"], "git_node": "78cd3859316157adec6f95acfc52be06ba2f392a", "git_parents": ["e3913f2f75cc85921803c390d2c1b47cafb265ea"], "node": "b81c107fd155561676cddc26457a5221d316981d", "parents": ["8568942f7844885b42c0f22c72db372feed41466"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 021f96f546\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/021f96f5462db3658bdbd3be5ebff2ca43acc9ae\n    Fix a bug where ICE restart with the same address would disconnect the selected connection on the callee side.\n\n    The root cause is that ports manage connections via remote addresses. If\n    a new generation candidate is applied on an old generation port, it may\n    create a new connection and replace any existing connection under the\n    same address, even when it is selected.\n\n    This change only blocks the replacement of selected connections so they\n    would still send data during ICE restart. The ICE restart should\n    conclude with selected connections under a new port with updated ufrag\n    and password. Then the connections kept here would be destroyed with the old port.\n\n    Unit test and integration test are updated accordingly.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:543082385\n    Change-Id: I9eb841b3f276d0c4d32d0d6d86906278e8a438a4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500240\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48545}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/p2p_transport_channel.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/p2p_transport_channel_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "07ed7756d84c52ab6f10912ff1fe42cd37abfac0", "git_parents": ["78cd3859316157adec6f95acfc52be06ba2f392a"], "node": "184137b405c7824449cafbc2a8ecf9ba983b88d8", "parents": ["b81c107fd155561676cddc26457a5221d316981d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from dab572fd15\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/dab572fd15e3fb975ed14a9e9290f723bb6e3f30\n    Fix flaky audio delay test by tracking samples cumulatively\n\n    In RenegotiateManyVideoTransceiversAndWatchAudioDelay,\n    AudioDelayStatsPercentageChecked() verifies that the audio concealment\n    ratio check ran by asserting that delta_samples \u003e= 2000 was reached.\n    Previously, delta_samples was computed per renegotiation step against a\n    trailing counter.\n\n    Following a fix[*] that reduced renegotiation latency, individual\n    renegotiation steps often complete in under 35 ms, producing fewer than\n    2000 samples per step and causing the test to fail on fast bots because\n    of the above assumptions.\n\n    * https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/494443\n\n    Track initial sample and concealment stats captured at the start of\n    watching delay stats, and evaluate the concealment ratio across all\n    cumulative samples.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Ia3dc524e920754be1f7eb39557a7930b500f232c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501440\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48546}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/integration_test_helpers.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/integration_test_helpers.h"], "git_node": "f3df2c76356dada5f0b3933da6674f37d1324db9", "git_parents": ["07ed7756d84c52ab6f10912ff1fe42cd37abfac0"], "node": "70bc466fab02b88460d8649ae3806d5e87b023dd", "parents": ["184137b405c7824449cafbc2a8ecf9ba983b88d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from c274fd80db\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c274fd80dbe9843ec9045f39d55e3843abcaf06c\n    Clean up dynamic configuration of logging in tests and default to LS_WARNING level logging.\n\n    Adds command-line flag `--log_level` in TestMainImpl (test_main_lib.cc),\n    defaulting to \"warning\" to reduce log noise during test runs on try\n    bots.\n\n    Removes ScopedSetLoggingLevel and its wrapper\n    OverrideLoggingLevelForTest from PeerConnectionIntegrationTestBase,\n    along with the call sites in peer_connection_integrationtest.cc.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42234107\n    Change-Id: I7ab44ff9279cf3fb74940a4d8934400672297f3a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501121\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48547}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/integration_test_helpers.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/integration_test_helpers.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/test_main_lib.cc"], "git_node": "46ab5c34deef7206b157eb54d0d59d20560972b7", "git_parents": ["f3df2c76356dada5f0b3933da6674f37d1324db9"], "node": "d4b14c87941929a517a1cfe52fb13ce88fc7d584", "parents": ["70bc466fab02b88460d8649ae3806d5e87b023dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from ee390f47cb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ee390f47cbc67b6feedeb3a62931907e13dfc1d8\n    Roll chromium_revision 7a79a07b9c..7b8e3afa63 (1694328:1694827)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/7a79a07b9c..7b8e3afa63\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/7a79a07b9c..7b8e3afa63\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * android_ndk_version: 2@30.0.16138531..2@30.0.16248370\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/b7e4cf2040..72be896edb\n    * src/buildtools/linux64: git_revision:c0e4aae6d809a08cd402432a7d23494fc3b2a776..git_revision:f99972118649814cd21b180eab5ae84df3c5fac7\n    * src/buildtools/mac: git_revision:c0e4aae6d809a08cd402432a7d23494fc3b2a776..git_revision:f99972118649814cd21b180eab5ae84df3c5fac7\n    * src/buildtools/win: git_revision:c0e4aae6d809a08cd402432a7d23494fc3b2a776..git_revision:f99972118649814cd21b180eab5ae84df3c5fac7\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/99dc4ecf7e..c428617d7c\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/08f81a9a88..b640ba8514\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/3c7ceaeb6b..2a983985ca\n    * src/third_party/android_build_tools/error_prone/cipd: nN5H1Y8S1tEwwsoItbX28RDCxerYmGsnnBVHo-t3PN8C..KpXELIonKxwvFae5F4Qkc3DaclJXQ_CSZGuF1NztP8UC\n    * src/third_party/android_build_tools/lint/cipd: OC5s2lVRF-HIZ1jTPeBpfvi1vP6b6N3QVqvDVn5ZkR0C..B6FDr2A7npJWaIE4uoGMlp4-3ZRkDnPK01MLp0Qi7M4C\n    * src/third_party/android_buil