ll diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/7b8e3afa63..34204b996b\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/72be896edb..1deee6343d\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/c428617d7c..b61cc4783d\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/b640ba8514..d477a5baad\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/2a983985ca..628012d6d9\n    * src/third_party/androidx/cipd: m2IdlD4IcWtEdjnBBz-NP7D3PjjD9wicibkIu2SWZxMC..Sb5Bagf0XbVAvJB_16gC0U7qRp2uKs35tBTX15kD3xwC\n    * src/third_party/boringssl/src: https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl.git/+log/f00ee8085f..ba26b4cb83\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/da08833a5d..1e5e3539fa\n    * src/third_party/eigen3/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen.git/+log/9ecb8f6fbc..68db0e246a\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/86600940b7..615c1fd5e4\n    * src/third_party/libFuzzer/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/compiler-rt/lib/fuzzer.git/+log/8c09a8f461..42af2c9785\n    * src/third_party/libyuv: https://chromium.googlesource.com/libyuv/libyuv.git/+log/2fed9193c9..3f3735e3f3\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/4c5b711791..8db6cf6029\n    * src/third_party/perfetto: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/perfetto.git/+log/ced94af64d..5bf9426822\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/39bed2aeaa..0c5c85c698\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/7b8e3afa63..34204b996b/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: Ic818c9cc69a16ffb3ff01dcbe92db65f1c300a20\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501602\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48549}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "f0c10f6366e72972cc5e740e12e5f00a41c5ebbe", "git_parents": ["2c7e2075b283798873e163ee48d0085f98a14690"], "node": "aeee3920042bc83c4f86099d7516fcae97fc8d5a", "parents": ["dfff2653576310bcc2f5464cbca8bbba08b9816b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9a6c973539\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9a6c973539e8afa908fa92a5dd87eeaf814aa33a\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-10T04:10:51).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I671b458b728be374fefc96bc9c197d5026fd6824\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501680\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48550}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "2c543eb846dbc3a0bce00dbd96563e1aeac1a9ad", "git_parents": ["f0c10f6366e72972cc5e740e12e5f00a41c5ebbe"], "node": "a6321701a85157a8cd5960919648d028ce7aaeb3", "parents": ["aeee3920042bc83c4f86099d7516fcae97fc8d5a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from c61fc59821\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c61fc59821a371ebe64e14ef172e1cb80d682ecd\n    Default worker thread to network thread\n\n    Currently, if no worker thread is injected in ConnectionContext,\n    a dedicated thread is created and started as a fallback. As part\n    of simplifying thread topologies, default to reusing the network thread\n    instead when no explicit worker thread dependency is provided.\n\n    - Annotate dependencies parameter with absl_nonnull.\n    - Change ConnectionContext::worker_thread_ type to Thread* const and\n      remove AlwaysValidPointer.\n    - Fall back to network_thread_ when dependencies-\u003eworker_thread is null.\n    - Add unit tests verifying worker thread fallback and injection.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:558821261\n    Change-Id: I533d4a9eb6ab580f77db37dbd2c782334554d56e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501620\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48551}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/connection_context.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/connection_context.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_factory_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "789146eb5d145a5c68dbe84bac959b2a90d53db9", "git_parents": ["2c543eb846dbc3a0bce00dbd96563e1aeac1a9ad"], "node": "4ad20d785f60c696a6a5d6d97b3ba44ae720456f", "parents": ["a6321701a85157a8cd5960919648d028ce7aaeb3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from bf31ff6fff\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bf31ff6fff0088bbbce706720e6f22be6f5294fa\n    pc: check remote ice-option validity and split ufrag/pwd UMA\n\n    which may allow enforcing the ice-char charset on some of them.\n\n    Bug: chromium:556773246\n    Change-Id: I3dc1b4a804e5d7f43c93db7bb53d8dbc96d31e52\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501140\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48552}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection.cc"], "git_node": "423f7cab5e2925b09976e2567bf952ce3aa4e1b8", "git_parents": ["789146eb5d145a5c68dbe84bac959b2a90d53db9"], "node": "e54937e667d22e7e4d9c1ccc392090d978bde76f", "parents": ["4ad20d785f60c696a6a5d6d97b3ba44ae720456f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7de2c300c0\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7de2c300c0b7187ed86e63f644237297886525e5\n    Batch transceiver channel teardown in ApplyRemoteDescription\n\n    When a remote answer lacks Sframe support for a media section that was\n    offered with Sframe, the transceiver is stopped and its channel is\n    cleared. Previously, this called RtpTransceiver::ClearChannel(), which\n    executes synchronous BlockingCalls to both the network and worker\n    threads from the signaling thread.\n\n    This change replaces the synchronous ClearChannel() call with tasks\n    batched via ScopedOperationsBatcher:\n    - Queue GetClearChannelNetworkTask() on network_tasks.\n    - Queue GetDeleteChannelWorkerTask() on worker_tasks.\n    - Run network_tasks before worker_tasks to ensure network teardown\n      precedes channel deletion on the worker thread.\n    - Guard receiver media channel setup with !transceiver-\u003estopped() so\n      stopped transceivers do not reinitialize receiver channels.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I540e89f2e07f15818bcd06876f6a16d5fced65f3\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501660\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48553}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc"], "git_node": "fd7253005d507b7a5e32bd3f2c8eac3ae1619965", "git_parents": ["423f7cab5e2925b09976e2567bf952ce3aa4e1b8"], "node": "ba48171342b033a8485b0c74e911d2bc95c5ee8a", "parents": ["e54937e667d22e7e4d9c1ccc392090d978bde76f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from f9e1d92faa\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f9e1d92faa04ca0193f0bea0e0c24298385179c1\n    Deflake ReceivedUlpfecPacketsNotNacked test\n\n    In hybrid NACK/FEC mode, VCMNackFecMethod::BitRateTooLowForFec disables\n    FEC when estimated bytes per frame falls below 400 bytes (96 kbps at\n    30 fps for 320x180 resolution) when RTT is under 200 ms.\n\n    Because FecEndToEndTest.ReceivedUlpfecPacketsNotNacked configured a\n    minimum bitrate of 30 kbps while immediately dropping 50% of media\n    packets, bandwidth estimation collapsed down to the 30 kbps floor.\n    This triggered BitRateTooLowForFec, permanently suppressing FEC\n    generation and causing the test to wait forever for FEC packets.\n\n    Additionally, dropping packets immediately from the start raced with\n    the initial RTCP SR/RR handshake needed to establish an RTT above the\n    20 ms threshold required for FEC in hybrid mode.\n\n    - Raise min_bitrate_bps from 30 kbps to 100 kbps to keep target bitrate\n      above the 96 kbps FEC cutoff.\n    - Introduce a 30-packet warm-up period to permit RTCP RTT measurement\n      and transport pipeline stabilization before injecting packet loss.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I51ced07de50d126f7847291db239b27b2cc4c6a8\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501700\n    Commit-Queue: Stefan Holmer \u003cstefan@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Stefan Holmer \u003cstefan@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48554}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/end_to_end_tests/fec_tests.cc"], "git_node": "91d25d2e28ea95c8bd4f2b316dc143d96aee9e24", "git_parents": ["fd7253005d507b7a5e32bd3f2c8eac3ae1619965"], "node": "9ee341c7bdac6c5953a0fe57a46dd2c3bbe2ce86", "parents": ["ba48171342b033a8485b0c74e911d2bc95c5ee8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0999bd55d3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0999bd55d3a2d39cc70b759ce4b27ff14a66fb1a\n    Roll chromium_revision 34204b996b..de383d292c (1695158:1695310)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/34204b996b..de383d292c\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/34204b996b..de383d292c\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/1deee6343d..aa37fbfbed\n    * src/buildtools/linux64: git_revision:f99972118649814cd21b180eab5ae84df3c5fac7..git_revision:0625da07ece7b1a374ec0719b6f40ebe3d0950c1\n    * src/buildtools/mac: git_revision:f99972118649814cd21b180eab5ae84df3c5fac7..git_revision:0625da07ece7b1a374ec0719b6f40ebe3d0950c1\n    * src/buildtools/win: git_revision:f99972118649814cd21b180eab5ae84df3c5fac7..git_revision:0625da07ece7b1a374ec0719b6f40ebe3d0950c1\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/b61cc4783d..4b3f93d588\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/d477a5baad..c6288d61ab\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/628012d6d9..b1f7430388\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/autorolled/cipd: JetADwuF_leE4vCWOHphTdfAtNxKScZBb6peZEwoXiQC..M5geAdO5h5u6qMhI5HJjtl2hy2rurxM_De07GBeU8rQC\n    * src/third_party/androidx/cipd: Sb5Bagf0XbVAvJB_16gC0U7qRp2uKs35tBTX15kD3xwC..B8AcZ1jNq7w5WmVpFSPqfX55cJ0lPw2l8N_YHf-jMPcC\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/1e5e3539fa..08f3e8c0eb\n    * src/third_party/eigen3/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen.git/+log/68db0e246a..198a61f683\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/615c1fd5e4..a65db1b513\n    * src/third_party/harfbuzz/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz.git/+log/46ea946ab4..f5efbbef38\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/0c5c85c698..5139c2ad5a\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/34204b996b..de383d292c/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: Ie8e9470b3573594dfb7f223a472a22c25ed435b0\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501760\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48555}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "f396db3cb71b3d75b370fee5c0558cd9e2dedb02", "git_parents": ["91d25d2e28ea95c8bd4f2b316dc143d96aee9e24"], "node": "745be8363c66a344ceeed71a78333733ea689465", "parents": ["9ee341c7bdac6c5953a0fe57a46dd2c3bbe2ce86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from b40276d490\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b40276d49053f0ee00b5423df3a58129c826b510\n    Fix RtpSenderReceiverTest.InjectVideoFrameOnDifferentThread flakey test.\n\n    Bug: chromium:532190488\n    Change-Id: I7a5933b2a1790399101d4f3f9bfbe452adf75ae5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501780\n    Reviewed-by: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48556}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_receiver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "0734c75b9455cee7ad9b3fad402cc7826386325b", "git_parents": ["f396db3cb71b3d75b370fee5c0558cd9e2dedb02"], "node": "ba705a91e87276e344583c3f0b5647d78cf849e4", "parents": ["745be8363c66a344ceeed71a78333733ea689465"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 84155da406\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/84155da40646576fd8de1063268e96fee8b998a6\n    opus: remove unused WebRtcOpus_PacketHasVoiceActivity\n\n    The side channel check was also wrong:\n\n      if (channels == 2 &&\n          (frame_data[frame][0] \u003c\u003c (silk_frames + 1)) \u003e\u003e (8 - silk_frames))\n\n    The byte promotes to int, so the left shift does not discard the mid\n    channel flags and the right shift brings them back down. That made the\n    side channel VAD test fire on the mid channel LBRR flag, a false\n    positive on stereo SILK frames carrying in-band FEC.\n\n    The correct form truncates to 8 bits after the left shift:\n\n      const uint8_t flags = frame_data[frame][0];\n      const uint8_t side = static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e(flags \u003c\u003c (silk_frames + 1));\n      if (channels == 2 && side \u003e\u003e (8 - silk_frames))\n\n    Note: the encoder never produces this combination so no consequence.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I8b7118a0c749287e6850e3b8d3fb136e4d4f9809\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501701\n    Reviewed-by: Jakob Ivarsson\u200e \u003cjakobi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jakob Ivarsson\u200e \u003cjakobi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48557}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/opus_interface.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/opus_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/opus_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "f9504fb2d5fd32486e9a61fae1cd7133608f5b6a", "git_parents": ["0734c75b9455cee7ad9b3fad402cc7826386325b"], "node": "76c6c30bfb18b14e47942b3c966233e7ecb92313", "parents": ["ba705a91e87276e344583c3f0b5647d78cf849e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from e101a4c2c6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e101a4c2c66232aaf60823e447ded36d6e8ebdfd\n    Invoke Audio Injector callback on ProxyAudioEncoder::OnReceivedTargetAudioBitrate calls.\n\n    Remove empty override of the OnReceivedTargetAudioBitrate method\n    overload in ProxyAudioEncoder and handle invocation from multiple\n    threads.\n\n    Bug: chromium:532190488\n    Change-Id: I28409904b57f7341120a9e37c2fd0a5ec948dcee\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501580\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48558}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/encoded_audio_frame_injector_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/encoded_audio_frame_injector.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/encoded_audio_frame_injector.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_receiver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "d19a4530d94d293631221f4d7ad4d8a2f4faa35d", "git_parents": ["f9504fb2d5fd32486e9a61fae1cd7133608f5b6a"], "node": "339ef9ce4bfa7bb99d81371fa9974025d0870240", "parents": ["76c6c30bfb18b14e47942b3c966233e7ecb92313"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from dc39512537\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/dc39512537add4a656e810d9774138b075510276\n    Add high complexity CBR test cases for V2 Video Encoder API.\n\n    This CL adds a synthetic frame generator that crops and scales a\n    (preferably) high-detail static image along a smooth, erratic,\n    non-repeating trajectory governed by double-pendulum chaotic physics\n    with dynamic zoom and optional luma noise. Designed as an absolute\n    stress test for video encoders and their rate control.\n\n    This generator and the recently added camera switching generator are\n    added as new unit tests for the V2 VideoEncoderInterface.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:496266459\n    Change-Id: I2a2da36e39d960a3eb802f8c0c0bbc9638a03e76\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/500802\n    Auto-Submit: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48559}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/test/video_quality_test_fixture.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_encoder_rate_control_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/frame_reader.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/pendulum_frame_generator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/pendulum_frame_generator.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/switching_frame_reader.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/switching_frame_reader.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/switching_frame_reader_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/yuv_frame_reader.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/yuv_frame_reader_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_loopback.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_quality_test.cc"], "git_node": "1ef43c0c4f351d224e4cda92263f1241885ca5e6", "git_parents": ["d19a4530d94d293631221f4d7ad4d8a2f4faa35d"], "node": "811ae55882a17f42a3308ba4c00537e1d617fcfd", "parents": ["339ef9ce4bfa7bb99d81371fa9974025d0870240"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 68c958e39f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/68c958e39fe36f202a66d4fcac353bd10d002f6b\n    Extract common Y4M header parser and add unit tests\n\n    Move duplicated and brittle Y4M header parsing out of\n    Y4mFrameGenerator and Y4mFrameReader into a safe, common\n    Y4mHeaderParser utility with unit tests.\n\n    The parser handles:\n    - Small frames with minimal headers (as short as width/height)\n    - Arbitrary tag order and optional framerate / color space / comments\n    - Maximum headers up to 2048 bytes, rejecting headers that exceed it\n    - Bound checks using absl::string_view and webrtc::StringToNumber\n    - std::optional\u003cFrequency\u003e framerate\n    - std::optional\u003cColorSpace\u003e color_space (rejecting unknown color spaces)\n    - DataSize header_size\n\n    Bug: webrtc:496266459\n    Change-Id: Ic449c9eaf9c48e0a2bf6eab07786e3d39896a1bd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501560\n    Reviewed-by: Artem Titov \u003ctitovartem@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48560}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/y4m_frame_generator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/y4m_frame_reader.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/y4m_header_parser.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/y4m_header_parser.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/y4m_header_parser_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "6448af7b971bfb1c560b7623267444d160b8530f", "git_parents": ["1ef43c0c4f351d224e4cda92263f1241885ca5e6"], "node": "f774c51196dc01d29b659858d161f368df2877df", "parents": ["811ae55882a17f42a3308ba4c00537e1d617fcfd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 782a8de7f1\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/782a8de7f1788c008e399efe2225ff5bad22ab4e\n    Remove rust libraries matching cxx bridges\n\n    cxx bridges creates such library automagically, having both may create\n    duplicate symbols linking issues.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:416446214\n    Change-Id: I1b1ccfab5a9