.git/+log/6794dd02d7..a2bdd581e7\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/a65db1b513..a1b4a9b2ac\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/8db6cf6029..439632ae95\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/2ea3a7770f..7c70df87eb\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:3d1174859c0a5bb00d87c78506f8c031afad16aa..git_revision:e8ff1a9251fd84ffa2645964347cf41281903c09\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:3d1174859c0a5bb00d87c78506f8c031afad16aa..git_revision:e8ff1a9251fd84ffa2645964347cf41281903c09\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:3d1174859c0a5bb00d87c78506f8c031afad16aa..git_revision:e8ff1a9251fd84ffa2645964347cf41281903c09\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/db0bd2e3b9..5334a28253/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: I94058e3a37f3c4b5344a32ed8f689e4b6e918bef\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/502200\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48567}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "a7377cbc9c64cee502c31840e8b3674ed8b2ae29", "git_parents": ["4de50f5a6dff8ea3591cc3438265bdc3e60c9154"], "node": "e722787b726394015a6e84282cfb7068a8535c7b", "parents": ["3a382cba66cd640f331d9a3e581c57ac39b68fe1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from e4edcbbeaf\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e4edcbbeaf11c05f4f3d5dfd1106784861298597\n    Fix building frame_analyzer_host target\n\n    While modifying the script, update its style to avoid warnings\n\n    Tested: autoninja -C out/Default frame_analyzer_host\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I6a56bf62e5e5d34423878c07dd73f05de6d2169b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/502141\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48568}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/executable_host_build.py"], "git_node": "0794d829264c88bc5b8b9aad24545355dab81d69", "git_parents": ["a7377cbc9c64cee502c31840e8b3674ed8b2ae29"], "node": "6286be0618c8c25fc308f61ba4112458f7c3b47e", "parents": ["e722787b726394015a6e84282cfb7068a8535c7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 22dfd42c3a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/22dfd42c3a74d3ad240cd95cfc1d289625e3116f\n    scale_resolution_down_to: Ensure lowest active stream is not disabled.\n\n    When scale_resolution_down_to is used in simulcast and resolution is adapted, upper streams exceeding the max pixel limit are disabled. However, currently all active streams could be dropped when the lowest stream is inactive (e.g. {inactive, inactive, active}).\n\n    Restrict max_num_layers to at least min_num_layers (the layer count required to include the first active stream) so that the lowest active stream is never disabled.\n\n    Bug: b/289987197\n    Change-Id: Ic8c464c697efb3d3bb82f57243e0962b95d0bf77\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501740\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48569}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third