 Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48592}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/acm2/acm_send_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/audio_network_adaptor/controller_manager_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/g722/audio_encoder_g722.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/audio_decoder_opus.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/audio_encoder_multi_channel_opus_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/audio_encoder_opus.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/test/lapped_transform.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/neteq/decoder_database.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/neteq/dtmf_tone_generator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/neteq/merge.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/neteq/neteq_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/neteq/tools/constant_pcm_packet_source.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/neteq/tools/input_audio_file.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0007.patch"], "git_node": "fcc08a0e8a7e7e4632bbde5057519cd498644f02", "git_parents": ["129282be3ad1c56ecfe3082350c1c13167208e9e"], "node": "767ca34f2860ddd76cc729968046eefda9f040d8", "parents": ["d40ad359489f9ce800c6c0eff9e1d18389480c15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from 8d208e76fb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/8d208e76fb1ad2b92d557f752e9d1d7d49059efa\n    Remove SetUseNetworkThreadAsWorkerThread\n\n    Support for a worker thread that is distinct from the network thread is\n    being removed from WebRTC, and the peer connection level test framework\n    no longer supplies a worker thread of its own. That left\n    InjectableComponents::worker_thread write only: nothing reads it.\n\n    - Remove PeerConfigurer::SetUseNetworkThreadAsWorkerThread().\n    - Remove InjectableComponents::worker_thread.\n    - Drop the calls in pc_full_stack_tests, since using the network thread\n      as the worker thread is now the only supported behavior.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:558821261\n    Change-Id: Iab6867ca6fee45216a6c06e3cfa0adad8c1abb00\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/502600\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48593}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/test/pclf/media_quality_test_params.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/test/pclf/peer_configurer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/test/pclf/peer_configurer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/pc_full_stack_tests.cc"], "git_node": "69608153245d7430fc49f13889b87e78debf24c3", "git_parents": ["fcc08a0e8a7e7e4632bbde5057519cd498644f02"], "node": "135c9077e0b1ae5f657b6212e3a442abc4adee0f", "parents": ["767ca34f2860ddd76cc729968046eefda9f040d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072400 - Vendor libwebrtc from c4f21b1f91\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c4f21b1f91386bae6d710540976dff5aae67b3c5\n    [M155] [Wayland] Fix crash in ProcessDMABuffer and clean up renegotiate event\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e [Wayland] Fix crash in ProcessDMABuffer and clean up renegotiate event\n    \u003e\n    \u003e When DMA-BUF modifier import fails, ProcessDMABuffer attempts to\n    \u003e renegotiate stream parameters via pw_loop_signal_event() using\n    \u003e pw_-\u003erenegotiate. However, if pw_-\u003erenegotiate is null (e.g., if\n    \u003e pw_loop_add_event failed due to eventfd/file descriptor exhaustion),\n    \u003e pw_loop_signal_event() invokes loop_signal_event() with a null\n    \u003e source, resulting in a SIGSEGV at address 0x0.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e This CL adds null checks for pw_ and pw_-\u003erenegotiate in\n    \u003e ProcessDMABuffer, consistent with UpdateScreenCastStreamResolution and\n    \u003e UpdateScreenCastStreamFrameRate. Additionally, PipeWireThreadLoop's\n    \u003e destructor now destroys the renegotiate event source using\n    \u003e pw_loop_destroy_source() to avoid leaking an eventfd on stream teardown.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e TAG=agy\n    \u003e CONV=8d6dd432-bbd6-43de-b1dd-6d1a0d68bffa\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: chromium:559350359\n    \u003e Change-Id: Id2463382532dac5a8b9efe58f15dc1d3e003e4fc\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/502020\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Jordan Bayles \u003cjophba@google.com\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48595}\n\n    (cherry picked from commit bbd82081bd7ec1477b6db52319ec5a4ab8ffcbaa)\n\n    Bug: chromium:562605633,chromium:559350359\n    Change-Id: Id2463382532dac5a8b9efe58f15dc1d3e003e4fc\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504240\n    Auto-Submit: Chrome Cherry Picker \u003cchrome-cherry-picker@chops-service-accounts.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/branch-heads/8059@{#1}\n    Cr-Branched-From: 8d208e76fb1ad2b92d557f752e9d1d7d49059efa-refs/heads/main@{#48593}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/linux/wayland/shared_screencast_stream.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/linux/wayland/shared_screencast_stream.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/linux/wayland/shared_screencast_stream_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0071.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0072.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0124.patch"], "git_node": "4ad2eb15b14e85132e844ef6d46c1ece5b3b9299", "git_parents": ["69608153245d7430fc49f13889b87e78debf24c3"], "node": "7c64a9ad6b0c91cc62a220d5652d8cb4d392128e", "parents": ["135c9077e0b1ae5f657b6212e3a442abc4adee0f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790328408, "git_changesets": ["6de37f960413fd8ea1f060b3648384f35f56e09c", "278294c4a36e50fdf1c54e44ceba5ac76fab5e3b", "b53ff906ada770011535be68f7b8f2ea16f3c4aa", "2d5ff85b7f7605339a11c48670981d03b06a941f", "6a8d03d969fdd98a4dee8c91c1dcd677d3c9e352", "85556049619ac3aee1c982a4111c62adf25081ff", "a6601ada0c6e85863805ee2f59474ca32b8435c5", "7a9177a411e7bc0bf4cd178bc7409ec2d89b3355", "878e02ff4f4d06b73546f87088b1a1792508cdbe", "5c63b9893707acb60f72d304cc73ac5b4b100a00", "c06404708ae16b200f4c3788728fff8080136dd0", "c1c9299301f195fdef99427b8bd8f8cf15f8b0cb", "2019978ddf6cfa93eceaeb65205f76baa2ca46f2", "dee155a8d067244396fb1027a9c10bbc78c9b01e", "7f9922f957ae6ef76bc555d6863f6cab241b03e2", "a44b73b9bd75ee1292cd0dea5133be174f564baf", "f90b7c7fb3e4582980e91362f75a0605984af5ac", "46654f4e465a174f193cdfa1d0a568f87fa8fbcb", "f90abc6fcb922480d02c0f09562072b26a6b8821", "6ad046357eb617550b192927ab536f275940b415", "41bb465bec47c6cbb182420aced921482e51f3dc", "cad5a429caec6f75fae3781e4ff0ee2b489343da", "519edc2f4b982619691598b0bd31ccde86ffa35d", "142e993daaad216a00086ef75564cbdaf532d292", "587f386dcd6cc73146ea289f236c6ff44084f5c1", "449c2dc0f4948b4e3b1499915b1126455e45135d", "b43b283a562822598403e0219cbb141b0f84ef7b", "86a6c55245318def12768305b5cef2c43ec0726a", "bc999fb86ef8931a6dbc62f53fef7b1dccdd92aa", "253f9aff8893136f6fb18254cfbdba4137f21f2c", "64ac7d11606d2f151e136b805a8c239a8bbf91a3", "10df5ef7808c44592155d6ec88f4d1525c305609", "58ce4ebd29540869240b6dbf29b5eb9c77711d93", "76d33e16c201