44b4b1de2dff7ad09f7f0fbb95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moyin \u003cmadeyemi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075164 - Add the reader view audio icon to readerable pages r=android-reviewers,matt-tighe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328926\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/ui/icons/src/main/res/drawable/mozac_ic_reader_view_audio_24.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/BrowserToolbarMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/BrowserToolbarMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "eaeaa505d1e5132d151231805144748e96e92d2c", "git_parents": ["ac32bef27d4d40d800e7339d5a52fcb5322815f6"], "node": "5a23a5c734625b3414bdba64f82d22b4e8f983da", "parents": ["6c2505def16d58f3f0148510b338797e878c2a72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064404 - Accelerate early 'events' pings in FOG r=chumphreys,perftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nEnsure we keep the old behaviour for most tests as they might record\nmore than 20 events and then expect them not to have been submitted out\nfrom underneath them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326741\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/gtest/mozilla/GTestRunner.cpp", "testing/profiles/common/user.js", "testing/profiles/perf/user.js", "testing/profiles/raptor-android/user.js", "testing/profiles/reftest/user.js", "testing/profiles/unittest-required/user.js", "testing/profiles/xpcshell/user.js", "toolkit/components/glean/docs/dev/preferences.md", "toolkit/components/glean/src/init/mod.rs", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/test_metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/xpcshell/test_FOGInit.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/marionette/tests/client/test_fog_user_activity.py"], "git_node": "93ef04757019034db56d7bba2f6549467bc3372e", "git_parents": ["eaeaa505d1e5132d151231805144748e96e92d2c"], "node": "23929dc2b3e0e87ae3bee24ae7e07ee69c1cc6b0", "parents": ["5a23a5c734625b3414bdba64f82d22b4e8f983da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074282 - Load saved wallpapers directly from the wallpaper library. r=mconley\n\nNew Tab used to copy the active wallpaper out of the library and send thumbnail data to each page because the wallpaper URL could not load library files. Firefox 158 can load them directly, so this patch uses the saved files for both the active wallpaper and picker previews while keeping older URLs working when the library is off.\n\nThe picker now uses lazy loaded images instead of full size CSS backgrounds. In a 100 image test, memory use fell from 222 MB to 56.8 MB. Opening the picker also refreshes the library so pages restored from the startup cache show current images.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328628\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/Actions.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/Reducers.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/WallpaperCategories/WallpaperCategories.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/WallpaperCategories/_WallpaperCategories.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Wallpapers/WallpaperFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Wallpapers/WallpaperFileNames.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Wallpapers/WallpaperThemeUtils.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/WallpaperCategories/WallpaperCategories.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/Wallpapers/WallpaperThemeUtils.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_WallpaperFeed.js"], "git_node": "9fa8525e8c3c4c3250a079c8de2eb8c879aa82fa", "git_parents": ["93ef04757019034db56d7bba2f6549467bc3372e"], "node": "9de40db14b0d2c0f71abda0b8675bb016155c1c9", "parents": ["23929dc2b3e0e87ae3bee24ae7e07ee69c1cc6b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-hy-rAM/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-ia/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-in/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-tg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-hy-rAM/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-ia/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-in/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-tg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hy-rAM/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ia/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-in/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-nn-rNO/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-tg/strings.xml"], "git_node": "1df5a3e58a456167984d5bd40c4bb8b7876c2f4b", "git_parents": ["9fa8525e8c3c4c3250a079c8de2eb8c879aa82fa"], "node": "20a5717b1f0c74002f9df043a9aa8d211510396d", "parents": ["9de40db14b0d2c0f71abda0b8675bb016155c1c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cristian Tuns \u003cctuns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2050488 - Run WPT testharness with --processes=3 on bare-metal macOS aarch64 r=jgraham\" for causing wpt failures in mousemove-across.html\n\nThis reverts commit 19dddd19a195fa68b01a1e203ea7228b2cfa9b61.\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/scripts/web_platform_tests.py"], "git_node": "f4c58ce43f5cfc4ce4042d9e94be2142aadd1962", "git_parents": ["1df5a3e58a456167984d5bd40c4bb8b7876c2f4b"], "node": "175e0fd93dc3ecc1e20e107554da6a92948e94b7", "parents": ["20a5717b1f0c74002f9df043a9aa8d211510396d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helena \u003chballent@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2009747 - Patch 1 - Replace the deprecated NSSharingService enumeration with NSSharingServicePicker. r=mac-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,hjones,bradwerth,bolsson\n\n+[NSSharingService sharingServicesForItems:] is deprecated. We used it to list share providers so we could build them as XUL menuitems. We will replace it with NSSharingServicePicker, which is maintained by macOS and provides a sharing service interface consistent with apps across macOS. This patch also fixes Bug 1698581 for macOS to now support sharing for more than one tab.\n\nThe new native interface resulted in a few UI changes in Firefox menus:\n\n - The submenu no longer lists each installed macOS share provider. It now shows Copy Link, Create QR Code, and a single entry \"AirDrop, Messages, and More...\" that opens the native picker.\n - The \"More...\" entry that opened the Sharing pane of System Settings is gone. The native picker exposes the same providers directly.\n - Copy Link and Create QR Code lose their icons since we are working on removing all icons in context menus.\n - \"Generate QR Code...\" is relabelled \"Create QR Code\"\n - The BrowserUsageTelemetry id for a macOS share goes from \"share-macos-provider\" to \"macos-share-picker\", since Firefox no longer knows which provider the user picks.\n\nFurther details:\n\nWhen invoked, shareUrlWithPicker() anchors the native picker popover to a relevant DOM element.\n\nSharing more than one tab cannot be expressed as a URL, so multi-URL shares are handed to the picker as a MOZShareURLPasteboardItem, which advertise plain text and HTML representations covering every URL. This was the solution to enable as many sharing services as possible to share multiple URLs in a nice format. Single-URL shares still pass a plain NSURL so the share picker can display a webpage preview.\n\nThe xpcshell test covered getSharingProviders() and is removed with it. The new pasteboard writer is covered by TestMOZShareURLPasteboardItem.mm instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308393\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser_contextmenu_share_macosx.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-menubar/browser_file_share_macosx.js", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_share_tab_button_macosx.js", "browser/components/qrcode/test/browser/browser_qrcode_share_menu.js", "browser/components/sharing/SharingUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/menubar.ftl", "browser/modules/BrowserUsageTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "widget/cocoa/MOZShareURLPasteboardItem.h", "widget/cocoa/MOZShareURLPasteboardItem.mm", "widget/cocoa/moz.build", "widget/cocoa/nsMacSharingService.mm", "widget/nsIMacSharingService.idl", "widget/tests/gtest/TestMOZShareURLPasteboardItem.mm", "widget/tests/gtest/moz.build", "widget/tests/unit/test_macsharingservice.js", "widget/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "9387bb66c8d86356549dcf5277b6090332fe75c9", "git_parents": ["f4c58ce43f5cfc4ce4042d9e94be2142aadd1962"], "node": "e9159a34aed94025a874bba9ccf647f08d996f33", "parents": ["175e0fd93dc3ecc1e20e107554da6a92948e94b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helena \u003chballent@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2009747 - Patch 2 - Update the picker's Copy Link to support sharing multiple links. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nNSSharingServicePicker provides its own Copy Link entry via the private SHKCopyToPasteboardSharingService class. However, we want to have the copy feature for when multiple tabs are selected consistent with Firefox's \"Copy x Links\" functionality and label.\n\nThere is no API for replacing an entry provided by the system, and appending our own NSSharingService results in two Copy services. MacShareCopyOverride swizzles -title, -canPerformWithItems: and -performWithItems:, so the entry keeps its native appearance but takes its label and its action from Firefox.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325555\n", "files": ["browser/components/sharing/SharingUtils.sys.mjs", "widget/cocoa/moz.build", "widget/cocoa/nsMacSharingCopyOverride.h", "widget/cocoa/nsMacSharingCopyOverride.mm", "widget/cocoa/nsMacSharingService.mm", "widget/nsIMacSharingService.idl"], "git_node": "46401e316e65899987d845b3c053358de74f6455", "git_parents": ["9387bb66c8d86356549dcf5277b6090332fe75c9"], "node": "76c9fbd072ab3b3ce18d964e81b80db423a655ef", "parents": ["e9159a34aed94025a874bba9ccf647f08d996f33"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helena \u003chballent@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2009747 - Patch 3 - Replace the address bar context menu Share submenu with Share and Create QR Code items. r=Standard8,urlbar-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nOn macOS the strip-on-share item joins the share group rather than sitting under Copy, so the group is built as a single item set: Share..., Create QR Code and Copy Clean Link.\n\nAnchoring strip-on-share after the Create QR Code item would have required #initShareURL to run first. Building the group in one fragment avoids that ordering requirement. Both paths share the item creation and the enable/hide logic.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325556\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser_contextmenu_share_macosx.js", "browser/components/qrcode/test/browser/browser_qrcode_share_menu.js", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl"], "git_node": "73b615eabb462135b47b45d7932da265735d2d49", "git_parents": ["46401e316e65899987d845b3c053358de74f6455"], "node": "c851ee341713a17278e8fefc0b9623fdd2ad8a1a", "parents": ["76c9fbd072ab3b3ce18d964e81b80db423a655ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helena \u003chballent@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2009747 - Patch 4 - Open the macOS share picker directly from the share toolbar button. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nOn macOS the share toolbar button is a custom toolbar item which directly opens the native picker.\n\nCreate QR Code gets injected as a custom service. It previously was listed in the button's submenu but since the native share picker gets directly invoked, in order to keep the function, it now is integrated in the native picker. shareUrlWithPicker() gains a customItems array for this, and BuildCustomServices() turns each one into an NSSharingService prepended to the picker's list.\n\nThe button keeps the submenu on other platforms.\n\nThis is a separate commit due to the work to create a link share button in the URL bar (Bug 2052253), so this toolbar button might become redundant.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325557\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableWidgets.sys.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_share_tab_button_macosx.js", "browser/components/sharing/SharingUtils.sys.mjs", "widget/cocoa/nsMacSharingService.mm", "widget/nsIMacSharingService.idl"], "git_node": "d0e1bdea6b70bc052a48952ca0684d049ac51109", "git_parents": ["73b615eabb462135b47b45d7932da265735d2d49"], "node": "c53d57e6c8722c1f9941e986a0ce9d2b9e8b4212", "parents": ["c851ee341713a17278e8fefc0b9623fdd2ad8a1a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings tld-suffixes mobile-experiments ct-logs - r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329037\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/raw/initial_experiments.json", "netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-telemetry-v2.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": "3fcfa9b00f258d17a39d4c2546672b0b4faa7e73", "git_parents": ["d0e1bdea6b70bc052a48952ca0684d049ac51109"], "node": "2b57cb0cde861601d5a144c86670450d5a08cd46", "parents": ["c53d57e6c8722c1f9941e986a0ce9d2b9e8b4212"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075302 - Update gn to 6b0190f746976a2e3b26ed529a9d487ae2587868. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nNewer abseil BUILD.gn files set check_includes_strict, which gn only understands since bc381971. Chromium pins\n127dd2a6, but gn requires \u003cexpected\u003e since 152bfad2, which the gcc 11 libstdc++ in our toolchain sysroot does\nnot have; 6b0190f7 is the last revision before that.\n\ngn's default ninja target now includes a formatter check that needs Chromium's cipd, so build only the gn\nbinary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328901\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-gn-common.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-gn-win64.sh"], "git_node": "37690aff75bc4120c11955850207cc0c7581bd23", "git_parents": ["3fcfa9b00f258d17a39d4c2546672b0b4faa7e73"], "node": "f11ddfe6f5d1c7d12deeacfe1c19274be3c9ec57", "parents": ["2b57cb0cde861601d5a144c86670450d5a08cd46"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075302 - updated abseil-cpp patch stack. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328902\n", "files": ["third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0001.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0002.patch", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-