TW -\u003e 1039b110ae767298c6de1c7b9db320454525e3e6\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "955ae6887a13d95dfa7b87e30894c8107020c235", "git_parents": ["4441a72a16672ae2c332f85f3c1fa4ce8f6d4190"], "node": "72c7c4f8e2843920bcf5f22eb98b6001a3143549", "parents": ["1a8272dd874fd7de4ca8d4aca5592abc0918b2ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2075271, Bug 2075001, Bug 2066245, Bug 2074974, Bug 2066247, Bug 2066248, Bug 2066246, Bug 2066244, Bug 2066242, Bug 2066240, Bug 2066236 - Stub the widget market prefs in newtab for older hosts r=thecount\" for causing marionette integration tests failures at test_backup.py\n\nThis reverts commit 408c0488f50a1b35a56c6561cd2aeaf4695be52d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075001 - Add a pref to enforce widget market gating on Nightly r=reemhamz\"\n\nThis reverts commit 12ad59ecce8c86508b6b8851967e9b51d5ec5350.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2066245 - Make Crossword available to English locales outside PL, off by default r=reemhamz\"\n\nThis reverts commit fecc41615f94b337b45d1908a409a37a1219a435.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2074974 - Turn Recent Searches widget off by default for all regions r=reemhamz\"\n\nThis reverts commit afd16432c09ae7ddbe0a2bd3fafa0fab7461cbc6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2066247 - Turn Stocks widget off by default for all regions r=reemhamz\"\n\nThis reverts commit 8b80c4a136764a3cdce50e295a559cad6925f10c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2066248 - Turn Privacy widget off by default for all regions. r=maxx\"\n\nThis reverts commit 0cbf500520186d01291262fd4f5ab6205cc3eb64.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2066246 - Turn POTD widget off by default for US, DE, FR, PL regions. r=maxx\"\n\nThis reverts commit 176fb01597ffde3e24e4261a9678c81b5a59880a.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2066244 - Turn Clocks widget off by default for US, DE, FR, PL regions. r=maxx\"\n\nThis reverts commit c1b94c3b58ae7fe0e9c8c2724228da52724c85c4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2066242 - Turn FocusTimer off by default in US, DE, FR, PL regions. r=maxx\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1e425296589c495e41533e246244a1fd02b6a759.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2066240 - Turn the Lists widget off by default in the US, DE and FR, and block it in PL r=reemhamz\"\n\nThis reverts commit 541999fd5257fcfc7f82bef7d8479f0a46eabda1.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2066236 - Gate widget availability by market r=reemhamz\"\n\nThis reverts commit d3ae9c59045f125917f35515b7e8771560af3158.\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_discovery_card.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_side_by_side_layout.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRegistry.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/ActivityStream.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/PrefsFeed.test.js", "testing/profiles/common/user.js", "testing/profiles/xpcshell/user.js"], "git_node": "cde1460a5f303941aace04bb4cabdd5e0b29a5cb", "git_parents": ["955ae6887a13d95dfa7b87e30894c8107020c235"], "node": "d7b0d74331276109774666b7bd412f5b77e367d3", "parents": ["72c7c4f8e2843920bcf5f22eb98b6001a3143549"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2075192 - Convert verifyGeneralSettingsItemsTest regression UI test to the efficiency framework r=aaronmt\" for causing fenix lints failures at SettingsGeneralTest.kt\n\nThis reverts commit 1fed5644168475e7e703fc0a2148a39a10218613.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SettingsGeneralTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SettingsGeneralTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SettingsTest.kt"], "git_node": "b533878ba802dccd671b06de440a5f339ab1ed91", "git_parents": ["cde1460a5f303941aace04bb4cabdd5e0b29a5cb"], "node": "fb8c64b07b187a5f3606ca265b8653f418e2cbdf", "parents": ["d7b0d74331276109774666b7bd412f5b77e367d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074284 - Lint all xpcom headers through clang-tidy r=xpcom-reviewers,mccr8,emilio,ipc-reviewers\n\nChanges includes:\n- using C++20 type aliases and inline avriables\n- using nullptr where appropriate\n- using range-based loop where appropriate\n- making deleted methods public\n- making some methods default\n- use std::forward instead of std::move to prevent lifetime issues\n- avoid confusing constructor through universal references\n- rework some include dependencies to make header self contained\n\nTo break some circular dependencies, allow to break MOZ_COUNTED_DTOR_VIRTUAL(_type) into\nMOZ_COUNTED_DTOR_VIRTUAL_DECL(_type) and MOZ_COUNTED_DTOR_VIRTUAL_DEF(_type).\n\nAll changes were detected either by header compilation failure, or by\nclang-tidy.\n\nFixes are either generated by clang-tidy or hand-made\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327970\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/GeckoChildProcessHost.cpp", "toolkit/xre/nsSigHandlers.cpp", "xpcom/base/CodeAddressService.h", "xpcom/base/EnumeratedArrayCycleCollection.h", "xpcom/base/HoldDropJSObjects.h", "xpcom/base/Logging.h", "xpcom/base/OwningNonNull.h", "xpcom/base/RLBoxUtils.h", "xpcom/base/StaticLocalPtr.h", "xpcom/base/nsCOMPtr.h", "xpcom/base/nsCycleCollectionNoteChild.h", "xpcom/base/nsISupportsImpl.h", "xpcom/base/nsISupportsUtils.h", "xpcom/base/nsIWeakReferenceUtils.h", "xpcom/build/LateWriteChecks.cpp", "xpcom/build/LateWriteChecks.h", "xpcom/components/nsCategoryManagerUtils.h", "xpcom/components/nsComponentManagerUtils.h", "xpcom/ds/ArrayIterator.h", "xpcom/ds/CycleCollectedUniquePtr.h", "xpcom/ds/PerfectHash.h", "xpcom/ds/nsAtomTable.cpp", "xpcom/ds/nsTHashtable.h", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileUnix.h", "xpcom/io/nsPipe.h", "xpcom/ioutils/PathUtils.cpp", "xpcom/string/RustRegex.h", "xpcom/string/nsCharTraits.h", "xpcom/string/nsString.h", "xpcom/string/nsTDependentSubstring.h", "xpcom/string/nsTStringHasher.h", "xpcom/string/nsTSubstring.cpp", "xpcom/string/nsTSubstring.h", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestAvailableMemoryWatcherMac.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestAvailableMemoryWatcherWin.cpp", "xpcom/threads/CondVar.h", "xpcom/threads/DataMutex.h", "xpcom/threads/DeadlockDetector.h", "xpcom/threads/Monitor.h", "xpcom/threads/Mutex.h", "xpcom/threads/Queue.h", "xpcom/threads/RWLock.h", "xpcom/threads/RecursiveMutex.h", "xpcom/threads/ReentrantMonitor.h", "xpcom/threads/SpinEventLoopUntil.h", "xpcom/threads/StateMirroring.h", "xpcom/threads/StateWatching.h", "xpcom/threads/ThreadBound.h"], "git_node": "bd8b71b80f29e75128fb6a2deaa99743a76cf995", "git_parents": ["b533878ba802dccd671b06de440a5f339ab1ed91"], "node": "3d493c14177a5acea1b83429340f42b957cce41f", "parents": ["fb8c64b07b187a5f3606ca265b8653f418e2cbdf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073144 - Lint all dom/html headers through clang-tidy r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nActually make every header self-contained by moving some definition to\nsource file to break circular dependencies.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327968\n", "files": ["dom/html/EditContext.h", "dom/html/HTMLFormSubmission.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLFormSubmission.h", "dom/html/HTMLTableRowElement.h"], "git_node": "12ec1ec1e2beeddd07c160d49a9ea39c64a33f6b", "git_parents": ["bd8b71b80f29e75128fb6a2deaa99743a76cf995"], "node": "4d65ab6e849e8845ce8781620d842b6bd9e18b93", "parents": ["3d493c14177a5acea1b83429340f42b957cce41f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073482 - Lint all parser/ headers through clang-tidy r=hsivonen\n\nChanges includes:\n- making some methods default\n- use nullptr instead of 0\n- rework some include dependencies to make header self contained\n- use std::copy for type-safe alternative to memcpy\n\nAll changes were detected either by header compilation failure, or by\nclang-tidy.\n\nFixes are either generated by clang-tidy or hand-made.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327342\n", "files": ["parser/html/nsAHtml5TreeBuilderState.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5ArrayCopy.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5ByteReadable.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5StreamParserPtr.h", "parser/htmlaccel/htmlaccelNotInline.h"], "git_node": "c3e43bd65e5f96ed94cfa97e4bffc2f1f76b3839", "git_parents": ["12ec1ec1e2beeddd07c160d49a9ea39c64a33f6b"], "node": "a0a0c55cc45f267625ca45a92432a20ed8ac54b3", "parents": ["4d65ab6e849e8845ce8781620d842b6bd9e18b93"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elissa Cha \u003cecha@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067867 - Smart Window resume activity cards resume action r=pdahiya\n\n- wire up resume path to resume button + card\n- dismiss and menu actions should not trigger resume\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327129\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-resume-card/smartwindow-resume-card.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-resume-card/smartwindow-resume-card.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_resume_card.js"], "git_node": "76d0919f41bae35071d6f6adfc23d502a9a0a014", "git_parents": ["c3e43bd65e5f96ed94cfa97e4bffc2f1f76b3839"], "node": "96f6e917d6b6afbe1f42a90b20b6c54d44732538", "parents": ["a0a0c55cc45f267625ca45a92432a20ed8ac54b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Osmond Arnesto \u003coarnesto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1998241 - Update moz-page-nav HCM colors r=desktop-theme-reviewers,akulyk,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321758\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/moz-page-nav/moz-page-nav.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-page-nav/moz-page-nav.tokens.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/nova-export-clean-variables.json"], "git_node": "51c733b272600550ff7dfdf5dd0898508923514a", "git_parents": ["76d0919f41bae35071d6f6adfc23d502a9a0a014"], "node": "81598d1d650eb59f2c20d9324aecc5e22fc26824", "parents": ["96f6e917d6b6afbe1f42a90b20b6c54d44732538"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074185 [wpt PR 62837] - Don't use FocusTrigger::kUserGesture when handling untrusted key events., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon't use FocusTrigger::kUserGesture when handling untrusted key events.\n\nThis makes menu elements stop using EventHandler::IsHandlingKeyEvent()\nand instead make decisions based on the event we're actually handling.\n\nFixed: 553335083\nChange-Id: Ie574a5595c9d476387ef3bcfa77a7244b00c83c0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8427363\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1701919}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 049bcc5717d2c82747c10e4ac8faae9b2d790255\nwpt-pr: 62837\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/focus-without-user-activation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/resources/focus-without-user-activation-helper.html"], "git_node": "56ed92a3e26d7157658c0306b60f449dade0c36d", "git_parents": ["51c733b272600550ff7dfdf5dd0898508923514a"], "node": "2693c380b6e79eb967101fe31109311e2f2bd5b9", "parents": ["81598d1d650eb59f2c20d9324aecc5e22fc26824"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074185 [wpt PR 62837] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62837\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/focus-without-user-activation.html.ini"], "git_node": "9c22ccc254ef47d86466b47e090e201add782e9f", "git_parents": ["56ed92a3e26d7157658c0306b60f449dade0c36d"], "node": "c36879723aafe1bdc3052aca8edf5acf1c6b748a", "parents": ["2693c380b6e79eb967101fe31109311e2f2bd5b9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074290 [wpt PR 62840] - [css] Move scroll-snap-type: pair tests to WPT, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css] Move scroll-snap-type: pair tests to WPT\n\nMove scroll-snap-type: pair tests into the standard external WPT\ndirectory structure:\n\n- Move pair/scroll-snap-type-pair.tentative.html into\n  parsing/scroll-snap-type-pair.html and remove the pair/ directory.\n- Move wpt_internal/css/css-scroll-snap/snap-pair-01..07.html to\n  external/wpt/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-001..007.html.\n- Update FlagExpectations/surface-embed to match the new path.\n\nBug: 542706103\nChange-Id: I27dfd9aa007edc616a97dbe96ec7fa55aa719f1c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8427845\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1701979}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d6bcfb4bff319a88051b0bd50afa12a83169d061\nwpt-pr: 62840\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/pair/scroll-snap-type-pair.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/parsing/scroll-snap-type-pair.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-007.html"], "git_node": "b012109f449d4cb540093d7ea76a5be186988eda", "git_parents": ["9c22ccc254ef47d86466b47e090e201add782e9f"], "node": "4eb9d0e0bbd905a33793df879be4f445db214327", "parents": ["c36879723aafe1bdc3052aca8edf5acf1c6b748a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074290 [wpt PR 62840] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62840\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/pair/scroll-snap-type-pair.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/parsing/scroll-snap-type-pair.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-007.html.ini"], "git_node": "29269e0bb9268980dc9c83aedadfcc0b1ec4ac20", "git_parents": ["b012109f449d4cb540093d7ea76a5be186988eda"], "node": "9c385fcdef0d3fdf9607e219baf14c927ad15410", "parents": ["4eb9d0e0bbd905a33793df879be4f445db214327"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074256 [wpt PR 62839] - Minimize antialiasing diff in ttwf-css-3d-polygon-cycle WPT, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMinimize antialiasing diff in ttwf-css-3d-polygon-cycle WPT\n\nThough passing on many platforms, this test historically fails on\nWindows by just a little more than the fuzzy allowance, though the\nunderlying functionality is still behaving correctly. This change\nupdates the -ref file to position the angled blue portion using the same\ntransform path as the main file, better aligning the antialiasing\nbetween the two. It also increases the size of one of the 2 blue\nsections so that they overlap slightly, eliminating antialiasing for\nthat edge. This does not detract from the target of this test, which is\nvalidating the overlap ordering.\n\nIn local runs of this change it reduced the max channel diff from 174 to\n41, and total pixels diff from 349 to 218, which is now below the\nexisting fuzzy thresholds on the test page.\n\nBug: None\nChange-Id: I516f4c752c3b462e6f18e0da6efb1fe8b4a94119\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8426074\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702054}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 34cfec8be4420b39fd7845691b7841a0998074a6\nwpt-pr: 62839\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transforms/reference/ttwf-css-3d-polygon-cycle-ref.html"], "git_node": "25ef6db3fc19b39b01b4afd6a8f68f5e47fb118e", "git_parents": ["29269e0bb9268980dc9c83aedadfcc0b1ec4ac20"], "node": "819deedc2f3ee95a63ed972e66d5ac4d5d631de8", "parents": ["9c385fcdef0d3fdf9607e219baf14c927ad15410"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074256 [wpt PR 62839] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62839\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-transforms/ttwf-css-3d-polygon-cycle.html.ini"], "git_node": "59fca16bc330e124042d57445c961d01032915ed", "git_parents": ["25ef6db3fc19b39b01b4afd6a8f68f5e47fb118e"], "node": "e29e370b5a86f0e2181cfe54af00d11eb719265d", "parents": ["819deedc2f3ee95a63ed972e66d5ac4d5d631de8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074253 [wpt PR 62838] - Fix table markup in WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix table markup in WPTs\n\nFix mismatched row-group closing tags in table-row-group-height.html and\nits reference, explicitly close the divs in td-box-sizing-001.html, and\nrepair the malformed and unclosed \u003cx\u003e elements in\nsynthesized-baseline-table-cell-001-ref.html.\n\nThese changes preserve the intended layout. html5lib produces an\nidentical tree for td-box-sizing-001.html. The row-group files differ\nonly in whitespace-only text nodes, while the baseline reference loses\nthe bogus \"\u003c\" and \"td\" attributes introduced by its malformed start\ntags.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: Id4aeb26c29b02a5febc4e0e1a0c9c7640c866930\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8225584\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Jacques Newman \u003cjanewman@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Jacques Newman \u003cjanewman@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702135}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 32b394049c9f67f8dc1d15d6ad7760e883bb0996\nwpt-pr: 62838\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/baseline-rules/synthesized-baseline-table-cell-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-tables/tentative/td-box-sizing-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/tables/table-row-group-height-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/tables/table-row-group-height.html"], "git_node": "6f98e2668e6fb187f170f02477cc256919be6651", "git_parents": ["59fca16bc330e124042d57445c961d01032915ed"], "node": "e2d6596375ef230df51e5af599b70a4f55f6c02b", "parents": ["e29e370b5a86f0e2181cfe54af00d11eb719265d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Reeves \u003cmichael.reeves077@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073693 [wpt PR 62801] - Blink: Select aligned snap targets in flat tree order, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBlink: Select aligned snap targets in flat tree order\n\nWhen multiple snap areas align at the same position, CSS Scroll Snap\nremoves ancestor areas and selects the first remaining area in tree\norder. Blink ordered areas by DOM layout preorder and inferred ancestry\nfrom rectangle containment. This could repeatedly select a later slotted\nsibling.\n\nOrder snap areas by flat tree position and pass each area's nearest\nsnap-area ancestor to cc. This distinguishes descendants from\ngeometrically contained siblings and fixes the WPT.\n\nBug: 543919183\nChange-Id: I3576b3fba8c67367cf984e94cdbb0dc2ba32e2e3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8238951\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702141}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a825bd10bdd8f794b204db56bc9479cc0f4c46e2\nwpt-pr: 62801\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/snap-after-relayout/multiple-aligned-targets/prefer-tree-order-over-geometric-containment.html"], "git_node": "29f5f93a74a8ea84b51e61d4ce02f415c1737ca1", "git_parents": ["6f98e2668e6fb187f170f02477cc256919be6651"], "node": "de942a8b2f062b8a39d5d8e13291c52b46e9c5a9", "parents": ["e2d6596375ef230df51e5af599b70a4f55f6c02b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074332 [wpt PR 62846] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324094, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324094 (#62846)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 14ae828f98dae429c9eab02d04854db2b7d2f8d6\nwpt-pr: 62846\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/IndexedDB/resources/transaction-inflight-worker-terminate-worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/IndexedDB/transaction-inflight-worker-terminate.window.js"], "git_node": "e757e8505848866c55ab7ee02ff9ba9132192cb3", "git_parents": ["29f5f93a74a8ea84b51e61d4ce02f415c1737ca1"], "node": "48dc1fb82abedfde48de3b37cdac92cbff650f29", "parents": ["de942a8b2f062b8a39d5d8e13291c52b46e9c5a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074343 [wpt PR 62847] - Fix flaky external/wpt/jpegxl/svg-image-element.html load-event race, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix flaky external/wpt/jpegxl/svg-image-element.html load-event race\n\nSVGImageElement has no \"complete\" attribute, so the listener attached in\nthe script after the markup could miss the 'load' event entirely; hook\nthe promise up via onload/onerror content attributes instead, which are\nregistered while the start tag is parsed, and drop the suppression.\n\nBug: 564516456\nChange-Id: I5c2bfef8dc4fcfe4422b1d8fc72e67d4d26e7cb8\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8437175\nCommit-Queue: Luca Versari \u003cveluca@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Luca Versari \u003cveluca@google.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702369}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 96e34c03675d509de3e54a4d871063412eba72fa\nwpt-pr: 62847\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/svg-image-element.html"], "git_node": "abc7d23774917379c5c2a6f92dd6adb9354eb2f2", "git_parents": ["e757e8505848866c55ab7ee02ff9ba9132192cb3"], "node": "f9f3652aab0eba6b5d49ffd21d7862dd62c14508", "parents": ["48dc1fb82abedfde48de3b37cdac92cbff650f29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074343 [wpt PR 62847] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62847\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/jpegxl/custom-primaries-icc-overflow-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "7cd090a92b8aeb001cdfe7a640dcf063f6158482", "git_parents": ["abc7d23774917379c5c2a6f92dd6adb9354eb2f2"], "node": "d5e60dea5829fa3b36850998728d7dd4bba69b96", "parents": ["f9f3652aab0eba6b5d49ffd21d7862dd62c14508"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rob Buis \u003crbuis@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074109 [wpt PR 62830] - block-ellipsis-025-ref.html should have no line-clamp, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nblock-ellipsis-025-ref.html should have no line-clamp (#62830)\n\nblock-ellipsis-025-ref.html should have no line-clamp, otherwise\nwe end up with a \"double ellipsis\" on the fully truncated last line.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 63fe1d876b6013e03fad520da3d84c5b21a75eac\nwpt-pr: 62830\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/block-ellipsis-025-ref.html"], "git_node": "3a5396d063d42542c58714706ff98bf9156e0e1a", "git_parents": ["7cd090a92b8aeb001cdfe7a640dcf063f6158482"], "node": "c448a17903536869c117a8ae4c117841a6061995", "parents": ["d5e60dea5829fa3b36850998728d7dd4bba69b96"], "tags": []}, {"author": "taher \u003c8665427+nullhook@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074426 [wpt PR 62430] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323237, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323237 (#62430)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a8e9d68758e0b68bcf617aa5b7901dd7375bc63e\nwpt-pr: 62430\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-currentcolor.tentativ