reply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074439 [wpt PR 62856] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324359, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324359 (#62856)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: eabd8786c67cb75a38fe06ad8f54a9ea9457a001\nwpt-pr: 62856\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-invalid-typed-value-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-invalid-typed-value.html"], "git_node": "c5e2488441218dbbde6e91026b701318431e3687", "git_parents": ["8922b4fe3b849b9d8e43f90a7a488a4f7905d3bf"], "node": "8e2f31ebce2e17e626b6971802699c2be0f6bede", "parents": ["a16d194b96148176ec90704d875ff536439ebcae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074439 [wpt PR 62856] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62856\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-invalid-typed-value.html.ini"], "git_node": "5f1a4a75d278791e4c9aec85755c3eef8ff296fb", "git_parents": ["c5e2488441218dbbde6e91026b701318431e3687"], "node": "dca6044a5b6573e524c9408f8b1673a6d481fe32", "parents": ["8e2f31ebce2e17e626b6971802699c2be0f6bede"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073761 [wpt PR 62773] - [AI WPTs] Standardize concurrent execution WPTs across Web AI APIs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[AI WPTs] Standardize concurrent execution WPTs across Web AI APIs (#62773)\n\nAdd dedicated *-concurrent and *-streaming-concurrent WPTs across\nWeb AI APIs, testing both identical and divergent inputs. Streaming\ntests properly drain ReadableStreams, and relevant test expectations\nare updated accordingly.\n\nFixed: 562173369\nChange-Id: I8865e933575d2f693035ab4c27b05c0ece058f29\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8415319\nAuto-Submit: Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike Wasserman \u003cmsw@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1701242}\n\nCo-authored-by: Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6801a359812f4e26ec60e5457379ccc865574533\nwpt-pr: 62773\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/ai/language-model/prompt/prompt-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/language-model/prompt/streaming/prompt-streaming-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/language_detection/language-detector-detect-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/proofreader/proofreader-proofread-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/proofreader/proofreader-proofread.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/resources/util.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/rewriter/rewriter-rewrite-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/rewriter/rewriter-rewrite-streaming-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/rewriter/rewriter-rewrite-streaming.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/rewriter/rewriter-rewrite.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/summarizer/summarizer-summarize-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/summarizer/summarizer-summarize-streaming-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/summarizer/summarizer-summarize-streaming.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/translator/translator-translate-concurrent.optional.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/translator/translator-translate-streaming-concurrent.optional.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/writer/writer-write-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/writer/writer-write-streaming-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/writer/writer-write-streaming.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/writer/writer-write.tentative.https.window.js"], "git_node": "e4268f9b7c2f71bb86fde73ecf1e13d8d0c9ba6c", "git_parents": ["5f1a4a75d278791e4c9aec85755c3eef8ff296fb"], "node": "3e79569b379ea6cfe2b510f3b8b3da1e7ecc5d43", "parents": ["dca6044a5b6573e524c9408f8b1673a6d481fe32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073761 [wpt PR 62773] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62773\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/ai/language-model/prompt/prompt-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/language-model/prompt/streaming/prompt-streaming-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/language_detection/language-detector-detect-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/proofreader/proofreader-proofread-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/rewriter/rewriter-rewrite-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/rewriter/rewriter-rewrite-streaming-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/summarizer/summarizer-summarize-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/summarizer/summarizer-summarize-streaming-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/translator/translator-translate-concurrent.optional.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/translator/translator-translate-streaming-concurrent.optional.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/writer/writer-write-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/ai/writer/writer-write-streaming-concurrent.tentative.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "c77d04d297e762bf5d84dc5b816b4d4048eeda99", "git_parents": ["e4268f9b7c2f71bb86fde73ecf1e13d8d0c9ba6c"], "node": "4071d08485ec1a6ca44a342119f2bd81631292b1", "parents": ["3e79569b379ea6cfe2b510f3b8b3da1e7ecc5d43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Evan Liu \u003cevliu@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073680 [wpt PR 62800] - Web Speech API: Require sticky activation for relaxed model downloads, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWeb Speech API: Require sticky activation for relaxed model downloads\n\nSpeechRecognition.install() currently requires no user activation when\nthe browser reports that a language pack is downloadable without a\ngesture (e.g. origin has microphone permission and language is in\nAccept-Language). Require sticky activation in that case, gated by the\nkOnDeviceWebSpeechRequiresStickyActivation kill switch, while still\nrequiring and consuming transient activation for unrelaxed downloads.\nAlso replace Accessibility.WebSpeech.DownloadRelaxed with\nDownloadActivationOutcome to record the observed activation state.\n\nOBSOLETE_HISTOGRAM[Accessibility.WebSpeech.DownloadRelaxed]=Replaced by Accessibility.WebSpeech.DownloadActivationOutcome, which distinguishes requests rejected for lack of a user gesture from requests rejected for lack of sticky activation.\n\nFixed: 559063678\nChange-Id: I698d06b9c470b6066993b9432112179ab47a3a9d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8407893\nReviewed-by: Elias Klim \u003celklm@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Frank Liberato \u003cliberato@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Evan Liu \u003cevliu@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mustafa Emre Acer \u003cmeacer@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1701041}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4e18f82983d1adae67988215422a5e20d854407c\nwpt-pr: 62800\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/speech-api/SpeechRecognition-installOnDevice.https.html"], "git_node": "21e74332c86a81b7dc087e565bf108d11d4ea0bf", "git_parents": ["c77d04d297e762bf5d84dc5b816b4d4048eeda99"], "node": "b2f81077bdbbea2f9bb721bb4cdc451068ba169f", "parents": ["4071d08485ec1a6ca44a342119f2bd81631292b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074687 [wpt PR 62868] - Apply position-area to \u003cmenulist\u003e by default., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nApply position-area to \u003cmenulist\u003e by default.\n\nRather than applying position-area to \u003cmenulist\u003e only when it's anchored\nto a menulist or menubar, apply it by default (so the styles apply to\nmenulists anchored to buttons too) and then override for the menubar\ncase.\n\nBug: 406566432\nChange-Id: I965fad8308abd24e02f6f30aa582d981d00b6ca1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8415229\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702760}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1557dd863933d004a98745d5f8cae22b5d67fe78\nwpt-pr: 62868\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-from-button-default-style-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-from-button-default-style.html"], "git_node": "afdb302d9d5156374012fef6fb3432bb2e27b897", "git_parents": ["21e74332c86a81b7dc087e565bf108d11d4ea0bf"], "node": "afb0e48e9000ecc7d739d25c4894d1d7366d7864", "parents": ["b2f81077bdbbea2f9bb721bb4cdc451068ba169f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074687 [wpt PR 62868] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62868\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-from-button-default-style.html.ini"], "git_node": "8429ae5637b472aa17857bb3fba450cc8b746237", "git_parents": ["afdb302d9d5156374012fef6fb3432bb2e27b897"], "node": "115ea115f519a2edd3eaa845e9ba159b782ea695", "parents": ["afb0e48e9000ecc7d739d25c4894d1d7366d7864"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074781 [wpt PR 62874] - Reduce WPT flakiness for CSS-based images, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReduce WPT flakiness for CSS-based images\n\nThese tests are passing the vast majority of the time, but still failing\nwith some regularity due to a race between the image being loaded and\nthe framework capturing the rendered pixels. This change eliminates that\nrace by adding preloads and explicitly having the test wait for them.\n\nAn earlier change for page-background-image-print (crrev.com/c/8334591)\nfound the preload alone was enough to remove the flakiness, but further\ninvestigation into tests failing a greater percentage of the time (e.g.\npage-background-005-print) found the preload was only a partial fix, and\ncorrected my previous misunderstanding that the test harness waited for\npreloads automatically.\n\nEfforts to fix this broadly at the harness level instead are tracked by\ncrbug.com/564820079\n\nBug: None\nChange-Id: Idfbbcb1d5298072b64f1903f518704f9c00482e5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8433968\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702812}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4c633507269f9c2eb26e315c70e8a9de4b02670c\nwpt-pr: 62874\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-page/background-image-only-for-print.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-page/margin-boxes/background-001-print.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-page/margin-boxes/content-003-print.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-page/page-background-005-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-page/page-background-005-print.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-page/page-background-image-print.html"], "git_node": "7b488480abc74a6ef2128f2ca110f3c543fe7dd1", "git_parents": ["8429ae5637b472aa17857bb3fba450cc8b746237"], "node": "a23fa7b4dcdefab31ab530d518d59f6cc771f76d", "parents": ["115ea115f519a2edd3eaa845e9ba159b782ea695"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074808 [wpt PR 62877] - Resume deferred media when loading attribute changes to eager, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nResume deferred media when loading attribute changes to eager\n\nThe loading attribute's missing and invalid value defaults are both the\nEager state, so removing the attribute or setting it to a bogus value\nmust run the lazy load resumption steps, not just the literal \"eager\".\n\nBug: 564285979\nChange-Id: I9a42f22e44a93f6d8c7df4769baabc36c6dac57d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8438396\nReviewed-by: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702866}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 57ce061de08c858fcf63584d2d150c38f35c6762\nwpt-pr: 62877\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-resume-on-loading-attribute-change.html"], "git_node": "90635e74a47384747be337ba143a93749ded9058", "git_parents": ["7b488480abc74a6ef2128f2ca110f3c543fe7dd1"], "node": "3d418111b40566520cefb07d6cab549d883e4a76", "parents": ["a23fa7b4dcdefab31ab530d518d59f6cc771f76d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074808 [wpt PR 62877] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62877\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-resume-on-loading-attribute-change.html.ini"], "git_node": "1b0c829476d1721600f35952dcd8e1dfe34d0754", "git_parents": ["90635e74a47384747be337ba143a93749ded9058"], "node": "18ff93507448ed3de8e30faca87cb94e8ec5cd4a", "parents": ["3d418111b40566520cefb07d6cab549d883e4a76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074809 [wpt PR 62883] - Fire scrollend event after layout scroll clamping and anchoring, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFire scrollend event after layout scroll clamping and anchoring\n\nWhen layout changes cause scroll clamping or anchoring adjustments,\nBlink enqueues a scroll event via LocalFrameView::scroll_event_queue_\nbut previously omitted the corresponding scrollend event.\n\nThis patch updates LocalFrameView::EnqueueScrollEvents() to enqueue\na scrollend event when a scroll event was dispatched, provided there\nis no running animation and the container is not currently latched\nfor a gesture scroll.\n\nBug: 482681552\nChange-Id: I7b35c36ebd3a3ad2597276d086271226badb3458\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8428159\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David A \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702934}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e0bcfcb6ec1d0348db4d95cf9f2e3a2d68c6cf6a\nwpt-pr: 62883\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/events/scrolling/scrollend-event-fired-after-layout-clamping.html"], "git_node": "1b9c3a50464a84517b322a41e65e962680267de9", "git_parents": ["1b0c829476d1721600f35952dcd8e1dfe34d0754"], "node": "229c1da9697d793c1cf730e3735f8aedd1adf259", "parents": ["18ff93507448ed3de8e30faca87cb94e8ec5cd4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lia Hiscock \u003cliahiscock@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074810 [wpt PR 62876] - [WebInstallAPI] Resolve relative manifest IDs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebInstallAPI] Resolve relative manifest IDs\n\nResolve manifest IDs against the document base URL for both\nnavigator.install() and the \u003cinstall\u003e element. Trim surrounding HTML\nwhitespace before resolution.\n\nFor \u003cinstall\u003e specifically, only attempt current document install if\nboth attributes are absent (previously, present but empty attributes\nalso qualified).\n\nBug: 397043069, 469801429, 333795265\nChange-Id: Ic418731be269fa8de63a16ab82181cdd7143d2f2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8384777\nReviewed-by: Lu Huang \u003cluhua@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Lia Hiscock \u003cliahiscock@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Daniel Murphy \u003cdmurph@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike West \u003cmkwst@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703014}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2471231e7d9f02bc02feffce8dcd70badd18aed3\nwpt-pr: 62876\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/install/install-element-invalid-targets.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/install/install-element-url-attributes.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-install/navigator-install-bad-inputs.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "524a4f149b729273b80afa145b436a37cd023560", "git_parents": ["1b9c3a50464a84517b322a41e65e962680267de9"], "node": "06c868f2b7188a69233b1ceb32aa55bdbb919f54", "parents": ["229c1da9697d793c1cf730e3735f8aedd1adf259"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074810 [wpt PR 62876] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62876\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/install/install-element-invalid-targets.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/install/install-element-url-attributes.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-install/navigator-install-bad-inputs.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "6bc969aad1e97eb3da7973cd2fe69a7b2f23c70c", "git_parents": ["524a4f149b729273b80afa145b436a37cd023560"], "node": "3d748014ce41dfaad53d1ff8ce21fc5c41fcd934", "parents": ["06c868f2b7188a69233b1ceb32aa55bdbb919f54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074833 [wpt PR 62885] - [focus-without-user-activation] Test click-handler attribution, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[focus-without-user-activation] Test click-handler attribution\n\nAdd tentative WPT coverage for a denied same-origin window invoking\nclick() on a button in an allowed window. A handler defined in the\nallowed window can focus its own control, whereas a handler defined in\nthe denied window cannot borrow the button owner's focus permission.\n\nCheck that the denied window's direct focus call is blocked, neither\ntested window has focus or transient activation, and the synthetic click\ndoes not grant activation. Use a third auxiliary window to park focus.\n\nThe test is tentative while initiator attribution is being specified:\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12032\n\nBug: 40095111\nChange-Id: I9180d6a51da5a0630db9d971d9cde98ba78e9492\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8428383\nReviewed-by: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703044}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6f4e01f9ed56dc31e6991f8f301f0f138386b640\nwpt-pr: 62885\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/experimental-features/focus-without-user-activation-click-handler.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/experimental-features/resources/focus-without-user-activation-click-handler.html"], "git_node": "1799b0a698306a9a97808fed9699fccdf54e8d7d", "git_parents": ["6bc969aad1e97eb3da7973cd2fe69a7b2f23c70c"], "node": "13e8d0a68e1fd12e89281c15ffcb06293c2738e8", "parents": ["3d748014ce41dfaad53d1ff8ce21fc5c41fcd934"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074833 [wpt PR 62885] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62885\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/experimental-features/focus-without-user-activation-click-handler.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "119a26de9ed2ec68bd383b8578afe27857bca777", "git_parents": ["1799b0a698306a9a97808fed9699fccdf54e8d7d"], "node": "e6629ff0d1116febb514f768035aab92cdcb11f0", "parents": ["13e8d0a68e1fd12e89281c15ffcb06293c2738e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074834 [wpt PR 62884] - Preserve negative timestamps in AudioDiscardHelper, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPreserve negative timestamps in AudioDiscardHelper\n\nUpdate AudioDiscardHelper to preserve negative initial timestamps\ninstead of clamping them to zero. As initial pre-skip frames and front\ndiscard padding are removed from buffers starting with negative\ntimestamps, AudioDiscardHelper advances timestamp_helper_ forward\naccordingly.\n\nFor Opus decoding via FFmpeg, clamp initial negative timestamps to zero\nin FFmpegAudioDecoder when decoder delay discarding is active to avoid\nduplicate pre-roll sample trimming.\n\nAdd unit tests in AudioDiscardHelperTest covering negative timestamp\nhandling across decoder delay reset, initial pre-skip discard, and front\ndiscard padding. Remove obsolete WebCodecs failure expectations for\ncodecs where negative timestamp decoding tests now pass.\n\nBug: 512772321\nChange-Id: I67e6cb5ec655f2cc4c4391da0d07762ef67c9013\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8103062\nReviewed-by: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703084}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0492d85bd92e39e6e36c717d31da95384c5eba09\nwpt-pr: 62884\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/audioDecoder-codec-specific.https.any.js"], "git_node": "224872fa851704c9810d9ec9a74aad10656c7d66", "git_parents": ["119a26de9ed2ec68bd383b8578afe27857bca777"], "node": "eaf5e73793ceeb48a4ca839ff1281244ced58ab0", "parents": ["e6629ff0d1116febb514f768035aab92cdcb11f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074834 [wpt PR 62884] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62884\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/audioDecoder-codec-specific.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "b721e07af92b253362ca9ef6147ddce657f9ace2", "git_parents": ["224872fa851704c9810d9ec9a74aad10656c7d66"], "node": "d3fbf6a25c18f7a2bbfc7cc4e06b4627238333cb", "parents": ["eaf5e73793ceeb48a4ca839ff1281244ced58ab0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Minseong Kim \u003cjja08111@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074837 [wpt PR 62886] - [css-overflow] Add WPTs text-overflow string with line-clamp and BiDi, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-overflow] Add WPTs text-overflow string with line-clamp and BiDi\n\nThis CL adds WPT coverage for mixed-direction markers, plaintext\nparagraph directions, neutral character isolation, and logical\ntruncation for text-overflow and line-clamp.\n\nThe failures on the other browsers are:\n- Firefox: All tests due to suppressed text-overflow markers inside\n  clamp containers:\n  https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2057345\n- Safari: *-006, *-009, due to plaintext paragraph direction\n  handling, and *-007 due to:\n  https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10844.\n\nBug: 40336192, 41492459\nChange-Id: Iafbed30cc79dbc2ebb22c1e679d811d2d05e3a84\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8439836\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Andreu Botella \u003cabotella@igalia.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Minseong Kim \u003cjja08111@gmail.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703133}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 289f7de340d6999d086956d2a8074a1e576bbd13\nwpt-pr: 62886\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-009.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-007-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-008-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-text-overflow-string-009-ref.html"], "git_node": "68bf7c11b80da353e974885d64449777def4dd11", "git_parents": ["b721e07af92b