 Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068913 - Let PushService ignore new push messages r=saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326875\n", "files": ["dom/push/PushComponents.sys.mjs", "dom/push/PushService.sys.mjs", "dom/push/PushServiceWebSocket.sys.mjs", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/test_notification_ignore.js", "dom/push/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "25a0c0534d7a259be5e45016daeb4a428ca1d326", "git_parents": ["a4cea56cb89cbc56e5833f20639f77398840f89a"], "node": "61717a510ea6bb43b71c2cf147e178488d8390f2", "parents": ["449dec47b71eb023f69919d97f44408013fb2bb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068913 - Wait for the service worker to finish a push message before exiting r=saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323645\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/push/PushCommandLineHandler.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/push/test/browser/browser_receive_push_messages.js"], "git_node": "f9ed9b763f27d50d8d9d365aa8f445cdb198c2ed", "git_parents": ["25a0c0534d7a259be5e45016daeb4a428ca1d326"], "node": "fb78127f2b86e1c68e9dd7b7cb09bdf5faead667", "parents": ["61717a510ea6bb43b71c2cf147e178488d8390f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075059 - Prevent infinite recursion in row subgrid intrinsic sizing. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nI wonder a bit whether the UsedTrackSizes() stuff can go wrong / be\nstale, but I think we need to go through the parent grid so it's\nprobably fine, other code from here also looks at that property.\n\nThis only fixes the immediate problem, I realized there are some\nother issues with intrinsic sizing of row subgrids where we don't\nmatch the spec, but they're harder to fix, see bug 2075211.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328826\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/subgrid/crashtests/nested-row-subgrids-intrinsic-sizing.html"], "git_node": "a8b0f885190c6d2085d264e1b6e121109be2a740", "git_parents": ["f9ed9b763f27d50d8d9d365aa8f445cdb198c2ed"], "node": "12d2f13f4b47319c689f633e53a6fa080f4ef648", "parents": ["fb78127f2b86e1c68e9dd7b7cb09bdf5faead667"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075211 - Improve stretch handling during intrinsic sizing. r=dholbert,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nThis will be used to implement the intrinsic sizing of grid items\nproperly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328827\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "layout/generic/WritingModes.h", "layout/generic/nsContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsFlexContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.h", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": "3778fb6f62a08b24eed4376d28d422d5a8ea69e2", "git_parents": ["a8b0f885190c6d2085d264e1b6e121109be2a740"], "node": "b5368637bc81a0a91942f8b0b20bce580372b2a2", "parents": ["12d2f13f4b47319c689f633e53a6fa080f4ef648"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075211 - Improve stretch handling further. r=dholbert,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nAfter the previous patch, most callers do have the right values to\nhandle stretch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328828\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.h", "layout/tables/BasicTableLayoutStrategy.cpp"], "git_node": "89f8ff6232b68972ad6029c06fa37eae8c2988e2", "git_parents": ["3778fb6f62a08b24eed4376d28d422d5a8ea69e2"], "node": "63c9136e6658b3501b5ffb87ea2fa1cb48893402", "parents": ["b5368637bc81a0a91942f8b0b20bce580372b2a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075211 - Plumb border-padding + margin instead of content-to-box-sizing through ComputeISizeValue(). r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nThis removes quite a few stretch special cases.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328829\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ReflowInput.cpp", "layout/generic/ReflowInput.h", "layout/generic/nsContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.h", "layout/tables/BasicTableLayoutStrategy.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/stretch/stretch-block-size-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/stretch/stretch-inline-size-003.html.ini"], "git_node": "692e4d4a550ec2c07ec58b47efcd57106a6cbc72", "git_parents": ["89f8ff6232b68972ad6029c06fa37eae8c2988e2"], "node": "c98d2438c46f6a2f60bdf2b7f2b53c47ede2454c", "parents": ["63c9136e6658b3501b5ffb87ea2fa1cb48893402"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075211: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h"], "git_node": "8ba955940ec4a5a53a351f05a9c37dc22b2f1a3c", "git_parents": ["692e4d4a550ec2c07ec58b47efcd57106a6cbc72"], "node": "ea3db7a6f9ab9c212fa0d3a5c44487c3b0232df2", "parents": ["c98d2438c46f6a2f60bdf2b7f2b53c47ede2454c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063781 - Implement dismissal for top site results r=adw,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324220\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderTopSites.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarProviderTopSites.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl"], "git_node": "26afb79bb8a9b7722fb7fac803334c294b7f2ecf", "git_parents": ["8ba955940ec4a5a53a351f05a9c37dc22b2f1a3c"], "node": "b662266830ff854243fb7a62bc5d53e64784b515", "parents": ["ea3db7a6f9ab9c212fa0d3a5c44487c3b0232df2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074413 - Stylelint: check a nested state variant's inherited text color against the background it paints. r=hjones,desktop-theme-reviewers,fchasen\n\nThe twelve `color` insertions are what `--fix` produced. Each hover or active text token resolves to the base one in the default theme, so the change shows only under forced colors, where the base is ButtonText and the states are SelectedItem.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328099\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/PictureOfTheDay/_PictureOfTheDay.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_TopSites.scss", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/translations/panel.css", "docs/code-quality/lint/linters/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/rules/use-paired-color-tokens.md", "toolkit/themes/shared/global-shared.css", "tools/lint/stylelint/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/rules/use-paired-color-tokens.mjs", "tools/lint/stylelint/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/tests/use-paired-color-tokens.no-text-color.tests.mjs"], "git_node": "95ab85c042dc9b56e14c4dad49de7a748180fe3e", "git_parents": ["26afb79bb8a9b7722fb7fac803334c294b7f2ecf"], "node": "b9a52fd6cf85ae92ff499a2a7e4b357ceb6eef67", "parents": ["b662266830ff854243fb7a62bc5d53e64784b515"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tiaan Louw \u003ctlouw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1995348 - Implement the \"grid-lanes\" value for the \"display\" property r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,dholbert,emilio\n\nUse the \"display: grid-lanes\" value to conform to current usage in web\nplatform tests.\n\nTwo tests are marked as CRASH, because the masonry code uses a sort\ncomparitor that is not valid strick weak ordering as required, so it\nasserts in debug builds. See bug 2068688.\n\nSee: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-grid-3/#masonry-model\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D273845\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp", "layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/inspector/tests/test_bug877690.html", "layout/style/test/property_database.js", "layout/style/test/test_position_float_display.html", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/grid-lanes-position-area-basic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-grid-lanes-oof-fragmentation-009.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-b