ddce9c2287d81f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073844 - Replace `extra_mozconfig_content` with mozconfig files. r=ahal\n\nThe goal is for every build to use one mozconfig file from the tree, so\nthat `MOZCONFIG=\u003cthat file\u003e ./mach build` reproduces it locally. Some\nbuilds instead had mozharness append extra lines to a copy of their\nmozconfig at run time. Those lines now live in new mozconfig files that\nsource the original and add them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329063\n", "files": ["browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64-aarch64/beta", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64-aarch64/debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64-aarch64/devedition", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64-aarch64/nightly", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64-aarch64/profile-generate", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64-aarch64/release", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64/debug-base-toolchains", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64/nightly-base-toolchains", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64/non-unified", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64/non-unified-debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64/profile-generate-as-release", "browser/config/mozconfigs/macosx64-aarch64/debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/macosx64-aarch64/debug-searchfox", "browser/config/mozconfigs/macosx64-aarch64/opt", "browser/config/mozconfigs/macosx64-aarch64/opt-searchfox", "browser/config/mozconfigs/macosx64-aarch64/profile-generate-as-release", "browser/config/mozconfigs/macosx64/non-unified", "browser/config/mozconfigs/win64/non-unified", "browser/config/mozconfigs/win64/profile-generate-as-release", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-aarch64-lite/beta", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-aarch64-lite/nightly", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-aarch64-lite/release", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-aarch64/non-unified", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-arm-lite/beta", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-arm-lite/beta-fat-aar", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-arm-lite/nightly", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-arm-lite/nightly-fat-aar", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-arm-lite/release", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-arm-lite/release-fat-aar", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-x86_64-lite/beta", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-x86_64-lite/nightly", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-x86_64-lite/release", "mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-x86_64/non-unified", "mobile/ios/config/mozconfigs/ios/non-unified", "taskcluster/kinds/build/android.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/ios.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/linux-base-toolchains.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/linux.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/macosx.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/windows.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/instrumented-build/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/searchfox/kind.yml", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_aarch64_lite.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_arm_lite.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_x86_64_lite.py"], "git_node": "5395c8f5cf33934c1446b5e6206d8f8496144af5", "git_parents": ["7b8805a1bf6384da1999fb0368af76998fda179d"], "node": "37bce6981a03a345cb43903c850f48e62a521fc0", "parents": ["f363a3fa69ad3d18987c77c81986a0813a47be71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073844 - Set `MOZCONFIG` in the environment of build tasks from a `mozconfig` key. r=ahal,taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers\n\nBuild tasks now name their mozconfig in the kind with a `mozconfig` key\ninstead of through mozharness configs, so the choice stays in taskgraph\nwhatever runs the build. A transform turns the key into `MOZCONFIG` in\nthe task environment. When the key leaves them out, the platform comes\nfrom the task name, and the application is `mobile/android` for Android\nor the graph's `product-dir` otherwise, which gives comm-central\n`comm/mail`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327665\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/python.toml", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_mozconfig.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/build.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/mozconfig.py", "taskcluster/kinds/artifact-build/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build-fat-aar/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/android-asan.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/android-stuff.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/android.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/fenix.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/ios.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/linux-base-toolchains.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/linux.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/macosx-native.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/macosx.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/windows-mingw.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/build/windows.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/instrumented-build/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-source/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/searchfox/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/valgrind/kind.yml"], "git_node": "7a9b9782439e2d2d57d89d0900e7480cb5d73d0e", "git_parents": ["5395c8f5cf33934c1446b5e6206d8f8496144af5"], "node": "f66fcb4075ade949615ff573e26eb13002d18b76", "parents": ["37bce6981a03a345cb43903c850f48e62a521fc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073844 - Take the mozconfig path from `MOZCONFIG` in mozharness builds. r=ahal\n\nmozharness builds now require `MOZCONFIG` in the task environment. mach\nreads that file itself, resolving the path against the source directory,\nso mozharness only logs it and no longer composes a mozconfig or writes\n`.mozconfig`. `get_mozconfig_path` stays for `desktop_l10n.py`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327666\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/building/buildbase.py"], "git_node": "502b42d06ba7cb7195dcf677d981eeef10fac4ee", "git_parents": ["7a9b9782439e2d2d57d89d0900e7480cb5d73d0e"], "node": "e030de9ecff0447e415421aa69d4a3126373063e", "parents": ["f66fcb4075ade949615ff573e26eb13002d18b76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073844 - Drop the mozconfig keys from the mozharness build configs. r=ahal\n\nNothing reads `app_name`, `mozconfig_platform`, `mozconfig_variant` or\n`src_mozconfig` from these files any more. Variant configs left with\nother settings stay as they are. Android variant configs that end up\nempty stay too, because `_is_configuration_shipped` still checks the\n`--custom-build-variant-cfg` name.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327667\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_base_android_64_builds.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_base_firefox.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_base_linux_64_builds.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_base_mac_64_cross_builds.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_base_windows_32_mingw_builds.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_base_windows_64_mingw_builds.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_aarch64.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_aarch64_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_aarch64_debug_searchfox.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_aarch64_fenix_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_aarch64_lite.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_aarch64_profile_generate.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_arm.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_arm_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_arm_lite.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_arm_profile_generate.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_fuzzing_asan_tc.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_fuzzing_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_geckoview_docs.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_x86.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_x86_64.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_x86_64_ccov.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_x86_64_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_x86_64_debug_isolated_process.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_x86_64_lite.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_x86_64_profile_generate.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/32_rusttests.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/32_rusttests_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/64_rusttests.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/64_rusttests_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/64_searchfox_and_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/64_searchfox_and_opt.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/64_source.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/64_stat_and_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_linux_configs/64_valgrind.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_mac_configs/64_cross_debug_searchfox.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_mac_configs/64_cross_opt_searchfox.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_mac_configs/64_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_mac_configs/rusttests.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_windows_configs/32_add-on-devel.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_windows_configs/32_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_windows_configs/32_mingwclang.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_windows_configs/64_add-on-devel.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_windows_configs/64_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_windows_configs/64_mingwclang.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/taskcluster_base_win32.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/taskcluster_base_win64.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/taskcluster_sub_win64/plain_opt.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/taskcluster_sub_win64/rusttests_opt.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/taskcluster_sub_win64/searchfox_debug.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/taskcluster_sub_win64/searchfox_opt.py"], "git_node": "3710a466303e81cfe42d60510838816711ab2287", "git_parents": ["502b42d06ba7cb7195dcf677d981eeef10fac4ee"], "node": "d84190968022eb3dd422369729459aa58667848c", "parents": ["e030de9ecff0447e415421aa69d4a3126373063e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068991: Load Safari's staged frameworks on older macOS so ASWebAuthenticationSession requests can be decoded. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nOn macOS 10.15 the ASWebAuthenticationSession broker runs the newer AuthenticationServices that Safari updates install in /Library/Apple/System/Library/StagedFrameworks/Safari, and the system copy that Firefox loads fails to decode its messages. The broker then retries in a tight loop, which is what keeps Firefox in front in bug 2075199. Safari loads its frameworks from that folder through LC_DYLD_ENVIRONMENT, so the firefox executable now does the same. Where the folder doesn't exist, dyld falls back to the system frameworks.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329358\n", "files": ["browser/app/moz.build"], "git_node": "ea46b0538d72aeafa6fddf5eb407345b0ee34411", "git_parents": ["3710a466303e81cfe42d60510838816711ab2287"], "node": "a278afb46bbe7747cfe414264c8accc8aeb6d320", "parents": ["d84190968022eb3dd422369729459aa58667848c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Drew Willcoxon \u003cadw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075759 - Always specify a size for moz-remote-image URLs used by Suggest. r=daisuke,urlbar-reviewers\n\nPass in the top-pick icon size for the `size` param. This will have the\nfollowing effects as the images are decoded out-of-process due to how\n`moz-remote-image` works (in conjunction with the fact that we also pass\n`stretch=false`):\n\n* Images that are no larger than the top-pick size won't be resized when they\n  are decoded\n\n* Images that are larger will be downsampled when they are decoded\n\n* For SVGs that don't have an intrinsic size, there are two possibilities: They\n  can either have an intrinsic ratio or not. For those with an intrinsic ratio,\n  they'll be drawn at the top-pick size while preserving their ratio. For SVGs\n  without an intrinsic ratio, they'll be stretched and probably distorted so\n  that their width and height both equal the top-pick size.\n\nOn top of all of that, these images will be resized again when they're drawn in\nthe UI if they aren't shown at exactly the top-pick size.\n\nFor a larger discussion, including why this patch only uses the top-pick size\neven though some of these images will be shown at a smaller size, see:\n\nhttps://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326836#11437885\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329353\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderQuickSuggest.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/FlightStatusSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/MarketSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/SportsSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/YelpRealtimeSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css"], "git_node": "1bfd39e70d8a9dd2dea9b6cb58513351db1c6991", "git_parents": ["ea46b0538d72aeafa6fddf5eb407345b0ee34411"], "node": "c6659cfa7da4b7dd72d9b676e62bd6dc60716dae", "parents": ["a278afb46bbe7747cfe414264c8accc8aeb6d320"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075837. Report why a vendor run failed instead of reporting what it left behind as drift. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe verification job looks at whether the working tree is clean before it looks at the\nexit code of mach vendor, so a run that failed part way is reported as drift. Vendoring\ncleans the library's directory before it unpacks the new copy, so a failed download leaves\nthe library's files missing, and the job reports them as differing. For example,\nzucchini often fails to fetch from googlesource and hits this (bug 2075616).\n\nThis does not stop the network failures, it only reports them as what they are more clearly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329411\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/verify-vendored-library.py"], "git_node": "78d59e2d14555eee3c2bdde06e36a21745720a90", "git_parents": ["1bfd39e70d8a9dd2dea9b6cb58513351db1c6991"], "node": "51f2162b6dd968bd82d09184cdaf7b5bc661a938", "parents": ["c6659cfa7da4b7dd72d9b676e62bd6dc60716dae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074552 - Rename OnlyFirstInFlows to PullKind for AbsoluteContainingBlock::PullAbsoluteFramesFrom(). r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nThis patch was originally written by hackbot.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329083\n", "files": ["layout/generic/AbsoluteContainingBlock.cpp", "layout/generic/AbsoluteContainingBlock.h"], "git_node": "a66d15ee2dd38514d16add868c9df326abb2e8e4", "git_parents": ["78d59e2d14555eee3c2bdde06e36a21745720a90"], "node": "d02e0c8b8543073193e8de51ade0394bfcbbe9c7", "parents": ["51f2162b6dd968bd82d09184cdaf7b5bc661a938"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074671 - Offer a Mini Window chooser on the Screenshots overlay. r=mconley,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio,flod,jhirsch\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328306\n", "files": ["browser/components/miniwindow/assets/mini-window.svg", "browser/components/miniwindow/jar.mn", "browser/components/miniwindow/moz.build", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_chooser_panel.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_region_entry.js", "browser/components/screenshots/ScreenshotsOverlayChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/screenshots/ScreenshotsUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/screenshots/overlay/overlay.css", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.css", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.js", "browser/components/screenshots/tests/browser/browser_mini_window_mode.js", "browser/locales-preview/miniWindow.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbutton-icons.css"], "git_node": "7c514e2cc83eb03e3bd439b935f84318799eb095", "git_parents": ["a66d15ee2dd38514d16add868c9df326abb2e8e4"], "node": "244d1ee3e5078ff98e30ec591fa91d5612de5116", "parents": ["d02e0c8b8543073193e8de51ade0394bfcbbe9c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075266 - Let a mini window's toolbar hide while the window is inactive. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328869\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css"], "git_node": "dd1ddf7c089575138d7abecd332133365d613772", "git_parents": ["7c514e2cc83eb03e3bd439b935f84318799eb095"], "node": "947994c16857b106de0bcaf1be4915a6acd25c0e", "parents": ["244d1ee3e5078ff98e30ec591fa91d5612de5116"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074672 - Open mini windows clear of other always-on-top windows. r=mconley\n\nmostly mimics how pip handles tiling - i have a bug on file to eventually make a shared\nspace for these sorts of windows so the helpers aren't duplicated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328870\n", "files": ["browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_overlap.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/xpcshell/test_MiniWindowUtils.js"], "git_node": "5837dd49937b3665b9603fdb6055353d8d97571d", "git_parents": ["dd1ddf7c089575138d7abecd332133365d613772"], "node": "f9dbf33aed368ff401b3f056c4789a20d43dd47a", "parents": ["947994c16857b106de0bcaf1be4915a6acd25c0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074671 - Update toolbar hiding behavior and make urlbar editable on full tab mini windows. r=mconley,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328891\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "7249cc55bf93bd6ff745840e4ea6690899c740df", "git_parents": ["5837dd49937b3665b9603fdb6055353d8d97571d"], "node": "fcb57108577e56245b5b654f7283f199fb649525", "parents": ["f9dbf33aed368ff401b3f056c4789a20d43dd47a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068991: Load Safari's staged frameworks on older macOS so ASWebAuthenticationSession requests can be decoded. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\" for causing bustages complaining about llvm-strip.\n\nThis reverts commit ea46b0538d72aeafa6fddf5eb407345b0ee34411.\n", "files": ["browser/app/moz.build"], "git_node": "3e5996eb62bf349769e22da0e8c21377b25697d9", "git_parents": ["7249cc55bf93bd6ff745840e4ea6690899c740df"], "node": "4e4ff650eb9f4ef569a3cd5dcbab26fa83b56a0c", "parents": ["fcb57108577e56245b5b654f7283f199fb649525"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cristian Tuns \u003cctuns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2075837. Report why a vendor run failed instead of reporting what it left behind as drift. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\" for causing vendor failures\n\nThis reverts commit 78d59e2d14555eee3c2bdde06e36a21745720a90.\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/verify-vendored-library.py"], "git_node": "858b769c7c14a7fef9db1b2f2d10dfbfe7830ddc", "git_parents": ["3e5996eb62bf349769e22da0e8c21377b25697d9"], "node": "ebb925d4affcdc9947a63e2b6963ea8b6b22942e", "parents": ["4e4ff650eb9f4ef569a3cd5dcbab26fa83b56a0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2074671, Bug 2075266, Bug 2074672 - Update toolbar hiding behavior and make urlbar editable on full tab mini windows. r=mconley,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,dao\" for causing failures at browser_chooser_panel.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 7249cc55bf93bd6ff745840e4ea6690899c740df.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2074672 - Open mini windows clear of other always-on-top windows. r=mconley\"\n\nThis reverts commit 5837dd49937b3665b9603fdb6055353d8d97571d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075266 - Let a mini window's toolbar hide while the window is inactive. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\"\n\nThis reverts commit dd1ddf7c089575138d7abecd332133365d613772.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2074671 - Offer a Mini Window chooser on the Screenshots overlay. r=mconley,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio,flod,jhirsch\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7c514e2cc83eb03e3bd439b935f84318799eb095.\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/assets/mini-window.svg", "browser/components/miniwindow/jar.mn", "browser/components/miniwindow/moz.build", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_chooser_panel.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_overlap.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_region_entry.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/xpcshell/test_MiniWindowUtils.js", "browser/components/screenshots/ScreenshotsOverlayChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/screenshots/ScreenshotsUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/screenshots/overlay/overlay.css", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.css", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.js", "browser/components/screenshots/tests/browser/browser_mini_window_mode.js", "browser/locales-preview/miniWindow.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbutton-icons.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "eaa6686b1c4289aba50153aea7ec3e4c55332f9c", "git_parents": ["858b769c7c14a7fef9db1b2f2d10dfbfe7830ddc"], "node": "eac3b513e54aeced255ef749dc7735b6c617ac95", "parents": ["ebb925d4affcdc9947a63e2b6963ea8b6b22942e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Segun Famisa \u003csfamisa@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074093 - Update detekt's LongParameterList rule to allow up to 9 constructor parameters r=pollymce\n\nNote - the behaviour of this rule changed in the next version. For version 1.23.8 we had to set the `constructorThreshold` to 10, to allow 9 parameters.\n\nIn version 1.23.8, the threshold specifies the number from which a violation is reported, and in newer versions, the threshold specifies the number *after* which, a violation is reported.\n\nWe should adjust the rule whenever we bump detekt's version.\n\nSee https://github.com/detekt/detekt/issues/3679 for more info\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/369\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/menu/item/BrowserMenuImageTextCheckboxButton.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/prompt/PromptRequest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/syncedtabs/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/syncedtabs/SyncedTabsFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/webnotifications/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/webnotifications/WebNotificationFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/config/detekt.yml", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/browser/src/main/java/org/mozilla/samples/browser/integration/ContextMenuIntegration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/OpenInAppOnboardingObserver.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/IntentProcessors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/ipprotection/IPProtection.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuNavigationMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/ToolbarsIntegration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/gestures/ToolbarHorizontalGesturesHandler.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/collections/migration/CollectionsToTabGroupsMigration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/recentsyncedtabs/RecentSyncedTabFeature.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/recentvisits/controller/RecentVisitsController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/ui/HomeSwipeIntegration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/library/history/HistoryView.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/library/recentlyclosed/RecentlyClosedController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/search/BrowserToolbarSearchMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/search/awesomebar/AwesomeBarComposable.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SyncPreferenceView.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/datachoices/DataChoicesMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/logins/ui/LoginsMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/studies/StudiesView.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/trustpanel/store/TrustPanelStore.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/summarization/SummarizationStoreViewModel.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/browser/compose/interactable/InteractableGrid.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/browser/compose/interactable/InteractableList.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/browser/compose/legacy/ReorderableList.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/redux/middleware/TabStorageMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/syncedtabs/SyncedTabsIntegration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/wallpapers/WallpapersUseCases.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/config/detekt.yml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/browser/integration/FullScreenIntegration.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/quality/detekt.yml"], "git_node": "04a8b8671ef0901782bfc6080002b7446daff61b", "git_parents": ["eaa6686b1c4289aba50153aea7ec3e4c55332f9c"], "node": "ddb329c57a2e5f8e51d5773917785e2f222266d1", "parents": ["eac3b513e54aeced255ef749dc7735b6c617ac95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067348 - Specifically load the test font to ensure it is ready before doing canvas2d text operations. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329439\n", "files": ["layout/reftests/svg/text-layout-09.svg", "layout/reftests/svg/text-layout-10.svg"], "git_node": "93450f97a91e7e72daa14fdca87f8c7887ca4a92", "git_parents": ["04a8b8671ef0901782bfc6080002b7446daff61b"], "node": "5362a7490db9ed6a9f24498d8d2b961c4d8ffad2", "parents": ["ddb329c57a2e5f8e51d5773917785e2f222266d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075505 - Update PDF.js to d52fdf411a6e4d338180687456e0df019e28475e r=pdfjs-reviewers,calixte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329117\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsVersion.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "bbacece95653b7cc86a6b76ebbebfdd78e640b51", "git_parents": ["93450f97a91e7e72daa14fdca87f8c7887ca4a92"], "node": "ec9c881d2e859783affed7645b84fee12527efbf", "parents": ["5362a7490db9ed6a9f24498d8d2b961c4d8ffad2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075013 - FFmpegAudioDecoder::PostProcessOutput should attempt to pull pts from frame before sample. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nFor ffvpx implemented decoders, there should not change things, but\non Android where the output frames can be delayed, we need to use\nthe pts from the frame first, if available. This is because the\nMediaCodec NDK audio decoders\n\nFor software decoders implemented within ffvpx, the frame pts and\nthe sample pts will always be the same. In those scenarios, this\npatch has no effect.\n\nFor platform decoders wrapped by ffvpx, by MediaCodec NDK on\nAndroid, the frame for a sample may be delayed, and will be yielded\nin a subsequent PostProcessOutput call. As such, we should prefer\nthe frame pts if given, the previous frame pts plus its duration if\nnot given, and finally the sample time if we have neither. This\navoids mismatching the wrong time on a given frame, which is the\ndecoded output from an earlier sample, and not the current sample.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328670\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegAudioDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegAudioDecoder.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegUtils.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "88d6d347057b34bf60af6d2f10cb68d7463bbee5", "git_parents": ["bbacece95653b7cc86a6b76ebbebfdd78e640b51"], "node": "9e82276bcd015c220dd25ac0df1a911124e4252f", "parents": ["ec9c881d2e859783affed7645b84fee12527efbf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "zhuangxiaosen \u003cxz.ganbaruibro@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071093 - Preserve HSL and HWB missing components in computed colors r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nKeep HWB whiteness and blackness values until RGB conversion so ratios above 100% use the original components. When any HSL or HWB component is missing, serialize in the corresponding modern color syntax rather than legacy rgb() or rgba(). Share this path in the existing HSL/HWB match arm and factor missing-component bits into ColorFlags::NONE_FLAGS.\n\nRemove both HSL and HWB WPT expected-failure metadata files. A Firefox binaries build and headless WPT runs pass all 3,753 HSL and 70 HWB subtests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329463\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/color/color_function.rs", "servo/components/style/color/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/color/to_css.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-hsl.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-hwb.html.ini"], "git_node": "14bd428bb79b702f4deba92a56dd18b688d4dd55", "git_parents": ["88d6d347057b34bf60af6d2f10cb68d7463bbee5"], "node": "5a9960fc77f4cbe7e6e955343fc9c7b5d5a7cfcb", "parents": ["9e82276bcd015c220dd25ac0df1a911124e4252f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2071093 - Preserve HSL and HWB missing components in computed colors r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\" for causing wpt tests failures at computed-relative-color.html\n\nThis reverts commit 14bd428bb79b702f4deba92a56dd18b688d4dd55.\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/color/color_function.rs", "servo/components/style/color/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/color/to_css.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-hsl.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-hwb.html.ini"], "git_node": "38de703b76c2961935cdf33dc5d45010651107ec", "git_parents": ["14bd428bb79b702f4deba92a56dd18b688d4dd55"], "node": "0f9368564765db3010bcf25730fe065ac3b20931", "parents": ["5a9960fc77f4cbe7e6e955343fc9c7b5d5a7cfcb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch":