, "55d27a314368fba286992875beaa1ce0c71beb00", "5b25044b9fe0914b6048670abe460cf827a1f7af", "eb8ceeebe16204dabfc82bd9673a09e3db4d0217"], "user": "csabou@mozilla.com"}, "45428": {"changesets": [{"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1945881 - Map drop shadow offsets through the surface transform when it is flipped. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328303\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/filter-drop-shadow-rotate-180-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/filter-drop-shadow-rotate-180.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/reftest.list"], "git_node": "9230bee70eb81bb0f5b361f0a5097c14774edfcd", "git_parents": ["eb8ceeebe16204dabfc82bd9673a09e3db4d0217"], "node": "b7ada0a2319cb0be6dfb9f4983abe7d40e6e537c", "parents": ["0c7f224166dfe41e6f360c76c52552de6af8b25a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1703102 - Take the FreeType glyph scale from the oriented glyph transform. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nFT_Set_Char_Size scales the glyph in its own space, before the transform\nis applied, but the x and y scales were taken from the device transform.\nFor transposed (sideways) glyphs under a non-uniform scale, this stretched\neach glyph along the wrong axis. Compute the scale after applying the\nflips and transpose instead. Other platforms rasterize with a uniform size\nand keep the non-uniform part in the transform, so they are unaffected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329099\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wr_glyph_rasterizer/src/platform/unix/font.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/writing-modes-scale-x-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/writing-modes-scale-x.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/writing-modes-scale-y-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/writing-modes-scale-y.yaml"], "git_node": "bf5a19399bf4e854dba8270a4536b782926ca75c", "git_parents": ["9230bee70eb81bb0f5b361f0a5097c14774edfcd"], "node": "4c8dfb4bdbd32a47bd134bfaa74d3a03caf73381", "parents": ["b7ada0a2319cb0be6dfb9f4983abe7d40e6e537c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073976 - Pt 3 - Carry the display list interning delta with the display list r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe builder now holds its DlInterners, retained across reset, and closes\ntheir build in end; the resulting DlDelta rides on BuiltDisplayList. In\nprocess (wrench, the parent-side pipelines) the receiver is handed the struct\ndirectly. Across the Gecko IPC boundary it travels as a third display list\nbuffer alongside the items and the spatial tree, bincode-encoded in into_data\nand decoded in from_data, following the same path through the FFI,\nDisplayListData and the bridge parent.\n\nA delta that asks for nothing is still encoded. It carries the build number,\nand builds have to stay contiguous for the receiver to tell an idle build\nfrom a lost one; dropping it would make the next real delta look out of\nsequence. With no interned types yet that is every delta: twelve bytes of\nbuilder id and build number per display list, and no other change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329068\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "gfx/layers/wr/AsyncImagePipelineManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/RenderRootTypes.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/RenderRootTypes.h", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderBridgeParent.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderTypes.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs"], "git_node": "312741f7b21bc81b1432f363318260dc45d0c957", "git_parents": ["bf5a19399bf4e854dba8270a4536b782926ca75c"], "node": "b96335f22ae42fbac3c2b9518771ebb93ba9bbec", "parents": ["4c8dfb4bdbd32a47bd134bfaa74d3a03caf73381"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073976 - Pt 4 - Drive the follower stores from the scene builder thread r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe scene builder gives each pipeline a namespace on first sight of one of\nits display lists, checks every arriving delta against the builder stream it\nis following, and rewrites it into ordered op lists: DlUpdates for the render\nbackend's DlStores, applied before anything that can drop the transaction,\nand SceneDlStores on the thread itself, applied the moment the delta is\nresolved so a scene built later in the same transaction sees its entries. A\ntakeover by a new builder closes and reopens the namespace; a removed\npipeline's namespace is released only at the next scene build, since the\nrender backend goes on drawing the previous scene until then, and deleting\na document or clearing a namespace retires the pipelines it takes with it\nthe same way; a loaded capture's pipelines get namespaces too.\n\nBoth sides are generated from one type list each, enumerate_dl_stores! and\nenumerate_scene_dl_stores!, paired with the api crate's\nenumerate_dl_interned_types!. Every store value is built from its content\nkey through DlResolve against a DlResolveContext carrying the id namespace,\nthe font resources and the default render mode, so adding a type is one line\nper list plus a resolve impl. The store sizes feed the per-type INTERNED_*\ngauges and a dl_stores sub-report reusing the interning report's field list,\nand applied adds and removes join INTERN_INSERTIONS / INTERN_REMOVALS.\n\nWith the lists still empty every delta is metadata only and every op list is\nempty, so nothing renders differently, but the namespace lifecycle and the\nstream checks run on every display list. The lint allows on the generated\nimpls go with the first type.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329069\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderMessageUtils.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/dl_interner.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs"], "git_node": "5ce3fa2f0e9dac137ab4bf40034c6b4a2ee8ae3e", "git_parents": ["312741f7b21bc81b1432f363318260dc45d0c957"], "node": "fc4f700fd37dfbfcdf15d3cbb957206eeccebaaf", "parents": ["b96335f22ae42fbac3c2b9518771ebb93ba9bbec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073976: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp"], "git_node": "0b19b04d8fac5e79fa014f0dbefc53c3bd99d154", "git_parents": ["5ce3fa2f0e9dac137ab4bf40034c6b4a2ee8ae3e"], "node": "1c144bd379108f6071003a2b4a2a115d4369f968", "parents": ["fc4f700fd37dfbfcdf15d3cbb957206eeccebaaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings tld-suffixes mobile-experiments ct-logs - r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329500\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/raw/initial_experiments.json", "netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json"], "git_node": "8278b60948c4b6a9dde082e6c99b2c5812c84bf4", "git_parents": ["0b19b04d8fac5e79fa014f0dbefc53c3bd99d154"], "node": "94976d5962c3bb91bca470bcdbfb433d275524a2", "parents": ["1c144bd379108f6071003a2b4a2a115d4369f968"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074176 - Pull a border's outer edge in to meet content snapped at its inner edge. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nUnder a fractional scale, a border's device thickness is rounded to whole\npixels (bug 1258112) and measured from its nearest-snapped outer edge, while\nthe background or replaced content that meets the border's inner edge in\nlayout snaps that same edge on its own. The two can land a pixel apart,\nleaving a white gap between border and content.\n\nSnap borders with a new SnapRounding::BorderInner mode: round the outer\nand inner edges to the nearest pixel as before, and where the whole-pixel\nwidth measured from the outer edge stops short of the inner edge's pixel,\npull the outer edge in to close the gap. Every side keeps its rounded width\nand the border never grows past its nearest-snapped rect.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328720\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/border-content-snap-scale-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/border-content-snap-scale.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/reftest.list"], "git_node": "ee1823453a2c855a6eb2a0bae942308772b31587", "git_parents": ["8278b60948c4b6a9dde082e6c99b2c5812c84bf4"], "node": "619dee91a57dab6aef27f7cec596b3d659c84868", "parents": ["94976d5962c3bb91bca470bcdbfb433d275524a2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790569539, "git_changesets": ["9230bee70eb81bb0f5b361f0a5097c14774edfcd", "bf5a19399bf4e854dba8270a4536b782926ca75c", "312741f7b21bc81b1432f363318260dc45d0c957", "5ce3fa2f0e9dac137ab4bf40034c6b4a2ee8ae3e", "0b19b04d8fac5e79fa014f0dbefc53c3bd99d154", "8278b60948c4b6a9dde082e6c99b2c5812c84bf4", "ee1823453a2c855a6eb2a0bae942308772b31587"], "user": "asilaghi@mozilla.com"}, "45429": {"changesets": [{"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074671 - Offer a Mini Window chooser on the Screenshots overlay. r=mconley,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio,flod,jhirsch\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328306\n", "files": ["browser/components/miniwindow/assets/mini-window.svg", "browser/components/miniwindow/jar.mn", "browser/components/miniwindow/moz.build", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_chooser_panel.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_region_entry.js", "browser/components/screenshots/ScreenshotsOverlayChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/screenshots/ScreenshotsUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/screenshots/overlay/overlay.css", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.css", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.js", "browser/components/screenshots/tests/browser/browser_mini_window_mode.js", "browser/locales-preview/miniWindow.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbutton-icons.css"], "git_node": "cfdad434a148d498719c55078824f40f5966d581", "git_parents": ["ee1823453a2c855a6eb2a0bae942308772b31587"], "node": "e59ce928d21729ac558a755d2f070ecb3cdc3cb2", "parents": ["619dee91a57dab6aef27f7cec596b3d659c84868"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075266 - Let a mini window's toolbar hide while the window is inactive. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328869\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css"], "git_node": "754ca3f30f7006578ce70e47b7cc5eb37b5e401e", "git_parents": ["cfdad434a148d498719c55078824f40f5966d581"], "node": "68c90d97f2ff8e9169da82c89ee53dd31d80b10d", "parents": ["e59ce928d21729ac558a755d2f070ecb3cdc3cb2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074672 - Open mini windows clear of other always-on-top windows. r=mconley\n\nmostly mimics how pip handles tiling - i have a bug on file to eventually make a shared\nspace for these sorts of windows so the helpers aren't duplicated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328870\n", "files": ["browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_overlap.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/xpcshell/test_MiniWindowUtils.js"], "git_node": "62e02bd814097121640e9cedf1cf8522d7ad3fd4", "git_parents": ["754ca3f30f7006578ce70e47b7cc5eb37b5e401e"], "node": "b2aa5669da7ac7ebab02b5583db3e3e5771cda4e", "parents": ["68c90d97f2ff8e9169da82c89ee53dd31d80b10d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074671 - Update toolbar hiding behavior and make urlbar editable on full tab mini windows. r=mconley,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328891\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "1d51b017b5fb6f5079491f90a3af8be9b96614c4", "git_parents": ["62e02bd814097121640e9cedf1cf8522d7ad3fd4"], "node": "227f214b46e073f72eb2b96307d00413a708a158", "parents": ["b2aa5669da7ac7ebab02b5583db3e3e5771cda4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075910 - When an inner window is torn down (nsGlobalWindowInner::FreeInnerObjects), its 2D canvas contexts now release their buffer providers right away. Before, they kept them until the canvas objects were garbage- and cycle-collected. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nWhen an inner window is torn down (nsGlobalWindowInner::FreeInnerObjects), its 2D canvas contexts now release their buffer providers right away. Before, they kept them until the canvas objects were garbage- and cycle-collected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329453\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h", "dom/canvas/nsICanvasRenderingContextInternal.h", "gfx/ipc/CanvasShutdownManager.cpp", "gfx/ipc/CanvasShutdownManager.h"], "git_node": "c7215fb6f63a0eaeff428ba3960161944d3ada9d", "git_parents": ["1d51b017b5fb6f5079491f90a3af8be9b96614c4"], "node": "d01e92e8d9f304a184d47be626335ec1bc4affd8", "parents": ["227f214b46e073f72eb2b96307d00413a708a158"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kiril Panayotov \u003ccontact@zakrok.dev\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043642 - Add more tests for powerless hue becoming missing after color conversion r=tlouw\n\nAdd several tests for conversions between hsl, hwb, lch and oklch. Additionally, add tests for when there is no conversion e.g. hsl to hsl to ensure that powerless hues become missing only after conversion.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303935\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-color-mix-function.html"], "git_node": "6771316268f8b004c44daaa220462c222dbcd0a3", "git_parents": ["c7215fb6f63a0eaeff428ba3960161944d3ada9d"], "node": "2e2c62a6752700b12fb39fb5115cd22528b21f6e", "parents": ["d01e92e8d9f304a184d47be626335ec1bc4affd8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041504 - Refresh the displayport base of a reused popup element. r=botond,tnikkel,layout-reviewers\n\nA select dropdown always reuses the #ContentSelectDropdownPopup element, which\nSelectParentHelper creates once per chrome window, and popups in the parent\nprocess get their own APZ. InitializeRootDisplayport() seeded that element's\ndisplayport base with SetDisplayPortBaseIfNotSet(), and nothing removes the\nproperty afterwards, so the base stayed at the geometry of the first dropdown\nopened in a given window for as long as that window lived.  A later dropdown\ntaller than the first one was therefore clipped to the stale base, and the\npart of its scroll port that fell outside was never painted.  It stays blank\nuntil some unrelated repaint fills it in, which is why scrolling the list\nfixes it.  This patch sets the base for popups unconditionally instead.\n\nThe tests open a three option dropdown before a three hundred option one in the\nsame window (and also try that same case, but pre-scrolled).  This was enough\nto reproduce the bug without any particular screen size or display scaling in\nthe pre-scrolled test.  The non-pre-scrolled test only failed for certain\nmonitor configurations (resolution, DPI, etc).  Neither should fail anywhere\nnow.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325984\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/browser.toml", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/browser_test_displayport_in_select_dropdown.js", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_bug2041504_select.html", "gfx/layers/apz/util/APZCCallbackHelper.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/util/APZCCallbackHelper.h", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "f2fa365dfe90922709d4426a8f99ae892e1c62d1", "git_parents": ["6771316268f8b004c44daaa220462c222dbcd0a3"], "node": "d793412e60a1539b0b431307c6b5ab134e75e0fc", "parents": ["2e2c62a6752700b12fb39fb5115cd22528b21f6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1672828 - Draw dotted borders up to 2 device pixels wide with square dots. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDots were always drawn as antialiased circles, so a 1px dot only reached\n50% coverage and a 2px dot 79%, making thin dotted borders and outlines\nlook faded. Like Gecko, draw dots no wider than two device pixels as\npixel-aligned squares without AA, for edges and single-dot corners.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329498\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/res/cs_border_segment.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/border.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/small-dotted-border.png", "layout/reftests/position-sticky/reftest.list"], "git_node": "133fd41d6d36979b1529dc537d0542126c2b62e0", "git_parents": ["f2fa365dfe90922709d4426a8f99ae892e1c62d1"], "node": "f5f543e996a25b63b1ff2870d2f94df67142c44e", "parents": ["d793412e60a1539b0b431307c6b5ab134e75e0fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075736 - Avoid a shift overflow when downscaling a box-shadow mask. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nA surface can legitimately have a device pixel scale large enough that the\nnumber of blur downscales reaches 32, which overflowed the shift computing\nthe divisor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329508\n", "files": ["gfx/tests/crashtests/2075736.html", "gfx/tests/crashtests/crashtests.list", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/box_shadow.rs"], "git_node": "6e500d7773a725da21f519d3747c38ebf529e920", "git_parents": ["133fd41d6d36979b1529dc537d0542126c2b62e0"], "node": "b2f96eddca4ebf0970772bfb36f6d1a4100ad2fe", "parents": ["f5f543e996a25b63b1ff2870d2f94df67142c44e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061927 - Use R10G10B10A2 for video swap chain of VpAutoHDR r=gfx-reviewers,ahale,lsalzman\n\nNVIDIA drivers do not support VpAutoHDR with P010 format video with R16G16B16A16 SwapChain. Then use R10G10B10A2 for VpAutoHDR like chromium.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329141\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp"], "git_node": "37f1f666232ba07c4b47b4f632b5b42023cf50c5", "git_parents": ["6e500d7773a725da21f519d3747c38ebf529e920"], "node": "7697918c5eb15d93d89bae34abcd541b62978923", "parents": ["b2f96eddca4ebf0970772bfb36f6d1a4100ad2fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076031 - Run code-review-issues on the built-in succeed worker. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum DONTBUILD\n\nThe task only exists to publish the pulse message once the analysis tasks are\nresolved, so there is no need to wait for a docker worker to run /bin/true.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329506\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/code-review/kind.yml"], "git_node": "3dff654fbe227e4f789c7cd820eccc137377bb29", "git_parents": ["37f1f666232ba07c4b47b4f632b5b42023cf50c5"], "node": "7e7ff7af742d1aa2ab198f06c7d169f4e01a4221", "parents": ["7697918c5eb15d93d89bae34abcd541b62978923"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-fi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-ja/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-ja/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-dsb/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-eu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-fi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-fr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-in/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-ja/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-pt-rPT/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-ru/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-tr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-dsb/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-eu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-in/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ja/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rPT/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ru/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-ace/strings.xml"], "git_node": "f6c134da33f24d4e606d5cd861920a110f6d5117", "git_parents": ["3dff654fbe227e4f789c7cd820eccc137377bb29"], "node": "68b079e7a8d898970db39ec12e86930f1041b8a8", "parents": ["7e7ff7af742d1aa2ab198f06c7d169f4e01a4221"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2074671, Bug 2074672, Bug 2075266 - Update toolbar hiding behavior and make urlbar editable on full tab mini windows. r=mconley,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,dao\" for causing bc and TV tests failures at chooser_panel.js\n\nThis reverts commit 1d51b017b5fb6f5079491f90a3af8be9b96614c4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2074672 - Open mini windows clear of other always-on-top windows. r=mconley\"\n\nThis reverts commit 62e02bd814097121640e9cedf1cf8522d7ad3fd4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075266 - Let a mini window's toolbar hide while the window is inactive. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\"\n\nThis reverts commit 754ca3f30f7006578ce70e47b7cc5eb37b5e401e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2074671 - Offer a Mini Window chooser on the Screenshots overlay. r=mconley,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio,flod,jhirsch\"\n\nThis reverts commit cfdad434a148d498719c55078824f40f5966d581.\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/assets/mini-window.svg", "browser/components/miniwindow/jar.mn", "browser/components/miniwindow/moz.build", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_chooser_panel.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_overlap.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_region_entry.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/xpcshell/test_MiniWindowUtils.js", "browser/components/screenshots/ScreenshotsOverlayChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/screenshots/ScreenshotsUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/screenshots/overlay/overlay.css", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.css", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.js", "browser/components/screenshots/tests/browser/browser_mini_window_mode.js", "browser/locales-preview/miniWindow.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbutton-icons.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "b478a70dbe9b20189bb57f12c05bc0d6a8f323bd", "git_parents": ["f6c134da33f24d4e606d5cd861920a110f6d5117"], "node": "5fafebaaa5bc47d17a93970fb6ce60e0e98ee788", "parents": ["68b079e7a8d898970db39ec12e86930f1041b8a8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790587399, "git_changesets": ["cfdad434a148d498719c55078824f40f5966d581", "754ca3f30f7006578ce70e47b7cc5eb37b5e401e", "62e02bd814097121640e9cedf1cf8522d7ad3fd4", "1d51b017b5fb6f5079491f90a3af8be9b96614c4", "c7215fb6f63a0eaeff428ba3960161944d3ada9d", "6771316268f8b004c44daaa220462c222dbcd0a3", "f2fa365dfe90922709d4426a8f99ae892e1c62d1", "133fd41d6d36979b1529dc537d0542126c2b62e0", "6e500d7773a725da21f519d3747c38ebf529e920", "37f1f666232ba07c4b47b4f632b5b42023cf50c5", "3dff654fbe227e4f789c7cd820eccc137377bb29", "f6c134da33f24d4e606d5cd861920a110f6d5117", "b478a70dbe9b20189bb57f12c05bc0d6a8f323bd"], "user": "pstanciu@mozilla.com"}, "45430": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging a9d3ddf164c6726e0fa285680bf0cb697f20ac8a with FIREFOX_158_0b1_BUILD2 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "9f504427e4c6553003995a2fa51d85a15b23240e", "git_parents": ["9c54b001d5088319f395f6613d1e9ee33c466b1d"], "node": "2018e07698f6ba642119d234407efedd424875ba", "parents": ["81a56e3bf83bd247ad80085fb52dc50dbf6c8031"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790609798, "git_changesets": ["9f504427e4c6553003995a2fa51d85a15b23240e"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45431": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging a9d3ddf164c6726e0fa285680bf0cb697f20ac8a with DEVEDITION_158_0b1_BUILD2 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "9aa908eaed2298ea185056ddf109218ab5993c25", "git_parents": ["9f504427e4c6553003995a2fa51d85a15b23240e"], "node": "98a3a541f695fea2fcc6cd7d85d1aa55fc37ab63", "parents": ["2018e07698f6ba642119d234407efedd424875ba"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790610045, "git_changesets": ["9aa908eaed2298ea185056ddf109218ab5993c25"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45432": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging a9d3ddf164c6726e0fa285680bf0cb697f20ac8a with FIREFOX-ANDROID_158_0b1_BUILD2 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "d5647c7f1a01fc4000cc8b084c54b1d0c6219dd0", "git_parents": ["9aa908eaed2298ea185056ddf109218ab5993c25"], "node": "de08fd4b80267d0af74b977e80d1777448dbdb3d", "parents": ["98a3a541f695fea2fcc6cd7d85d1aa55fc37ab63"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790610191, "git_changesets": ["d5647c7f1a01fc4000cc8b084c54b1d0c6219dd0"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45433": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging a9d3ddf164c6726e0fa285680bf0cb697f20ac8a with FIREFOX-ANDROID_158_0b1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "d910ff74e32c340e9daeb4cc907cf924208d9f88", "git_parents": ["d5647c7f1a01fc4000cc8b084c54b1d0c6219dd0"], "node": "6737b3d4be990db41acd040cb1a1f7455c86367e", "parents": ["de08fd4b80267d0af74b977e80d1777448dbdb3d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790622921, "git_changesets": ["d910ff74e32c340e9daeb4cc907cf924208d9f88"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45434": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging a9d3ddf164c6726e0fa285680bf0cb697f20ac8a with FIREFOX_158_0b1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "8d9afb3c74c2c80ff945661b30feff5248dd57fc", "git_parents": ["d910ff74e32c340e9daeb4cc907cf924208d9f88"], "node": "2448d1b9cb5d9965764d702662609103a7ba8810", "parents": ["6737b3d4be990db41acd040cb1a1f7455c86367e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790623611, "git_changesets": ["8d9afb3c74c2c80ff945661b30feff5248dd57fc"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45435": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging a9d3ddf164c6726e0fa285680bf0cb697f20ac8a with DEVEDITION_158_0b1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "500bb43d09af48219d6f91746b8026cf318e410b", "git_parents": ["8d9afb3c74c2c80ff945661b30feff5248dd57fc"], "node": "38a84ed27b45f218545beb06cba4fa9f78100320", "parents": ["2448d1b9cb5d9965764d702662609103a7ba8810"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790627483, "git_changesets": ["500bb43d09af48219d6f91746b8026cf318e410b"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45436": {"changesets": [{"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Cover every reachable chain state of FindFirstScrollable(). r=botond\n\nFindFirstScrollable() decides which frame a gesture is applied to, and the\nlast patch in this series changes that decision. Land the tests first so\nthat patch shows exactly which outcomes change.\n\nAdd a fixture over a three-level chain of nested scroll frames\n(innermost -\u003e middle -\u003e root content) and a table-driven test over the\nstates each frame can be observed in: overscroll-behavior of auto, contain,\nchain or none, crossed with having room to scroll, being at the end of a\nrange, and having no range at all.\n\nThe rows marked FIXME record today's behaviour, which is the bug. The last\npatch updates them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319841\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "1e114ddc265f1f40838e278bba686dc883393246", "git_parents": ["b478a70dbe9b20189bb57f12c05bc0d6a8f323bd"], "node": "be628755877fc43eb1f26bd5e8a48613a1489f30", "parents": ["5fafebaaa5bc47d17a93970fb6ce60e0e98ee788"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Test per-axis overscroll-behavior in FindFirstScrollable(). r=botond\n\nThe table added by the previous patch keeps overscroll-behavior uniform\nacross the two axes, which never produces a partially narrowed\naOutAllowedScrollDirections. So this patch covers the asymmetric cases\nseparately, one test per mechanism in the function that works per axis, and\na comment maps each mechanism to the test that covers it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319842\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp"], "git_node": "673fe3ef123cbaf14419a4175d5f44f77c8e362c", "git_parents": ["1e114ddc265f1f40838e278bba686dc883393246"], "node": "64664a46e09de476f2271ed7ce57ab1b56d1b80c", "parents": ["be628755877fc43eb1f26bd5e8a48613a1489f30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Test zero-delta and non-pan input in FindFirstScrollable(). r=botond\n\nTwo cases the table cannot express, because they are about the input rather\nthan the chain.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319843\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp"], "git_node": "9027ade3648e0ae7a83437a7bc3f083bd6b6178a", "git_parents": ["673fe3ef123cbaf14419a4175d5f44f77c8e362c"], "node": "f6efe0cbd7c388e531aa861e9b676402525d6631", "parents": ["64664a46e09de476f2271ed7ce57ab1b56d1b80c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Add mochitests for overscroll-behavior during overscroll handoff. r=botond\n\nCover what the user actually sees: pan with native touchpad events and read\nthe overscrolled scroll ids out of the compositor's APZ test data.\n\nSpecifically, this patch includes a mochitest which reproduces the original\nbug and also mochitests which check various combinations of overscroll-behavior\nin nested scrollers.\n\nWhere that is not what happens today the assertion is todo(), and the last\npatch in this series turns those into ok().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319844\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/apz_test_utils.js", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_chain_no_effect.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_pan_during_overscroll_animation.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_three_scrollers.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_two_scrollers.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_in_subscroller.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_stuck_pan_end.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/test_group_overscroll_behavior.html"], "git_node": "8b3900bb66529a90f42252ae849368fba4b532e4", "git_parents": ["9027ade3648e0ae7a83437a7bc3f083bd6b6178a"], "node": "a6daf16150f26b132c6b6334671505abae0ed5de", "parents": ["f6efe0cbd7c388e531aa861e9b676402525d6631"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Let a non-root scroll frame take the overscroll effect. r=botond\n\nFindFirstScrollable() has the two problems below, and the bug needs both\nof them.\n\nFirst, when no APZC in the handoff chain can be scrolled by the event, the\nfunction only ever considered the root content APZC as the frame that may\nshow an overscroll effect instead. So `none` on the root suppressed a\nsubframe's own overscroll as well, even though the subframe's own\noverscroll-behavior permits it.\n\nSecondly, aOutAllowedScrollDirections does not consistently mean one\nthing. The caller rebuilds the handoff chain from the returned APZC, so\nthe value should carry only the restrictions of the APZCs that drop out\nof the chain, because those are the ones that can no longer enforce their\nown overscroll-behavior when the scroll is dispatched (CallDispatchScroll()\napplies it per axis at every handoff). But the old code also folded the\nreturned APZC's own overscroll-behavior into it, and left it narrowed.\nSo null and empty can be returned at the same time.\n\nTogether they cause the freeze reported in Bug 1860662. When a sub scroll\ncontainer is allowed to overscroll while the root is not, and the sub\ncontainer is at its edge and the user pans further in that direction,\nthe first problem means only the root is considered as a candidate for\nthe effect, and it is not allowed one, so null is returned. By then the\nsecond problem has left aOutAllowedScrollDirections emptied by the root's\n`none`. An empty PanGestureBlockState::mAllowedScrollDirections makes\nGetDisplacementsForPanGesture() produce a zero displacement in\nCallDispatchScroll() for every event in the pan block, so the whole\ngesture appears frozen until the fingers are lifted.\n\nThis patch solves both. For the first, split the function into two\npasses:\n\n  1. innermost to outermost, looking for a frame the event can actually\n     scroll, accumulating the handoff-allowed directions as before.\n  2. if there is none, outermost to innermost over the frames the first\n     pass reached, looking for a frame that can show an overscroll\n     effect, governed by that frame's own overscroll-behavior\n     intersected with the directions handoff still allowed when the\n     first pass entered it.\n\nThe second pass starts at the outermost frame the gesture can still\nreach rather than at the root content frame, and falls back inwards. That\nmatches how the overscroll is applied at dispatch time (see\nAttemptScroll()).\n\nFor the second, report only the handoff restrictions of the frames that\nprecede the returned one, and report both directions when null is\nreturned. The chain is not rebuilt then, nothing drops out of it, and\nthere is nothing to carry. This also addresses the asymmetry noted in\nBug 1860662 comment 12.\n\nTwo consequences worth spelling out:\n- `none` on an ancestor no longer suppresses a descendant's overscroll.\n  The effect goes to the outermost reachable frame that permits one.\n- `contain` on a subframe now shows a local overscroll effect on that\n  subframe, which is what the property means, i.e. no chaining, but the\n  effect is permitted.\n\nUpdate the gtest table and the mochitest expectations accordingly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319845\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.h", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestPanning.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_pan_during_overscroll_animation.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_three_scrollers.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_two_scrollers.html"], "git_node": "c218ff4e06b7c347be923afb78bd0919002b0bb8", "git_parents": ["8b3900bb66529a90f42252ae849368fba4b532e4"], "node": "b2dfb9dc7e6e106679919f36d0e16fd730ad5e9d", "parents": ["a6daf16150f26b132c6b6334671505abae0ed5de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Botond Ballo \u003cbotond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Additional test cases exercising a direction reversal mid-gesture. r=canalun\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329328\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp"], "git_node": "d58c8598609a53a69a0574b59674407a1f7fb490", "git_parents": ["c218ff4e06b7c347be923afb78bd0919002b0bb8"], "node": "8db582f346471d690d753201857cb52272ac3f1b", "parents": ["b2dfb9dc7e6e106679919f36d0e16fd730ad5e9d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074812 - Create new report broken site related regression UI tests r=jajohnson,aaronmt,android-reviewers,rebecatudor273\n\nCreated 4 new \"regression\" UI tests:\n\nverifyTheReportBrokenSiteFormWithNoReasonSelectedTest\nverifyTheReportBrokenSiteURLIsNotSavedOnDismissTest\nverifyTheReportBrokenSiteFormAfterSelectingReasonInLandscapeTest\nverifyTheReportBrokenSiteFormAfterChangingTheReasonTest\nAll 4 UI tests successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\n\u2757 Added a new test tag and needs to be reviewed by someone from the development team\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328458\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/VerbContractTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/core/Verbs.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/WebCompatReporterSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/MainMenuTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/ReportBrokenSiteTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/BrokenSiteReporterTestTags.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/ui/ReadOnlyUrlField.kt"], "git_node": "c1ec4a285306d848175fa4eaea9b3461d9c9530f", "git_parents": ["d58c8598609a53a69a0574b59674407a1f7fb490"], "node": "df78c00f4d0136a6f8652e22f33af9bcc9cf464e", "parents": ["8db582f346471d690d753201857cb52272ac3f1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068991: Let llvm-objcopy and llvm-strip copy LC_DYLD_ENVIRONMENT load commands. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nllvm-objcopy rejects LC_DYLD_ENVIRONMENT as an unsupported load command, so the packaging step's llvm-strip fails on any Mach-O executable linked with -dyld_env. The load command only carries a string, like LC_LOAD_DYLINKER, so it can be copied unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329528\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/clang-22.json", "build/build-clang/clang-23.json", "build/build-clang/clang-trunk.json", "build/build-clang/llvm-objcopy-macho-dyld-environment.patch"], "git_node": "1553fae0ec50872409a42b1bd14589a1f0f9a7a3", "git_parents": ["c1ec4a285306d848175fa4eaea9b3461d9c9530f"], "node": "d06dc7e3aca7f6a2d7d49a2b74f28ac21348e654", "parents": ["df78c00f4d0136a6f8652e22f33af9bcc9cf464e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068991: Load Safari's staged frameworks on older macOS so ASWebAuthenticationSession requests can be decoded. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nOn macOS 10.15 the ASWebAuthenticationSession broker runs the newer AuthenticationServices that Safari updates install in /Library/Apple/System/Library/StagedFrameworks/Safari, and the system copy that Firefox loads fails to decode its messages. The broker then retries in a tight loop, which is what keeps Firefox in front in bug 2075199. The firefox executable now carries a DYLD_VERSIONED_FRAMEWORK_PATH load command for that folder, as Safari's executable does on macOS 10.15 and 12, so dyld uses a framework from it only when it is newer than the system copy. Safari updates for macOS 11 and 12 use the same folder. Where it doesn't exist, nothing changes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329358\n", "files": ["browser/app/moz.build"], "git_node": "db6b9d29f685627e260756a1044baf45fdce6b5d", "git_parents": ["1553fae0ec50872409a42b1bd14589a1f0f9a7a3"], "node": "8ea4ddb2f3f132e9fcd0d42a30f70245c277c8c3", "parents": ["d06dc7e3aca7f6a2d7d49a2b74f28ac21348e654"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1860662 - Additional test cases exercising a direction reversal mid-gesture. r=canalun\" for causing android build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit d58c8598609a53a69a0574b59674407a1f7fb490.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1860662 - Let a non-root scroll frame take the overscroll effect. r=botond\"\n\nThis reverts commit c218ff4e06b7c347be923afb78bd0919002b0bb8.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1860662 - Add mochitests for overscroll-behavior during overscroll handoff. r=botond\"\n\nThis reverts commit 8b3900bb66529a90f42252ae849368fba4b532e4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1860662 - Test zero-delta and non-pan input in FindFirstScrollable(). r=botond\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9027ade3648e0ae7a83437a7bc3f083bd6b6178a.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1860662 - Test per-axis overscroll-behavior in FindFirstScrollable(). r=botond\"\n\nThis reverts commit 673fe3ef123cbaf14419a4175d5f44f77c8e362c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1860662 - Cover every reachable chain state of FindFirstScrollable(). r=botond\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1e114ddc265f1f40838e278bba686dc883393246.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.h", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestPanning.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/moz.build", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/apz_test_utils.js", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_chain_no_effect.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_pan_during_overscroll_animation.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_three_scrollers.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_two_scrollers.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_in_subscroller.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_stuck_pan_end.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/test_group_overscroll_behavior.html"], "git_node": "9cb33e121eced426401715944d8ad3b6dbdb8eb4", "git_parents": ["db6b9d29f685627e260756a1044baf45fdce6b5d"], "node": "14e53bd4165fc5ba9dcb8dfb2036cf2d99574088", "parents": ["8ea4ddb2f3f132e9fcd0d42a30f70245c277c8c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 5724516b2c989b6977126db7250b141df2a6cddb\naf -\u003e 5724516b2c989b6977126db7250b141df2a6cddb\nan -\u003e 5724516b2c989b6977126db7250b141df2a6cddb\nar -\u003e 5724516b2c98