, "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Cover every reachable chain state of FindFirstScrollable(). r=botond\n\nFindFirstScrollable() decides which frame a gesture is applied to, and the\nlast patch in this series changes that decision. Land the tests first so\nthat patch shows exactly which outcomes change.\n\nAdd a fixture over a three-level chain of nested scroll frames\n(innermost -\u003e middle -\u003e root content) and a table-driven test over the\nstates each frame can be observed in: overscroll-behavior of auto, contain,\nchain or none, crossed with having room to scroll, being at the end of a\nrange, and having no range at all.\n\nThe rows marked FIXME record today's behaviour, which is the bug. The last\npatch updates them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319841\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "282e9a32bf06d1f9a499a376fa75de8f583f6385", "git_parents": ["6698511b6b479211d8c3f2d9f11884c3cea09fbe"], "node": "fd90de4d0abc53fed13871645ecd021994ce7e71", "parents": ["359681c05e3df838c9527624d5d4eb8121ac6b1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Test per-axis overscroll-behavior in FindFirstScrollable(). r=botond\n\nThe table added by the previous patch keeps overscroll-behavior uniform\nacross the two axes, which never produces a partially narrowed\naOutAllowedScrollDirections. So this patch covers the asymmetric cases\nseparately, one test per mechanism in the function that works per axis, and\na comment maps each mechanism to the test that covers it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319842\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp"], "git_node": "6ebeb730146484c927b886a0e86c0d8f06a9b402", "git_parents": ["282e9a32bf06d1f9a499a376fa75de8f583f6385"], "node": "c631c1d79537c7125c342f9477c3f2c79baa5cf3", "parents": ["fd90de4d0abc53fed13871645ecd021994ce7e71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Test zero-delta and non-pan input in FindFirstScrollable(). r=botond\n\nTwo cases the table cannot express, because they are about the input rather\nthan the chain.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319843\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp"], "git_node": "d933543de7de031d6a392e0f99b0b89a56b72a9e", "git_parents": ["6ebeb730146484c927b886a0e86c0d8f06a9b402"], "node": "b0ab24495199604eff73a92dc21e02358bd76c98", "parents": ["c631c1d79537c7125c342f9477c3f2c79baa5cf3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Add mochitests for overscroll-behavior during overscroll handoff. r=botond\n\nCover what the user actually sees: pan with native touchpad events and read\nthe overscrolled scroll ids out of the compositor's APZ test data.\n\nSpecifically, this patch includes a mochitest which reproduces the original\nbug and also mochitests which check various combinations of overscroll-behavior\nin nested scrollers.\n\nWhere that is not what happens today the assertion is todo(), and the last\npatch in this series turns those into ok().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319844\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/apz_test_utils.js", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_chain_no_effect.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_pan_during_overscroll_animation.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_three_scrollers.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_two_scrollers.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_in_subscroller.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_stuck_pan_end.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/test_group_overscroll_behavior.html"], "git_node": "1bd0d0856253022d32b438171a0d44229781ddb0", "git_parents": ["d933543de7de031d6a392e0f99b0b89a56b72a9e"], "node": "66a7d9605646cc84e1fca9ca4fd2a52f4e0a1fe5", "parents": ["b0ab24495199604eff73a92dc21e02358bd76c98"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Let a non-root scroll frame take the overscroll effect. r=botond\n\nFindFirstScrollable() has the two problems below, and the bug needs both\nof them.\n\nFirst, when no APZC in the handoff chain can be scrolled by the event, the\nfunction only ever considered the root content APZC as the frame that may\nshow an overscroll effect instead. So `none` on the root suppressed a\nsubframe's own overscroll as well, even though the subframe's own\noverscroll-behavior permits it.\n\nSecondly, aOutAllowedScrollDirections does not consistently mean one\nthing. The caller rebuilds the handoff chain from the returned APZC, so\nthe value should carry only the restrictions of the APZCs that drop out\nof the chain, because those are the ones that can no longer enforce their\nown overscroll-behavior when the scroll is dispatched (CallDispatchScroll()\napplies it per axis at every handoff). But the old code also folded the\nreturned APZC's own overscroll-behavior into it, and left it narrowed.\nSo null and empty can be returned at the same time.\n\nTogether they cause the freeze reported in Bug 1860662. When a sub scroll\ncontainer is allowed to overscroll while the root is not, and the sub\ncontainer is at its edge and the user pans further in that direction,\nthe first problem means only the root is considered as a candidate for\nthe effect, and it is not allowed one, so null is returned. By then the\nsecond problem has left aOutAllowedScrollDirections emptied by the root's\n`none`. An empty PanGestureBlockState::mAllowedScrollDirections makes\nGetDisplacementsForPanGesture() produce a zero displacement in\nCallDispatchScroll() for every event in the pan block, so the whole\ngesture appears frozen until the fingers are lifted.\n\nThis patch solves both. For the first, split the function into two\npasses:\n\n  1. innermost to outermost, looking for a frame the event can actually\n     scroll, accumulating the handoff-allowed directions as before.\n  2. if there is none, outermost to innermost over the frames the first\n     pass reached, looking for a frame that can show an overscroll\n     effect, governed by that frame's own overscroll-behavior\n     intersected with the directions handoff still allowed when the\n     first pass entered it.\n\nThe second pass starts at the outermost frame the gesture can still\nreach rather than at the root content frame, and falls back inwards. That\nmatches how the overscroll is applied at dispatch time (see\nAttemptScroll()).\n\nFor the second, report only the handoff restrictions of the frames that\nprecede the returned one, and report both directions when null is\nreturned. The chain is not rebuilt then, nothing drops out of it, and\nthere is nothing to carry. This also addresses the asymmetry noted in\nBug 1860662 comment 12.\n\nTwo consequences worth spelling out:\n- `none` on an ancestor no longer suppresses a descendant's overscroll.\n  The effect goes to the outermost reachable frame that permits one.\n- `contain` on a subframe now shows a local overscroll effect on that\n  subframe, which is what the property means, i.e. no chaining, but the\n  effect is permitted.\n\nUpdate the gtest table and the mochitest expectations accordingly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319845\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.h", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestPanning.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_pan_during_overscroll_animation.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_three_scrollers.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_overscroll_behavior_two_scrollers.html"], "git_node": "d470ef883173a59d3f6712752e8b842096e2fb6e", "git_parents": ["1bd0d0856253022d32b438171a0d44229781ddb0"], "node": "b3010c334a52ce8adbf4e521d812c360f58feead", "parents": ["66a7d9605646cc84e1fca9ca4fd2a52f4e0a1fe5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Botond Ballo \u003cbotond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860662 - Additional test cases exercising a direction reversal mid-gesture. r=canalun\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329328\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestOverscrollHandoffChain.cpp"], "git_node": "0741fd134221c83fcb814d8c7ea77e7607a541a0", "git_parents": ["d470ef883173a59d3f6712752e8b842096e2fb6e"], "node": "9f9c929d34b8cbdf06031a64554a032b154b94aa", "parents": ["b3010c334a52ce8adbf4e521d812c360f58feead"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075646 - Add a bench subcommand to wrench. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nwrench bench repeatedly builds and/or renders the frame of a yaml file or\ncapture and reports timings, as a basis for frame building and renderer\nperformance work.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329237\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/profiler.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/init.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/args.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/bench.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/main.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs"], "git_node": "fa01ff41e547d98df8b848ebd4326d2fcf18d534", "git_parents": ["0741fd134221c83fcb814d8c7ea77e7607a541a0"], "node": "59793d7ed462430bf023423fdbbbf2ed185eeb7d", "parents": ["9f9c929d34b8cbdf06031a64554a032b154b94aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Vandyke \u003ckzar@kzar.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1973071 - Expand AddonManager.getInstallForURL's add-on validation r=robwu\n\nAdd optional `id` and `type` options to `AddonManager.getInstallForURL()`, so\nthat the caller can specify the expected add-on type and ID. When provided,\nthose details should be checked against the provided add-on before it is\ninstalled.\n\nAlso expand enforcement of the existing `version` option for fresh installs and\nmanual upgrades. Previously, that was only checked when the existing add-on was\nalready known (e.g. updates via `addon.findUpdates()`).\n\nFix some related tests, one of which passed a mismatched version, and some\nothers that failed to pass through the add-on name + version due to a typo.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326452\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_AMBrowserExtensionsImport.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/AddonManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIInstall.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_AMBrowserExtensionsImport.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_AMBrowserExtensionsImport.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_install.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_install_expected_addon_details.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "72527647512e84e4457c50a9a0e7fa02f5fac1bc", "git_parents": ["fa01ff41e547d98df8b848ebd4326d2fcf18d534"], "node": "e00253623cccceb6233ae1ec908456db37e78347", "parents": ["59793d7ed462430bf023423fdbbbf2ed185eeb7d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075309: Store ID is not mismatched if profiles.ini does not contain an ID for the current profile. r=jhirsch\n\nUnless the user has used selectable profiles it is normal for profiles.ini to contain no store ID for the current profile. This should not be considered a mismatch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328910\n", "files": ["toolkit/profile/ProfileMetrics.sys.mjs", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/test_profile_metrics_store_id_null.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "98cdd1f71b6fd62dbc18a40a67b9614547aeb8e6", "git_parents": ["72527647512e84e4457c50a9a0e7fa02f5fac1bc"], "node": "1d16569aaa156af33d9e47742052dfdc7294b20f", "parents": ["e00253623cccceb6233ae1ec908456db37e78347"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064612 - Add download, ping, rel, relList and referrerPolicy attributes to MathMLAnchorElement r=emilio,webidl,smaug\n\nMove referrerpolicy attribute parsing to Element::ParseAttribute.\n\nEnable creating ReferrerPolicy from referrerpolicy attribte for SVG a element.\n\nUpdate WPT tests and expectations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317723\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-mathml/a_referrerpolicy.html", "browser/base/content/test/browser-mathml/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-mathml/browser_a_referrerpolicy.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-mathml/browser_mathml_download.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-mathml/download_page_mathml.html", "browser/base/moz.build", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsPingListener.cpp", "dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/mathml/MathMLAnchorElement.cpp", "dom/mathml/MathMLAnchorElement.h", "dom/security/ReferrerInfo.cpp", "dom/webidl/MathMLAnchorElement.webidl", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/lists/DOMTokenList-coverage-for-attributes.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-ping.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-rel-getter-setter.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-rel-policy.html.ini"], "git_node": "fdc1e3eb487f0212458d77e81f65e0febed60838", "git_parents": ["98cdd1f71b6fd62dbc18a40a67b9614547aeb8e6"], "node": "046e58cb6dc30bd37fedd9092daaa343dc4335e1", "parents": ["1d16569aaa156af33d9e47742052dfdc7294b20f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007259 - Enable test_caches_delete_cleanup_after_shutdown.py in CI. r=whimboo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329569\n", "files": ["dom/cache/test/marionette/manifest.toml"], "git_node": "288be5f0fdbf90862ebafe9677bd495c03bbd648", "git_parents": ["fdc1e3eb487f0212458d77e81f65e0febed60838"], "node": "5f88fd47d86301617c8d473a0a6cd826eb8eac4e", "parents": ["046e58cb6dc30bd37fedd9092daaa343dc4335e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sarah Clements \u003csclements@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066086 - Fix hide tabs and sidebar logic and refactor sidebar state logic r=sfoster,jsudiaman,sidebar-reviewers,nsharpley,sessionstore-reviewers,kcochrane,extension-reviewers,rpl\n\n* Refactor sidebar visibility and sidebar state logic, removing multiple properties in browser-sidebar and sidebarState that handle launcher visibility\n* Update test coverage, particularly for hide-sidebar setting\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327791\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_uidensity_auto_compact.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_sidebarAction.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/session.schema.json", "browser/components/sidebar/SidebarManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/SidebarState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/docs/index.md", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-main.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_adopt_sidebar_from_opener.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_customize_sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_launcher_hidden_restore.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_panel_states.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_prefs.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/marionette/test_last_used_sidebar_panel.py", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/unit/test_sidebar_state.js"], "git_node": "0896f9cd23e07a8edaac747402eb15daf1ec1f4b", "git_parents": ["288be5f0fdbf90862ebafe9677bd495c03bbd648"], "node": "76a26ecfc701a0e63a0fe80b5b54a71ee96e49b8", "parents": ["5f88fd47d86301617c8d473a0a6cd826eb8eac4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "pstanciu \u003cpstanciu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2066086 - Fix hide tabs and sidebar logic and refactor sidebar state logic r=sfoster,jsudiaman,sidebar-reviewers,nsharpley,sessionstore-reviewers,kcochrane,extension-reviewers,rpl\" for causing bc failures @ browser_remove_sidebar_button_and_sidebar.js\n\nThis reverts commit 0896f9cd23e07a8edaac747402eb15daf1ec1f4b.\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_uidensity_auto_compact.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_sidebarAction.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/session.schema.json", "browser/components/sidebar/SidebarManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/SidebarState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/docs/index.md", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-main.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_adopt_sidebar_from_opener.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_customize_sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_launcher_hidden_restore.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_panel_states.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_prefs.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/marionette/test_last_used_sidebar_panel.py", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/unit/test_sidebar_state.js"], "git_node": "4bd4ba1850d92cf8f8f5ddf7f41aa40f1ad0cec6", "git_parents": ["0896f9cd23e07a8edaac747402eb15daf1ec1f4b"], "node": "1cddf1f4902c00ba71970b686662d46857ea1efd", "parents": ["76a26ecfc701a0e63a0fe80b5b54a71ee96e49b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maryam \u003cmomar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1999534 - Remove MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT(XRE_IsParentProcess()) in UpdateAntiTrackingInfoForChannel. r=emz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329561\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/AntiTrackingUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "474b0249d6ded6f14f0b539a3a1bdc806a1f0da2", "git_parents": ["4bd4ba1850d92cf8f8f5ddf7f41aa40f1ad0cec6"], "node": "7138bbe94c809b01bd838aa38b0c28dfc94ab19b", "parents": ["1cddf1f4902c00ba71970b686662d46857ea1efd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072245 - Wire the testsummary log into the web-platform-tests mozharness script r=ahal\n\nweb_platform_tests.py discarded the test_summary_file path returned by\nget_indexed_logs() and never called append_test_summary(), so wpt jobs\n(regular and test-verify) uploaded no summary.jsonl, unlike mochitest,\nxpcshell and the Android harnesses. Pass --log-testsummary to wptrunner\nand concatenate each harness run into summary.jsonl like the other\nscripts do.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326198\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/scripts/web_platform_tests.py"], "git_node": "33d8a86f715562bb3dfe123a6647c3e62cc53635", "git_parents": ["474b0249d6ded6f14f0b539a3a1bdc806a1f0da2"], "node": "326d8464ae75289b17852313fe758730aa769052", "parents": ["7138bbe94c809b01bd838aa38b0c28dfc94ab19b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076059 - Fix the ignored AssertCalled annotation in GeckoSessionTestRuleTest. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nAn annotation on a lambda compiled to invokedynamic is not retained at runtime, so the test harness never saw\nthe AssertCalled(count = 1) on the Runnable lambda. Kotlin 2.5 warns about this.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329529\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/GeckoSessionTestRuleTest.kt"], "git_node": "2dcfeec315e47fdf428f61eaf7a0796854c4ed4b", "git_parents": ["33d8a86f715562bb3dfe123a6647c3e62cc53635"], "node": "e554a6e2d37c3b07a7b7f9a6a2f53ea6d4c51bfa", "parents": ["326d8464ae75289b17852313fe758730aa769052"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076059 - Use the class name instead of the name of a javaClass property reference. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\n`X::javaClass.name` is the name of the property reference, the string \"javaClass\", which the\nGeckoActivityDelegate and NimbusExperimentDelegate loggers and a fenix idling resource used as their tag or\nname. Kotlin 2.5 warns about this and language version 2.6 makes it an error. Two more fenix idling resources\nwith the same problem are unused, so remove them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329530\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/activity/GeckoActivityDelegate.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/main/java/mozilla/components/experiment/NimbusExperimentDelegate.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/idlingresource/AddonsInstallingIdlingResource.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/idlingresource/AddonsLoadingIdlingResource.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/idlingresource/NetworkConnectionIdlingResource.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/reviewprompt/ReviewPromptMiddlewareTriggerCriteriaTest.kt"], "git_node": "431daad3c1e4c1a477fec0d4949573989652c564", "git_parents": ["2dcfeec315e47fdf428f61eaf7a0796854c4ed4b"], "node": "fc874a02e40cc92dde5a252950bca4b9ef2ddd69", "parents": ["e554a6e2d37c3b07a7b7f9a6a2f53ea6d4c51bfa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076059 - Give platform-typed when subjects a non-null type. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nKotlin 2.5 warns about a `when` on a platform-typed subject that has no null branch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329531\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/menu2/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/menu2/adapter/MenuCandidateListAdapter.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/exceptions/ExceptionsAdapter.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/searchsuggestions/ui/SearchSuggestionsFragment.kt"], "git_node": "e13a666d17555ec53611e81178d2e2c513c20020", "git_parents": ["431daad3c1e4c1a477fec0d4949573989652c564"], "node": "c3e1b3c0c78eb2c83c00e6c9b0e1074086871e22", "parents": ["fc874a02e40cc92dde5a252950bca4b9ef2ddd69"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076059 - Replace the deprecated kotlin.test assertNotNull overload taking a block. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nKotlin 2.5 deprecates it in favor of assertNotNull(...).let { }.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329532\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/prompt/GeckoPromptDelegateTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/action/ContentActionTest.kt"], "git_node": "f2e037a3bfd766bd9a89f8e5c309db8bc80f7f0b", "git_parents": ["e13a666d17555ec53611e81178d2e2c513c20020"], "node": "f9cbdfcbe24099c1b758b85d9295ebba90a87533", "parents": ["c3e1b3c0c78eb2c83c00e6c9b0e1074086871e22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Frederik Braun \u003cfbraun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062999 - Remove telemetry mirroring for the security.ui probe r=tschuster,rpl,chumphreys\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325765\n", "files": ["dom/security/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json", "toolkit/components/telemetry/histogram-allowlists.json"], "git_node": "7bd27e5a2a24abac0deaece464383f09c778ad5e", "git_parents": ["f2e037a3bfd766bd9a89f8e5c309db8bc80f7f0b"], "node": "9f4d2e77f72d88ca55584dea5c0ac5ac09debd20", "parents": ["f9cbdfcbe24099c1b758b85d9295ebba90a87533"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029784: Ensure frame table is valid after adjusting selection r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327502\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsFrameSelection.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/input-events/table-selection-crash.html"], "git_node": "48224bb2ad2f87f7de3c598786956cfb4d48c4e5", "git_parents": ["7bd27e5a2a24abac0deaece464383f09c778ad5e"], "node": "a0792c8a4e2248765fb4511b031155fe66c810c8", "parents": ["9f4d2e77f72d88ca55584dea5c0ac5ac09debd20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "pollymce \u003cpmceldowney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073095 - make the home screen tests safe to be run with different configurations of pinned and sponsored shortcuts r=mcarare\n\nSponsored shortcuts were located by their absolute position in the top sites list, which assumes a fixed number of pinned shortcuts precedes them. getSponsoredShortcutTitle and verifySponsoredShortcutDetails now take an index among the sponsored shortcuts only, resolved through the sponsored label that only sponsored shortcuts carry.\n\nTopSitesTest's setUp asserted the entire default top sites list where, as its comment says, it only needs to wait for the list to be displayed.\n\nThis makes the tests more resilient to changes in top sites and will allow these tests to pass on a nightly build as well as a debug build.\n\n[try after rebase is running here]( https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=4eed3db2680212ca0e700810435c932a029d1bfd)\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/367\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/AppAndSystemHelper.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/Constants.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/DataGenerationHelper.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SponsoredShortcutsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/TopSitesTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/robots/HomeScreenRobot.kt"], "git_node": "a187dc02d4c42b62b1f8590ba8de51cf5b8a44c8", "git_parents": ["48224bb2ad2f87f7de3c598786956cfb4d48c4e5"], "node": "e145ba3c35526e6e68d204eeab6d872816a1d4c5", "parents": ["a0792c8a4e2248765fb4511b031155fe66c810c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070865 - Add a profile-capture agent skill for recording Firefox profiles r=ai4dev-reviewers,profiler-reviewers,suhaib,canova\n\n`profiler-analysis` covers analyzing a profile that already exists, but\nnothing covered recording one. `profile-capture` records through the\nfirefox-devtools MCP and hands the profile to `profiler-analysis`.\n\nProfiles recorded through the MCP skip the profiler front-end's objdir\nsymbolication, so profiler-analysis needs to load them with\n`--with-samply`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328513\n", "files": [".agents/skills/profile-capture/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/profile-capture/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "073faff7f138a6fdcdf24ba5aafe119b1558a762", "git_parents": ["a187dc02d4c42b62b1f8590ba8de51cf5b8a44c8"], "node": "5b0e1b17d0d3fb0e02b9c39d00852c6f756b1c09", "parents": ["e145ba3c35526e6e68d204eeab6d872816a1d4c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Jakobi \u003cajakobi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075197 - Return SnapTarget*s instead of Maybe\u003cnscoord\u003e from GetCandidateFromLastTargets r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328831\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollSnap.cpp"], "git_node": "142b7680feab19c3da71825ea399a9d43257847d", "git_parents": ["073faff7f138a6fdcdf24ba5aafe119b1558a762"], "node": "3598356d38de0846a625c1203c40ac231cb8ecda", "parents": ["5b0e1b17d0d3fb0e02b9c39d00852c6f756b1c09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2075197 - Return SnapTarget*s instead of Maybe\u003cnscoord\u003e from GetCandidateFromLastTargets r=layout-reviewers,dshin\" for causing reftest failures at crashtests/323386-1.html\n\nThis reverts commit 142b7680feab19c3da71825ea399a9d43257847d.\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollSnap.cpp"], "git_node": "13dd2a70c14b0a01ed3a4d9ffedb68e8f8b72697", "git_parents": ["142b7680feab19c3da71825ea399a9d43257847d"], "node": "cc002fe021328e73bc306d6e3761c0a064b59590", "parents": ["3598356d38de0846a625c1203c40ac231cb8ecda"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072203 - Keep the objdir of the clang-tidy source-test tasks out of the cached checkout. r=taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau DONTBUILD\n\nThese tasks leave MOZ_OBJDIR unset, so the objdir lands inside the checkout,\nwhich lives in a cache volume reused by later tasks on the same worker.\nrobustcheckout then purges the whole objdir as an ignored directory at the\nstart of every warm run, and the thousands of backend files written into the\ncache volume churn it for nothing.\n\nPut the objdir in the task-local workspace instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326148\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/source-test-clang-setup.sh"], "git_node": "259c00185af84d38a1c754955cb0c67ee0337aaa", "git_parents": ["13dd2a70c14b0a01ed3a4d9ffedb68e8f8b72697"], "node": "fff59e5ad4c904dcea96ada080a04779dd73575f", "parents": ["cc002fe021328e73bc306d6e3761c0a064b59590"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070483 - Fall back to a direct capture when a stored Ctrl+Tab thumbnail fails to load. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,sclements\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328688\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/browser-ctrlTab.js"], "git_node": "526d29b392eb04a7df02d95a9f00e2a58db07c56", "git_parents": ["259c00185af84d38a1c754955cb0c67ee0337aaa"], "node": "bec98524e2f7a6540ca587891b3e8e642bb38dd7", "parents": ["fff59e5ad4c904dcea96ada080a04779dd73575f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 780014 - Add startup_session_availability telemetry to help answer was there anything to restore? r=sessionstore-reviewers,sthompson\n\n- noFilesFound now also includes no legacy .js files found\n- Log and record telemetry for which session files we examined (stat-ing them all would regress startup performance)\n- New xpcshell test for SessionFile.read to verify it gives back the expected results given the files in the profile\n- New marionette test to check the telemtry for clean session restore and restore_session_once behavior is as expected\n- Updated the typelib artifacts\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326800\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionFile.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStartup.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/manifest.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/test_session_availability.py", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/test_session_availability.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.glean.d.ts"], "git_node": "d15046d1e1d59b5804bf43e1f64749f2051f0f8e", "git_parents": ["526d29b392eb04a7df02d95a9f00e2a58db07c56"], "node": "fa2408b79fbe54b9ed82eba151fb05e799f4ce56", "parents": ["bec98524e2f7a6540ca587891b3e8e642bb38dd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064354 - [webdriver-bidi] Implement the support for the \"prefers-color-scheme\" parameter in the \"emulation.setMediaFeaturesOverride\" command. r=webdriver-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328777\n", "files": ["remote/shared/messagehandler/sessiondata/SessionData.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/_configuration.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/emulation.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/windowglobal/emulation.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "bf947e18639691996b0e2a26d09f163f2c79d7a4", "git_parents": ["d15046d1e1d59b5804bf43e1f64749f2051f0f8e"], "node": "3d933c44a6024b1da0463f462ac920637b30db66", "parents": ["fa2408b79fbe54b9ed82eba151fb05e799f4ce56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064354 - [wdspec] Use \"prefers-color-scheme\" in the tests for the \"emulation.setMediaFeaturesOverride\" command. r=webdriver-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328781\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_media_features_override/contexts.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_media_features_override/features.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_media_features_override/global.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_media_features_override/invalid.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_media_features_override/user_contexts.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_media_features_override/conftest.py"], "git_node": "3df4680c3ab768aba8b36c87c3ddb51550ba927f", "git_parents": ["bf947e18639691996b0e2a26d09f163f2c79d7a4"], "node": "2b5355ef68d6edf09ad7fd4f5d9bcf8d681497c0", "parents": ["3d933c44a6024b1da0463f462ac920637b30db66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064354 - [wdspec] Add a test for existing iframes for the \"prefers-color-scheme\" feature and for an invalid feature name in the \"emulation.setMediaFeaturesOverride\" command. r=webdriver-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328782\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_media_features_override/contexts.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_media_features_override/invalid.py"], "git_node": "1de82b849a7963faf473e7f7115ce764847a1aa0", "git_parents": ["3df4680c3ab768aba8b36c87c3ddb51550ba927f"], "node": "534bab6edfac769c594dff05ac0543570655ec9f", "parents": ["2b5355ef68d6edf09ad7fd4f5d9bcf8d681497c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071241 - Remove panel-list's workaround for bug 2066409. r=tgiles,reusable-components-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329608\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.mjs"], "git_node": "0026b4f087f5585c736b3873a10497885b38d2fa", "git_parents": ["1de82b849a7963faf473e7f7115ce764847a1aa0"], "node": "bd8432bf4293ad28cb20291760fb22e8a81b29a9", "parents": ["534bab6edfac769c594dff05ac0543570655ec9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075053 - Share Gecko's system font logic with Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nServo will still not have any system font, but now it will use the same\nlogic as Gecko, avoiding a bunch of `#[cfg(feature = \"gecko\")]`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328709\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs"], "git_node": "30f2fd8a1a967c37c67008c0b5bf50884e9305d0", "git_parents": ["0026b4f087f5585c736b3873a10497885b38d2fa"], "node": "4a5ef8b34f176572acc13146eba140b8c15b12f4", "parents": ["bd8432bf4293ad28cb20291760fb22e8a81b29a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060428 - Part 10 - Quote the per directory linker flags passed to the Cargo linker wrapper r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\n`build/cargo-linker` splits `MOZ_CARGO_WRAP_LDFLAGS` with shell rules, so an\nunquoted Windows path lost its backslashes. The clang-cl coverage build links\n`clang_rt.profile` by absolute path and failed to find it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329510\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/rust_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_rust_commands.py"], "git_node": "b333202cd8d8385cb382c42404a03995dbc126ec", "git_parents": ["30f2fd8a1a967c37c67008c0b5bf50884e9305d0"], "node": "3b6a7b4f130a63b46201acce0b9ec88f9e513176", "parents": ["4a5ef8b34f176572acc13146eba140b8c15b12f4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790629385, "git_changesets": ["1e114ddc265f1f40838e278bba686dc883393246", "673fe3ef123cbaf14419a4175d5f44f77c8e362c", "9027ade3648e0ae7a83437a7bc3f083bd6b6178a", "8b3900bb66529a90f42252ae849368fba4b532e4", "c218ff4e06b7c347be923afb78bd0919002b0bb8", "d58c8598609a53a69a0574b59674407a1f7fb490", "c1ec4a285306d848175fa4eaea9b3461d9c9530f", "1553fae0ec50872409a42b1bd14589a1f0f9a7a3", "db6b9d29f685627e260756a1044baf45fdce6b5d", "9cb33e121eced426401715944d8ad3b6dbdb8eb4", "9bc55a377293e7771c86556989a5db748927da53", "6698511b6b479211d8c3f2d9f11884c3cea09fbe", "282e9a32bf06d1f9a499a376fa75de8f583f6385", "6ebeb730146484c927b886a0e86c0d8f06a9b402", "d933543de7de031d6a392e0f99b0b89a56b72a9e", "1bd0d0856253022d32b438171a0d44229781ddb0", "d470ef883173a59d3f6712752e8b842096e2fb6e", "0741fd134221c83fcb814d8c7ea77e7607a541a0", "fa01ff41e547d98df8b848ebd4326d2fcf18d534", "72527647512e84e4457c50a9a0e7fa02f5fac1bc", "98cdd1f71b6fd62dbc18a40a67b9614547aeb8e6", "fdc1e3eb487f0212458d77e81f65e0febed60838", "288be5f0fdbf90862ebafe9677bd495c03bbd648", "0896f9cd23e07a8edaac747402eb15daf1ec1f4b", "4bd4ba1850d92cf8f8f5ddf7f41aa40f1ad0cec6", "474b0249d6ded6f14f0b539a3a1bdc806a1f0da2", "33d8a86f715562bb3dfe123a6647c3e62cc53635", "2dcfeec315e47fdf428f61eaf7a0796854c4ed4b", "431daad3c1e4c1a477fec0d4949573989652c564", "e13a666d17555ec53611e81178d2e2c513c20020", "f2e037a3bfd766bd9a89f8e5c309db8bc80f7f0b", "7bd27e5a2a24abac0deaece464383f09c778ad5e", "48224bb2ad2f87f7de3c598786956cfb4d48c4e5", "a187dc02d4c42b62b1f8590ba8de51cf5b8a44c8", "073faff7f138a6fdcdf24ba5aafe119b1558a762", "142b7680feab19c3da71825ea399a9d43257847d", "13dd2a70c14b0a01ed3a4d9ffedb68e8f8b72697", "259c00185af84d38a1c754955cb0c67ee0337aaa", "526d29b392eb04a7df02d95a9f00e2a58db07c56", "d15046d1e1d59b5804bf43e1f64749f2051f0f8e", "bf947e18639691996b0e2a26d09f163f2c79d7a4", "3df4680c3ab768aba8b36c87c3ddb51550ba927f", "1de82b849a7963faf473e7f7115ce764847a1aa0", "0026b4f087f5585c736b3873a10497885b38d2fa", "30f2fd8a1a967c37c67008c0b5bf50884e9305d0", "b333202cd8d8385cb382c42404a03995dbc126ec"], "user": "amarc@mozilla.com"}, "45437": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Hynson \u003cmhynson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061871 - Add scrollbar inset for browser content area. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton,akulyk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317586\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css"], "git_node": "4579bceb72b0b840ba3ce55ef40e03e07596f957", "git_parents": ["b333202cd8d8385cb382c42404a03995dbc126ec"], "node": "47cc73fda4e89bd1ae3f107d6e807a966a09041c", "parents": ["3b6a7b4f130a63b46201acce0b9ec88f9e513176"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075971 - Propagate computed value errors due to lack of context properly. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nWhen we don't have the necessary context we should bail, not leave\nspecified values around.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329601\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/color/color_function.rs", "servo/components/style/color/component.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/calc.rs"], "git_node": "d03cad88b298524add6556819b638f54c9ac08bb", "git_parents": ["4579bceb72b0b840ba3ce55ef40e03e07596f957"], "node": "199ad6ca808785dd34f3c1f17057c5d08c9bb558", "parents": ["47cc73fda4e89bd1ae3f107d6e807a966a09041c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vanessa Prema \u003cvprema@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074592 - fix(pbw): Relay promo and basics spotlight fixes from QA r=tgiles,emcminn,desktop-theme-reviewers,omc-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329029\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/BrowserUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f127f0bac1cbcf0b61f2e2e82fedbcc7f0d6c3f2", "git_parents": ["d03cad88b298524add6556819b638f54c9ac08bb"], "node": "dfce7d5d3059e587c9c5886816b5a6027e19af51", "parents": ["199ad6ca808785dd34f3c1f17057c5d08c9bb558"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074540 - Avoid unsynchronized glMapBufferRange with Metal ANGLE on Radeon GFX10 GPUs. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe unsynchronized WebGLContext::BufferSubData path causes rendering\nglitches with Metal ANGLE on certain Radeon GPUs. Fall back to\nglBufferSubData on affected devices.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329596\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLBuffer.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLContext.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLContext.h", "gfx/gl/GLContextEGL.h", "gfx/gl/GLLibraryEGL.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLLibraryEGL.h"], "git_node": "00701cbab942403744abf6e4417a8cbaf7e30e08", "git_parents": ["f127f0bac1cbcf0b61f2e2e82fedbcc7f0d6c3f2"], "node": "c2e558acc66c32731ba4164e8a97c5a387ce1498", "parents": ["dfce7d5d3059e587c9c5886816b5a6027e19af51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074620 - Part 1: Add the Horoscopes widget strings r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328956\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "ddab26d81e093b5f7633921da6405b2d376013bd", "git_parents": ["00701cbab942403744abf6e4417a8cbaf7e30e08"], "node": "9f896c6ef4ce188411e6175f47ad4aff129d92ff", "parents": ["c2e558acc66c32731ba4164e8a97c5a387ce1498"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076206 - Remove unnecessary gecko-only guard for filter effect computation. r=TYLin\n\nNothing in there is Gecko-specific, afaict.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329616\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/specified/effects.rs"], "git_node": "7611dc768534c90870f939fb426f236ea11e1932", "git_parents": ["ddab26d81e093b5f7633921da6405b2d376013bd"], "node": "d3ff5a4ce95d6c211d58e45900e37d2c73a04a6d", "parents": ["9f896c6ef4ce188411e6175f47ad4aff129d92ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074921 - Remove extra space from the empty identity box r=desktop-theme-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328661\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/identity-block/identity-block.css"], "git_node": "516dd73da15fc39632577c6c73588b3cfffd73d9", "git_parents": ["7611dc768534c90870f939fb426f236ea11e1932"], "node": "4d1bf22b83d4545c31bbefc973309308b9fe387b", "parents": ["d3ff5a4ce95d6c211d58e45900e37d2c73a04a6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075971 - Test that element-context-requiring colors random() aren't parsed in OffscreenCanvas. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329613\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.em-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.em-1.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.em-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.em-2.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.em-3.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.em-3.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.em-4.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.em-4.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.random-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.random-1.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.random-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.random-2.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.random-3.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.random-3.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.random-4.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/fill-and-stroke-styles/2d.fillStyle.parse.invalid.no-context.random-4.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/tools/yaml/fill-and-stroke-styles.yaml"], "git_node": "681ef7aca34869d291df11a6ab0e9f955fe103f6", "git_parents": ["516dd73da15fc39632577c6c73588b3cfffd73d9"], "node": "b8eac3212006626c78e1b02bc0543f65e9cfcd42", "parents": ["4d1bf22b83d4545c31bbefc973309308b9fe387b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Schomburg \u003cdschomburg@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075384 - Ensure that Firefox is used to open FxQ pairing QR codes r=Roger,android-reviewers\n\nAdd an autoVerify intent filter to IntentReceiverActivity for https on\naccounts.firefox.com and accounts.stage.mozaws.net with a /pair path prefix.\nFxA already serves assetlinks.json for both hosts with the release, beta and\nnightly fingerprints, but Fenix only had scheme-only http/https filters, which\nAndroid cannot verify. This caused scanned pairing QR codes open in default\nbrowser instead of Firefox.\n\nThe new filter must precede the scheme-only filter. Android keeps only the\nfirst matching filter per activity and uses it to classify the app; with the\nscheme-only filter first, Fenix is treated as a generic browser and skipped\nduring App Links resolution even when the domains are approved.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329052\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/nightly/AndroidManifest.xml"], "git_node": "dc1bf7ba5d714a328b040bbd9ade1c57d88c640e", "git_parents": ["681ef7aca34869d291df11a6ab0e9f955fe103f6"], "node": "e46dcd43031c60466d7f940f900bd3537418daea", "parents": ["b8eac3212006626c78e1b02bc0543f65e9cfcd42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075979 - Allow user CSS to override native theming. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nI wrote this originally for bug 2048483 but that stalled. I think it's\nthe right thing to do tho.\n\nThe new names are a bit of a mouthful but this should be fine-ish...\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310810\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "layout/forms/nsProgressFrame.cpp", "layout/forms/nsRangeFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsTextFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsTextPaintStyle.cpp", "layout/style/ComputedStyle.cpp", "layout/style/ComputedStyle.h", "servo/components/style/properties/cascade.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/computed_value_flags.rs", "servo/components/style/rule_tree/level.rs", "servo/components/style/style_adjuster.rs", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/css/css-forms/user-sheet-border-background-disables-theming-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/css/css-forms/user-sheet-border-background-disables-theming.html", "widget/nsNativeTheme.cpp"], "git_node": "851f49645fb8389d7b6d9f058b46d08e00dde71d", "git_parents": ["dc1bf7ba5d714a328b040bbd9ade1c57d88c640e"], "node": "5f8801c669141b0be7cdfb3c68861600dcce9ea2", "parents": ["e46dcd43031c60466d7f940f900bd3537418daea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076127 - Remove state dirs of deleted checkouts when creating a new one. r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nEach checkout, including every git worktree, gets its own state dir under\n~/.mozbuild/srcdirs/, holding virtualenvs and caches. Nothing removed them once\nthe checkout was deleted, so they kept piling up.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329578\n", "files": ["python/mach/mach/test/python.toml", "python/mach/mach/test/test_util.py", "python/mach/mach/util.py"], "git_node": "1746a02ade5edea5f1461455167675b5f63bf2c0", "git_parents": ["851f49645fb8389d7b6d9f058b46d08e00dde71d"], "node": "f4f7f12303ea930ea94d2ca25d3b9cf68e2b8b8c", "parents": ["5f8801c669141b0be7cdfb3c68861600dcce9ea2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072202 - Log the duration of each phase of `mach static-analysis check`. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe export tiers run with make output suppressed, so nothing in the CI logs\nshows how the time splits between preparing the compilation database, the\nexport tiers and clang-tidy itself. Log the duration of each phase, and record\nit as a profiler marker in a resource usage profile.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326147\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/code_analysis/mach_commands.py", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/clang-tidy.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/clang.yml"], "git_node": "b6b5ed73f8cd1cf6b5902c679925191171c3dadf", "git_parents": ["1746a02ade5edea5f1461455167675b5f63bf2c0"], "node": "d86f6ab080109a3b52248b7b2613c820fe72b497", "parents": ["f4f7f12303ea930ea94d2ca25d3b9cf68e2b8b8c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075448 - Make the Tabbrowser members used only in its own module static. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329089\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/api.md"], "git_node": "e297bc19f0b933faf4e99e58f32ea934484a31ba", "git_parents": ["b6b5ed73f8cd1cf6b5902c679925191171c3dadf"], "node": "d088f96c4fd25504a1a1f0a9f8c4f7ba4884c47f", "parents": ["d86f6ab080109a3b52248b7b2613c820fe72b497"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072085 - Rework align-content on input/buttons as proposed on the CSSWG issue. r=layout-reviewers,dholbert\n\nMake align-content: normal behave appropriately blocks, and respect any\nother value.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329213\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.h", "layout/style/res/forms.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/form-controls/align-content-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/form-controls/align-content.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/form-controls/resets.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/button-layout/anonymous-button-content-box-ref.html", "xpcom/ds/StaticAtoms.py"], "git_node": "00e98d1bcbdfffc5a98621ee11400a8580e5beab", "git_parents": ["e297bc19f0b933faf4e99e58f32ea934484a31ba"], "node": "ec2038e3a94e2e028129aa0d725d157ae52f7c8f", "parents": ["d088f96c4fd25504a1a1f0a9f8c4f7ba4884c47f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073788 - Part 1: Keep exposing BrowserParent on discarded WindowGlobalParent, r=dom-core-reviewers,mccr8\n\nThis method was originally guarded behind CanSend() because at the time,\nIPDL actors only held a raw pointer to their Manager() after being torn\ndown. That has since changed, and all Manager() references are now\nowning, even after IPDL actors have been disconnected, so it is now\npossible to keep these methods working later.\n\nThe crash in this bug was caused due to code receiving unexpected values\nwhen accessing process-specific information on a discarded WGP, leading\nto a falsely-detected owning process ID mismatch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328975\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h"], "git_node": "c8c23be1d9739a5d0ce04d4ede6cfda20794cc78", "git_parents": ["00e98d1bcbdfffc5a98621ee11400a8580e5beab"], "node": "6daf171a848bbf981ab5cdd5057c8a8ab6c2b63d", "parents": ["ec2038e3a94e2e028129aa0d725d157ae52f7c8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073788 - Part 2: Directly look up ContentParent in WGP, r=dom-core-reviewers,mccr8\n\nA number of callers were doing unnecessary extra work to look up the\nContentParent via. the BrowserParent in WindowGlobalParent, likely due\nto the getter being added later. Simplify a few of these callers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328976\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp"], "git_node": "1c45b0c0b8c199edd2bbb00de05ce8f5bf8390ac", "git_parents": ["c8c23be1d9739a5d0ce04d4ede6cfda20794cc78"], "node": "3db27ceb14aac633c0f254e291b3f02204d3a5b4", "parents": ["6daf171a848bbf981ab5cdd5057c8a8ab6c2b63d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075554 - Make the design system's test runner wait for its tests before reporting. r=hjones,reusable-components-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nEach test is async, so runTests counted every pending Promise as a pass and the job could only fail through its TEST-UNEXPECTED-FAIL lines.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329152\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/tests/try-runner.js"], "git_node": "ab64d121555ad26660a107ad212eb1b79e5e9c40", "git_parents": ["1c45b0c0b8c199edd2bbb00de05ce8f5bf8390ac"], "node": "5f7613edbb3608c578d9342b38c47c9ce851a1ed", "parents": ["3db27ceb14aac633c0f254e291b3f02204d3a5b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075554 - Add the missing text color tokens for background variants, and test that none goes missing again. r=hjones,desktop-theme-reviewers,reusable-components-reviewers\n\nThe new tokens alias their component's base text color, so the sweep renders nothing differently: the two panel sites sit in arrow panels, which do not redefine --panel-text-color, and the urlbar box text color is inherit. With every variant paired, the rule's suggestion to fall back to the base text color can no longer fire, so it goes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329153\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/UITour.css", "browser/themes/shared/downloads/downloads.inc.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/dynamic-results.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/urlbar.tokens.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/urlbar.tokens.json", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css", "docs/code-quality/lint/linters/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/rules/use-paired-color-tokens.md", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.tokens.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/panel.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/panel.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/tests/try-runner.js", "tools/lint/stylelint/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/rules/use-paired-color-tokens.mjs", "tools/lint/stylelint/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/tests/use-paired-color-tokens.not-paired.tests.mjs"], "git_node": "d4c68753819d41610cf3c417faf4c568af59c80f", "git_parents": ["ab64d121555ad26660a107ad212eb1b79e5e9c40"], "node": "e8ee8049257ccdd77eecabdad412ae1924fc5054", "parents": ["5f7613edbb3608c578d9342b38c47c9ce851a1ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teow \u003cjteow@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068609 - Add skip menu using tab key option in preferences - r=settings-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,mstriemer,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325969\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/config/accessibility.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/config/search.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/preferences.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser-srd.toml", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_addressBarNavigation.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl"], "git_node": "fcec974b804e847b5f75080e5323ea6eb0cc89b7", "git_parents": ["d4c68753819d41610cf3c417faf4c568af59c80f"], "node": "5f7cfd1743bcbfd3fbc6b88fca9ef17d821c74be", "parents": ["e8ee8049257ccdd77eecabdad412ae1924fc5054"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2061871 - Add scrollbar inset for browser content area. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton,akulyk\" for causing bc failures @ browser_parsable_css.js\n\nThis reverts commit 4579bceb72b0b840ba3ce55ef40e03e07596f957.\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css"], "git_node": "75952a83f7803b18ff78797efc8f31fda22d73d8", "git_parents": ["fcec974b804e847b5f75080e5323ea6eb0cc89b7"], "node": "90d10d88695121e7c34d3c92367d58a135948b53", "parents": ["5f7cfd1743bcbfd3fbc6b88fca9ef17d821c74be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075211 - Use stretch to improve grid intrinsic sizing. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nThis more thoroughly fixes intrinsic sizing of row subgrids to match the\nspec, and also fixes some transferred size cases it seems.\n\nThe Gecko reftest changed matches Chromium and the spec to my knowledge.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328830\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/reftests/css-grid/grid-item-intrinsic-ratio-normal-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-items/aspect-ratio-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-items/grid-item-inline-contribution-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-items/grid-item-inline-contribution-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/subgrid/row-subgrid-intrinsic-size-transfer-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/subgrid/row-subgrid-intrinsic-size-transfer-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/subgrid/row-subgrid-intrinsic-size-transfer-003.html"], "git_node": "165c4506d7ea1aa4de6c4f44494aff15c56765ab", "git_parents": ["75952a83f7803b18ff78797efc8f31fda22d73d8"], "node": "ee04021e95d709d93f5a9626a7c3edfd857d2be7", "parents": ["90d10d88695121e7c34d3c92367d58a135948b53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longs