i.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075069 - Allow the crash reporter client to send annotations under their altname. r=crashreporting-reviewers,afranchuk\n\nThe .extra file uses an annotation's altname when it has one. The Addons annotation is\nwritten as \"Add-ons\". Build the allowlist from the altname when one is set, so it matches the\nnames in the .extra file.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329559\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/client/app/build.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/client/app/src/test.rs"], "git_node": "9d36c91e030edca98b625fb514315c6c71ca450d", "git_parents": ["be57c9e952dc8dd42fdbd8ba0e8f51c3e842b7cb"], "node": "48c473e6eef7ac19d1b5557bc94cccbaf385ae6e", "parents": ["a88ffc006b246e17eb216f5595b9e60084d36e02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075419: Fix assertion failure in line-clamp containers with 0-height non-empty lines. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329618\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-043-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/webkit-line-clamp-054-crash.html"], "git_node": "41eb98d6e3ad9e582a353b31102f28b903cb20dc", "git_parents": ["9d36c91e030edca98b625fb514315c6c71ca450d"], "node": "8d91754c411c438a8f0e7b7099b4da774327c713", "parents": ["48c473e6eef7ac19d1b5557bc94cccbaf385ae6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Shin \u003cdshin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075194: Prevent @scopes with non-trivial attribute selectors from being style shared unconditionally. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329347\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/stylesheets/scope_rule.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-cascade/scope-style-sharing-002.html"], "git_node": "c5cb6a8714ecd42d3d0f8c6c91fdd254a20c93b5", "git_parents": ["41eb98d6e3ad9e582a353b31102f28b903cb20dc"], "node": "2d04042257b614d449253165240337d48f8ba014", "parents": ["8d91754c411c438a8f0e7b7099b4da774327c713"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Shin \u003cdshin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2028622: Graceful handling of @scope rule overflow/infinite recursion. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329360\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/stylist.rs"], "git_node": "254e1f5db2de0e4ab4b371a3f4002dda5066f6ff", "git_parents": ["c5cb6a8714ecd42d3d0f8c6c91fdd254a20c93b5"], "node": "69b41893fe38c56369b905eda968a9df79a18b94", "parents": ["2d04042257b614d449253165240337d48f8ba014"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1978727 - Allow LOAD_DOCUMENT_NEEDS_COOKIE to differ in DocumentLoadListener::Open. r=nika,necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nAs the sandbox flags may have changed by the time we compute the flags\non the parent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D258391\n", "files": ["netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/sandboxing/sandbox-dynamic-change-on-navigation-crash.sub.html"], "git_node": "e875038c754b24d1d7a5edc9902ec51d676ff048", "git_parents": ["254e1f5db2de0e4ab4b371a3f4002dda5066f6ff"], "node": "560d086f7789404cf5279a9ef578a19a0e314fe4", "parents": ["69b41893fe38c56369b905eda968a9df79a18b94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2075554 - Add the missing text color tokens for background variants, and test that none goes missing again. r=hjones,desktop-theme-reviewers,reusable-components-reviewers\" for causing bc failures @ browser_parsable_css.js\n\nThis reverts commit d4c68753819d41610cf3c417faf4c568af59c80f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075554 - Make the design system's test runner wait for its tests before reporting. r=hjones,reusable-components-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit ab64d121555ad26660a107ad212eb1b79e5e9c40.\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/UITour.css", "browser/themes/shared/downloads/downloads.inc.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/dynamic-results.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/urlbar.tokens.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/urlbar.tokens.json", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css", "docs/code-quality/lint/linters/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/rules/use-paired-color-tokens.md", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.tokens.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/panel.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/panel.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/tests/try-runner.js", "tools/lint/stylelint/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/rules/use-paired-color-tokens.mjs", "tools/lint/stylelint/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/tests/use-paired-color-tokens.not-paired.tests.mjs"], "git_node": "d5e00c1562247d8f4c6a24b4f417ba55a99bfd41", "git_parents": ["e875038c754b24d1d7a5edc9902ec51d676ff048"], "node": "e01b520a48974f63c7ad32ba5f3d3d0c756c9320", "parents": ["560d086f7789404cf5279a9ef578a19a0e314fe4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065560 - Persist AITabStore - r=omarg,rrando\" for causing bc failures @ browser_smartwindow_telemetry.js\n\nThis reverts commit 9e1506f7c59a695a6c46a61ee3460c7118bce7ea.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Chat.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/agents/Monitor.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/AITab.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/search/SearchWorkflow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/aitab_attacker_page.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/aitab_source_page.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab_generation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_tools_get_page_content.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Chat.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Tools_GetPageContent.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AITabMigrations.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AITabSql.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AITabStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/AIWindowTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_AITabStore.js"], "git_node": "44cb6778bb90447638ba836aebc0ce059ccb3e8a", "git_parents": ["d5e00c1562247d8f4c6a24b4f417ba55a99bfd41"], "node": "0ecc76c97258f4772e9135a302a4808f0083e9f1", "parents": ["e01b520a48974f63c7ad32ba5f3d3d0c756c9320"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074325 - Pt 5 - Read WebRender pixels back from an explicit source r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nReading pixels back was a stateful sequence: attach a texture to the read\nframebuffer, read from whatever is bound, then reset the read target. In an\nexplicit graphics API a readback is a copy from a named texture or target, so\nthe trait now offers read_pixels_into from a ReadTarget, read_texture for the\nwhole of any device texture, and, for captures only, read_external_texture\nfor an application-owned one. The two attach methods, read_pixels and\nreset_read_target leave the trait; the GL backend still resets its read\nbinding at the end of a frame and after a blit inside a pass.\n\nThe renderer's reset after the resolve blits was also what made the tile\nblit of a slice with a backdrop-filter rebind its source on macOS: the\nnative compositor's partial-update copy binds both framebuffer targets\ninside Compositor::bind, which the GL backend's binding cache never saw.\nThe cache now records that the bindings are unknown when a render pass on\na native surface begins and ends, since the embedder binds and unbinds\nthose surfaces itself, so the next bind of either target is always issued.\n\nGecko and wrench read the presented frame through the default target, which\nis what the read binding held at that point, so the GL calls are unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329518\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs"], "git_node": "c02bde177e1b76969aba5f22bc8a2400bdf657c8", "git_parents": ["44cb6778bb90447638ba836aebc0ce059ccb3e8a"], "node": "17451717a4ff2ae85909b50eeaa974f913313190", "parents": ["0ecc76c97258f4772e9135a302a4808f0083e9f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074325 - Pt 6 - Fix WebRender sampler bindings when a program is linked r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe renderer bound each sampler to its texture slot with a separate\nbind_shader_samplers call after linking, which required binding the program\nfirst. Explicit graphics APIs fix sampler slots in the pipeline layout when\nthe pipeline is created, so link_program now takes the sampler bindings and\nbind_shader_samplers leaves the trait. The GL backend binds the freshly\nlinked program itself to set them, as the renderer used to.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329519\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/debug.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/shade.rs"], "git_node": "98ad68a8edadababcfc85719bff43ffdddb3454a", "git_parents": ["c02bde177e1b76969aba5f22bc8a2400bdf657c8"], "node": "605ffeb471fec5441f1b4f033bc221127fb83212", "parents": ["17451717a4ff2ae85909b50eeaa974f913313190"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074325 - Pt 7 - Make WebRender vertex and index buffers explicit resources r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe VAO type owned three GL buffer names and decided which of them it\nshared with the VAO it was derived from, so vertex data was written through\nthe VAO and the renderer reached the shared instance buffer by a raw buffer\nid. Explicit graphics APIs have buffers as resources the application\ncreates, writes and deletes, and take the vertex layout with the pipeline,\nso the trait now has Buffer, created with a BufferKind and written whole,\nrepeated, reallocated or through an unsynchronized mapping, and\nVertexArray, which pairs a layout with the buffers it reads and is bound as\na unit. The renderer owns the quad index and vertex buffers, the instance\nbuffers and the shared instance buffer, and the VAO type, its update\nmethods and the VBO and IBO ids leave the trait.\n\nThe GL backend records the buffers of the bound vertex array. An index\nbuffer is written through the element array target only while the array\nreading it is bound, since that binding is vertex array state, and through\nthe array buffer target otherwise, which a buffer object is indifferent to.\nThe Adreno rebind after orphaning the bound array's instance buffer is\nunchanged. The debug renderer's line array no longer has an unused index\nbuffer, and its arrays no longer create buffers they never used; all other\nGL calls are unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329520\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/types.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/debug.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/vertex.rs"], "git_node": "26c46345ece504901d216bfc519758f50d9a3d4a", "git_parents": ["98ad68a8edadababcfc85719bff43ffdddb3454a"], "node": "d5ae303dfe453dea6db1065ac0b869c09379a7eb", "parents": ["605ffeb471fec5441f1b4f033bc221127fb83212"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074325 - Pt 8 - Keep GL-only WebRender device settings out of the neutral types r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDeviceOptions carried two settings only the GL backend can act on, and\nCapabilities mixed what the renderer consults with GL implementation\ndetails that only the backend reads. The GL context now travels in a\nGlBackendConfig together with allow_texture_storage and panic_on_error,\nwhich leave DeviceOptions and WebRenderOptions; Gecko passes its\npanic-on-error flag through the config, and wrench and the examples take\nthe defaults. The eight capabilities read only by the GL backend move to a\nprivate struct there, and three the renderer does read are named for what\nthey mean rather than the GL feature behind them.\n\nThe device's memory report no longer takes the SWGL context. That context\nbelongs to the embedder's software compositor, so the renderer reports its\nmemory itself before adding the device's.\n\nNo behaviour change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329521\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/common/boilerplate.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/multiwindow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/types.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/upload.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/init.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/shade.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/wrench.rs"], "git_node": "a8e6206f65e3050b76bc922e53d6b4e4bb034e42", "git_parents": ["26c46345ece504901d216bfc519758f50d9a3d4a"], "node": "1caa138307765e323e682aed33c2a8d03d33f098", "parents": ["d5ae303dfe453dea6db1065ac0b869c09379a7eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071124 - Await FOG init before setting debug tag in test r=TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329605\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/marionette/tests/client/test_fog_deletion_request_ping.py"], "git_node": "07b3352b399b721aabb3fd9060a58ecca4d46011", "git_parents": ["a8e6206f65e3050b76bc922e53d6b4e4bb034e42"], "node": "23dfdde50f7ae1a1d4bba4a43662338454ea1e1c", "parents": ["1caa138307765e323e682aed33c2a8d03d33f098"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Devota Aabel \u003cdaabel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070475 - Remove extra spacing from below shortcuts, and hide shortcuts header when show more experiment is turned on r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326943\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/store/HomepageState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSites.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/ui/Shortcuts.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSitesExpandToggleTest.kt"], "git_node": "f06a0aaa3138da5ae2d323792359d23a46f63aea", "git_parents": ["07b3352b399b721aabb3fd9060a58ecca4d46011"], "node": "375984a62e70accf83e5cfcaecf9efc1a0a8c154", "parents": ["23dfdde50f7ae1a1d4bba4a43662338454ea1e1c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069528 - rework when internal modules search for certificates r=jschanck\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323773\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/ipcclientcerts/src/backend.rs", "security/manager/ssl/ipcclientcerts/src/lib.rs", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSComponent.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/osclientcerts/src/backend_android.rs", "security/manager/ssl/osclientcerts/src/backend_macos.rs", "security/manager/ssl/osclientcerts/src/backend_windows.rs", "security/manager/ssl/osclientcerts/src/lib.rs", "security/manager/ssl/rsclientcerts/src/manager.rs", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/pkcs11testmodule/src/backend.rs", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/pkcs11testmodule/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "85afc2b8f02315214c05831a7fe86c0e92ac3cc2", "git_parents": ["f06a0aaa3138da5ae2d323792359d23a46f63aea"], "node": "a8f1db3ed15d390aed5e135b6040faa8b47ac06b", "parents": ["375984a62e70accf83e5cfcaecf9efc1a0a8c154"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069528 - make certificates on remote PKCS#11 modules available to the parent process r=jschanck\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323774\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "security/certverifier/NSSCertDBTrustDomain.cpp", "security/certverifier/NSSCertDBTrustDomain.h", "security/manager/ssl/IPCClientCertsParent.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleChild.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleChild.h", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleDB.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleDB.h", "security/manager/ssl/PPKCS11Module.ipdl", "security/manager/ssl/PSMIPCTypes.ipdlh", "security/manager/ssl/TLSClientAuthCertSelection.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/ipcclientcerts/src/backend.rs", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSComponent.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSComponent.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSIOLayer.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSIOLayer.h",