art 3: Use LSX_FLAGS in media/libpng moz.build. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329486\n", "files": ["media/libpng/moz.build"], "git_node": "f42809677d4f48bbbfe473580fbe9b4b27feb4b6", "git_parents": ["4ce82d38cf432b8e26999df8d94b480c0ae9825f"], "node": "28c3ae97e46ee476303de9b232a3f3bb2094e4c4", "parents": ["343fa28d7d4247b2f493c9d87513ae659fdd8dbf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075953 - Part 4: Use LSX_FLAGS in media/libvpx moz.build. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329487\n", "files": ["media/libvpx/moz.build"], "git_node": "5997a5e30d28e9f8ff85876fc3429baab5ceeea3", "git_parents": ["f42809677d4f48bbbfe473580fbe9b4b27feb4b6"], "node": "fa319a6f6b6486f23db67cacff46d2502210d777", "parents": ["28c3ae97e46ee476303de9b232a3f3bb2094e4c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076145 - Stop scheduling the app-services lint job copies on code review pushes r=marco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329615\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test-appservices/kind.yml"], "git_node": "452ad48a2cdef5d3ae98c2a83a105c9b01d80a15", "git_parents": ["5997a5e30d28e9f8ff85876fc3429baab5ceeea3"], "node": "626cb722b9672da866e0c9b7a19a5c301226e042", "parents": ["fa319a6f6b6486f23db67cacff46d2502210d777"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076038 - Decode the `cargo metadata` output of the SBOM as UTF-8 r=sylvestre\n\n`text=True` decodes with the locale encoding, which is cp1252 on Windows and\ncannot decode the metadata.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329509\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_cargo.py"], "git_node": "7949d2a13c4d6c2628313a41e07d37599290e8d1", "git_parents": ["452ad48a2cdef5d3ae98c2a83a105c9b01d80a15"], "node": "c7cf8051c66a8bca11cc0174fad89771bc6bdd84", "parents": ["626cb722b9672da866e0c9b7a19a5c301226e042"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060428 - Part 11 - Use the new Python Cargo actions by default r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325635\n", "files": ["moz.configure"], "git_node": "993bce46919a168a92f294140abe98c2c17bb43b", "git_parents": ["7949d2a13c4d6c2628313a41e07d37599290e8d1"], "node": "da176f32c0e9ef67aaf07cda9300c98ed0b747e9", "parents": ["c7cf8051c66a8bca11cc0174fad89771bc6bdd84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071656 - Manage private browsing cipher keys in the OPFS quota client. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nPrivate browsing files have to be encrypted, which needs a key that stays the\nsame for as long as an origin's files do and is forgotten together with them.\nThe quota client is an appropriate place. So hold one FileSystemCipherKeyManager\nper private origin there, the way LocalStorage already does.\n\nInvalidating them follows the lifetime of the files.\nOnRepositoryClearCompleted() drops every key when the private browsing session\nends and the private repository is cleared, while OnOriginClearCompleted()\ndrops a single origin's data.\n\nThe clear callbacks assert they run on the quota manager IO thread, so the map\nhas to be touched from that thread (confining every access to that thread is\ncheaper than locking it). That makes GetOrCreateCipherKeyManager() IO thread\nonly, so FileSystemDataManager fetches the manager for its origin from the step\nof BeginOpen() which already runs there.\n\nNothing consumes the keys yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325744\n", "files": ["dom/fs/parent/FileSystemCipherKeyManager.h", "dom/fs/parent/FileSystemQuotaClient.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/FileSystemQuotaClient.h", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemDataManager.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemDataManager.h", "dom/fs/parent/moz.build"], "git_node": "51cf3d5e5c87ec5e359175abf524c92be95d0733", "git_parents": ["993bce46919a168a92f294140abe98c2c17bb43b"], "node": "5e4955ecee327714cf9c2313290156736da09fc0", "parents": ["da176f32c0e9ef67aaf07cda9300c98ed0b747e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071656 - Encrypt the OPFS metadata database in private browsing. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nPass the origin's cipher key as the key query parameter of the database file\nURL, which enables mozilla::storage::obfsvfs. IDB hands their keys over the\nsame way.\n\nThe database gets its own cipher key id, so that the page cipher and\nEncryptedRandomAccessStream never share a key.\n\nThe database also has to use a page size of 8192 due to the restriction of\nobfsvfs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325745\n", "files": ["dom/fs/parent/FileSystemCipherKeyManager.h", "dom/fs/parent/FileSystemQuotaClient.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemDataManager.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemDataManager.h", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemFileManager.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemFileManager.h", "dom/fs/test/gtest/parent/FileSystemParentTest.cpp"], "git_node": "abe0b8f5f43a76c4c5cdac2f8a591bc45c5efeef", "git_parents": ["51cf3d5e5c87ec5e359175abf524c92be95d0733"], "node": "a339c7f739e60703fd4f65f696f482a447e2ca5d", "parents": ["5e4955ecee327714cf9c2313290156736da09fc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071656 - Enable OPFS in private browsing behind a pref, for namespace operations only. r=jari,jdescottes,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nGate the private browsing block on the new dom.fs.privateBrowsing.enabled pref,\nand store private origins in the private repository rather than in the default\none, so that their data is wiped when the private browsing session ends.\n\nReading or writing file contents is still rejected, because nothing encrypts\nthem yet. Only the namespace operations needed to get to a file handle are allowed.\n\ntest_iframes.html passes in private browsing now, so drop its expectation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325746\n", "files": ["dom/fs/api/FileSystemManager.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/FileSystemManagerParent.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/FileSystemManagerParentFactory.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/FileSystemQuotaClient.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemDatabaseManagerVersion001.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemFileManager.cpp", "dom/fs/test/marionette/manifest.toml", "dom/fs/test/marionette/test_OPFS_encryption_PBM.py", "dom/fs/test/mochitest/mochitest-private.toml", "dom/fs/test/moz.build", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/integration-tests.toml", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/www/dom/fs/basicOPFS_PBM.html"], "git_node": "4f5ab98df9ee0f6451b6487e6f851f9fb2052bbb", "git_parents": ["abe0b8f5f43a76c4c5cdac2f8a591bc45c5efeef"], "node": "f4edc269ea893f804553c54f6453761e40854f8f", "parents": ["a339c7f739e60703fd4f65f696f482a447e2ca5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070040 - Reuse the quota object when serializing an already opened FileRandomAccessStream. r=jari\n\nnsFileStreamBase::DoOpen() clears mOpenParams through CleanUpOpen() once it has\nthe file descriptor, so FileRandomAccessStream::Serialize() cannot look the\nquota object up again for a stream which has already been opened. DoOpen()\nacquires that object before losing the file, so reuse it instead.\n\nNo consumer serialized an opened quota stream so far. But an\nEncryptedRandomAccessStream wrapping one does, because it reads the final block\nin Create() to derive the plaintext size.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325747\n", "files": ["dom/quota/FileStreams.cpp"], "git_node": "a66465a5426ea091da750ed29841af857085fe41", "git_parents": ["4f5ab98df9ee0f6451b6487e6f851f9fb2052bbb"], "node": "a0f7aeefa103d56d8126fd669db21f66e92d7727", "parents": ["f4edc269ea893f804553c54f6453761e40854f8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070040 - Implement nsIFileMetadata on EncryptedRandomAccessStream. r=jari,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nConsumers reach a random access stream's size through nsIFileMetadata, which\nFileSystemSyncAccessHandle::GetSize() queries for. EncryptedRandomAccessStream\ndid not implement it, so the query returned null.\n\nsize reports the plaintext size rather than the size of the file, including\nwrites which have not been saved to the base stream yet, which matches\nnsFileStreamBase::GetSize() where a write has already reached the file\ndescriptor by the time it returns.\n\nThe other two attributes have no consumer and are refused rather than\ndelegated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325748\n", "files": ["dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp", "dom/quota/EncryptedRandomAccessStream.h", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestEncryptedRandomAccessStream.cpp"], "git_node": "697802dcb668f1a445149e255f6da780911b3cff", "git_parents": ["a66465a5426ea091da750ed29841af857085fe41"], "node": "d0b16cf0a4c2b0b43ac6ef1daf32385ebf8ec05c", "parents": ["a0f7aeefa103d56d8126fd669db21f66e92d7727"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070040 - Encrypt and enable sync access handle files in private browsing. r=jari,jdescottes,dom-storage-reviewers\n\nBack a sync access handle of a private origin with an\nEncryptedRandomAccessStream, and stop rejecting the request. The child\nreconstructs the stream from the parameters, which already carry the master key,\nso it reads and writes plaintext while only ciphertext reaches the disk.\n\nAsk the origin's cipher key manager for a master key per FileId.\nNSSRandomAccessCipherStrategy derives the key of a block from the master key and\nthe block number, and the AAD of a block identifies only the block, so a single\nmaster key per origin would give the same-numbered blocks of all its files the\nsame derived key. A block could then be substituted between two files without\nthe authentication noticing, and the random nonces of all those blocks would\nhave to stay collision free under one key, which is fatal for ChaCha20-Poly1305.\n\nForget the key of a FileId in RemoveFileId(), once its file is gone, so that\nthe keys don't pile up in the cipher key manager for as long as the origin\nlives. CipherKeyManager gets a Remove() method for that.\n\ncreateWritable() and getFile() stay rejected, so they cannot see the files a\nsync access handle wrote. Note that they still can't be called in PBM.\n\nEnable test_syncAccessHandle_worker.html in private browsing now that the whole\nAPI works there, and list the remaining tests of the non-private manifest with\ntheir expected failures, since createWritable() and getFile() are still\nrejected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325749\n", "files": ["dom/fs/parent/FileSystemAccessHandle.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/FileSystemManagerParent.cpp", "dom/fs/parent/datamodel/FileSystemDatabaseManagerVersion002.cpp", "dom/fs/test/marionette/manifest.toml", "dom/fs/test/marionette/test_OPFS_syncAccessHandle_encryption_PBM.py", "dom/fs/test/mochitest/mochitest-private.toml", "dom/quota/CipherKeyManager.h", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/www/dom/fs/syncAccessHandleOPFS_PBM.html", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/www/dom/fs/syncAccessHandleOPFS_PBM.js"], "git_node": "21dac90a5e59047556c9ef74f5ae20e04b9461a9", "git_parents": ["697802dcb668f1a445149e255f6da780911b3cff"], "node": "077d6961342bc000536a14148fbc3605e9fd8936", "parents": ["d0b16cf0a4c2b0b43ac6ef1daf32385ebf8ec05c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076298 - Update libpng to v1.6.59 r=tnikkel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329676\n", "files": ["media/libpng/ANNOUNCE", "media/libpng/AUTHORS", "media/libpng/CHANGES", "media/libpng/README", "media/libpng/arm/arm_init.c", "media/libpng/arm/filter_neon.S", "media/libpng/libpng-manual.txt", "media/libpng/moz.yaml", "media/libpng/png.c", "media/libpng/png.h", "media/libpng/pngconf.h", "media/libpng/pngget.c", "media/libpng/pnginfo.h", "media/libpng/pngpread.c", "media/libpng/pngpriv.h", "media/libpng/pngread.c", "media/libpng/pngrtran.c", "media/libpng/pngrutil.c", "media/libpng/pngset.c", "media/libpng/pngstruct.h", "media/libpng/pngwrite.c", "media/libpng/pngwutil.c"], "git_node": "ad71a86b562bb74b8aa21d774383bea30fcaf141", "git_parents": ["21dac90a5e59047556c9ef74f5ae20e04b9461a9"], "node": "21513ae2dcc4649992d3fe89dfac5bb495f7ab9c", "parents": ["077d6961342bc000536a14148fbc3605e9fd8936"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076298 - Apply mozilla patches for libpng r=tnikkel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329677\n", "files": ["media/libpng/arm/arm_init.c", "media/libpng/arm/filter_neon.S", "media/libpng/png.h", "media/libpng/pngget.c", "media/libpng/pnginfo.h", "media/libpng/pngpread.c", "media/libpng/pngpriv.h", "media/libpng/pngread.c", "media/libpng/pngrutil.c", "media/libpng/pngset.c", "media/libpng/pngstruct.h", "media/libpng/pngwrite.c", "media/libpng/pngwutil.c"], "git_node": "704d48fe30542e423885c4b10448139b37b4423c", "git_parents": ["ad71a86b562bb74b8aa21d774383bea30fcaf141"], "node": "b4104a055d5b341f10e34cd6df62b23c24495891", "parents": ["21513ae2dcc4649992d3fe89dfac5bb495f7ab9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073580: Fully implement extended name section. r=yury\n\nImplements all \"newly\"-specified name subsections, and reworks parsing\ngenerally with a new Decoder per custom section and name subsection. I\njust prefer it that way because otherwise you have to jump through hoops\nto detect if you overrun or underrun a section, and in the past we have\ndone so inconsistently.\n\nAlso switches storage of names from vectors to hash maps.\n\nWe still don't actually _store_ names beyond module and func names\nbecause we have no need for them and we don't need to keep that data\naround in memory and on disk. But validation is complete and we can\ntrivially start storing them whenever we feel like it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329308\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/binary.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/bug1951874.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmBinary.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmBinary.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmConstants.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmMetadata.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmModuleTypes.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmModuleTypes.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmSerialize.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmValidate.cpp"], "git_node": "6355877aa60196bc964e49b1d08dc255c4ae346f", "git_parents": ["704d48fe30542e423885c4b10448139b37b4423c"], "node": "407b620dbaa8c1b50a74093a43783ab7430584c1", "parents": ["b4104a055d5b341f10e34cd6df62b23c24495891"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073580: Update wasm-tools to 259. r=yury,supply-chain-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329309\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "js/src/fuzz-tests/gluesmith/Cargo.toml", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/components/instantiation.js", "js/