 nursery active chunk range r=jonco\n\nWe can't just start allocating in any chunk; we can either start from\nthe beginning, after evicting a space or when switching spaces, or we\ncan continue with the next chunk.\n\n- Refactor to better name the range of chunks used for allocation since\n  the last collection.  Allow a space to have *no* active chunks; this is\n  the case in the promote-only nursery configuration.\n\n- Add a Space::chunk accessor that ensures the chunk is in the active\n  range.\n\n- Don't bother ensuring that fromspace has an current chunk.\n\n- Don't eagerly flip the gckind of a space's allocated but inactive\n  pages; lazily flip them just before allocation.\n\n- Simplify poisoning under generational GC zeal.\n\n- Simplify nursery growth/shrinkage under generational GC zeal.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325424\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.h"], "git_node": "9ec5bb31ea473e1e98ae516ded127b264ee3dcba", "git_parents": ["6c48a00bf9cda4e845fb7db394f44aa07eeb6003"], "node": "9ca3b69a2f11dcf41c3899e9de7dfa87ad6d35a5", "parents": ["2f4e9793d8ba51e3c2c07d73322adcacfb013afa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740752 - Part 2: Implement contiguous nursery mode r=jonco\n\nShould speed up chunk acquisition / release and isInside checks.\nEnabled if -DJS_CONTIGUOUS_NURSERY.\n\nfoo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325425\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery-inl.h", "js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.h", "js/src/gc/Scheduling.cpp"], "git_node": "63566204a1aa021bf9b1e7fa938b55b69f1bf114", "git_parents": ["9ec5bb31ea473e1e98ae516ded127b264ee3dcba"], "node": "7b818852c7a4bd02af338c51a4a9b06e527bfa74", "parents": ["9ca3b69a2f11dcf41c3899e9de7dfa87ad6d35a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740752 - Part 3: Use contiguous nursery on 64-bit platforms r=jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325427\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery.h"], "git_node": "4ea8dc66d17c2b9c4c9c1155d9bdb51135a22922", "git_parents": ["63566204a1aa021bf9b1e7fa938b55b69f1bf114"], "node": "98ffb19e5acfc993b008ac9c3257582048d5d669", "parents": ["7b818852c7a4bd02af338c51a4a9b06e527bfa74"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073852 Use maximal align for ffmpeg custom get_buffer2() buffer allocator r=alwu,media-playback-reviewers\n\nffmpeg/libavcodec/internal.h defines STRIDE_ALIGN for\navcodec_default_get_buffer2() according to used instructions set.\nThe recent biggest value is 64 for AVX-512.\nWe need to keep our internal align in sync with the biggest value\nto make sure our custom get_buffer2() allocator works with any system\nprovided ffmpeg.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327769\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegUtils.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/test/test_vp9_buffer_overread.html", "dom/media/test/vp9_256x128.webm", "dom/media/test/vp9_256x128.webm^headers^"], "git_node": "ed5e6f2ec99828d7d367cf5dcfd6432b5bc62808", "git_parents": ["4ea8dc66d17c2b9c4c9c1155d9bdb51135a22922"], "node": "39ce126fd51f60d3652ffc4686978d70700a5920", "parents": ["98ffb19e5acfc993b008ac9c3257582048d5d669"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076054 - Fix and wire up gfxAlphaRecoveryNeon.cpp on AArch64 and NEON-capable ARM platforms. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329698\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxAlphaRecovery.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxAlphaRecoveryNeon.cpp", "gfx/thebes/moz.build"], "git_node": "f7ac3210791ba25ed87a5cc2a89dc192260ce4cd", "git_parents": ["ed5e6f2ec99828d7d367cf5dcfd6432b5bc62808"], "node": "01d100f6f21db86dde793c87dd336a7084326d51", "parents": ["39ce126fd51f60d3652ffc4686978d70700a5920"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1740752 - Part 3: Use contiguous nursery on 64-bit platforms r=jonco\" for causing SM failures\n\nThis reverts commit 4ea8dc66d17c2b9c4c9c1155d9bdb51135a22922.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1740752 - Part 2: Implement contiguous nursery mode r=jonco\"\n\nThis reverts commit 63566204a1aa021bf9b1e7fa938b55b69f1bf114.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1740752 - Part 1: Refactor nursery active chunk range r=jonco\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9ec5bb31ea473e1e98ae516ded127b264ee3dcba.\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery-inl.h", "js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.h", "js/src/gc/Scheduling.cpp"], "git_node": "3afa9f54e1458e1ad923c030982310a86ab67311", "git_parents": ["f7ac3210791ba25ed87a5cc2a89dc192260ce4cd"], "node": "493604737cadbe44ac33efc8da2d880331b81ba3", "parents": ["01d100f6f21db86dde793c87dd336a7084326d51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sugarycandybar \u003ccandybaralt@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067952 - Pick largest MediaMetadata artwork sizes first. r=media-playback-reviewers,stransky\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323921\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediasession/MediaMetadata.cpp", "dom/media/mediasession/MediaMetadata.h", "dom/media/mediasession/test/gtest/TestMediaMetadataArtwork.cpp", "dom/media/mediasession/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "b7a54ee2036634ba92ab42f7bf8d2236fc7ade29", "git_parents": ["3afa9f54e1458e1ad923c030982310a86ab67311"], "node": "9e9fb9cfab7de5c62305582dffe621d09c00cd5a", "parents": ["493604737cadbe44ac33efc8da2d880331b81ba3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076313 - Update PDF.js to 91041fb94d6744bc2a5bccd9aad28d617faa8195 r=pdfjs-reviewers,calixte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329680\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsVersion.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "f0d874330af32bdd7690bc1c8320080dcbc604c4", "git_parents": ["b7a54ee2036634ba92ab42f7bf8d2236fc7ade29"], "node": "18bfbf1a355a203ceffd42459c96e2fa7d46759f", "parents": ["9e9fb9cfab7de5c62305582dffe621d09c00cd5a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075088 - Disable video overlay whlie video position is moving on Windows r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nWhen video overlay was scrolled DCSurfaceVideo::CallVideoProcessorBlt() was called very often. It made Render thread very busy.\nThen it seems better to disable video overlay when video position is moving.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329580\n", "files": ["dom/media/webvtt/test/reftest/reftest.list", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/init.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/track/track-element/track-webvtt-two-cue-layout-after-first-end.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/bidi/bidi_ruby.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/bidi/u0041_first.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/bidi/u06E9_no_strong_dir.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/cue_selector_single_colon.html.ini", "testing/web-pla