883d9e79a08378f679366"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 1 - Remove the WebRender example-compositor crate. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nIt no longer builds against the current Compositor trait.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329665\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/ci-scripts/linux-debug-tests.sh", "gfx/wr/ci-scripts/macos-debug-tests.sh", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor-wayland/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor-wayland/build.rs", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor-wayland/src/lib.cpp", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor-wayland/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor-windows/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor-windows/build.rs", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor-windows/src/lib.cpp", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor-windows/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor/src/main.rs", "tools/lint/clippy.yml"], "git_node": "3a98f269ee96d47590e466b57464dbeedf471b03", "git_parents": ["539edd58b558dcd310ea41e1c6476ed6218f5498"], "node": "d915f14fd240c93c414c07a660a9e3ec23256994", "parents": ["7d0277f76d4ee30dd7df838288d1f975dc9aed6b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 2 - Remove DebugCommand::EnableNativeCompositor. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nNothing sends it, so the compositor kind never changes after the renderer is created.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329666\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_api.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs"], "git_node": "4822206377f69913468c2ec2a582b08840bbd3ab", "git_parents": ["3a98f269ee96d47590e466b57464dbeedf471b03"], "node": "788bcdde94548b413b488e1f2dfe57ecfb05032a", "parents": ["d915f14fd240c93c414c07a660a9e3ec23256994"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 3 - Keep the renderer's compositor kind when loading a capture. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nLoading a capture replaced the window's compositor kind with the captured one, which\nwas the only remaining way for frames to reach the renderer with a different kind.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329667\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs"], "git_node": "55c082dffd071a1c402be2f91b12ab52108edbda", "git_parents": ["4822206377f69913468c2ec2a582b08840bbd3ab"], "node": "e6e3967b5137628f23795cecb0ff25b4be742c1b", "parents": ["788bcdde94548b413b488e1f2dfe57ecfb05032a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 4 - Remove Compositor::enable_native_compositor and the renderer's compositor kind switching. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329668\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/compositor/sw_compositor.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs"], "git_node": "e689edd1e757b9b3c3b0e2ff96cead8005c07045", "git_parents": ["55c082dffd071a1c402be2f91b12ab52108edbda"], "node": "e2170d3e28ae2a117845a328cf9e208e720bb2f3", "parents": ["e6e3967b5137628f23795cecb0ff25b4be742c1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 5 - Stop checking tile caches for tiles from another compositor kind. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe compositor kind is fixed for a window's lifetime now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329669\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs"], "git_node": "2c8c41dbf5ee1df31864357790caa1b637aa7955", "git_parents": ["e689edd1e757b9b3c3b0e2ff96cead8005c07045"], "node": "f23a36ade2949abda390c1fb212352571e5bfc4a", "parents": ["e2170d3e28ae2a117845a328cf9e208e720bb2f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 6 - Remove virtual compositor surface support. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nOnly the removed DirectComposition native compositor used virtual surfaces. ANGLE still\nreported a size, but it never takes the native compositor path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329670\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorANGLE.cpp", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/slice_builder.rs", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "81f721e334bdc174bcfec02edc8cb804a86e9ebe", "git_parents": ["2c8c41dbf5ee1df31864357790caa1b637aa7955"], "node": "c529039fe7636caaf911e1982313f010035491e3", "parents": ["f23a36ade2949abda390c1fb212352571e5bfc4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 7 - Remove the tile-based compositor methods from RenderCompositorANGLE and DCLayerTree. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThey are only used by the native compositor, which ANGLE no longer uses.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329671\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorANGLE.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorANGLE.h"], "git_node": "ccb602a417a0f4e8a1712443eeec6c7107969dae", "git_parents": ["81f721e334bdc174bcfec02edc8cb804a86e9ebe"], "node": "4a60e69b8f422d126488bbc4e910f40a31c19f82", "parents": ["c529039fe7636caaf911e1982313f010035491e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 8 - Remove the native compositor case from DCLayerTree::CompositorEndFrame. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329672\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp"], "git_node": "cf69ea9f7a48fa60c293387138de59aafec82c68", "git_parents": ["ccb602a417a0f4e8a1712443eeec6c7107969dae"], "node": "b80bb35e143d4cb10e16a76657e86e74433f4408", "parents": ["4a60e69b8f422d126488bbc4e910f40a31c19f82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 9 - Remove the virtual offset parameter from Compositor::create_surface. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nIt is always zero now, and no compositor implementation reads it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329673\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositor.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositor.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayerNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayerNative.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayersSWGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayersSWGL.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorNative.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/compositor/sw_compositor.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/debug.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/resource_cache.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs"], "git_node": "3dc9cd465f7123103bd3d79b88c7d20c8c00c34a", "git_parents": ["cf69ea9f7a48fa60c293387138de59aafec82c68"], "node": "01d16e041d5a26080b479198f66920cbe88b4737", "parents": ["b80bb35e143d4cb10e16a76657e86e74433f4408"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 10 - Remove CompositorCapabilities::supports_external_compositor_surface_negative_scaling. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nOnly ANGLE cleared it, and it is only read by the native compositor path, which ANGLE\nno longer uses.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329674\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorANGLE.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorANGLE.h", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs"], "git_node": "ab876f8c6e54e8c5fa093fc92fe34b661cedc97b", "git_parents": ["3dc9cd465f7123103bd3d79b88c7d20c8c00c34a"], "node": "c29eb7e1642c5d8934bc38070b59bfe8fc8b4b76", "parents": ["01d16e041d5a26080b479198f66920cbe88b4737"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076283 - Part 11 - Remove the tile-based compositor methods from RenderCompositorLayerNative. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe layer compositor never calls them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329675\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayerNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayerNative.h"], "git_node": "cd9abd5e0778f5699fd0426c753f15e1c53e2886", "git_parents": ["ab876f8c6e54e8c5fa093fc92fe34b661cedc97b"], "node": "cacf4c0e94e82f821002b0be427a66b5c7fbb2c3", "parents": ["c29eb7e1642c5d8934bc38070b59bfe8fc8b4b76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2066086 - Fix hide tabs and sidebar logic and refactor sidebar state logic r=sfoster,jsudiaman,sidebar-reviewers,nsharpley,sessionstore-reviewers,kcochrane,extension-reviewers,rpl\" for causing failures at browser_extensions_sidebar.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 6b4126508e0f4af2fe2291dd12b7a927f7e883ce.\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_remove_sidebar_button_and_sidebar.js", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_uidensity_auto_compact.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_sidebarAction.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/session.schema.json", "browser/components/sidebar/SidebarManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/SidebarState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/docs/index.md", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-main.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_adopt_sidebar_from_opener.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_customize_sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_launcher_hidden_restore.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_panel_states.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_prefs.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/marionette/test_last_used_sidebar_panel.py", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/unit/test_sidebar_state.js"], "git_node": "c7b9d683393e3d20b64ae8f97193c997a8688319", "git_parents": ["cd9abd5e0778f5699fd0426c753f15e1c53e2886"], "node": "13c81ddd9c41c04747a4ed5d7e00732e3ad05311", "parents": ["cacf4c0e94e82f821002b0be427a66b5c7fbb2c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052757 - Only anchor an inline spellcheck status to the caret on its first slice. r=masayuki\n\nA spellcheck slice that runs out of time reschedules the same mozInlineSpellStatus, and the next slice runs\nFinishInitOnEvent again. For a status created with SetAnchorToCaret::Yes, mAnchorRange was already set by the\nfirst slice, so MOZ_ASSERT(!mAnchorRange) fired on slow debug builds. Clear the flag once it has been handled\nso a resumed status keeps the anchor its first slice set, like every other status does. Regressed by bug\n2049464.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329515\n", "files": ["extensions/spellcheck/src/mozInlineSpellChecker.cpp", "extensions/spellcheck/src/mozInlineSpellChecker.h"], "git_node": "908e7adc8341563b550f92b4248d3c2111437f63", "git_parents": ["c7b9d683393e3d20b64ae8f97193c997a8688319"], "node": "2f2c4c6d93f12977026abb9e7b4ff9a544965ce4", "parents": ["13c81ddd9c41c04747a4ed5d7e00732e3ad05311"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074377 - Use moz-src for browser/components r=sessionstore-reviewers,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,sidebar-reviewers,sfoster,niklas,omc-reviewers,emcminn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328076\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-performance/browser_startup.js", "browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/StartupTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouterTargeting.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_targeting.js", "browser/components/components.conf", "browser/components/moz.build", "browser/components/places/PlacesBrowserStartup.sys.mjs", "browser/components/places/tests/unit/test_browserGlue_distribution.js", "browser/components/profiles/tests/unit/test_command_line_handler.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/test_restore_sidebar.py", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/marionette/test_contextual_password_manager_disabled.py", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/marionette/test_default_launcher_visible.py", "browser/components/tests/marionette/test_no_errors_clean_profile.py", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_distribution.js", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_distribution_bookmarks_first.js", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_distribution_cachedexistence.js", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_distribution_idonly.js", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_distribution_mozillaonline.js", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_distribution_observer.js", "services/fxaccounts/tests/browser/browser_open_uri.js", "services/fxaccounts/tests/browser/head.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "6734399b536a68acc4404a604e15787070b5d55b", "git_parents": ["908e7adc8341563b550f92b4248d3c2111437f63"], "node": "8be4039eee472371ad9909131cf6ac9a594854dc", "parents": ["2f2c4c6d93f12977026abb9e7b4ff9a544965ce4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Sharma \u003cabhishekcs@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073644 - pt1. Add x64 Assembler ops for CET instructions RDSSPQ and INCSSPQ r=jandem,iain\n\nAdd encodings and Assembler ops for two new CET shadow-stack instructions on x86_64.\n\nOpcode group table assignments are based on the ones used by the Linux kernel:\nhttps://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/315a4af8cd2469fcf5dacc58b5e73944b4f0c561\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327548\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/x64/Assembler-x64.h", "js/src/jit/x64/BaseAssembler-x64.h", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/Encoding-x86-shared.h"], "git_node": "2679e9f65da12048247e53fd07d2c8154f738ca8", "git_parents": ["6734399b536a68acc4404a604e15787070b5d55b"], "node": "653c03d6aa421b93a12bef21a9604cea2cd61683", "parents": ["8be4039eee472371ad9909131cf6ac9a594854dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Sharma \u003cabhishekcs@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073644 - pt2. Unwind the shadow stack when handling JS exceptions r=jandem,iain\n\n- Add --enable-js-hardware-shadow-stack configuration option that can currently be enabled\nonly on x86_64. This enables code guarded by JS_HW_SHADOW_STACK.\n- A shadowStackPointer field in ResumeFromException tracks the shadow stack pointer\nthroughout JIT frame iteration during exception unwinding.\n- The shadowStackPointer field is initialized with the active shadow stack pointer\nvalue whenever it is allocated by the JIT - before entering HandleException.\n- After HandleException returns, this shadowStackPointer field is used to actually\nincrement the hardware shadow stack pointer and unwind it along with the native\nstack.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327549\n", "files": ["js/moz.configure", "js/src/jit/JitFrames.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitFrames.h", "js/src/jit/x64/MacroAssembler-x64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x64/MacroAssembler-x64.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmStubs.cpp"], "git_node": "22a5e65848b994e1af33db7778464558cf197b27", "git_parents": ["2679e9f65da12048247e53fd07d2c8154f738ca8"], "node": "a218ea70fd81f2ed214824ff0fb095e268f7757c", "parents": ["653c03d6aa421b93a12bef21a9604cea2cd61683"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Sharma \u003cabhishekcs@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073644 - pt3. Unwind the shadow stack when handling exceptions in WASM r=jandem,iain\n\nWasm frame unwinding reuses the shadowStackPointer field introduced in the\nResumeFromException struct for JS frame unwinding.\n\n- Add the unwoundFrame field to TrapData to let wasm::HandleExceptionWasm know\n  if wasm::StartUnwinding() actually unwound a frame. This allows the shadowStackPointer\n  to be adjusted to match.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327550\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/JitActivation.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmBuiltins.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmCodegenTypes.h"], "git_node": "67e28b6564db1a47bfe037a54cd638a708f7b53b", "git_parents": ["22a5e65848b994e1af33db7778464558cf197b27"], "node": "b378c8ff81aa9d416250063c7387936686d62ea4", "parents": ["a218ea70fd81f2ed214824ff0fb095e268f7757c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Sharma \u003cabhishekcs@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073644 - pt4. Fix shadow stack mismatch when DebugEpilogue fails r=jandem,iain\n\nWhen the DebugEpilogue call in DebugEpilogueOnBaselineReturn fails it\neffectively pops the exit frame by updating packedExitFP in\nEnsureUnwoundJitExitFrame. HandleException can account for that by checking\nthe FrameType of the intial frame and ensuring that the initial shadow stack entry\nmatches the return address in the initial JitFrame in the frame iterator.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327551\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/JitFrames.cpp"], "git_node": "fa6350ef4bf935b2f48c82e18b74022d2806edc1", "git_parents": ["67e28b6564db1a47bfe037a54cd638a708f7b53b"], "node": "9c921dc97ae2af9e7dbb998f6d5bcb21dbee1b2d", "parents": ["b378c8ff81aa9d416250063c7387936686d62ea4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Sharma \u003cabhishekcs@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073644 - pt5. Fix shadow stack mismatch during invalidation bailout r=jandem,iain\n\nInvalidation bailout performs a call from an OSI point in the Ion script to the\ninvalidation epilogue. Before jumping to the bailout tail, the corresponding\nshadow stack entry must be removed to mirror the existing removal of the dead\nframe from the native stack.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327552\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/x64/MacroAssembler-x64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x64/MacroAssembler-x64.h", "js/src/jit/x64/Trampoline-x64.cpp"], "git_node": "bee800efc997014a9459052aafd1674ed7a45335", "git_parents": ["fa6350ef4bf935b2f48c82e18b74022d2806edc1"], "node": "a724faf5bef11b1a8a7d54001411e078b72b6477", "parents": ["9c921dc97ae2af9e7dbb998f6d5bcb21dbee1b2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Arnaud Bienner \u003cabienner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076134 - Quota manager: improvements to resyncQuotaUsage function. r=janv\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329582\n", "files": ["dom/quota/FileStreams.cpp"], "git_node": "f927eb6dbc11d97da2af53043a8c6bf30d4e52e1", "git_parents": ["bee800efc997014a9459052aafd1674ed7a45335"], "node": "2db0d8d1c84c95a0c0499c6c4cbfde6d218427d0", "parents": ["a724faf5bef11b1a8a7d54001411e078b72b6477"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076332 - Only restore the backups that the current updater run created. r=application-update-reviewers,cdupuis\n\nOn failure, every action restores the backup of its file whenever one exists,\nincluding the actions that never reached Execute. A backup left behind by an\nearlier updater run then puts back an old file next to newer ones. Each action\nnow only restores the backup it created. The backup that a precomplete remove\nshares with the add that follows it is restored by the remove, which rolls back\nlast.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329687\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/marFailurePartialStaleBackup.js", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_base.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/update/tests/unit_update_binary/xpcshell_service.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/updater.cpp"], "git_node": "c678c950244e309257a22108ff4614a5e7177169", "git_parents": ["f927eb6dbc11d97da2af53043a8c6bf30d4e52e1"], "node": "0b9dc405ebe9ad373e4093eb3c3fb594600c1726", "parents": ["2db0d8d1c84c95a0c0499c6c4cbfde6d218427d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076421 - Keep providing tighter bounds for painting svg items. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329729\n", "files": ["layout/svg/DisplaySVGItem.h"], "git_node": "6486cfcf8f4b546bd4ac72c969f540529ec01317", "git_parents": ["c678c950244e309257a22108ff4614a5e7177169"], "node": "7ed5b13995b900475709433e8e24d713528c4c24", "parents": ["0b9dc405ebe9ad373e4093eb3c3fb594600c1726"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073674 - Use moz-src for browser/components/migration r=settings-reviewers,migration-reviewers,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop,Gijs,joschmidt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327480\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/compon