vision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329590\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs"], "git_node": "ff604db5704f80a6850f8bd4871a5f0e824d37ce", "git_parents": ["536c98b4efa16a402dd4cbce4acf6859955ee839"], "node": "0650b7ceeff334023d2305eb8e6098b1aaa1fae9", "parents": ["1630f408875dae131eaff51a49f923319664f4ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Replace the tab's _fullyOpen expando and Tabbrowser's tabAnimationsInProgress counter with a set of opening tabs in the tab strip. r=kcochrane,tabbrowser-reviewers,sidebar-reviewers\n\ntabAnimationsInProgress becomes the number of opening tabs plus gBrowser._removingTabs, so it can't drift out of step with the tabs; the old counter didn't return to zero on Windows try runs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329593\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-performance/browser_tabclose.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-performance/head.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_vertical_tabs_fitts.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabs.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_drag_horizontal_overflow.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_drag_tab_group_expand_on_drop.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_overflowScroll.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_scroll_size_determination.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tabCloseProbes.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_groups.js", "testing/mochitest/BrowserTestUtils/BrowserTestUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d0caf60394c37c38c41119e402e1f244e32d4bec", "git_parents": ["ff604db5704f80a6850f8bd4871a5f0e824d37ce"], "node": "72ae7288f7d40c3c3cf27858a2c071d76e0db982", "parents": ["0650b7ceeff334023d2305eb8e6098b1aaa1fae9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Derive the tab's permanentKey from its browser. r=kcochrane,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nA closed tab now returns undefined, since _endRemoveTab clears linkedBrowser; every reader works on live tabs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329768\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/test_persist_closed_tabs_restore_manually.py", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs"], "git_node": "eda5f9e63a592a169e8426d4e3cd9b72a727405a", "git_parents": ["d0caf60394c37c38c41119e402e1f244e32d4bec"], "node": "812c55f608a5fd0893e0b1bf1871fed992b111ef", "parents": ["72ae7288f7d40c3c3cf27858a2c071d76e0db982"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Make the tab's canonicalUrl a public field. r=kcochrane,tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329770\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs", "browser/components/tabnotes/TabNotesController.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "0ab9d2ead6ce8db965df2c343dab92775e576d1d", "git_parents": ["eda5f9e63a592a169e8426d4e3cd9b72a727405a"], "node": "5e56e66052527403fef0730548bd1512dd26cde4", "parents": ["812c55f608a5fd0893e0b1bf1871fed992b111ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Make the tab's linkedBrowser a public field. r=kcochrane,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329771\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs"], "git_node": "b054941d8a6de0e10101e19e7d3ec1cbdcea9d32", "git_parents": ["0ab9d2ead6ce8db965df2c343dab92775e576d1d"], "node": "419e15c6122e7fdb9f0c1e8866147d9ec507a864", "parents": ["5e56e66052527403fef0730548bd1512dd26cde4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072811 - Make most BTP purge telemetry permanent and renew purge event probe. r=manuel\n\nThese metrics measure the core effectiveness of bounce tracking\nprotection, so they stay relevant for as long as the feature ships.\nRather than renewing them every few versions, mark the collection\npermanent, as bug 2026438 already did for\n`bounce.tracking.protection.mode`.\n\nPermanent collections must have instrumentation tests. Each metric is\ncovered by a `testGetValue()` assertion:\n  num_hosts_per_purge_run   test_bouncetracking_telemetry_purge_num_hosts.js\n  purge_count               browser_bouncetracking_telemetry_purge_count.js\n  purge_count_classified_tracker  test_bouncetracking_purge_telemetry.js\n  purge_duration            browser_bouncetracking_telemetry_purge_duration.js\n  (purge_action              browser_bouncetracking_telemetry_purge_events.js)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326888\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "0951b30ae2681d7b5952862a185bd2f2b23881d9", "git_parents": ["b054941d8a6de0e10101e19e7d3ec1cbdcea9d32"], "node": "a2bb789eace660f187ddde58aa2cce50fbc4e13b", "parents": ["419e15c6122e7fdb9f0c1e8866147d9ec507a864"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luk\u00e1\u0161 Lipinsk\u00fd \u003c6032558+Mr-Tao@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 500911 - Preserve focus during bulk session restore. r=sfoster,tabbrowser-reviewers,sthompson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315350\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_history_recently_closed.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/SessionStoreTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_906076_lazy_tabs.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_closed_tabs_windows.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_restore_preserves_focus.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_restore_window_closed_before_show.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_lastSeenActive.js", "browser/modules/BrowserWindowTracker.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "43f5a9e0a11db5b39720aeac9e44ddff6e96510e", "git_parents": ["0951b30ae2681d7b5952862a185bd2f2b23881d9"], "node": "2e7ad1a4eb5c99bbed176e0911134f3ea9a8f280", "parents": ["a2bb789eace660f187ddde58aa2cce50fbc4e13b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067742 - Update ffvpx Vulkan Video sources with FFmpeg ebb6f28da5. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nTake Vulkan video sources from FFmpeg ebb6f28da5 (libavcodec 63.14.100,\nlibavutil 61.7.100; Ampere COINCIDE-only init fix). The rest of ffvpx,\nincluding version.h, stays 9.0.1 (libavcodec 63.1.101, libavutil\n61.1.101). Drop av1_tilesize.patch (that change is already upstream).\nCompile FFmpeg random_seed.c and sha.c only with GTK Vulkan so vulkan.c\nkeeps av_get_random_seed(); do not add them to Windows mozavutil\n(HAVE_BCRYPT would import bcrypt.dll). Add uuid.c for\nhwcontext_vulkan.c's av_uuid_parse. Comment out h264dec.h in\nvulkan_decode.c (ffvpx does not ship the H.264 decoder). Replace\nff_vk_exec_add_dep_buf in avutil.symbols with the AVRefStruct exec-dep\nhelpers.\n\nSystem FFmpeg is built with --enable-libdrm, so vulkan_map_from() for\nDRM_PRIME is compiled in. ffvpx left CONFIG_LIBDRM unset. Enable it only\nfor hwcontext_vulkan.c. Reuse widget/gtk va_drmcommon.h through a mozva\nstub, and drmGetDevice from mozdrm.cpp (NSPR_LIBS; the mozbuild sysroot\ndoes not provide -ldrm).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329759\n", "files": ["media/ffvpx/README_MOZILLA", "media/ffvpx/av1_tilesize.patch", "media/ffvpx/config_override.h", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_av1.c", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_decode.c", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_decode.h", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_video.c", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_video.h", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_vp9.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/avutil.symbols", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/moz.build", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/random_seed.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/sha.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/sha.h", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/uuid.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/uuid.h", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/vulkan.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/vulkan.h", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/vulkan_functions.h", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/vulkan_loader.h", "media/ffvpx/vulkan-decode-no-h264dec.patch", "media/mozva/va/va_drmcommon.h", "third_party/drm/libdrm/mozdrm.cpp"], "git_node": "d8cf6823574299af77c32b32ca6cfd894717e541", "git_parents": ["43f5a9e0a11db5b39720aeac9e44ddff6e96510e"], "node": "e442e4ef248286148f6e7afda19c7aa22cc8a268", "parents": ["2e7ad1a4eb5c99bbed176e0911134f3ea9a8f280"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the SSE2 startup error `-march` flag from `browser/app/Makefile.in` to `browser/app/moz.build` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre,sergesanspaille\n\nThe `CXX` filter removed nothing, because `mozconfig.linux32` passes the SSE\nflags through `CXXFLAGS` and `browser/app/moz.build` already strips them from\n`OS_CXXFLAGS`. Only the appended `-march=pentiumpro` had an effect.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329022\n", "files": ["browser/app/Makefile.in", "browser/app/moz.build"], "git_node": "853c52d6485009a7e50d420380e07ec70d70c53f", "git_parents": ["d8cf6823574299af77c32b32ca6cfd894717e541"], "node": "71eb17c2675c74ca69fbf999d544ff889673f59b", "parents": ["e442e4ef248286148f6e7afda19c7aa22cc8a268"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Remove the unused `MK_COMPILE_DEFINES` from `config.mk` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nNothing in the tree assigns it, so all four references expand to nothing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328993\n", "files": ["config/config.mk"], "git_node": "bafa06ddb83a2d64aafb8110a2d653ca235ccd1c", "git_parents": ["853c52d6485009a7e50d420380e07ec70d70c53f"], "node": "31f6ad54c2a9277cf35988adcd9f07ae42c0f87b", "parents": ["71eb17c2675c74ca69fbf999d544ff889673f59b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Remove the unset `MOZ_GLUE_LDFLAGS` from `rules.mk` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nNothing in the tree assigns it and it is absent from a generated `autoconf.mk`,\nso it expands to nothing on every shared library link. Supplying it to Make by\nhand used to reach that link and no longer does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328995\n", "files": ["config/rules.mk"], "git_node": "71924504c2533f567c37b8412e50346e40085625", "git_parents": ["bafa06ddb83a2d64aafb8110a2d653ca235ccd1c"], "node": "a133f69cf0931298cf66d407779a68bb6c6a9590", "parents": ["31f6ad54c2a9277cf35988adcd9f07ae42c0f87b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Correct the stale `config/export` comment in `recurse.mk` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329014\n", "files": ["config/recurse.mk"], "git_node": "0af02bf1bdb6e7bb121aaa47f8c9a2d4131adbff", "git_parents": ["71924504c2533f567c37b8412e50346e40085625"], "node": "84f4bd21dd655835ad7fc5df52a69d26cb033793", "parents": ["a133f69cf0931298cf66d407779a68bb6c6a9590"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Pass `append_env` to `BuildBackend.build()` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\n`BuildDriver` sets the PGO mode through `append_env`, and a backend with its own\n`build()` never received it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329015\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/base.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/controller/building.py"], "git_node": "57985b58b7034556d74f935da75ba8999ae1a472", "git_parents": ["0af02bf1bdb6e7bb121aaa47f8c9a2d4131adbff"], "node": "e07948d339de865e65a1273a65495d797758939b", "parents": ["84f4bd21dd655835ad7fc5df52a69d26cb033793"], "tags": []}, {"author": "KayanoLiam \u003cKayano04@outlook.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044440 - Suppress accessibility click checks when cancelling drag start r=jsudiaman,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nFollow the existing synthesizeDropAfterDragOver pattern and suppress accessibility click handling only around the cancellation-path mouseup, as suggested in bug 2044440 comment 1.\n\nRemove the horizontal-overflow test waiver and add a real cancelled-drag regression test. The splitview test no longer has the old waiver.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329756\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_drag_horizontal_overflow.js", "testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/EventUtils.js", "testing/mochitest/tests/browser/browser.toml", "testing/mochitest/tests/browser/browser_EventUtils_drag_and_drop.js"], "git_node": "83a8c125dd551fcb109dcc389f5b6d42d679278a", "git_parents": ["57985b58b7034556d74f935da75ba8999ae1a472"], "node": "3a7b63f1b9d02a9569253b308bdcb2f9dbdba923", "parents": ["e07948d339de865e65a1273a65495d797758939b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 500911 - Preserve focus during bulk session restore. r=sfoster,tabbrowser-reviewers,sthompson\" for causing bc failures @ browser_restore_preserves_focus\n\nThis reverts commit 43f5a9e0a11db5b39720aeac9e44ddff6e96510e.\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_history_recently_closed.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/SessionStoreTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_906076_lazy_tabs.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_closed_tabs_windows.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_restore_preserves_focus.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_restore_window_closed_before_show.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_lastSeenActive.js", "browser/modules/BrowserWindowTracker.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "444288ee85a0671e9b852fd658c4d7bc2a46916c", "git_parents": ["83a8c125dd551fcb109dcc389f5b6d42d679278a"], "node": "7839634b7f69a19a84feb114b0927245122bd0b1", "parents": ["3a7b63f1b9d02a9569253b308bdcb2f9dbdba923"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2034831 - Improve static-analysis to lint all headers r=ahochheiden\n\nThis patch introduces a new moz.build variable, SOURCE_HEADERS, that\nlists headers source files that should be known to the build.\n\nThis variable is automatically populated based on the content of\nEXPORTS.* values.\n\nIt is used by the static analysis backend to generate compile commands\nentry to analyse those headers.\n\nAs a side effect of linting all those headers, list some problematic\nones in tools/clang-tidy/config.yaml.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328206\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/common.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/static_analysis.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/code_analysis/mach_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/compilation/database.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/context.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/data.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/emitter.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/reader.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/reader-source-headers-duplicate/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/reader-source-headers/exported.h", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/reader-source-headers/exported.inc", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/reader-source-headers/header.h", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/reader-source-headers/installed.h", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/reader-source-headers/installed.inc", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/reader-source-headers/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/test_emitter.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/test_reader.py", "tools/clang-tidy/config.yaml", "tools/lint/header-guards.yml"], "git_node": "a5ab2a134d7e90fa9d000d934efd079ec8bf6f6d", "git_parents": ["444288ee85a0671e9b852fd658c4d7bc2a46916c"], "node": "170c009a7c3b427249afa9b0c3f039004fc70b01", "parents": ["7839634b7f69a19a84feb114b0927245122bd0b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076509 - Retry transient upstream errors when vendor hosts look up the latest commit r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe googlesource, github, codeberg, and angle vendor hosts queried the\nupstream host with a bare requests.get() + raise_for_status(), bypassing the\nretrying session that BaseHost configures (retries on 429/500/502/503/504).\nA single transient 5xx from the upstream host therefore aborted\n`./mach vendor --check-for-update` outright.\n\nRoute these lookups through self.session so transient errors are retried,\nmatching what host_gitlab and BaseHost.download_single_file already do.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329794\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/host_angle.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/host_codeberg.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/host_github.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/host_googlesource.py"], "git_node": "d89e9533829055484156fc93b08c98e656befeee", "git_parents": ["a5ab2a134d7e90fa9d000d934efd079ec8bf6f6d"], "node": "33be635fe8e54616253ebdb9b7fb7aba58420199", "parents": ["170c009a7c3b427249afa9b0c3f039004fc70b01"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055094 - Remove Fxa-Tokens on Error rather then after use r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\n\nRN IP-Protections destroys fxa-tokens after use, we should rather do that after guardian\nhas told us they are not valid.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316980\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/GuardianTypes.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/enterprise/IPPEnterpriseAuthProvider.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/fxa/GuardianClient.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/fxa/IPPAndroidAuthProvider.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/fxa/IPPFxaActivateAuthProvider.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_GuardianClient.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPFxaActivateAuthProvider.js"], "git_node": "28b8f089d4b17cd75a321c0ae987b79571121bf7", "git_parents": ["d89e9533829055484156fc93b08c98e656befeee"], "node": "0946641cb0b32537fca2452f5c9d49b8a94f1d84", "parents": ["33be635fe8e54616253ebdb9b7fb7aba58420199"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075881 - Remove obsolete parts of the mingw clang toolchain build. r=tjr,firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nmingw-w64 has provided the stack protector functions in libmingwex since v11, so libssp no longer needs to be\nbuilt from GCC sources; clang still links -lssp_nonshared -lssp, so empty archives are installed instead. That\nleaves the GCC 9.5.0 source fetch used only by the linux64-gcc-9 toolchain, which nothing uses, so both are\nremoved. llvm-windres replaces llvm-mingw's windres-wrapper, which leaves nothing using the llvm-mingw fetch.\nLike GNU windres, llvm-windres strips unescaped quotes from -D values as a shell would, unless --use-temp-file\nis passed; create_res.py passes it so quoted string defines such as PBMODE_ICO survive (GNU windres and the\nold wrapper accept it too).\n\nThe dispatchqueue and ts_sd patches are already upstream (they only applied with fuzz), ucrt is already the\nmingw-w64 configure default, the toolchain's default _WIN32_WINNT moves from 0x601 to mingw-w64's default of\n0xa00 (the value Gecko defines for itself), the toolchain task has no binutils fetch to add to PATH, the\ndropped CMake variables are no longer read by LLVM's runtimes, and LLVM's CMake already defines\n_LIBCXXABI_DISABLE_VISIBILITY_ANNOTATIONS and _LIBCPP_HAS_THREAD_API_WIN32 for static Windows builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329434\n", "files": ["config/create_res.py", "taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/clang.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/gcc.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-clang-mingw.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/mingw-dispatchqueue.patch", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/mingw-ts_sd.patch"], "git_node": "e8652e39f5cf0dbaa4c228b97702c979a5c6bba9", "git_parents": ["28b8f089d4b17cd75a321c0ae987b79571121bf7"], "node": "8e2dcca20a7298ec5180676a9b448f088dcf2c64", "parents": ["0946641cb0b32537fca2452f5c9d49b8a94f1d84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075881 - Define ABSL_FORCE_THREAD_IDENTITY_MODE for mingw builds. r=tjr,firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nabseil picks the pthread_setspecific mode for mingw, and upstream\nhttps://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp/pull/2155 made ABSL_FORCE_THREAD_IDENTITY_MODE usable there. Defining it\nin mozilla-config.h, which every compile force-includes, keeps protobuf and every other abseil includer on the\nsame mode, which is what moz-patch-stack/0004.patch did by editing the header. thread_identity.h goes back to\nupstream.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329435\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/windows.configure", "third_party/abseil-cpp/absl/base/internal/thread_identity.h", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0004.patch"], "git_node": "b40a6e8eaca4147f51547f445f8a9069a80cd593", "git_parents": ["e8652e39f5cf0dbaa4c228b97702c979a5c6bba9"], "node": "5372a168c1072ef05d598b5b5b303b295d61ba37", "parents": ["8e2dcca20a7298ec5180676a9b448f088dcf2c64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075881 - Remove obsolete settings from the mingw build configuration. r=tjr,firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nwidl no longer reads WIDL_TIME_OVERRIDE, the binutils PATH entry points at a fetch the mingw builds do not\nhave, geckodriver is already off by default in automation, and lld enables --dynamicbase by default for MinGW\ntargets. The 32-bit and 64-bit mozharness base configs only differed in the platform key, which the\nsub-configs override, so they become one file, without the Mercurial share settings the build action never\nreads. The two mingwclang mozconfigs differed only in the target CPU and now share build/mozconfig.mingwclang,\nand the build jobs' common run config, fetches and settings move to task-defaults (the generated task\ndefinitions are unchanged).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329436\n", "files": ["browser/config/mozconfigs/win32/mingwclang", "browser/config/mozconfigs/win64/mingwclang", "build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure", "build/mozconfig.mingwclang", "taskcluster/kinds/build/windows-mingw.yml", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_base_windows_32_mingw_builds.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_base_windows_64_mingw_builds.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_base_windows_mingw_builds.py", "toolkit/moz.build", "widget/windows/moz.build"], "git_node": "cf41d3891ea99e1ad02e1cb584eaf4fc287cd49f", "git_parents": ["b40a6e8eaca4147f51547f445f8a9069a80cd593"], "node": "5b6f595359e2055d27fe29129ac36533fc189e16", "parents": ["5372a168c1072ef05d598b5b5b303b295d61ba37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075881 - Use the windows-gnullvm Rust targets in mingwclang builds. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe *-pc-windows-gnu Rust targets assume mingw-gcc: rustc links libgcc, libgcc_eh and libpthread, passes\n-nodefaultlibs, and creates import libraries with binutils dlltool. That is what the dummy libraries in\nbuild/win32, the explicit -lunwind, -C default-linker-libraries=yes and -C dlltool were working around. The\n*-pc-windows-gnullvm targets (tier 2, Windows 10+) are meant for LLVM-based mingw toolchains like ours: they\nlink libunwind themselves, keep the compiler's default libraries and write import libraries with LLVM.\nconfigure maps the mingw targets to them instead. bindgen passes cargo's target to libclang, which rejects the\ngnullvm triple, so configure now gives it the configure target explicitly, as it already does for other cross\ntargets.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329437\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/bindgen.configure", "build/moz.configure/rust.configure", "build/win32/dummy_libs.py", "build/win32/moz.build", "config/makefiles/rust.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/rust_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/configure/test_toolchain_configure.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_rust_commands.py", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/rust.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/repack_rust.py"], "git_node": "7ef9ec18caf1a3821f44c3eac7b5892cfbabebfe", "git_parents": ["cf41d3891ea99e1ad02e1cb584eaf4fc287cd49f"], "node": "e28111032ffda7157785cd1a21c7200367379e76", "parents": ["5b6f595359e2055d27fe29129ac36533fc189e16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1561797 - Build the update agent in mingwclang builds. r=tjr,firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe Rust link failure it was disabled for no longer happens with the current mingw-clang toolchain and lld.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329438\n", "files": ["build/mozconfig.mingwclang"], "git_node": "da734bbc6260412e51bd1a955a362b81fa744ae9", "git_parents": ["7ef9ec18caf1a3821f44c3eac7b5892cfbabebfe"], "node": "c2ade6b75a9f605b7c80a38d9bda3e6d839f515a", "parents": ["e28111032ffda7157785cd1a21c7200367379e76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2067742 - Update ffvpx Vulkan Video sources with FFmpeg ebb6f28da5. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit d8cf6823574299af77c32b32ca6cfd894717e541.\n", "files": ["media/ffvpx/README_MOZILLA", "media/ffvpx/av1_tilesize.patch", "media/ffvpx/config_override.h", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_av1.c", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_decode.c", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_decode.h", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_video.c", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_video.h", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vulkan_vp9.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/avutil.symbols", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/moz.build", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/random_seed.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/sha.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/sha.h", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/uuid.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/uuid.h", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/vulkan.c", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/vulkan.h", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/vulkan_functions.h", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/vulkan_loader.h", "media/ffvpx/vulkan-decode-no-h264dec.patch", "media/mozva/va/va_drmcommon.h", "third_party/drm/libdrm/mozdrm.cpp"], "git_node": "3ba090fc2f365740424e6dabd4ae24591c5c6c0b", "git_parents": ["da734bbc6260412e51bd1a955a362b81fa744ae9"], "node": "a97299af253676b07b52d8d36210e47e812df504", "parents": ["c2ade6b75a9f605b7c80a38d9bda3e6d839f515a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055094 - Remove Fxa-Tokens on Error rather then after use r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\" for causing xpcshell failures @ test_GuardianClient\n\nThis reverts commit 28b8f089d4b17cd75a321c0ae987b79571121bf7.\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/GuardianTypes.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/enterprise/IPPEnterpriseAuthProvider.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/fxa/GuardianClient.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/fxa/IPPAndroidAuthProvider.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/fxa/IPPFxaActivateAuthProvider.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_GuardianClient.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPFxaActivateAuthProvider.js"], "git_node": "e53bd221f218ff86dfa0615fbfe0c6ba738593e6", "git_parents": ["3ba090fc2f365740424e6dabd4ae24591c5c6c0b"], "node": "82b1478343418e277f2367c35889462f2ac0f1ce", "parents": ["a97299af253676b07b52d8d36210e47e812df504"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Mendez \u003cjmendez@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067888 - Remove leftover popPrefEnv calls in test helper. r=mstriemer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322408\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/printing/tests/head.js"], "git_node": "8a1f0c3910cc763e8c0a1bbb8ad88e46c9bd6da9", "git_parents": ["e53bd221f218ff86dfa0615fbfe0c6ba738593e6"], "node": "98af161dd4333eda1d984d19240e92918e084db3", "parents": ["82b1478343418e277f2367c35889462f2ac0f1ce"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790784152, "git_changesets": ["d2647098b912fa0b8b1bba735d237f916835a35f", "ceae86235f6a5558a07620117ea4d22e6d35f282", "9257c327ff7e3cd76233473434f615f0e9068100", "9b9c3b939af110250cd586e9a881b8d17187f97f", "8c37fcbb59db59f5636a9515be6bf2856e94d5b2", "bb44c0986df5a41e75af8fcd9a0d7cd0f6ea34b3", "bf0dd2eb06540125b9ba0d975d4c45095913f189", "4f64a8898108e6814e6140650468694af1b7b6a5", "660cc474e58da70216cdadde4612eb34c5ab41e1", "3f478a6656b23d3255406f882763f2bbc55dce3d", "9fb298cd5568e85e7221d2a48302e36a8129b7bd", "d969610cf36715dddff64cebb05d5ca48fbf0740", "3c5b87784f8127e1f4f33385b56a677ed2a8b02c", "058a566a27230df0684fb661fe0e4b8eaa830093", "fd8b5f0d805ce26e053ccdf5e9e2e9521dd2c235", "ddf89dbf4d3b665f5dc3719e482f22be321fd0ee", "3bb0188f98c21d404ec984b6d75d85b43f16a921", "f75cf62900ed33f6d440fdbd5e1ca9476f57447b", "236ac0b91469842a0e57920976882d5c3ca8ff3d", "21346e5a26c411d41835d5ce86226538f952b671", "f7e9c503bd37d0eb8ca2d8e08de553ac0155f60e", "24aaee3c87762962c0af41ce969f343b36ee747c", "51cf54526a1d01ef6c25d2b3e2c790c6d4c67f77", "138887a75b63f4417cb4ac8de5212dcb95ef03c4", "62a5514aaaf8a664edb7912faff4767a8b1d6dc5", "536c98b4efa16a402dd4cbce4acf6859955ee839", "ff604db5704f80a6850f8bd4871a5f0e824d37ce", "d0caf60394c37c38c41119e402e1f244e32d4bec", "eda5f9e63a592a169e8426d4e3cd9b72a727405a", "0ab9d2ead6ce8db965df2c343dab92775e576d1d", "b054941d8a6de0e10101e19e7d3ec1cbdcea9d32", "0951b30ae2681d7b5952862a185bd2f2b23881d9", "43f5a9e0a11db5b39720aeac9e44ddff6e96510e", "d8cf6823574299af77c32b32ca6cfd894717e541", "853c52d6485009a7e50d420380e07ec70d70c53f", "bafa06ddb83a2d64aafb8110a2d653ca235ccd1c", "71924504c2533f567c37b8412e50346e40085625", "0af02bf1bdb6e7bb121aaa47f8c9a2d4131adbff", "57985b58b7034556d74f935da75ba8999ae1a472", "83a8c125dd551fcb109dcc389f5b6d42d679278a", "444288ee85a0671e9b852fd658c4d7bc2a46916c", "a5ab2a134d7e90fa9d000d934efd079ec8bf6f6d", "d89e9533829055484156fc93b08c98e656befeee", "28b8f089d4b17cd75a321c0ae987b79571121bf7", "e8652e39f5cf0dbaa4c228b97702c979a5c6bba9", "b40a6e8eaca4147f51547f445f8a9069a80cd593", "cf41d3891ea99e1ad02e1cb584eaf4fc287cd49f", "7ef9ec18caf1a3821f44c3eac7b5892cfbabebfe", "da734bbc6260412e51bd1a955a362b81fa744ae9", "3ba090fc2f365740424e6dabd4ae24591c5c6c0b", "e53bd221f218ff86dfa0615fbfe0c6ba738593e6", "8a1f0c3910cc763e8c0a1bbb8ad88e46c9bd6da9"], "user": "amarc@mozilla.com"}, "45455": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 0286569ff81e3989d717dee3bd73fb2a1f097339 with DEVEDITION_158_0b2_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "e29f270fd9b649873347c30925aa4b23a74ed77f", "git_parents": ["9f823fd23fb9457e51151670e9d033acc146b136"], "node": "ce35cdb2f435763feefcd5da388e66fe3964aa45", "parents": ["cdf0d78dbd340037ba9ac5c704bf1bba892f9b60"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790790029, "git_changesets": ["e29f270fd9b649873347c30925aa4b23a74ed77f"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45456": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 0286569ff81e3989d717dee3bd73fb2a1f097339 with FIREFOX_158_0b2_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "63a4619f4d4ac6dd13827bb15d4e5ce10018c2a8", "git_parents": ["e29f270fd9b649873347c30925aa4b23a74ed77f"], "node": "70066e9142f26d889ca61c2ee2278eb6ce84f391", "parents": ["ce35cdb2f435763feefcd5da388e66fe3964aa45"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790792699, "git_changesets": ["63a4619f4d4ac6dd13827bb15d4e5ce10018c2a8"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45457": {"changesets": [{"author": "Helena \u003chballent@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066774 - Expose the pasted transferable's data in the paste event instead of the clipboard r!masayuki r=masayuki\n\nThe bug in macOS Writing tools happened because PasteTransferableAsAction dispatches a paste event before inserting, and built that event's DataTransfer from the global clipboard for HTMLEditor. It is left  empty for TextEditor, so a page which handles the paste event itself received the clipboard contents rather than the data being pasted. The fix is to build the DataTransfer from the transferable instead, for both editors.\n\nCreating a DataTransfer from a transferable consumes the input streams in it, so the same DataTransfer is passed on to HandlePasteTransferable and to the editor which handles the paste when a paste event listener changes focus.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327911\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/EditorBase.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorBase.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDataTransfer.cpp", "editor/libeditor/TextEditor.h", "editor/libeditor/TextEditorDataTransfer.cpp", "editor/libeditor/tests/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_pasteTransferable_data_in_paste_event.html"], "git_node": "eadc6ab534cacf743a3becfd11667ae80fbfe01c", "git_parents": ["8a1f0c3910cc763e8c0a1bbb8ad88e46c9bd6da9"], "node": "cd18caf0683fe6b1bff86f5bb9c6a4d02cc27422", "parents": ["98af161dd4333eda1d984d19240e92918e084db3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070642 - Add an assertion_failure structured log action and a shared parser r=ahal\n\nNative assertion failures (MOZ_ASSERT's \"Assertion failure:\", \"Hit\nMOZ_CRASH\", NS_ASSERTION's \"###!!! ASSERTION\" and \"###!!! ABORT\") and the\nstack MozWalkTheStack prints after them only exist in test logs as raw\nprocess_output lines, so nothing downstream can attach the stack to the\nevent.\n\nAdd an assertion_failure structured log action carrying the kind, message,\nsource location, process/thread, whether the assertion is fatal, and the\nstack as profiler-format frames, and a shared AssertionFailureParser in\nmoztest, modelled on the TSan parser, that harnesses feed with their\nprocess output. The parser understands the frame shapes produced by\nfix_stacks (breakpad and native symbols), partially fixed and unfixed\nframes, tolerates a few interleaved lines from other processes, and folds\nthe \"Hit MOZ_CRASH([...] ###!!! ASSERTION ...)\" line that\nXPCOM_DEBUG_BREAK=stack-and-abort prints after an NS_ASSERTION into that\nassertion instead of reporting it twice.\n\nThe mach formatter renders the action on one line; the tbpl formatter\ndeliberately does not, so the task log (and Treeherder's failure summary)\nkeep showing the original line only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324872\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/machformatter.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/structuredlog.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_formatters.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_structured.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_testsummary.py", "testing/mozbase/moztest/moztest/assertions.py", "testing/mozbase/moztest/tests/manifest.toml", "testing/mozbase/moztest/tests/test_assertions.py"], "git_node": "084739c10aafd42fa321db332659f9f4db305a56", "git_parents": ["eadc6ab534cacf743a3becfd11667ae80fbfe01c"], "node": "4a694325d756c151f2d824a370ab81cce1db5e3e", "parents": ["cd18caf0683fe6b1bff86f5bb9c6a4d02cc27422"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070642 - Record assertion failures as markers in resource usage profiles r=ahal\n\nDispatch the assertion_failure action from both the local ResourceHandler\nand the CI StructuredOutputParser to a new SystemResourceMonitor handler,\nso each assertion becomes an \"AssertionFailure\" marker named after its\nkind, carrying the message, source location, process and thread, and the\nreal native stack (red when fatal, orange for a non-fatal NS_ASSERTION).\n\nThe monitor already built a \"C++ assertion\" marker out of the raw\n\"###!!! ASSERTION\" process_output line, with a synthetic one-frame stack,\nwhile the \"#NN:\" frames that followed became generic output markers, and\n\"Assertion failure:\"/\"Hit MOZ_CRASH\" lines were not recognized at all.\nKeep a line-based path for harnesses that do not emit the action yet, but\ndrive it with the shared AssertionFailureParser: the frames are folded into\nthe marker instead of producing output markers, and a pending line-based\nreport is dropped when the structured action for the same assertion\narrives, so wired harnesses get exactly one marker per assertion. The\nprevious single-line marker remains as the fallback when moztest is not\nimportable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324873\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/handlers/resourcehandler.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/mozsystemmonitor/resourcemonitor.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/tests/test_resource_monitor.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/structuredlog.py"], "git_node": "54d9999691f71e95daaaddcd980edbffc3b905b9", "git_parents": ["084739c10aafd42fa321db332659f9f4db305a56"], "node": "ece015aa7a65e9b1ecf68ba9bef254f4743e0591", "parents": ["4a694325d756c151f2d824a370ab81cce1db5e3e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070642 - mochitest/xpcshell: emit assertion_failure from process output r=ahal\n\nFeed the process output of mochitest (OutputHandler, after stack fixing,\nkeyed by the emitting GECKO stream) and xpcshell (each test's lines as\nthey are logged, live or replayed) to the shared AssertionFailureParser,\nso the assertion_failure action follows the raw lines in the structured\nlog and the resource usage profile gets a marker with the real stack.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324874\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/runtests.py", "testing/xpcshell/runxpcshelltests.py", "testing/xpcshell/selftest.py"], "git_node": "c0dddd155fdc05245da7d7ef10bd0c4d6cf873b4", "git_parents": ["54d9999691f71e95daaaddcd980edbffc3b905b9"], "node": "5b109009726e6fdc418330d898c21781b5c8dd92", "parents": ["ece015aa7a65e9b1ecf68ba9bef254f4743e0591"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075598 - Run safari perf tests on the macOS 27 r=perftest-reviewers,aglavic,mozperftest-reviewers\n\nThis patch routes the safari performance tests on a new (but limited)\nmacOS 27.x pool. Safari/Safari-tech-preview versions are generally tied\nto the OS version so this gives us more up to date performance numbers\nfor these applications.\n\nAdditionally, properly report the webkit build version (CFBundleVersion)\nalong with the marketing version.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329203\n", "files": ["python/mozperftest/mozperftest/perfdocs/hardware.yml", "taskcluster/config.yml", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/target_tasks.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/other.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/raptor.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/worker.py", "taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/desktop.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/test-platforms.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/test-sets.yml", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/raptor.py", "testing/perfdocs/generated/performance-infrastructure.md", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md", "testing/raptor/raptor/cmdline.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/perftest.py"], "git_node": "e99653056624be68e0e34705553ba7486e49a38b", "git_parents": ["c0dddd155fdc05245da7d7ef10bd0c4d6cf873b4"], "node": "7de7eae8733817101c319140eeeb2a9abf22ffa2", "parents": ["5b109009726e6fdc418330d898c21781b5c8dd92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057979 - Part 8 - Remove the Make driven Windows installer build r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nThe uninstaller, the maintenance service installer and the test stub\ninstaller are built and installed from `browser/installer/windows/moz.build`,\nand `setup.exe` from the `stage_installer` rule, all through `nsis_stage` and\n`nsis_build`. Locale repacks build their uninstaller through the same actions\nin process, so `l10n_repackage` no longer needs a make binary.\n\nOnly the installer and the stub scripts read `MOZ_BUILDID`, so the build id\nleaves `defines.nsi` and reaches makensis as a define on those compiles. The\nshared staging then has no input that changes on every build, and an\nincremental build recompiles the test stub alone rather than every installer\n`dist/bin` carries.\n\ncomm-central's `mail/Makefile.in` still runs the shared `uninstaller` and\n`maintenanceservice_installer` rules this removes, and its installer relied on\nthe shared `$(CONFIG_DIR)/setup.exe` recipe, so Thunderbird has to declare its\nown `nsis_stage` and `nsis_build` edges before this lands.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325636\n", "files": ["browser/Makefile.in", "browser/build.mk", "browser/installer/windows/Makefile.in", "browser/installer/windows/docs/InstallerBuild.md", "browser/installer/windows/moz.build", "browser/installer/windows/nsis/Makefile.in", "browser/installer/windows/nsis/defines.nsi.in", "browser/moz.build", "moz.configure", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/l10n_repackage.py", "toolkit/locales/l10n.mk", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/windows/nsis/makensis.mk"], "git_node": "7b33b38397fa93f6902cdf00874e4002a34cef1b", "git_parents": ["e99653056624be68e0e34705553ba7486e49a38b"], "node": "a90a80153cde3e1c392b1a25930d80f21c1f2b53", "parents": ["7de7eae8733817101c319140eeeb2a9abf22ffa2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Bonardo \u003cmbonardo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072501. r=Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329224\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/reputationservice/ApplicationReputation.cpp", "toolkit/components/reputationservice/test/gtest/TestExecutableLists.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileCommon.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileCommon.h"], "git_node": "57c3f4e2ba4adf5f415991cd02887dbd3dbe8680", "git_parents": ["7b33b38397fa93f6902cdf00874e4002a34cef1b"], "node": "f8ef08a51fa3008659535186aae61a1b2d57fd97", "parents": ["a90a80153cde3e1c392b1a25930d80f21c1f2b53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076727 - Mark conformance2/glsl3/vector-dynamic-indexing.html as failing on macOS aarch64 non-nightly builds. r=release-managers,diannaS\n\nOn macOS, ANGLE is only enabled on Nightly (`webgl.disable-angle` is false only for `XP_MACOSX && NIGHTLY_BUILD` in StaticPrefList.yaml). Beta/Release on Apple Silicon use the native GL backend, and this test fails there (\"at (0, 0) expected: 0,255,0,255 was 255,0,0,255\"). The failure shows up in the central-as-beta simulation, so it would go perma-orange when 159 merges to beta.\n\nThis adds `fail-if = os == 'mac' && os_version == '15.30' && arch == 'aarch64' && !nightly_build` to the errata, the same annotation many other WebGL conformance tests in this file already use for this backend difference, and regenerates the generated manifest.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329941\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/generated/generated-mochitest-webgl2-ext-conformance2-glsl3.toml", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/mochitest-errata.toml"], "git_node": "55e81b9afbd1e6ca2b286ebb8d5798f90d2039db", "git_parents": ["57c3f4e2ba4adf5f415991cd02887dbd3dbe8680"], "node": "f06f336eef0c0ab9ef8e4c50e93268ad3eb3baa3", "parents": ["f8ef08a51fa3008659535186aae61a1b2d57fd97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryan Johns \u003cbjohns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069436 - Added /answer path for search_the_web r=gazhibekova,ai-platform-reviewers,npodgurski\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323775\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Chat.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Conversation.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/SecurityProperties.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/openAIEngine.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/search/SearchWorkflow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_search_the_web.js", "toolkit/components/ml/content/EngineProcess.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/content/backends/OpenAIPipeline.mjs"], "git_node": "7241acfee727a8b0a993a32926834d522e55bc57", "git_parents": ["55e81b9afbd1e6ca2b286ebb8d5798f90d2039db"], "node": "27a5de58a3577a52c0f4b6cc86568d9419eebe61", "parents": ["f06f336eef0c0ab9ef8e4c50e93268ad3eb3baa3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072270 - Migrate the remaining gtest markers to BaseMarkerType. r=canova,profiler-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328459\n", "files": ["tools/profiler/tests/gtest/GeckoProfiler.cpp"], "git_node": "eab9d325199c91cb607b87da5a76ea145ae388a1", "git_parents": ["7241acfee727a8b0a993a32926834d522e55bc57"], "node": "8e5b1a1f1e2e726230e278be06d794f034984d2d", "parents": ["27a5de58a3577a52c0f4b6cc86568d9419eebe61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072270 - Require marker types to derive from BaseMarkerType. r=canova,profiler-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328460\n", "files": ["mozglue/baseprofiler/public/BaseProfilerMarkersDetail.h", "mozglue/baseprofiler/public/BaseProfilerMarkersPrerequisites.h"], "git_node": "a81cf2e599bac99505648dffed64f51418f534d0", "git_parents": ["eab9d325199c91cb607b87da5a76ea145ae388a1"], "node": "83b5bd8072597b142f8152aaf5beb2442302690d", "parents": ["8e5b1a1f1e2e726230e278be06d794f034984d2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072270 - Update the profiler docs now that BaseMarkerType is required. r=canova,profiler-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328461\n", "files": ["tools/profiler/docs/code-overview.md", "tools/profiler/docs/markers-guide.md"], "git_node": "7ec48cf17455383a58cac5333987aaa5041e2c24", "git_parents": ["a81cf2e599bac99505648dffed64f51418f534d0"], "node": "d5915d0a684cf4d04c8e26a65d5d357d8de48252", "parents": ["83b5bd8072597b142f8152aaf5beb2442302690d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Farre \u003cfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075579 - #process-scroll-behavior should not restore scroll for \"reload\". r=sfarre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329159\n", "files": ["dom/events/NavigateEvent.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/scroll-behavior/after-transition-reload-no-scroll-anchoring.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/scroll-behavior/after-transition-reload.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/scroll-behavior/manual-scroll-reload-no-scroll-anchoring.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/scroll-behavior/manual-scroll-reload.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/scroll-behavior/after-transition-reload-after-traverse.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/scroll-behavior/after-transition-reload-no-fragment.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/scroll-behavior/after-transition-traverse-no-fragment.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/scroll-behavior/after-transition-traverse-to-fragment.html"], "git_node": "f501ef1617e86d6910da7e34a67d97c617364b22", "git_parents": ["7ec48cf17455383a58cac5333987aaa5041e2c24"], "node": "2fe781d90f5cf3f2065dd1b98200084999f723fa", "parents": ["d5915d0a684cf4d04c8e26a65d5d357d8de48252"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076619: Properly handle the case where both 'grid-template-rows' and 'grid-template-columns' are set in a grid-lanes container. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nPer spec (and interop with other browsers), this scenario should take\nthe \"Otherwise\" case in\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-grid-3/#grid-lanes-orientation and should\nestablish columns (and do masonry-layout aka stacking in the row axis).\n\nAs part of this, this patch also updates the documentation for the\nstate bits (the bits that we're setting here) to use the up-to-date\nspec terms, i.e. mentioning grid-lanes and defining which axis is the\n\"stacking axis\" instead of defining which axis has \"masonry layout\".\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329876\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsFrameStateBits.h", "layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/baseline/grid-lanes-grid-item-self-baseline-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/baseline/grid-lanes-grid-item-self-baseline-002a.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/baseline/grid-lanes-grid-item-self-baseline-002b.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/items/column-minimum-size-grid-items-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/column-track-sizing-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "4a3e4ad498639bfe5d6fe016574c9ef4597b3096", "git_parents": ["f501ef1617e86d6910da7e34a67d97c617364b22"], "node": "ce15670b49d3e8d2e868c6f55fc6e7c7c6d895e9", "parents": ["2fe781d90f5cf3f2065dd1b98200084999f723fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1922759 - Make nr_crypto_nss_hmac() work with FIPS enabled r=rrelyea,webrtc-reviewers,keeler,bwc\n\nHMAC is used for hash calculation only at nr_crypto_nss_hmac() so use derive instead of import to be FIPS compliant.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D224587\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/transport/nricectx.cpp"], "git_node": "91de7c72bccac01be2a1901dffdd55eea3cd0199", "git_parents": ["4a3e4ad498639bfe5d6fe016574c9ef4597b3096"], "node": "f618980879322690d800471393bf9d7b82853ab8", "parents": ["ce15670b49d3e8d2e868c6f55fc6e7c7c6d895e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Sirringhaus \u003cmartin.sirringhaus@suse.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1797270 - Make WebRTC work with FIPS enabled r=keeler,webrtc-reviewers,kershaw,bwc,webidl,smaug,ipc-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D225034\n", "files": ["dom/crypto/WebCryptoTask.cpp", "dom/crypto/WebCryptoTask.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestRTCCertStore.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build", "dom/media/webrtc/MediaTransportParent.h", "dom/media/webrtc/PMediaTransport.ipdl", "dom/media/webrtc/PRTCCertService.ipdl", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertCleanupTimer.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertCleanupTimer.h", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertService.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertService.h", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertServiceChild.h", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertServiceData.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertServiceData.h", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertServiceParent.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertServiceParent.h", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertStore.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertStore.h", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertificate.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/RTCCertificate.h", "dom/media/webrtc/WebrtcIPCTraits.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/MediaTransportHandler.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/MediaTransportHandler.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/MediaTransportHandlerIPC.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/MediaTransportHandlerIPC.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/MediaTransportParent.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.h", "dom/media/webrtc/moz.build", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/identity/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/identity/mochitest_no_socket_process.toml", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_certificates.html", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/build/moz.build", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/common.build", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/dtlsdigest.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/dtlsdigest.h", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/dtlsidentity.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/dtlsidentity.h", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/test/transport_unittests.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/transportlayerdtls.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transport/transportlayerdtls.h", "dom/tests/mochitest/whatwg/test_structuredCloneAndExposed.html", "dom/webidl/RTCCertificate.webidl", "ipc/glue/BackgroundParentImpl.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/mediapipeline_unittest.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/PSocketProcessBridge.ipdl", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessBridgeChild.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessBridgeParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessBridgeParent.h"], "git_node": "a7482b1babe9741e8e33beb370f6f038b6dbc2fa", "git_parents": ["91de7c72bccac01be2a1901dffdd55eea3cd0199"], "node": "42212185f7f1efaa48e78824b56691f3f827d6c5", "parents": ["f618980879322690d800471393bf9d7b82853ab8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1797270, 1922759: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/MediaTransportHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "95fdf608df3a6b747bf7e8909651e81f1ab184b9", "git_parents": ["a7482b1babe9741e8e33beb370f6f038b6dbc2fa"], "node": "f700d1e32debbc7f1f5f124b078bbb59b8d629e8", "parents": ["42212185f7f1efaa48e78824b56691f3f827d6c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075243 - Link within about:license by fragment only r=dao\n\nThe page URL is already about:license, so the absolute about:license#\nprefix is redundant, and it sends readers away when the file is opened\nfrom its chrome:// URL or from disk.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328961\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/license.html.mako"], "git_node": "ee43b686708555efe1ffc9d7c1cae8367da9d77c", "git_parents": ["95fdf608df3a6b747bf7e8909651e81f1ab184b9"], "node": "0c3aa8240469109600107bf2f8fa27cb1c590684", "parents": ["f700d1e32debbc7f1f5f124b078bbb59b8d629e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maryam \u003cmomar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062037 - reworking the Privacy Overview Documentation r=manuel\n\nThe goal is to make the python file (etp_matrix.py) and the doc easier\nto read and maintain.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326184\n", "files": ["docs/_addons/etp_matrix.py", "toolkit/components/antitracking/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "42231562f124d2bb7a0a327880b42f4b7c9d51a9", "git_parents": ["ee43b686708555efe1ffc9d7c1cae8367da9d77c"], "node": "c94a5e756579239e9973aa0ea89277c627278a6b", "parents": ["0c3aa8240469109600107bf2f8fa27cb1c590684"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Move _endRemoveArgs from the tab into Tabbrowser's private state. r=nsharpley,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329455\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs"], "git_node": "39f55f02f718019e021f880f611ec62cad9f2982", "git_parents": ["42231562f124d2bb7a0a327880b42f4b7c9d51a9"], "node": "c34ee9790c6bcdfc670586e02f307ac848bba4c5", "parents": ["c94a5e756579239e9973aa0ea89277c627278a6b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Move the tab close stopwatch IDs from the tab into Tabbrowser's private state. r=nsharpley,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329456\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs"], "git_node": "cf1e515a60be31cb1785e3f0efa1983a39fa50f9", "git_parents": ["39f55f02f718019e021f880f611ec62cad9f2982"], "node": "9e04648aa9279d4e5927b00100811334c8ba8d93", "parents": ["c34ee9790c6bcdfc670586e02f307ac848bba4c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Move _pendingPermitUnload from the tab into Tabbrowser's private state. r=nsharpley,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329457\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs"], "git_node": "375a137c2ea63527a2d217d1465b6514085437e8", "git_parents": ["cf1e515a60be31cb1785e3f0efa1983a39fa50f9"], "node": "a2e46d9f0191236b1cf0df29e5cef6a208b7f332", "parents": ["9e04648aa9279d4e5927b00100811334c8ba8d93"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Move _browserParams from the tab into Tabbrowser's private state. r=nsharpley,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329458\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/docs/lazy-browsers.md"], "git_node": "88457f76e191b399958e028663c82995e1215327", "git_parents": ["375a137c2ea63527a2d217d1465b6514085437e8"], "node": "f050c60dd729cd0a5cf516f7d14269b2e76ff506", "parents": ["a2e46d9f0191236b1cf0df29e5cef6a208b7f332"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Move _originalRegisteredOpenURI from the tab into Tabbrowser's private state. r=nsharpley,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329459\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs"], "git_node": "80a5dc5a0c25e13e75fff0929fdabed04e4d4d32", "git_parents": ["88457f76e191b399958e028663c82995e1215327"], "node": "3d646de7a7f6b6f7efeff94facdabf282651d217", "parents": ["f050c60dd729cd0a5cf516f7d14269b2e76ff506"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075016 - Move the tab's find bar references from the tab into Tabbrowser's private state. r=nsharpley,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\ngetCachedFindBar and isFindBarInitialized now also answer for a tab in another window; no caller passes one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329460\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.mjs"], "git_node": "8552664d9a3bc046a273d5ef4ee2780ee0e1550d", "git_parents": ["80a5dc5a0c25e13e75fff0929fdabed04e4d4d32"], "node": "63980a8e0ab8d84d654fdf97e92ae13690299e0b", "parents": ["3d646de7a7f6b6f7efeff94facdabf282651d217"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075335 - Fix selection shortcuts popup position when the browser's UI is an RTL language. r=yjamora\n\nFor background on the new Highlight to Search project, here is [[ https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lpprhnIKYbXSNnVE-OSmVcE1Vpm9_vBBIKIOjW8_0lE/edit?tab=t.os3nbc21wjhe | the current spec ]].\n\nThe selection shortcuts popup anchors to the \u003cbrowser\u003e element with a manually computed screen offset that assumes a fixed anchor corner, which flips when the anchor resolves to RTL (an RTL Firefox UI locale, regardless of the selected content's own language) and lands the popup far from the selection; mirror the offset for an RTL anchor instead of switching to a different anchoring API, to keep the popup's tab-tied lifecycle intact.\n\nTo test this out manually, use `./mach run --setpref browser.ml.chat.provider='https://chatgpt.com' --setpref intl.l10n.pseudo=bidi`. Then run `for (const id of [\"search-action-button\", \"copy-action-button\", \"more-actions-button\"]) { document.getElementById(id).hidden = false; }` in the browser toolbox to show the other action buttons that are part of the new Highlight to Search menu. (Those other buttons will have their behavior hooked up in later patches.) The menu appears when you select some text on a webpage.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329097\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js"], "git_node": "122db3c5ba277a74ca1058809dc9090628467a0f", "git_parents": ["8552664d9a3bc046a273d5ef4ee2780ee0e1550d"], "node": "1ce1a64d86ea6daa5b484417bd03d56db3495f62", "parents": ["63980a8e0ab8d84d654fdf97e92ae13690299e0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Moss \u003cjmoss@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074922 - Use mozharness ZIP helper for Talos archives r=ahal,releng-reviewers\n\nExtract Talos ZIP files with the existing mozharness helper. Use the path returned by ZipFile.extract when restoring permissions, because Windows replaces invalid filename characters. Update the Windows extraction test to check the sanitized output file.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328957\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/base/script.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/talos.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_base_script.py"], "git_node": "1d88fcebfcccbba062031d4d26c7c74f96066d32", "git_parents": ["122db3c5ba277a74ca1058809dc9090628467a0f"], "node": "dd28ae27aaf3ca86b831811634b12a5a00445ee9", "parents": ["1ce1a64d86ea6daa5b484417bd03d56db3495f62"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Oberhauser \u003cj.git@obez.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060659 - Part 1: Disable autofill settings on Automotive OS r=android-reviewers,sfamisa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://ph