/settingssearch/DefaultFenixSettingsIndexer.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/settingssearch/SettingsSearchFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/settingssearch/SettingsSearchProviderRegistrationTest.kt"], "git_node": "cd21d6c757065a6b899100cd5e3a2d3f4000edf6", "git_parents": ["cd36f1af73f3429c61c07975f0e10f1ad7bdf63f"], "node": "d440aa773c8fffc2285d49b93547983172b215a1", "parents": ["4c7c6b9612092946ef42e944b5fe51c94dd65d82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Oberhauser \u003cj.git@obez.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060659 - Part 4: Hide passwords in menu on Automotive OS r=android-reviewers,sfamisa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328936\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/MainMenu.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/MainMenuTest.kt"], "git_node": "aa93bd883217b4696655a6b4e2fdd0507773c035", "git_parents": ["cd21d6c757065a6b899100cd5e3a2d3f4000edf6"], "node": "5e130a27db2deb3287059b26816a7e7f1c5cb44f", "parents": ["d440aa773c8fffc2285d49b93547983172b215a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075690 - Fix file-bug.py to open URLs reliably under WSL r=ai4dev-reviewers,marco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329272\n", "files": [".agents/skills/bug-filing/file-bug.py", ".claude/skills/bug-filing/file-bug.py"], "git_node": "329bb36a25200f95614a090fa0a9dd491d1ea037", "git_parents": ["aa93bd883217b4696655a6b4e2fdd0507773c035"], "node": "f8e5847ed739a4b84f451e2255ce058a208ab784", "parents": ["5e130a27db2deb3287059b26816a7e7f1c5cb44f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075003 - Document why an engagement from a search bar in a web page survives a same-tab load. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329946\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/docs/telemetry.md"], "git_node": "e7c790b61d9055721feb713e63ab007e87fad1be", "git_parents": ["329bb36a25200f95614a090fa0a9dd491d1ea037"], "node": "a3c1525bf6642552dd5d53430a806dc4344e08d3", "parents": ["f8e5847ed739a4b84f451e2255ce058a208ab784"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076684 - Forget the right tab in sessions.forgetClosedTab() when the window has a closed tab group. r=extension-reviewers,robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329902\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-sessions.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_sessions_forgetClosedTab.js"], "git_node": "9ac436884589037d4908149ab77702ed8184acd5", "git_parents": ["e7c790b61d9055721feb713e63ab007e87fad1be"], "node": "985b4d1e2980a0c46b0a391dfb5bbe9ba7924126", "parents": ["a3c1525bf6642552dd5d53430a806dc4344e08d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 1: Move FPUDefaultQNaN\u003cT\u003e to Architecture-loong64.h for reuse. r=yury\n\nDue to the various mismatches among LoongArch ISA FP behavior, IEEE Std\n754-2008 and WASM semantics, it is sometimes required to manually\nconstruct canonical QNaNs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329414\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Architecture-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/Simulator-loong64.cpp"], "git_node": "daec05a8a2a3fca25063f293dab56b5bc0a9a848", "git_parents": ["9ac436884589037d4908149ab77702ed8184acd5"], "node": "59e8d8e0df91372eaa14e89c820b39c88b57bc40", "parents": ["985b4d1e2980a0c46b0a391dfb5bbe9ba7924126"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 2: Add register definitions for LSX. r=yury\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329415\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/LIR.h", "js/src/jit/Safepoints.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Architecture-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MoveEmitter-loong64.cpp"], "git_node": "27d947a0b1865d5b417fa18192dc8c3c7b5fcbcf", "git_parents": ["daec05a8a2a3fca25063f293dab56b5bc0a9a848"], "node": "817eeddffb769ac99ef6430b0c27a5105272237d", "parents": ["59e8d8e0df91372eaa14e89c820b39c88b57bc40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 3: Add commonly-used LSX {,dis}assembly methods. r=yury\n\nThe implemented instructions is only ~30% of the whole LSX instruction\nset, but they should be sufficient for implementing a working SIMD\nbackend. The selection is inspired by V8 and driven by later parts.\n\nLink: https://github.com/loongson-community/loongarch-opcodes\n (\"LoongArch Opcodes (unofficially compiled list)\")\nLink:\n https://jia.je/unofficial-loongarch-intrinsics-guide/migrating_sse/\n (\"Unofficial LoongArch Intrinsics Guide: Migrating from SSE to LSX\")\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329416\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/disasm/Disasm-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/disasm/Disasm-loong64.h"], "git_node": "c0d12b03bfa4578f42d099cb58d75cefb63e572d", "git_parents": ["27d947a0b1865d5b417fa18192dc8c3c7b5fcbcf"], "node": "03e3d7a16848d5ecd155a23a99374b1a54c38ab4", "parents": ["817eeddffb769ac99ef6430b0c27a5105272237d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 4: Implement frame and move operations for LSX. r=yury\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329417\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/Architecture-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MoveEmitter-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MoveEmitter-loong64.h"], "git_node": "59bdcf059b4e44861830e82224ce7bcc3463071a", "git_parents": ["c0d12b03bfa4578f42d099cb58d75cefb63e572d"], "node": "0cb375d2a61729215fca7314f543268bde9920c7", "parents": ["03e3d7a16848d5ecd155a23a99374b1a54c38ab4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 5: Add crashing stubs for SIMD-related methods on Loong64. r=yury\n\nThese are required for compiling with ENABLE_JIT_SIMD and will be\nimplemented in a later part.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329418\n", "files": ["js/src/irregexp/RegExpNativeMacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/LIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/Lowering-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/shared/CodeGenerator-shared.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmStubs.cpp"], "git_node": "c512b8e381ea6d6e8ae8f32a1323a37d3970c655", "git_parents": ["59bdcf059b4e44861830e82224ce7bcc3463071a"], "node": "15177167990566c31b44f86c838c9af498ce629f", "parents": ["0cb375d2a61729215fca7314f543268bde9920c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 6: Recognize LSX memory instructions in SummarizeTrapInstruction. r=yury\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329419\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmSummarizeInsn.cpp"], "git_node": "51dd37c7e056fa941cd2df9a4f49b9ff93035c73", "git_parents": ["c512b8e381ea6d6e8ae8f32a1323a37d3970c655"], "node": "cf950ca03afc272ae2cce2cf888c228aa6f9b36a", "parents": ["15177167990566c31b44f86c838c9af498ce629f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 7: Make --enable-jit-simd effective on Loong64. r=yury\n\nThis allows explicit enablement of SIMD on Loong64 backend. It's not\nenabled by default since most methods are stubs and will crash.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329420\n", "files": ["js/moz.configure"], "git_node": "715041e3663c9ff098396bc5a9567e7f3362c95f", "git_parents": ["51dd37c7e056fa941cd2df9a4f49b9ff93035c73"], "node": "11af78c273e06654e63e14f18fc63fc4d2befa3f", "parents": ["cf950ca03afc272ae2cce2cf888c228aa6f9b36a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 8: Implement SIMD-related methods and remove stubs. r=yury\n\nThis is the heavy part. Thanks to \"Unofficial LoongArch Intrinsics\nGuide\", the x{86,64} and arm64 backend, the precedent is rich.\n\nCertain relaxed SIMD tests are updated to reflect LoongArch specifics,\nwhich are captured on a Loongson 3B6000. Since we don't have\nauthoritative sources on how the ISA mandates the behavior, this is just\nan observation.\n\nNote that per psABI, the system vector calling convention requires three\nkinds of passing method: GPR pair, one GPR plus one stack slot, and two\nstack slots. This is not easily implemented. Since I don't see any\nnative vector calls, this is currently asserted out. For WASM-internal\ncalls, arguments are stored in available arg-passing FPRs (which are\naliases of the vector registers anyway) and spilled to stack when\nexhausted.\n\nLink:\n https://github.com/loongson/la-abi-specs/blob/44ef5f63e1755e1a165915ea3b2d98d35f68eed0/lapcs.adoc#passing-arguments\n (\"Procedure Call Standard for the LoongArch(tm) Architecture: Passing\n arguments\")\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329421\n", "files": ["js/src/irregexp/RegExpNativeMacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/simd/bug1946618.js", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Lowering-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Lowering-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp"], "git_node": "89b46a893253cb67de1e721eb0ccefc9d2a86860", "git_parents": ["715041e3663c9ff098396bc5a9567e7f3362c95f"], "node": "b1b934b4db4ac047adf9257d37bed90e6746d999", "parents": ["11af78c273e06654e63e14f18fc63fc4d2befa3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 9: Introduce vldi for loading common SIMD constants quickly. r=yury\n\nCross-domain (e.g. GPR to FPR) moves seems to be extremely slow and have\nterrible IPC. Fortunately, vldi can help materializing small, repetitive\nconstant patterns directly in the vector register.\n\nLink: https://areweloongyet.com/asmdb/vldiHelper (\"AreWeLoongYet? - VLDI\n Helper\")\nLink:\n https://github.com/loongson-community/areweloongyet/blob/49a0f6d22506c1fbebc97da24d4c34a9cc116ee5/src/components/AsmDB/vldi.ts\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329423\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64-inl.h"], "git_node": "a05ce9708faf1ab7783c39b82c450197c3c56bfb", "git_parents": ["89b46a893253cb67de1e721eb0ccefc9d2a86860"], "node": "3c951e6e80b0e2646fe7c8cb2624bf83f7062965", "parents": ["b1b934b4db4ac047adf9257d37bed90e6746d999"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 10: Implement LSX feature detection via HWCAP. r=yury\n\nLSX feature detection differs from the previous LAM_BH and LAMCAS ones,\nbecause it introduces extra architectural states that require explicit\nkernel support to preserve context. Thus, it's not sufficient to read\nthem via CPUCFG (which indicates hardware support only).\n\nA few codegen guards against Assembler::HasLSX() are also added, in\nsimilar fashion as x{86,64}'s Assembler::HasSSSE3() and others.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329422\n", "files": ["js/src/irregexp/RegExpNativeMacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Architecture-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Architecture-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "43e8a988df8665303c8214ffffaf9b1192e0df90", "git_parents": ["a05ce9708faf1ab7783c39b82c450197c3c56bfb"], "node": "b14772739f76924b10d7a70bade04fd2b9c0cbe8", "parents": ["3c951e6e80b0e2646fe7c8cb2624bf83f7062965"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075633 - [loong64] Part 11: Auto-enable SIMD by feature detection by default on Loong64. r=yury\n\nFinally, this completes the stack.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329424\n", "files": ["js/moz.configure"], "git_node": "21e5982bcd73ba691dc8f79cf3e0cf66dfdb6696", "git_parents": ["43e8a988df8665303c8214ffffaf9b1192e0df90"], "node": "a3a1c0922431ed6218d3d40aea2107ec93728b8b", "parents": ["b14772739f76924b10d7a70bade04fd2b9c0cbe8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Sudiaman \u003cjsudiaman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076296 - Add revamped sidebar switcher to the legacy bookmarks panel, and make it accessible from GenAI onboarding. r=sidebar-reviewers,places-reviewers,sclements,Mardak,mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329839\n", "files