3d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nte -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nth -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\ntl -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\ntr -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\ntrs -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nuk -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nur -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nuz -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nvi -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nwo -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nxh -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nzam -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nzh-CN -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\nzh-TW -\u003e 6d43d769fa8fcf7163bd2432553429ab45151799\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "226a68f10af545eb9f06eec03cbd3a2ac4faf6fe", "git_parents": ["c06dd2126a1347a3add1d4b9ea827a27a6f22e3e"], "node": "955b6b30f66c587e6f91aedf03ca858453e83702", "parents": ["99ebd8eb6539319d71f7359760486f180e263f49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076292 - Limit one SDR video overlay in Renderer::composite_simple() for Non-Intel GPU on Windows r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nSeveral GPUs consume a lot of GPU power during converting Video frame in DCSurfaceVideo::CallVideoProcessorBlt() on Windows. Then it seems better to permit only one video overlay for non-Intel GPUs. It is same to chromium.\n\nThe restriction does not apply to HDR video overlay, since WebRender does not support full HDR yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329870\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/init.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs"], "git_node": "d8c4b7593afaec127d150db5cfa70ead6c4d432f", "git_parents": ["226a68f10af545eb9f06eec03cbd3a2ac4faf6fe"], "node": "db9b7beea8df2558b9af773806e8284a59873bf0", "parents": ["955b6b30f66c587e6f91aedf03ca858453e83702"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Sapin \u003csimon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076755 - Upgrade Servo to rust-phf 0.14 and intermediate dependencies. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/460, but also implementing\n`AtomExt` for Gecko's `Atom` and `WeakAtom`. And the unit test is\nrestricted to Servo, since rust tests cannot link against Gecko symbols\nlike Gecko_Atomize, Gecko_AddRefAtom and Gecko_ReleaseAtom.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329986\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/bloom.rs", "servo/components/style/custom_properties.rs", "servo/components/style/dom_apis.rs", "servo/components/style/selector_map.rs"], "git_node": "9164248aff3897679d687022ef74e35e14c3f84a", "git_parents": ["d8c4b7593afaec127d150db5cfa70ead6c4d432f"], "node": "6785814237046498a44081b2489fdfa9f7f5efad", "parents": ["db9b7beea8df2558b9af773806e8284a59873bf0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Sapin \u003csimon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076755 - Enable `user-select` for Servo + `contain` value. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/462\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329987\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/specified/ui.rs"], "git_node": "606f2323de990adb2c51b37f1d802c41b9b5fb88", "git_parents": ["9164248aff3897679d687022ef74e35e14c3f84a"], "node": "2a94f447480ea0c76936ca4a8d6a0fc831001cad", "parents": ["6785814237046498a44081b2489fdfa9f7f5efad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "TIN TUN AUNG \u003c62133983+rayguo17@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076755 - Enable ::-moz-progress-bar pseudo-element for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/434\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329988\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs"], "git_node": "3504d2e0bd384ef7bc289874eb7ff2e95690378e", "git_parents": ["606f2323de990adb2c51b37f1d802c41b9b5fb88"], "node": "5bf39b2373a4163a35b7d5c84df1d2e00865670e", "parents": ["2a94f447480ea0c76936ca4a8d6a0fc831001cad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076755 - Fix compile problems for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nFixups so that the Servo flavor of Stylo still compiles after these changes:\n- https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/357\n- https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324114\n- https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325602\n- https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326808\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329989\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/helpers.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/random.rs"], "git_node": "189f0058aca3e5737a37e16d47340715b7a33ba7", "git_parents": ["3504d2e0bd384ef7bc289874eb7ff2e95690378e"], "node": "61502dc2ce310fe278be717c57ca7bdd8963d6ca", "parents": ["5bf39b2373a4163a35b7d5c84df1d2e00865670e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076541 - Centralize loadgroup flag inheritance checks. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nHave a single version of the flags we inherit from the loadgroup.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329635\n", "files": ["image/imgLoader.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsIRequest.idl", "netwerk/base/nsLoadGroup.cpp"], "git_node": "d3fe14f3f843caafa8f0c634d4af3e0c922ec0cc", "git_parents": ["189f0058aca3e5737a37e16d47340715b7a33ba7"], "node": "ba859f013b1e388286379dd22e8f112ef6227792", "parents": ["61502dc2ce310fe278be717c57ca7bdd8963d6ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075004 - Document how browser-newtab tests drive a content-process search bar. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329977\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/docs/testing.md"], "git_node": "4b88e421855d98eb227caa6ae1db80076a55c5d4", "git_parents": ["d3fe14f3f843caafa8f0c634d4af3e0c922ec0cc"], "node": "d771a41727e5a63476353e29b4c78a3225c71bfe", "parents": ["ba859f013b1e388286379dd22e8f112ef6227792"], "tags": []}, {"author": "pollymce \u003cpmceldowney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073095 - fix a few more top site tests to support running ui tests on nightly. r=sfamisa\n\n- SettingsAddonTests noCrashWithAddonInstalledTest(): this now just opens the first available top site tab, as this is not really the main point of the test. I've added a new method into HomeScreenRobot to support this.\n\n- HomeScreenTest: the bit where it is actually checking that default top sites are available uses the new method i added to say whether or not we expect them to be there (isDefaultPinnedShortcutsOnHomepage)\n\n- UnsubmittedCrashDialogTest: this was mocking the context but didn't actually use it, so i could just get rid of that part :tada:\n\n[try is running here](https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=98489)\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/372\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/HomeScreenTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SettingsAddonsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/UnsubmittedCrashDialogTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/robots/HomeScreenRobot.kt"], "git_node": "bcb6f6d7a2e8bf4adb37212a4f6eed329082608b", "git_parents": ["4b88e421855d98eb227caa6ae1db80076a55c5d4"], "node": "8416b77afecd92453829412467bd0323fe0988c7", "parents": ["d771a41727e5a63476353e29b4c78a3225c71bfe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Farre \u003csfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076142 - Remove now invalid WPT assertions from the history interface r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nThe language \"remove any tasks queued by the history traversal task source\" seems to have existed in the spec at one point; the same language was found in Gecko but is removed by 2067178.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329584\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/001.html"], "git_node": "cceef31541301b8d72bb9d151e7d03655f47f5ba", "git_parents": ["bcb6f6d7a2e8bf4adb37212a4f6eed329082608b"], "node": "7dcc849e8ffdcc6fd66dc4b3c135881d4c3b3b73", "parents": ["8416b77afecd92453829412467bd0323fe0988c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075751 - Describe the bundled npm code in the SBOM r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nwebpack folds React, Redux and Fluent into the newtab, aboutwelcome and\nasrouter bundles, so those packages had no component and no pkg:npm purl.\n\nsbom_npm.py reads the lockfiles listed in its SHIPPED_MANIFESTS allowlist\n(third_party/node, browser/components/aboutwelcome and\nbrowser/components/asrouter), in package-lock.json v2/v3 or pnpm-lock.yaml v9\nformat, and reports the runtime closure only: each package becomes a component\nwith a pkg:npm purl, the lockfile's SHA-512 and the license from the\nchecked-in package.json. Its bom-ref is npm:\u003cname\u003e@\u003cversion\u003e.\n\nVendored libraries that are also published on npm can declare it in moz.yaml\nwith `origin: npm-name`, which gives them a pkg:npm purl. Both are documented\nin the \"What Becomes a Component\" and identity sections of\npython/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329132\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/python.toml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_npm.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/template.yaml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/moz_yaml.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_npm.py", "third_party/js/PKI.js/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-commands/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-history/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-keymap/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-markdown/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-model/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-schema-basic/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-state/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-suggestions/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-transform/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-view/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "96c3f0bfff62fab56088953a2309714a360ce39e", "git_parents": ["cceef31541301b8d72bb9d151e7d03655f47f5ba"], "node": "bbd3bbcd7a06e532c3cb65b59d91cfb1b472c39b", "parents": ["7dcc849e8ffdcc6fd66dc4b3c135881d4c3b3b73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075752 - Write GeckoView's resolved Gradle runtime dependencies for the SBOM r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe AndroidX, Play services and other libraries Gradle fetches are packaged\ninto every application embedding GeckoView, and only Gradle knows which ones\nthe published variant resolves.\n\nThe writeRuntimeDependencies task, of the WriteRuntimeDependencies type the\nconventions plugin defines so that Fenix can register it too, runs during\n`mach android export` when MOZ_GENERATE_SBOM is set and writes the resolved\nruntime closure of the published variant to\ngradle/build/mobile/android/geckoview/sbom/runtime-dependencies.json in the\nobjdir: a JSON object with a `components` list of\n{group, name, version, files, dependencies}. Nothing reads it yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329425\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/build.gradle", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/WriteRuntimeDependencies.kt", "mobile/android/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "7030b027a05f15fae8d90c8a8952b1e15044314e", "git_parents": ["96c3f0bfff62fab56088953a2309714a360ce39e"], "node": "5a7754c1360b87474bd6c98d8c173d3601bdb467", "parents": ["bbd3bbcd7a06e532c3cb65b59d91cfb1b472c39b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075752 - Map GeckoView's Gradle runtime dependencies onto SBOM records r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nsbom_gradle.py reads the runtime-dependencies.json the writeRuntimeDependencies\ntask writes and turns each entry into a pkg:maven record with the artifact's\nSHA-256, the POM's licenses, following the parent chain where the POM declares\nnone, and the edges; its bom-ref is maven:\u003cgroup\u003e:\u003cname\u003e@\u003cversion\u003e. What it\ncannot read -- a missing POM or artifact, an artifact with a classifier only --\nis reported in a property rather than skipped. The SBOM does not use it yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329426\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/python.toml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_gradle.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_gradle.py"], "git_node": "133aa36960e8b3909feb0e9be157dc797dfefb4d", "git_parents": ["7030b027a05f15fae8d90c8a8952b1e15044314e"], "node": "e79da46666b7788c4489e90690f4b813284839d6", "parents": ["5a7754c1360b87474bd6c98d8c173d3601bdb467"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075752 - Describe GeckoView's Maven dependencies in the SBOM r=ahochheiden\n\nThe AndroidX, Play services and other libraries Gradle fetches are packaged\ninto every application embedding GeckoView, yet the Android SBOM described\nnone of them.\n\nOn an Android build, generate_sbom.py now adds the records sbom_gradle.py\nbuilds from the runtime-dependencies.json the Gradle export wrote earlier in\nthe same build, and sbom.json depends on that export. A missing or unreadable\nfile fails the build under --strict, since the document would otherwise\ndescribe less than the AAR brings in.\n\nThis is documented in the \"What Becomes a Component\" section of\npython/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329133\n", "files": ["mobile/android/mach_commands.py", "moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md"], "git_node": "680f1e3375f84315f6cc2460f338c60d8133c424", "git_parents": ["133aa36960e8b3909feb0e9be157dc797dfefb4d"], "node": "619fea439a5bf80462a232fcc4e1321d4bab892c", "parents": ["e79da46666b7788c4489e90690f4b813284839d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075752 - Publish an SBOM for the shipping Fenix builds r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nFenix is built by Gradle alone in the build-apk tasks, which never run the\nbuild that generates sbom.json, so nothing described what its APKs package.\n\nFenix registers the runtime closure task per variant, and `mach sbom\n--gradle-runtime-dependencies` turns that closure into a document of its own,\nin which GeckoView is one component that its own SBOM describes. The nightly,\nbeta and release APK builds publish it as public/build/sbom.json: the bundle\ntasks package the same variants, and the Firebase test builds ship nothing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329134\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/WriteRuntimeDependencies.kt", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/licensing_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_gradle.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_gradle.py", "taskcluster/android_taskgraph/transforms/build_android_app.py"], "git_node": "b77871b59d10fdf05ab4e27a245cca9d1d578a43", "git_parents": ["680f1e3375f84315f6cc2460f338c60d8133c424"], "node": "b09b870efb07bd600bb3f4b7a318635b7fa8dda2", "parents": ["619fea439a5bf80462a232fcc4e1321d4bab892c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075753 - Add a build tooling SBOM for what builds and tests the tree r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe product SBOM describes what ships, so the third-party code the tree only\nruns to build and test the product -- webpack, babel, the harnesses -- is left\nout on purpose, although it is as much a supply-chain input.\n\n`mach sbom --build-tooling` describes it in a document of its own, with the\nsame root and identifiers, the pre-build, build and post-build lifecycles in\nits metadata -- the harnesses run once the product is built -- every component\nscoped `excluded` and a serial number distinct from the product document's. It\nstarts with the npm packages of the lockfiles the product document already\nreads that are not in the runtime closure. The build does not generate it and\nautomation does not publish it yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329135\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/licensing_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_cyclonedx.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_npm.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_cyclonedx.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_npm.py"], "git_node": "c47106207ef83aa8f9b0e4a2a2af25e5fc5691f3", "git_parents": ["b77871b59d10fdf05ab4e27a245cca9d1d578a43"], "node": "5fca6f21a922b7cd24d158a77544c94ea00fc7d9", "parents": ["b09b870efb07bd600bb3f4b7a318635b7fa8dda2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075753 - Describe the vendored Python packages in the build tooling SBOM r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe 96 packages under third_party/python are what mach, the build system and\nthe test harnesses run on. None ships in the product, so they go to the build\ntooling document rather than the product one.\n\nsbom_python.py reads third_party/python/uv.lock for the versions, the pkg:pypi\npurls, the edges and the SHA-256 of the archive `mach vendor python` unpacked,\nwhich is the pure wheel where one exists and the sdist otherwise. The licenses\ncome from the vendored copy's metadata. A package that declares none, or whose\nmetadata cannot be read, says so in a property.\n\nThe packages `mach vendor python` leaves alone and uv.lock does not name --\ndlmanager, filelock, gyp and vsdownload -- are described from their moz.yaml or\ntheir own metadata, and vsdownload's moz.yaml no longer puts it in the product\ndocument.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329136\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/python.toml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_python.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_python.py"], "git_node": "2b629a98a78c7f0cb1ed1dedd22ea95dd7c3f419", "git_parents": ["c47106207ef83aa8f9b0e4a2a2af25e5fc5691f3"], "node": "fd877a45645e5f87ad6335e6b785bbbff5a5d354", "parents": ["5fca6f21a922b7cd24d158a77544c94ea00fc7d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075753 - Move the test and tooling crates to the build tooling SBOM r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe product SBOM listed as shipped every crate the workspace reaches other\nthan as a dev dependency, which includes what only its test servers, test\nmodules and code generators build: hyper, tokio and warp for the http3server\nand geckodriver, and the test-only crates such as mockall.\n\nThe walk now starts from the shipped roots, with the members that only build\nor test the product listed in TOOLING_MEMBERS. The 56 crates reached only as\ndev or tooling dependencies go to the build tooling document instead. Without\ncargo metadata, in an unconfigured tree, nothing can be told apart, so every\ncrate stays in the product document.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329137\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_python.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_cyclonedx.py"], "git_node": "ddb78bff114b80d65e69c7e212423728f447bca7", "git_parents": ["2b629a98a78c7f0cb1ed1dedd22ea95dd7c3f419"], "node": "fc9a075dde34d3470f2842f9867349d37947440d", "parents": ["fd877a45645e5f87ad6335e6b785bbbff5a5d354"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075753 - Publish the build tooling SBOM from the shippable builds r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\n`mach sbom --build-tooling` was only run by hand. The builds that set\nMOZ_GENERATE_SBOM now also generate `sbom-build-tooling.json` next to\n`sbom.json`, and upload it as `public/build/sbom-build-tooling.json`.\n\nThe build generates it strictly: without `cargo metadata`, the test and tooling\ncrates cannot be told apart from the shipped ones and would silently be left\nout, so the build fails instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329403\n", "files": ["moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_cargo.py", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/upload-files.mk"], "git_node": "a33cfe12092c2d7aa94faf88e8d91f7983cc3af7", "git_parents": ["ddb78bff114b80d65e69c7e212423728f447bca7"], "node": "ba436bb26ad1e5cfdb10dd0104e49b70cd5725d7", "parents": ["fc9a075dde34d3470f2842f9867349d37947440d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2076142 - Remove now invalid WPT assertions from the history interface r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\" for causing wpt failures @the-history-interface/001.html.\n\nThis reverts commit cceef31541301b8d72bb9d151e7d03655f47f5ba.\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/001.html"], "git_node": "69ed3c2b570e7bf4127bee040b71bc30c502361f", "git_parents": ["a33cfe12092c2d7aa94faf88e8d91f7983cc3af7"], "node": "59f10c8026ee0176e1bb597cb6694a1e09bddece", "parents": ["ba436bb26ad1e5cfdb10dd0104e49b70cd5725d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2075753, Bug 2075752, Bug 2075751 - Publish the build tooling SBOM from the shippable builds r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\" for causing doc generate failures.\n\nThis reverts commit a33cfe12092c2d7aa94faf88e8d91f7983cc3af7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075753 - Move the test and tooling crates to the build tooling SBOM r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\"\n\nThis reverts commit ddb78bff114b80d65e69c7e212423728f447bca7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075753 - Describe the vendored Python packages in the build tooling SBOM r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2b629a98a78c7f0cb1ed1dedd22ea95dd7c3f419.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075753 - Add a build tooling SBOM for what builds and tests the tree r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\"\n\nThis reverts commit c47106207ef83aa8f9b0e4a2a2af25e5fc5691f3.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075752 - Publish an SBOM for the shipping Fenix builds r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\"\n\nThis reverts commit b77871b59d10fdf05ab4e27a245cca9d1d578a43.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075752 - Describe GeckoView's Maven dependencies in the SBOM r=ahochheiden\"\n\nThis reverts commit 680f1e3375f84315f6cc2460f338c60d8133c424.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075752 - Map GeckoView's Gradle runtime dependencies onto SBOM records r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\"\n\nThis reverts commit 133aa36960e8b3909feb0e9be157dc797dfefb4d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075752 - Write GeckoView's resolved Gradle runtime dependencies for the SBOM r=mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7030b027a05f15fae8d90c8a8952b1e15044314e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2075751 - Describe the bundled npm code in the SBOM r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\"\n\nThis reverts commit 96c3f0bfff62fab56088953a2309714a360ce39e.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/geckoview/build.gradle", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/WriteRuntimeDependencies.kt", "mobile/android/mach_commands.py", "moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/licensing_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/python.toml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_generate_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_cyclonedx.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_gradle.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_npm.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_python.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/licensing.md", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/docs/template.yaml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/moz_yaml.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_cyclonedx.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_gradle.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_npm.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_python.py", "taskcluster/android_taskgraph/transforms/build_android_app.py", "third_party/js/PKI.js/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-commands/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-history/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-keymap/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-markdown/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-model/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-schema-basic/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-state/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-suggestions/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-transform/moz.yaml", "third_party/js/prosemirror/prosemirror-view/moz.yaml", "toolkit/mozapps/installer/upload-files.mk"], "git_node": "edfbec372f785cfcb15f21d3d26f72669fcff709", "git_parents": ["69ed3c2b570e7bf4127bee040b71bc30c502361f"], "node": "6d2bdc1d49e05d9d7cb1a2a79debcb67a70267af", "parents": ["59f10c8026ee0176e1bb597cb6694a1e09bddece"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077049 - Document address bar utility modules that content-process code can import. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330099\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarContentUtils.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/utilities.md"], "git_node": "23cbe95b74f2ed84b66abec38f4b3c29944aba2c", "git_parents": ["edfbec372f785cfcb15f21d3d26f72669fcff709"], "node": "56fce97d14bb7bbe603014987fb8755ff0faff55", "parents": ["6d2bdc1d49e05d9d7cb1a2a79debcb67a70267af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077049 - Make UrlbarContentUtils a class so its docs can be generated from the source. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330105\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarContentUtils.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarEventBufferer.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/utilities.md"], "git_node": "e0d594731803f84789bd4687d0a4554a5975ac7f", "git_parents": ["23cbe95b74f2ed84b66abec38f4b3c29944aba2c"], "node": "3e9700f2e6f1fa4159cd7d58974699bcdacd065b", "parents": ["56fce97d14bb7bbe603014987fb8755ff0faff55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076678 - Fix Reopen Closed Tab after deleting a saved tab group. r=sfoster,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329903\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_tab_groups_undo.js"], "git_node": "3bf620cb3e8f51b2b10c70c31b3ff8b6b016b5ac", "git_parents": ["e0d594731803f84789bd4687d0a4554a5975ac7f"], "node": "4747779096081b7851fe0bf4774c6c3b2f3082c4", "parents": ["3e9700f2e6f1fa4159cd7d58974699bcdacd065b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "delan azabani \u003cdazabani@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070868 - Invalidate `\u003cinput\u003e.labels` when `\u003clabel for\u003e` changes. r=edgar\n\n`\u003cinput\u003e` and other elements with `.labels` use LabelsNodeList to dynamically\nreflect the `\u003clabel\u003e` elements that reference it. while LabelsNodeList detects\nsome changes, like changes to ancestry (for implicit label association) and\nchanges to `\u003cinput type\u003e` (for `\u003cinput type=hidden\u003e`), it does not yet detect\nchanges to `\u003clabel for\u003e`.\n\nthis patch adds a call to SetDirty() in LabelsNodeList when AttributeChanged()\nis called for any `\u003clabel for\u003e` in the subtrees under observation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324913\n", "files": ["dom/base/ContentList.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-label-element/labels-live-attribute-changes.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/shadow-dom/reference-target/tentative/dom-mutation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/shadow-dom/reference-target/tentative/dom-mutation.html"], "git_node": "2c786e89d088799c8974131a42f685b714da572a", "git_parents": ["3bf620cb3e8f51b2b10c70c31b3ff8b6b016b5ac"], "node": "1ae823106424e9cb1fd5978f99d4ea35f53d19ba", "parents": ["4747779096081b7851fe0bf4774c6c3b2f3082c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mathew Hodson \u003cmathew.hodson@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068828 - Convert SessionWriterInternal to a JS class r=jswinarton\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323150\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionWriter.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "1756a6ab15916c9f17ab5c59fd35c9ee925bc644", "git_parents": ["2c786e89d088799c8974131a42f685b714da572a"], "node": "e1319e49fc0fb7121685121edbe3ea82151ff9f5", "parents": ["1ae823106424e9cb1fd5978f99d4ea35f53d19ba"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790870507, "git_changesets": ["2787d68374d61010e913997d5488d3b64ae0b568", "6514031a0addf855b7ebda215d0500b15aeec8d4", "69a26ae93fb6d73c4d17047835dd0840acd6f2ac", "7cb2283c65608936743bac3e0d0f063877421bba", "cffc0859a898d84ed1ff8bfbe94d8f7848c6fd45", "d105184fe0e7a7d8f8b743275d96633bd5b66f65", "c06dd2126a1347a3add1d4b9ea827a27a6f22e3e", "226a68f10af545eb9f06eec03cbd3a2ac4faf6fe", "d8c4b7593afaec127d150db5cfa70ead6c4d432f", "9164248aff3897679d687022ef74e35e14c3f84a", "606f2323de990adb2c51b37f1d802c41b9b5fb88", "3504d2e0bd384ef7bc289874eb7ff2e95690378e", "189f0058aca3e5737a37e16d47340715b7a33ba7", "d3fe14f3f843caafa8f0c634d4af3e0c922ec0cc", "4b88e421855d98eb227caa6ae1db80076a55c5d4", "bcb6f6d7a2e8bf4adb37212a4f6eed329082608b", "cceef31541301b8d72bb9d151e7d03655f47f5ba", "96c3f0bfff62fab56088953a2309714a360ce39e", "7030b027a05f15fae8d90c8a8952b1e15044314e", "133aa36960e8b3909feb0e9be157dc797dfefb4d", "680f1e3375f84315f6cc2460f338c60d8133c424", "b77871b59d10fdf05ab4e27a245cca9d1d578a43", "c47106207ef83aa8f9b0e4a2a2af25e5fc5691f3", "2b629a98a78c7f0cb1ed1dedd22ea95dd7c3f419", "ddb78bff114b80d65e69c7e212423728f447bca7", "a33cfe12092c2d7aa94faf88e8d91f7983cc3af7", "69ed3c2b570e7bf4127bee040b71bc30c502361f", "edfbec372f785cfcb15f21d3d26f72669fcff709", "23cbe95b74f2ed84b66abec38f4b3c29944aba2c", "e0d594731803f84789bd4687d0a4554a5975ac7f", "3bf620cb3e8f51b2b10c70c31b3ff8b6b016b5ac", "2c786e89d088799c8974131a42f685b714da572a", "1756a6ab15916c9f17ab5c59fd35c9ee925bc644"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45462": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings mobile-merino-manifest ct-logs - r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329799\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-manifest/src/main/assets/manifest/manifest.json", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-config-icons.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-config-overrides-v2.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-config-v2.json"], "git_node": "ce9c5cc2745e38393019103e5c86fea87ce5c1d2", "git_parents": ["1756a6ab15916c9f17ab5c59fd35c9ee925bc644"], "node": "a4924989ed01afea798e1ae57148cb452e167995", "parents": ["e1319e49fc0fb7121685121edbe3ea82151ff9f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077030 - Reset zoom level across crashtests. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nIn RecordResult, the TYPE_LOAD (crashtest), TYPE_SCRIPT and TYPE_PRINT\nbranches call FinishTestItem() and return before ResetRenderingState().\n\nThis is the root cause of the backout in bug 2075197, where some test\nfailed if only a couple manifests ran but not otherwise, since it causes\ngfx/tests/crashtests/{1771556,1771561}.html, which set reftest-zoom=\"3\"\nto run earlier than the problematic case.\n\nPretty sure this is correct but a try to make sure that this doesn't\ncause more / less asserts is in progress.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330094\n", "files": ["layout/tools/reftest/reftest.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "541495e265ec04c44518e9beee1ff8a9a15d8d3d", "git_parents": ["ce9c5cc2745e38393019103e5c86fea87ce5c1d2"], "node": "23ebf506367620bd6a97ac83c1b463335a791c6e", "parents": ["a4924989ed01afea798e1ae57148cb452e167995"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1960845 - Parse \u003cnoscript\u003e with scripting disabled in Document.parseHTML() and parseHTMLUnsafe() r=tschuster\n\nparseHTML & parseHTMLUnsafe using a document with no browsing context, so\nscripting is disabled and the parser's scripting mode is Disabled, meaning\n`\u003cnoscript\u003e` content is parsed as markup. `parseHTML()` parsed it as raw text,\nand `parseHTMLUnsafe()` do so only when given a sanitizer, so\n`parseHTMLUnsafe(html, {})` and `parseHTMLUnsafe(html)` built different trees.\n\nThis change ensures both of these entry points always pass `false` to\n`aScriptingEnabledForNoscriptParsing` so that they're consistent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328191\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/parsehtml-noscript.html"], "git_node": "00f863ad7091c618c50ac42b11a7ccbf60354ff7", "git_parents": ["541495e265ec04c44518e9beee1ff8a9a15d8d3d"], "node": "9d0a9dd98ecb2e128ddb4f7c1e8d2ce395c3e9e8", "parents": ["23ebf506367620bd6a97ac83c1b463335a791c6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076944 - Update harfbuzz to 14.5.1 r=jfkthame\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330073\n", "files": ["gfx/harfbuzz/NEWS", "gfx/harfbuzz/moz.yaml", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/OT/Var/VARC/VARC.cc", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/gen-tag-table.py", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/graph/graph.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-font.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ft.cc", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-gpu-paint.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-limits.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-cmap-table.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-layout-common.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-tag-table.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-version.h", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-wasm-shape.cc"], "git_node": "4a61df7976f3b02b66cf487816538a80e8b2a28a", "git_parents": ["00f863ad7091c618c50ac42b11a7ccbf60354ff7"], "node": "c8ba5ae54e83097682dc4d8ef8cb66df16eb855f", "parents": ["9d0a9dd98ecb2e128ddb4f7c1e8d2ce395c3e9e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076648 - Clear previously-focused content after blurring due to caret move. r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329959\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsFocusManager.cpp", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/focus/focus-navigation-starting-point-caret-browsing.html"], "git_node": "471985ecd522622a9d01eef561c2097f3d8108ce", "git_parents": ["4a61df7976f3b02b66cf487816538a80e8b2a28a"], "node": "2dbb0451919aded9509b19d2b7ccfec0835ca2fb", "parents": ["c8ba5ae54e83097682dc4d8ef8cb66df16eb855f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075998 - Root QueueWithSizes when dequeued r=saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330015\n", "files": ["dom/streams/QueueWithSizes.h"], "git_node": "281b985a90968e0e309a383163ccb12f61a6033f", "git_parents": ["471985ecd522622a9d01eef561c2097f3d8108ce"], "node": "22c562465890d203b0132c3956c73612948ac890", "parents": ["2dbb0451919aded9509b19d2b7ccfec0835ca2fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075954 - Part 1: Add LoongArch L{,A}SX feature detection to mozglue. r=glandium\n\nThese features need kernel support to save and restore contexts. So we\nmust use HWCAP to detect them. See also Bug 2075633.\n\nLink: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329422 (\"Implement LSX\n feature detection via HWCAP\")\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329488\n", "files": ["mozglue/misc/LSX.cpp", "mozglue/misc/LSX.h", "mozglue/misc/moz.build"], "git_node": "e170de1998a2912181fec2cc994623b11ba90918", "git_parents": ["281b985a90968e0e309a383163ccb12f61a6033f"], "node": "bf2dcacb0caad7d5a4895bbdd2a963974b0113ea", "parents": ["22c562465890d203b0132c3956c73612948ac890"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075954 - Part 2: Implement LSX version for string functions in mozglue SIMD.cpp. r=glandium\n\nThe organization of functions are learned from the NEON implementation,\nand the implementation is learned from the SSE implementation. Thanks to\nthe \"Unofficial LoongArch Intrinsics Guide\" by Jiajie Chen, there are\nsome established mappings at hand.\n\nLink:\n https://jia.je/unofficial-loongarch-intrinsics-guide/migrating_sse/\n (\"Migrating from SSE to LSX\")\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329489\n", "files": ["mozglue/misc/SIMD.cpp", "mozglue/misc/SIMD.h", "mozglue/misc/SIMD_lsx.cpp", "mozglue/misc/moz.build"], "git_node": "6d95c518a75c8eebc4221da327f736d10a66f2c5", "git_parents": ["e170de1998a2912181fec2cc994623b11ba90918"], "node": "59364d63dad8e8d985d8502e3fea7fd457610225", "parents": ["bf2dcacb0caad7d5a4895bbdd2a963974b0113ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kui-Feng Lee \u003cthinker.li@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1759952 - [GTK] Run a native menu item's command before popuphiding r=stransky,gtk-reviewers,emilio\n\nGTK unmaps a menu before it activates the chosen item, so\nNativeMenuGtk::OnUnmap() fired popuphiding and popuphidden before the item's\ncommand ran. The hiding handlers tear down what the command needs: the\ncontent area context menu sets gContextMenu to null (Copy Link, Save Page As\nthrow), the tab context menu clears contextTab, and in a text field the\nremoved spell check items rebuild the menu model, dropping the action of the\nitem being activated (Copy and Paste do nothing).\n\nFire the events from a runnable instead, so the command runs first, as it\ndoes for XUL menus. Close() fires them right away, since a close requested by\ncode activates no item and the popup manager may show a new menu for the same\nelement right after it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329276\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/NativeMenuGtk.cpp", "widget/gtk/NativeMenuGtk.h"], "git_node": "635794860d63b0e58869478052e28ca705bea795", "git_parents": ["6d95c518a75c8eebc4221da327f736d10a66f2c5"], "node": "12b75ec0bc83f81f278112fb028fdfb90182b6ce", "parents": ["59364d63dad8e8d985d8502e3fea7fd457610225"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074257 - Stocks widget: rename the user-facing name to Finance. r=fluent-reviewers,Dre,flod\n\nThe widget's user-facing name has become \"Finance\", as the product review ahead\nof the v1 experiment asked. The four messages that carried the old name have all\nbeen given new ids, since the values changed and the old translations must not\ncarry over. The widget's internal name remains \"stocks\".\n\nThe context menu button's tooltip and accessible name have been normalised to\n\"Finance options\" at the same time. Every other widget already used the shorter\nform, without the word \"widget\".\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330040\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/ContentSection/ContentSection.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/Stocks.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/_Stocks.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Nova/CustomizeMenu/WidgetsManagementPanel/WidgetsManagementPanel.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/AboutPreferences.test.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "228840f836cf1a4b01af9f38f8f86da803c0691b", "git_parents": ["635794860d63b0e58869478052e28ca705bea795"], "node": "f4a3563e5e6aa61a499372353adbf39a22a8baa6", "parents": ["12b75ec0bc83f81f278112fb028fdfb90182b6ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@ritter.vg\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1700396: Bump updatebot for day frequency r=nkulatova\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330143\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/updatebot/updatebot-version.sh"], "git_node": "e74efacf35a6a95d31855066b0c2b273d98b1b99", "git_parents": ["228840f836cf1a4b01af9f38f8f86da803c0691b"], "node": "f931924616d80bb5919176e217dbbc10a5054c0c", "parents": ["f4a3563e5e6aa61a499372353adbf39a22a8baa6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anna Weine \u003canna.weine@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076832 - Allow day-based frequencies in moz.yaml updatebot tasks r=tjr\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330000\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_manifest.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/moz_yaml.py"], "git_node": "ef73b2bc1045ffedcebdb78ce14f10d6b94bc5e2", "git_parents": ["e74efacf35a6a95d31855066b0c2b273d98b1b99"], "node": "a77148e720aa2db089198ec72f9d0df38d6e60b5", "parents": ["f931924616d80bb5919176e217dbbc10a5054c0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076590 - Update NSS to 824793aca473a0bb4a9dc3d4a88a6d0f2786bd7b UPGRADE_NSS_RELEASE r=ai4dev-reviewers,padenot,nkulatova\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329842\n", "files": ["security/nss/CLAUDE.md", "security/nss/automation/abi-check/expected-report-libnss3.so.txt", "security/nss/automation/abi-check/expected-report-libnssutil3.so.txt", "security/nss/automation/abi-check/expected-report-libsmime3.so.txt", "security/nss/automation/abi-check/expected-report-libssl3.so.txt", "security/nss/automation/abi-check/previous-nss-release", "security/nss/cmd/certutil/certutil.c", "security/nss/cmd/certutil/keystuff.c", "security/nss/cmd/httpserv/httpserv.c", "security/nss/cmd/lib/secutil.c", "security/nss/cmd/p7content/p7content.c", "security/nss/cmd/pk11importtest/pk11importtest.c", "security/nss/cmd/shlibsign/shlibsign.c", "security/nss/cpputil/nss_scoped_ptrs.h", "security/nss/gtests/certdb_gtest/cert_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/der_gtest/secasn1decode_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_eddsa_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_eddsa_vectors.h", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_module_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_rsapkcs1_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_signature_test.cc", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_signature_test.h", "security/nss/gtests/pkcs11testmodule/pkcs11testmodule.cpp", "security/nss/gtests/smime_gtest/smime_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/softoken_gtest/softoken_gtest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/softoken_static_gtest/softoken_static_gtest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/softoken_static_gtest/softoken_static_gtest.gyp", "security/nss/lib/certdb/alg1485.c", "security/nss/lib/certdb/cert.h", "security/nss/lib/certdb/certdb.c", "security/nss/lib/certdb/certv3.c", "security/nss/lib/certdb/genname.c", "security/nss/lib/certdb/genname.h", "security/nss/lib/certdb/polcyxtn.c", "security/nss/lib/certdb/stanpcertdb.c", "security/nss/lib/certdb/xconst.c", "security/nss/lib/certdb/xconst.h", "security/nss/lib/certhigh/certhigh.c", "security/nss/lib/certhigh/certvfy.c", "security/nss/lib/certhigh/crlv2.c", "security/nss/lib/cryptohi/seckey.c", "security/nss/lib/cryptohi/secsign.c", "security/nss/lib/cryptohi/secvfy.c", "security/nss/lib/libpkix/pkix_pl_nss/pki/pkix_pl_nameconstraints.c", "security/nss/lib/nss/nss.def", "security/nss/lib/nss/nss.h", "security/nss/lib/pk11wrap/pk11akey.c", "security/nss/lib/pk11wrap/pk11auth.c", "security/nss/lib/pk11wrap/pk11cxt.c", "security/nss/lib/pk11wrap/pk11mech.c", "security/nss/lib/pk11wrap/pk11obj.c", "security/nss/lib/pk11wrap/pk11pk12.c", "security/nss/lib/pk11wrap/pk11priv.h", "security/nss/lib/pk11wrap/pk11slot.c", "security/nss/lib/pk11wrap/secmodti.h", "security/nss/lib/pki/certificate.c", "security/nss/lib/pki/pki.h", "security/nss/lib/pki/pki3hack.c", "security/nss/lib/pki/trustdomain.c", "security/nss/lib/smime/cmsdigest.c", "security/nss/lib/softoken/lowkey.c", "security/nss/lib/softoken/lowkeyti.h", "security/nss/lib/softoken/pkcs11.c", "security/nss/lib/softoken/pkcs11c.c", "security/nss/lib/softoken/pkcs11u.c", "security/nss/lib/softoken/sftkpwd.c", "security/nss/lib/softoken/softkver.h", "security/nss/lib/util/derdec.c", "security/nss/lib/util/nssutil.h", "security/nss/lib/util/secasn1d.c", "security/nss/lib/util/secoid.c", "security/nss/lib/util/secoidt.h", "security/nss/mach", "security/nss/moz.yaml", "security/nss/nss.gyp", "security/nss/nss/automation/abi-check/new-report-libssl3.so.txt", "security/nss/tests/cert/cert.sh", "security/nss/tests/common/tsan_suppressions.txt", "security/nss/tests/fips/fips.sh", "security/nss/tests/gtests/gtests.sh", "security/nss/tests/tools/openssl-ed25519.p12", "security/nss/tests/tools/tools.sh"], "git_node": "b6e86598fad7eb55b581149308886c927aa1269d", "git_parents": ["ef73b2bc1045ffedcebdb78ce14f10d6b94bc5e2"], "node": "ab4944e8df710aa35327d67d52abb4e26ded2814", "parents": ["a77148e720aa2db089198ec72f9d0df38d6e60b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anna Weine \u003canna.weine@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076590 - Export SEC_ASN1DecodeInteger_Util from nss3 for the softoken build r=crypto-reviewers,jschanck\n\nThe NSS upgrade commit 0f05975dac0cd8b66b590eef4b6ac05180243cb7 (the sole commit in the push) broke the build-win64/debug task.\n\nRoot cause: the commit added a call to SEC_ASN1DecodeInteger() in sftk_unwrapPrivateKey (security/nss/lib/softoken/pkcs11c.c). Because softoken includes utilrename.h, this resolves to the symbol SEC_ASN1DecodeInteger_Util. In the Firefox folded-libs build, softokn3.dll links against security/nss3.lib whose exports are driven by the Firefox-maintained list security/nss.symbols. That list exported SEC_ASN1DecodeInteger and neighbours such as SEC_ASN1DecodeItem_Util/SEC_ASN1Decode_Util, but not SEC_ASN1DecodeInteger_Util, so the reference was left unresolved:\n\n  lld-link: error: undefined symbol: SEC_ASN1DecodeInteger_Util\n    \u003e\u003e\u003e referenced by security/nss/lib/softoken/pkcs11c.c:7492 (sftk_unwrapPrivateKey)\n\nFix: add SEC_ASN1DecodeInteger_Util to security/nss.symbols in alphabetical order, between SEC_ASN1DecodeInteger and SEC_ASN1DecodeItem.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330128\n", "files": ["security/nss.symbols"], "git_node": "9b10dc6ce678bb5155e2f21994d27562f5ee0818", "git_parents": ["b6e86598fad7eb55b581149308886c927aa1269d"], "node": "40ef2b20123a8ddedb2f05fe9fe0bee993c7c1d0", "parents": ["ab4944e8df710aa35327d67d52abb4e26ded2814"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1042341 - Record a startup_session_decision event metric. r=sessionstore-reviewers,sclements\n\n- New startup_session_decision event metric captures the restore decision at startup\n- Bug 2076441 noted and left as a todo to fix the `iniState.savedGroups` check\n- New test to verify we end up with the correct telemetry for each condition\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329753\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/manifest.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/test_session_decision.py", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.glean.d.ts"], "git_node": "0b32deef55891fd8ef5a4d3d8f1c481b383f4d87", "git_parents": ["9b10dc6ce678bb5155e2f21994d27562f5ee0818"], "node": "3bf31fb129ef6e02d2e958027f9ffc580465a592", "parents": ["40ef2b20123a8ddedb2f05fe9fe0bee993c7c1d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Moss \u003cjmoss@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075792 - Preserve coverage environment in crash reporter subprocess. r=gsvelto,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329762\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/test/unit/test_crashreporter_omnijar_loading.js"], "git_node": "46e483a3e541740e033dbea6659e2d66b980646d", "git_parents": ["0b32deef55891fd8ef5a4d3d8f1c481b383f4d87"], "node": "641d88bea29c70b6b684855352d92f02eca24c26", "parents": ["3bf31fb129ef6e02d2e958027f9ffc580465a592"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Graham \u003cjames@hoppipolla.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071055 [wpt PR 62594] - Fixes required to make Firefox Android runs work again., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon't run the userspace oom killer for firefox_android\n\nIn this case all the memory is likely to be in the emulator; we can't\njust kill the browser from the host using this approach. So instead\njust log memory usage and depend on the kernel OOM killer if we really\nget into a low memory situation.\n\n--\nShut down processes cleanly when running via run-tc\n\nThis allows them to clean up and makes it much easier to reuse the docker\ncontainer afterwards.\n\n--\nDon't try t raise the return value of pthread_kill\n\nThis doesn't actually return an exception, so there's nothing to raise\n\n--\nAdd retry for download_and_extract\n\n--\nLog a warning, but don't raise when cleaning up firefox_android\n\nIf cleanup fails we should try to continue and see if we can cleanly restart\nthe browser rather than assuming that we're now in a broken state.\n\n--\nDowngrade to emulator version 36.3.10\n\nThis appears to be the last version that supports the host GPU mode that\nwe're using. Without this we see crashes in some graphics tests when\nrunning firefox_android which take down the entire emulator\n\n--\nSplit test262 into 16 chunks on android\n\n--\nAdd logging of test group selection\n\n--\nEnable debug level logging\n\n--\nAllow downloads to retry for HTTPError as well as socket errors\n\n--\nSplit tests into groups of depth 3 in CI\n\n--\nPass logger explicitly in more of testloader\n\n--\nUnzip using helper rather than unzip tool\n\n--\nMake get_download_to_descriptior use requests\n\n--\nAdd types to more wpt.utils functions\n\n--\nMove http helpers to their own module\n\nThis can depend on requests\n\n--\nRun tc-run in a virtualenv\n\nThis is needed so that it can install dependencies.\n\n--\nHandle urllib3 exceptions during download\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 30ad79c882f5f59432d2431544ca8c369a25fd96, 474f0cb60137e8e16811a756ff3612326d8332b4, 12f9719b14edd3a3350262f0b8d7f33368388f44, 1c145d2323c7f5baf926221a138e8cad8989e637, 874d639ae13d2d85561574ca20d79eaf93b6d4da, 621bc0a0b751d7c5ac5824212bc41724b0d78d53, d6d6440feea6c25b3085f44c960d4de37a8a2e15, ccfc26e4c0cb8946f4f1f1d8eeee88f837e10427, d93951ac4a77064debb9a9d893dc3c6b807e1996, 32986223c0176cbc963345e0e4dad950b260a351, 9028d436a38f747afb6729cd3f6a3502b0e71148, cc415400808e95bc2496decc371543782d68625f, f33fba71144b2d6e41b6d07e205a212e64c45152, 3ac7fd7b23c259eed33853d886ac3a60f2652160, 1f1f3ba29ded3f0005e5ccf94fc695db6b9bfbf9, f9403ee73be8739384e05fdbde42a99fdf81260a, 8d4aab9f9f1833b136ce326b8e833f797c4b8b16, 733e005cad890bc96221a054c6d2229cf0aa0053\nwpt-pr: 62594\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/ci_resources_unittest.sh", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/ci_tools_integration_test.sh", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/ci_tools_unittest.sh", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/commands.json", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/run_tc.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/taskcluster-run.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/tasks/test.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/tests/test_valid.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/android.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/browser.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/httputils.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/utils.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/browsers/firefox_android.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/environment.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/metadata.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/testloader.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/tests/conftest.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/tests/test_testloader.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/tests/test_update.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/tests/test_wptrunner.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/tests/test_wpttest.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/update/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/wptlogging.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/wptrunner.py"], "git_node": "5c474c28403c33e8bbd10b6a0917521d3ee3a041", "git_parents": ["46e483a3e541740e033dbea6659e2d66b980646d"], "node": "9ccad02f7b24de0d3cac86c9042c4c8a21d96b22", "parents": ["641d88bea29c70b6b684855352d92f02eca24c26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Rego Casasnovas \u003crego@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073354 [wpt PR 62768] - aamtests: Add test to check events when `disabled` attribute changes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\naamtests: Add test to check events when `disabled` attribute changes\n\nThis passes in Chromium but fails in Firefox\nbecause it doesn't fire `SENSITIVE` event as expected.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ab4b0e8cd04dd07bf6864a34fbf6418046e815cc\nwpt-pr: 62768\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html-aam/aamtests/conftest.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/html-aam/aamtests/event/disabled.py"], "git_node": "322968e479e5bab81eed9e906b8596b68a1d69e7", "git_parents": ["5c474c28403c33e8bbd10b6a0917521d3ee3a041"], "node": "58243eabe048041518b5fa2efd55a3256d3b8491", "parents": ["9ccad02f7b24de0d3cac86c9042c4c8a21d96b22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073354 [wpt PR 62768] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62768\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html-aam/aamtests/event/disabled.py.ini"], "git_node": "5eeab21d43fe797f050e2f884a6a77f7184d4c65", "git_parents": ["322968e479e5bab81eed9e906b8596b68a1d69e7"], "node": "37834a1e18a18cd00c52ee207070462fcdb5198b", "parents": ["58243eabe048041518b5fa2efd55a3256d3b8491"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seonggon Cho \u003cjmsmg1@me.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074911 [wpt PR 62900] - [payments] Fix the WPT for multiple payment-method-manifest Link headers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[payments] Fix the WPT for multiple payment-method-manifest Link headers\n\nThe \"Multiple rel=payment-method-manifest link headers cause fetch to\nabort\" subtest of link-header-selection.https.window.js expected the\nuser agent to abort when a payment method identifier response carries\nmore than one payment-method-manifest link. The spec does not say\nthat: the fetch algorithm walks the Link headers and uses the first\none whose rel is payment-method-manifest\n(https://w3c.github.io/payment-method-manifest/#fetch-pmm), which is\nwhat Chromium already does.\n\nRewrite the subtest to check that the first manifest link is the one\nthat gets fetched, and drop the Chromium baseline that recorded the\nold subtest as a known failure.\n\nR=smcgruer@chromium.org\n\nBug: 545843242\nChange-Id: Ib8df47892752d3dc3551cf96c1052f47a49259a7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8449730\nReviewed-by: Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Jayden Nikifork \u003cnikifork@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703401}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d78575918e30a10b5a81f03931d5bf2d9afb2268\nwpt-pr: 62900\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/link-header-selection.https.window.js"], "git_node": "6533429e55d354605d6daa4a04d7acab09e8c8ed", "git_parents": ["5eeab21d43fe797f050e2f884a6a77f7184d4c65"], "node": "65bde48849c1a974f3ff5afd794d22ece0790362", "parents": ["37834a1e18a18cd00c52ee207070462fcdb5198b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074911 [wpt PR 62900] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62900\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/link-header-selection.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "1beb3ab4b13d36642b695708049186158ebb876e", "git_parents": ["6533429e55d354605d6daa4a04d7acab09e8c8ed"], "node": "049369f59fc721407f9d492de73846c943123488", "parents": ["65bde48849c1a974f3ff5afd794d22ece0790362"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Amos Lim \u003ceui-sang.lim@samsung.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074949 [wpt PR 62899] - [webauthn] Ignore duplicate credential hints, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[webauthn] Ignore duplicate credential hints\n\nThe WebAuthn specification requires second and later occurrences of a\nhint to be ignored. Blink currently forwards duplicates to the browser,\nincluding when requests are delegated to the Windows WebAuthn API.\n\nDeduplicate recognized hints while preserving their first-occurrence\norder in the shared creation and request options converter. Cover both\nconversion paths and update the Windows API expectations.\n\nExtend WPT coverage to accept repeated recognized hints in create/get\nrequests and preserve them during JSON parsing. Internal deduplication\nis checked by the converter tests.\n\nRemove resources/utils.js from the creation hints test because its\nbase64urlEncode shadows the Uint8Array encoder in helpers.js used by\ncredential validation.\n\nBug: 369331496\nChange-Id: I72856a814f7fcc99f8785375035e728db5fa0df7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8391839\nReviewed-by: Ken Buchanan \u003ckenrb@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nina Satragno \u003cnsatragno@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Amos Lim \u003camoseui@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703450}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8053be7a37a811ae38de8882588fdcecc6ebb081\nwpt-pr: 62899\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webauthn/createcredential-hints.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webauthn/getcredential-hints.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webauthn/public-key-credential-creation-options-from-json.https.window.js"], "git_node": "902d619f95867c1399a4dd34f18017328bc7cf0b", "git_parents": ["1beb3ab4b13d36642b695708049186158ebb876e"], "node": "6204d2f3f82ae3c6e629b048fa7085864f399ce7", "parents": ["049369f59fc721407f9d492de73846c943123488"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074969 [wpt PR 62902] - Keep menus open when using side arrows to move between toplevel submenus., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nKeep menus open when using side arrows to move between toplevel submenus.\n\nThis makes a related set of changes to menu keyboard behavior:\n\n* When focus is on a menuitem in a menulist and that menulist is in a\n  menubar, the old side arrow behavior closed the current open menulist\n  and focused the adjacent menuitem.  For example, if focus was on File\n  -\u003e Open, the right arrow would close the File menu and focus Edit.\n  This makes the change that we now also *open* the Edit menu, although\n  we leave the focus on the Edit menuitem.  This introduces the new\n  possibility that a menuitem can have keyboard focus while its submenu\n  is open.\n\n* When focus is on a menuitem in a menubar and its submenu is open (a\n  new possibility introduced by the previous change), right or left\n  arrows now move to the adjacent menuitem while closing the open\n  submenu and opening a new one.  (Note that the new one doesn't\n  necessarily have a submenu, so we need to close the old one\n  explicitly.)\n\nBug: 406566432\nChange-Id: I69e53e1b28505ccb128bd89f132a31097e14a619\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8426748\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703458}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6eb7c10af0fbb971b746f0a50d1fcc921814a597\nwpt-pr: 62902\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/focus-menu-elements-side-arrowoperations.html"], "git_node": "28e77fd80150bb1ec9dbce06e8606dbe5283fa9f", "git_parents": ["902d619f95867c1399a4dd34f18017328bc7cf0b"], "node": "b745c6ef9db3c73b0b81e2eb203895d50e1a8748", "parents": ["6204d2f3f82ae3c6e629b048fa7085864f399ce7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074969 [wpt PR 62902] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62902\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/focus-menu-elements-side-arrowoperations.html.ini"], "git_node": "c976374a08f7c5605b297c8a2258ae9f31d01c8d", "git_parents": ["28e77fd80150bb1ec9dbce06e8606dbe5283fa9f"], "node": "31a896d1fdd3ad8135c7f67302fd5331674c9ec1", "parents": ["b745c6ef9db3c73b0b81e2eb203895d50e1a8748"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074939 [wpt PR 62894] - Add a test for scroll-axis-lock: none on the viewport., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd a test for scroll-axis-lock: none on the viewport.\n\nBug: 479472367, 561877895\nChange-Id: Iac61c5377ff8b0830e50ae2e6d94d84b368d54ef\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8369240\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703471}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c6b5895fa2c1cc649609473608350e99482c9f00\nwpt-pr: 62894\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-none-touch-viewport.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-none-wheel-viewport.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/support/scroll-axis-lock.js"], "git_node": "d5ee17569c5f0061ef3cfdd287d7575f5a644670", "git_parents": ["c976374a08f7c5605b297c8a2258ae9f31d01c8d"], "node": "e70d0135fe7d56504fa0eb7e4fb155bdb66fed70", "parents": ["31a896d1fdd3ad8135c7f67302fd5331674c9ec1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074939 [wpt PR 62894] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62894\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/chrome-480554290-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-none-touch-viewport.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-none-wheel-viewport.html.ini"], "git_node": "cfdb68f341a214d36f5b6658ae7a3bff6c3e6122", "git_parents": ["d5ee17569c5f0061ef3cfdd287d7575f5a644670"], "node": "298d94f2e496c4f4cb8c0b60291cf7d389d3b24c", "parents": ["e70d0135fe7d56504fa0eb7e4fb155bdb66fed70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andres Ricardo Perez \u003candresrperez@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074986 [wpt PR 62904] - [Canvas2D] Respect image orientation in createPattern(), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Canvas2D] Respect image orientation in createPattern()\n\nEnsure `Canvas2DRecorderContext::createPattern` respects image\norientation when creating pattern fills. Previously, the resolved\norientation setting was not forwarded to `CanvasPattern` and\n`ImagePattern`, which caused pattern shaders to render raw, unoriented\ntiles and led to inconsistencies with `drawImage`.\n\nPass the resolved `RespectImageOrientationEnum` through `CanvasPattern`\nand `Pattern` into `ImagePattern`, reorienting the tile image when\norientation must be respected and the source image has non-default\norientation. Also preserve orientation metadata in multi-frame\n`BitmapImage::ImageForDefaultFrame()`.\n\nThe WPT test matches its equivalent for drawImage():\nhttps://crsrc.org/c/third_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/css/css-images/image-orientation/image-orientation-none-cross-origin-canvas.html\n\nBug: 514422784\nChange-Id: I4e4586efe50669331f2cf9308b79000dfb94376e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8399726\nReviewed-by: Jean-Philippe Gravel \u003cjpgravel@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Andres Ricardo Perez Rojas \u003candresrperez@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Andres Ricardo Perez Rojas \u003candresrperez@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703515}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8486f1dbfad2efc846f3475574deda4ea3e98afa\nwpt-pr: 62904\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/image-orientation/image-orientation-none-cross-origin-canvas-pattern.html"], "git_node": "8c652dcb711c0a5b3d42fbd14b5d489abe9b9368", "git_parents": ["cfdb68f341a214d36f5b6658ae7a3bff6c3e6122"], "node": "2579c0bae2d5dd5a18294e8d8f57428f1c13a3ca", "parents": ["298d94f2e496c4f4cb8c0b60291cf7d389d3b24c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074986 [wpt PR 62904] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62904\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/image-orientation/image-orientation-none-cross-origin-canvas-pattern.html.ini"], "git_node": "ff5ec43d4c17ef62e144278bfb03c1cbcdd95bba", "git_parents": ["8c652dcb711c0a5b3d42fbd14b5d489abe9b9368"], "node": "06ae753443eed1cca51f0d5110ab811c68a4362b", "parents": ["2579c0bae2d5dd5a18294e8d8f57428f1c13a3ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075019 [wpt PR 62909] - Fire \"checked\" event at checkable menuitems., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFire \"checked\" event at checkable menuitems.\n\nThis follows the current spec PR in terms of when it does or doesn't\nfire, although I'm not sure if those rules will stick.\n\nBug: 406566432\nChange-Id: Ic0ad19277768b6fc33138bc033c0cfe266b0c762\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8425645\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703502}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c39e25f16d8d768ac3f00d441d6a88bfaff81d0d\nwpt-pr: 62909\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/checkable.html"], "git_node": "9e48b7d207a1a39c92418a8673d732e43cd0814e", "git_parents": ["ff5ec43d4c17ef62e144278bfb03c1cbcdd95bba"], "node": "b92808472dc6cd01a3dd9cf6f77ff4af4c170a7a", "parents": ["06ae753443eed1cca51f0d5110ab811c68a4362b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075019 [wpt PR 62909] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62909\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/checkable.html.ini"], "git_node": "5fba1b407717d085315f095bbeede5d1911a76c1", "git_parents": ["9e48b7d207a1a39c92418a8673d732e43cd0814e"], "node": "107cca7f6550be7ed97b1c69a1ee2fc8c6f5ff79", "parents": ["b92808472dc6cd01a3dd9cf6f77ff4af4c170a7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075062 [wpt PR 62921] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321821, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321821 (#62921)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b18c7cddecba4d21acb1a3398096a5c42346e2a1\nwpt-pr: 62921\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/per-entry-events/dispose-for-navigation-in-child-entries-updated.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/per-entry-events/dispose-for-navigation-in-sibling-detach-frame.html"], "git_node": "8cbdc53ec6e6c4e8ce2ed7981c08c20d6d5b0ebc", "git_parents": ["5fba1b407717d085315f095bbeede5d1911a76c1"], "node": "af452aff2ffcace046a924cc259abb1235d42c13", "parents": ["107cca7f6550be7ed97b1c69a1ee2fc8c6f5ff79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074419 [wpt PR 62851] - Fix background color mismatch in MathML ::first-letter test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix background color mismatch in MathML ::first-letter test\n\nThe test used `lightgreen` but its reference used `lime`, so it failed\nin all engines. Use `lime` like the other tests in the series.\n\nBug: 333971751\nChange-Id: I2d04fcffbc9173ea1f3b05541a0b33da2654a258\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8429005\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703074}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 42477769a19c2fd7501508eeced7b8879656aaff\nwpt-pr: 62851\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/css-styling/first-line-first-letter-pseudo-elements-004.html"], "git_node": "5ffc716262ce80c2c071435215cdb6d4fcdd1f30", "git_parents": ["8cbdc53ec6e6c4e8ce2ed7981c08c20d6d5b0ebc"], "node": "9c3456751f1a560c8780bfa24625f866c0d25e85", "parents": ["af452aff2ffcace046a924cc259abb1235d42c13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mo Jamal \u003cjamalmo@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074948 [wpt PR 62898] - [webauthn] Add remoteClientDataJSON renderer surface, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[webauthn] Add remoteClientDataJSON renderer surface\n\nAdd the complete renderer-side input and output surface for the `remoteClientDataJSON` WebAuthn extension. The preceding CLs provide the Mojo contract and browser-side input/output handling.\n\n- Add the experimental WebAuthenticationRemoteClientDataJson runtime feature and map device::kWebAuthnRemoteClientDataJson to it.\n- Add remoteClientDataJSON to the input, FromJSON, output, and output-JSON IDL dictionaries behind the runtime feature.\n- Convert renderer input values to Mojo and browser output values back to the IDL boolean result.\n- Surface the create-flow output through getClientExtensionResults().\n- Advertise extension:remoteClientDataJSON from getClientCapabilities().\n- Reject incompatible conditional and immediate mediation combinations at the renderer boundary.\n- Cover input conversion, JSON round trips, mediation rejection, and extension output conversion.\n\nAI-Assisted Development: developed with assistance from Anthropic's Claude (Claude Code CLI).\n\nBug: 506062130\nChange-Id: Ie2a65b4a5153894ab4e670d10507479dde6578c1\nSpec: https://w3c.github.io/webauthn/#sctn-remote-client-data-json-extension\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8177083\nReviewed-by: Ken Buchanan \u003ckenrb@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Martin Kreichgauer \u003cmartinkr@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ken Buchanan \u003ckenrb@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rick Byers \u003crbyers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703589}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 892e178e491bd541326b80ca086253fa03b84233\nwpt-pr: 62898\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webauthn/getclientcapabilities.https.html"], "git_node": "b5bfceb6eef56d06366e0b41f62a7e8f7898600e", "git_parents": ["5ffc716262ce80c2c071435215cdb6d4fcdd1f30"], "node": "0942364f54c2c9acca9be6ec636f15d2dc6a139b", "parents": ["9c3456751f1a560c8780bfa24625f866c0d25e85"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luke Warlow \u003clwarlow@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075046 [wpt PR 62913] - Add initial base appearance UA-styles for temporal inputs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd initial base appearance UA-styles for temporal inputs\n\nThese changes are gated behind the AppearanceBase flag.\n\nSee https://drafts.csswg.org/css-forms-1\n\nBug: 450139531\nChange-Id: Ibf85efa815c03464d06f90f0f62dc12a6e000e22\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8393297\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703678}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b42a965afe0ca3507de839a92cc0c3efa69ccb90\nwpt-pr: 62913\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-forms/appearance-base-basic.html"], "git_node": "3f284f9a70ee2174cc32cc3d0ea0ce15bddcc7bd", "git_parents": ["b5bfceb6eef56d06366e0b41f62a7e8f7898600e"], "node": "7ff1dc22128f23d5a90196f6761571b4c5ae9f28", "parents": ["0942364f54c2c9acca9be6ec636f15d2dc6a139b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luke Warlow \u003clwarlow@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075045 [wpt PR 62912] - Add initial base appearance UA-styles for meter elements., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd initial base appearance UA-styles for meter elements.\n\nThese changes are gated behind the AppearanceBase flag.\n\nSee https://drafts.csswg.org/css-forms-1\n\nBug: 450139531\nChange-Id: Id7d8e49e179ef40235ab8f434da81a87d65b4c03\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8394017\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703689}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0d8832b8b51b5c4d7acf534b3524bfc81c52feaf\nwpt-pr: 62912\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-forms/meter-base-appearance-rendering-ref.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-forms/meter-base-appearance-rendering.tentative.html"], "git_node": "4ebd2f59ada7bdcbab82d36b32aef02b6f1bbe0c", "git_parents": ["3f284f9a70ee2174cc32cc3d0ea0ce15bddcc7bd"], "node": "ac0ca635e3433bdc759498ba9781a02d735e486c", "parents": ["7ff1dc22128f23d5a90196f6761571b4c5ae9f28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075045 [wpt PR 62912] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62912\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-forms/meter-base-appearance-rendering.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "2fd5254d2859d49a89821b539d249bb136e774cd", "git_parents": ["4ebd2f59ada7bdcbab82d36b32aef02b6f1bbe0c"], "node": "dd5e48ec0749ed18aba0efd6a0b4e180c59fcfdf", "parents": ["ac0ca635e3433bdc759498ba9781a02d735e486c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075096 [wpt PR 62926] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324519, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324519 (#62926)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cbcebc72d1476c2b62c0afce2920bf2c8b95b7fb\nwpt-pr: 62926\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/alignment/grid-container-baseline-first-item-in-grid-order.html"], "git_node": "c7bbf5e245d2625610ba5e446199e61f2d0c8821", "git_parents": ["2fd5254d2859d49a89821b539d249bb136e774cd"], "node": "7a3921b30b1f12db0533504255dca43a7ff482fc", "parents": ["dd5e48ec0749ed18aba0efd6a0b4e180c59fcfdf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Domenic Denicola \u003cd@domenic.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074076 [wpt PR 62827] - Wait for focus fixup in fieldset disabling tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWait for focus fixup in fieldset disabling tests\n\nHTML clarified focus fixup in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8392, merged on January 27, 2023. It split the old rule into synchronous fixup when the focused node is removed, without blur events, and asynchronous fixup during \"update the rendering\" when the focused area becomes non-focusable. Disabling a fieldset falls into the latter case: the rendering update runs the focusing steps for the document's viewport.\n\ndisabled-003.html was added on April 7, 2023 in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/commit/5857a9b5776d85fe77883fadf62c398dc05cf608 as a regression test for Chromium's exponential-time fieldset traversal and a crash caused by reentrant blur handling. Although it postdates the HTML change, its assertions require Chromium's synchronous focus change after disabling a fieldset. They therefore fail implementations that defer the change until a rendering update.\n\nThe dedicated focus-fixup timing tests were updated in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/38062, merged on June 4, 2025, to check that focus remains unchanged synchronously and is fixed up after rendering. More recently, https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62292, merged on August 31, 2026, changed the moveBefore() focus-fixup tests to use waitForAtLeastOneFrame() before checking document.activeElement.\n\nUse the same rendering wait here by converting both nested-fieldset cases to promise tests. Assert that each input initially receives focus before disabling the fieldset, then check that focus has moved away after rendering. This preserves the original shallow and deeply nested crash/hang cases.\n\nDo not add exact-timing assertions here that would fail Chromium for changing focus synchronously. Timing after disabling a fieldset is already covered by the #button4 subtest in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/532766fee262a2b41054665505b9dc37bd7c0a25/html/interaction/focus/processing-model/focus-fixup-rule-one-no-dialogs.html. That case focuses a button and disables its parent fieldset; the shared helper checks that focus remains unchanged synchronously, during the first animation-frame callback, and during ResizeObserver delivery, then checks that focus is fixed up after rendering.\n\nBoth subtests change from failing to passing in Firefox 151 and WebKit 26.5, and continue to pass in Chromium 149.\n\nCo-authored-by: codex \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8e9f3e2199fca135a62526a75410ecf10d3f9e3d\nwpt-pr: 62827\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-fieldset-element/disabled-003.html"], "git_node": "e54af4a49aa26f9edc4d0b9fa90722f123c4a426", "git_parents": ["c7bbf5e245d2625610ba5e446199e61f2d0c8821"], "node": "d0174234741490e96f935047be72d1cd22ef3b71", "parents": ["7a3921b30b1f12db0533504255dca43a7ff482fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074076 [wpt PR 62827] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62827\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-fieldset-element/disabled-003.html.ini"], "git_node": "0e1e4df0b42ec9d15dc7ecb8a14c0608b4afbefb", "git_parents": ["e54af4a49aa26f9edc4d0b9fa90722f123c4a426"], "node": "d02a2c586b6bfe12ded4294489dd529537a21799", "parents": ["d0174234741490e96f935047be72d1cd22ef3b71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075090 [wpt PR 62924] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323524, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323524 (#62924)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b16aeea13b18b83b53081e5a7ecddcae66e2dc21\nwpt-pr: 62924\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/getComputedStyle-insets-grid.html"], "git_node": "39a76287cf69417ab0f617ad99b41d18412ae3c1", "git_parents": ["0e1e4df0b42ec9d15dc7ecb8a14c0608b4afbefb"], "node": "bb39349b359c7d9a480a81c9a675f857b9b00d10", "parents": ["d02a2c586b6bfe12ded4294489dd529537a21799"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shivani Sharma \u003cshivanisha@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075056 [wpt PR 62917] - [Fenced Frames] Remove fenced frames code keeping stubs intact, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Fenced Frames] Remove fenced frames code keeping stubs intact\n\nThis CL removes internal fenced frames code while continuing to\nsupport the FF stub as per the I2S for fenced frames removal:\nhttps://chromestatus.com/feature/6366274495053824\n\nFollowing the parent CL that stubs out \u003cfencedframe\u003e and\nFencedFrameConfig: crrev.com/c/8144979,\nthis CL removes the underlying internal MPArch host\ninfrastructure, Mojo reporting beacon interfaces, and renderer-side\nframe tree logic.\n\nFor consistency with the FF element being stubbed, this CL also stubs\nwindow.fence methods.\n\nIt hardcodes IsInFencedFrameTree() and similar methods in blink and\nbrowser code to always return false. To keep this CL a reasonable\nsize, those methods and their hundreds of callers will be cleaned up in\na follow-up.\n\nMain Details:\n1. Mojo:\n   - Removed beacon reporting methods (SendFencedFrameReportingBeacon,\n     SendFencedFrameReportingBeaconToCustomURL,\n     SetFencedFrameAutomaticBeaconReportEventData) from LocalFrameHost.\n   - Removed AdScriptDidCreateFencedFrame from SubresourceFilterHost.\n2. Blink Renderer:\n   - Deleted window.fence JS API (Fence, fence.idl, fence_event.idl,\n     fence.h, fence.cc, fence_test.cc).\n   - Deleted DocumentFencedFrames and cleaned up all traversals.\n   - Deleted WebRemoteFrameImpl::CreateForFencedFrame.\n   - Hardcoded Frame::IsInFencedFrameTree() and IsFencedFrameRoot() to\n     unconditionally return false.\n3. Content Browser & Chrome:\n   - Deleted content::FencedFrame, FencedDocumentData,\nAutomaticBeaconInfo, and fenced_frame_unittest.cc.\n   - Removed fenced_frames_, GetFencedFrames(), and DestroyFencedFrame()\n     from RenderFrameHostImpl.\n   - Removed SiteInstanceImpl::CreateForFencedFrame.\n   - Deleted chrome/browser TaskManager's FencedFrameTask.\n   - Updated TestRenderFrameHost::AppendFencedFrame() and test utilities\n     to remove FencedFrame dependencies.\n\nFollow-up CLs:\n1. Call site cleanup: Remove remaining checks for IsInFencedFrameTree()\n   and IsNestedWithinFencedFrame() across content/, chrome/, and\n   components/ now that they unconditionally return false.\n2. Navigation plumbing: Clean up _unfencedTop navigation logic and\n   is_unfenced_top_navigation IPC parameter across Navigator and\n   NavigationControllerImpl.\n3. Test cleanup: Remove obsolete unit and browser tests specifically\n   asserting feature restrictions or behaviors inside fenced frame\n   trees.\n4. Data structure cleanup: Remove FencedFrameStatus and\n   FrameTree::Type::kFencedFrame enums once all remaining references are\n   eliminated.\n5. Cleanup URN:UUID to URL related functionality during navigation.\n\nLow-Coverage-Reason: Tests needed to be removed as FF code is only a\nstub. The remaining unreached code will be removed in the follow-up CLs\ntracked in bug 564522508.\n\nBug: 538634423, 540020364\nFixed: 40227465\nAX-Relnotes: n/a.\n\nChange-Id: I0bd9d4d3b9a75270d74f1a5137ae7efe381617f9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8144621\nReviewed-by: Colin Blundell \u003cblundell@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Josh Karlin \u003cjkarlin@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joe Mason \u003cjoenotcharles@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Xiaochen Zhou \u003cxiaochenzh@chromium.org\u003e\nSLSA-Policy-Verified: SLSA Policy Verification Service \u003cdevtools-gerritcodereview-exitgate@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Shivani Sharma \u003cshivanisha@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Lei Zhang \u003cthestig@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Andrew Verge \u003caverge@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dave Tapuska \u003cdtapuska@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alex Moshchuk \u003calexmos@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703783}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e00846900c4974eaa7d12f7110d66e254c0f99b8\nwpt-pr: 62917\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/fenced-frame-stub.https.html"], "git_node": "91cf21132ae60211fcff347a04f6baaf9683a5bd", "git_parents": ["39a76287cf69417ab0f617ad99b41d18412ae3c1"], "node": "9e0711cde2af8367b90c7faac8f1a546c298c903", "parents": ["bb39349b359c7d9a480a81c9a675f857b9b00d10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075080 [wpt PR 62923] - [gap-decorations] Remove stale TODOs from GapDecorations code, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[gap-decorations] Remove stale TODOs from GapDecorations code\n\nFor the inset TODO comments we already have test coverage here:\nthird_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/css/css-gaps/parsing/rule-inset-shorthand.html\n\nChange-Id: I2507fbfd4509776184e466b5099a700e8dbd6387\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8446502\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703802}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8e8294c09bb2d8a3c21e9d8f891874b15ecded20\nwpt-pr: 62923\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/parsing/rule-inset-cap-start-end-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/parsing/rule-inset-cap-start-end-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/parsing/rule-inset-junction-start-end-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/parsing/rule-inset-junction-start-end-invalid.html"], "git_node": "d683aa3fcb371c9937da22c853e069b6f07ef21b", "git_parents": ["91cf21132ae60211fcff347a04f6baaf9683a5bd"], "node": "e074db4c0b31d783d7e409da722faf64b1867c95", "parents": ["9e0711cde2af8367b90c7faac8f1a546c298c903"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075110 [wpt PR 62928] - [WebCodecs] Fix conflicting description tests in audio-decoder WPT, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebCodecs] Fix conflicting description tests in audio-decoder WPT\n\nPer https://github.com/w3c/webcodecs/issues/826,\n`AudioDecoder.isConfigSupported()` does not require\n`AudioDecoderConfig.description`, even when `description` is required by\n`AudioDecoder.configure()` (such as for `flac`, `vorbis`, or\nmulti-channel `opus`).\n\nThis CL fixes two issues in `audio-decoder.https.any.js`:\n1. Removes the conflicting multi-channel `opus` entry from\n  `invalidConfigs`.\n2. Awaits`AudioDecoder.isConfigSupported()` only for\n  `supportedButErrorOnConfiguration` entries in the `shouldError` loop.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=99ce3bb9-84d9-495a-b0e2-f29a2e07431a\n\nBug: 360083330\nChange-Id: Iedc22144f78291549cc47c8af18b7044589e3900\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8449240\nReviewed-by: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703867}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: be7a4efae6cadad861ed9e03270f41f0de262cd2\nwpt-pr: 62928\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/audio-decoder.https.any.js"], "git_node": "6ed6025a07b875db692fd39937bb74c07850329b", "git_parents": ["d683aa3fcb371c9937da22c853e069b6f07ef21b"], "node": "8ea72b10f2f0efe27f63161ca862e91c5d20c12d", "parents": ["e074db4c0b31d783d7e409da722faf64b1867c95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brent Fulgham \u003c44174109+brentfulgham@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075149 [wpt PR 62931] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=203509, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=203509 (#62931)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e35344a20f922751f5ea8cc678cfd79d65056d5c\nwpt-pr: 62931\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/replaced-element-max-content-contribution-transferred-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/table-cell-definite-height-transferred-size.html"], "git_node": "3f5c5f0bffddbb1478f7df5a89cf524334836129", "git_parents": ["6ed6025a07b875db692fd39937bb74c07850329b"], "node": "4419dd8341e060763785e33083b95335405c4ee8", "parents": ["8ea72b10f2f0efe27f63161ca862e91c5d20c12d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stalgia Grigg \u003cstalgiag@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075036 [wpt PR 62871] - [direct-sockets] Add vkrot-cell as suggested reviewer, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[direct-sockets] Add vkrot-cell as suggested reviewer\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6052c521aff26ed90e620c1ec2c9a61d665b9b3c\nwpt-pr: 62871\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/direct-sockets/META.yml"], "git_node": "62a582b35dba8130bcafb9f85eeaaa553855439c", "git_parents": ["3f5c5f0bffddbb1478f7df5a89cf524334836129"], "node": "196da59f5de9d0d61705a9d1bd0944fe64144be0", "parents": ["4419dd8341e060763785e33083b95335405c4ee8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075052 [wpt PR 62915] - [anchor] Scrolling doesn't affect fallbacks inside fragmentation., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[anchor] Scrolling doesn't affect fallbacks inside fragmentation.\n\nA scrollable container inside a fragmentation context is always\nmonolithic, so it's not possible to have fragmented anchor-positioned\nOOFs that are affected by scrolling. The scroll ranges collected would\nbe in the stitched coordinate system anyway, which is useless. So don't\ncollect them.\n\nDiscovered while trying to make this work with the FragmentedOofInCb\nfeature.\n\nWe still need to choose the right fallback during layout, though. There\nwas no test coverage for this, so add a couple of tests.\n\nNo behavior changes intended.\n\nBug: 40267498\nChange-Id: I2503a6a8d87d0e30c24df39d0e60eeb33058531d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8442276\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1704130}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f63601f60d1627c76390c095feaacf5d511edec3\nwpt-pr: 62915\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-try-fallbacks-multicol-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-try-fallbacks-multicol-002.html"], "git_node": "e775c1b0d20b9b29833fef41088b692b8f417001", "git_parents": ["62a582b35dba8130bcafb9f85eeaaa553855439c"], "node": "9d56ba0ed1794a0531a0c74d860a410625dfbd43", "parents": ["196da59f5de9d0d61705a9d1bd0944fe64144be0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075052 [wpt PR 62915] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62915\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-as-multicol-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "fa49816c23bd78a3a86e3012cbdea45374aef855", "git_parents": ["e775c1b0d20b9b29833fef41088b692b8f417001"], "node": "d4a44c4e8cb913353347c4d44b5fdb6b8ee5d5d1", "parents": ["9d56ba0ed1794a0531a0c74d860a410625dfbd43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075055 [wpt PR 62916] - Deflake css-anchor-position/scroll-to-anchored-fixed-*, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDeflake css-anchor-position/scroll-to-anchored-fixed-*\n\nSome of the tests/refs were missing an await for document.fonts.ready.\nAdd it everywhere.\n\nLocally scroll-to-anchored-fixed-001.html and\nscroll-to-anchored-fixed-002.html had a pass rate of about 25% without\nthis fix.\n\nscroll-to-anchored-fixed-000.html is still failing (consistently), but\nfix that test too, so that it doesn't become flaky once we fix the bug,\nwhatever that is.\n\nBug: 469481151\nChange-Id: Ic9127455d6d778768839e2dc997a99250ca4ec2e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8446078\nReviewed-by: Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1704135}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3834b07555e8115b900633c9ad972ef8a8cbe433\nwpt-pr: 62916\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/scroll-to-anchored-fixed-000-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/scroll-to-anchored-fixed-000.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/scroll-to-anchored-fixed-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/scroll-to-anchored-fixed-002-ref.html"], "git_node": "28dfa845b82913f1d3ccf835fadfc00dc3217686", "git_parents": ["fa49816c23bd78a3a86e3012cbdea45374aef855"], "node": "0a7bd93f9dd0b8f1dcd962540063752d385aacc0", "parents": ["d4a44c4e8cb913353347c4d44b5fdb6b8ee5d5d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074683 [wpt PR 62867] - Add test to verify scroll-axis-lock does not propagate from the body to viewport in quirks mode., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd test to verify scroll-axis-lock does not propagate from the body to viewport in quirks mode.\n\nSee https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13207#issuecomment-5549971412\n\nBug: 479472367, 561877895\nChange-Id: I08afa773230b04a4704a3ba829259d859f5c82d4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8412467\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1704169}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cda230b4e4678b4de993e8fa95752348af4b8c56\nwpt-pr: 62867\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-not-propagated-from-body-quirks.html"], "git_node": "a158c1b1de160e99e7a51bf93adad38b63a71a8c", "git_parents": ["28dfa845b82913f1d3ccf835fadfc00dc3217686"], "node": "ce25cc8490bf95020a2b32a6b18b5a171725b6f3", "parents": ["0a7bd93f9dd0b8f1dcd962540063752d385aacc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074683 [wpt PR 62867] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62867\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock-not-propagated-from-body-quirks.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/text-overflow-string-in-textarea-focused.html.ini"], "git_node": "e009a66d1e0b527d7c20aac72f0899311fd52e13", "git_parents": ["a158c1b1de160e99e7a51bf93adad38b63a71a8c"], "node": "c6a1548b0de97162dfa7e7beab6b61215de90fea", "parents": ["ce25cc8490bf95020a2b32a6b18b5a171725b6f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "BruceDai \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075169 [wpt PR 62933] - webnn: add a test of casting uint32 tensors to uint64 for cast op, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebnn: add a test of casting uint32 tensors to uint64 for cast op\n\nChange-Id: I62947fdfbb4424d91a1b1a31f79f491ee3c6e5be\nBug: 564071954\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:win11-blink-rel, mac14.arm64-blink-rel, mac15.arm64-blink-rel\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8427348\nCommit-Queue: Dai, Feng \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Reilly Grant \u003creillyg@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Dai, Feng \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Hu, Ningxin \u003cningxin.hu@intel.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1704192}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c4824748946e110f005a9496151f1321878bbea5\nwpt-pr: 62933\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/cast.https.any.js"], "git_node": "60b4cef69a39698bddab149eee2f3e43ecd0ad7d", "git_parents": ["e009a66d1e0b527d7c20aac72f0899311fd52e13"], "node": "7ba4dc5f3fc5f921c57f371b9c19e8934aab56fe", "parents": ["c6a1548b0de97162dfa7e7beab6b61215de90fea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "BruceDai \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075060 [wpt PR 62920] - webnn: add rank-range validation helpers and apply to simple operators, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebnn: add rank-range validation helpers and apply to simple operators\n\nopSupportLimits() declares a rankRange (min/max) for every operand of\nevery operator, but nothing in the WPT validation suite checks that an\nimplementation actually honours the range it advertises. A rank the\nimplementation wrongly accepts is reported as supported and then reaches\nthe backend, where internal limits are tighter than the WebNN global max\nof 8 (e.g. XNNPACK's XNN_MAX_TENSOR_DIMS is 6).\n\nThis CL adds shared helpers to resources/utils_validation.js:\n\n - validateOperandRankTooSmall / validateOperandRankInRange /\n   validateOperandRankTooLarge assert that an operand's rank is rejected\n   below rankRange.min, accepted throughout [min, max], and rejected\n   above max. The out-of-range helpers iterate the whole out-of-range\n   region rather than just the boundary.\n - validateOperandRank / validateOperandRankOutOfRange bundle those so a\n   caller cannot forget one region.\n - pickSupportedDataTypeInfo / buildInputOperand pick a dtype the\n   operand declares that is also creatable as a graph input, falling\n   back to a widening-compatible dtype plus a cast() when the declared\n   dtype is not directly creatable.\n\nApply the helpers to operators whose rank check is a single call with no\ncompanion operands: activations, element-wise unary, pooling, reduction,\ncast, concat, cumulativeSum, expand, pad, reshape, reverse, slice,\nsplit, tile, transpose and triangular.\n\nThis is the first of a series; subsequent CLs cover operators with\ncompanion operands, Cartesian multi-operand rank coverage, and the\ngather/scatter/quantize families.\n\nChange-Id: If18b77397f46dfcbfe5ecdb2e7969b28c2d81d17\nBug: 501135993\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:win11-blink-rel, mac14.arm64-blink-rel, mac14-blink-rel, mac15.arm64-blink-rel, mac15-blink-rel, linux-blink-rel\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8423780\nReviewed-by: Reilly Grant \u003creillyg@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Dai, Feng \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Hu, Ningxin \u003cningxin.hu@intel.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dai, Feng \u003cfeng.dai@intel.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1704212}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cfb07da1a3581fd1c1c46e236adf32b43ed95fbc\nwpt-pr: 62920\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/resources/utils_validation.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/cast.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/clamp.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/concat.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/cumulativeSum.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/elementwise-unary.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/elu.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/expand.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/gelu.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/hardSigmoid.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/hardSwish.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/instanceNormalization.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/leakyRelu.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/linear.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/pad.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/pooling.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/reduction.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/relu.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/reshape.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/reverse.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/sigmoid.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/slice.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/softmax.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/softplus.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/softsign.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/split.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/tanh.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/tile.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/transpose.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/validation_tests/triangular.https.any.js"], "git_node": "01182ff133ac65c819265840fb079e735772977d", "git_parents": ["60b4cef69a39698bddab149eee2f3e43ecd0ad7d"], "node": "b5f9c63b8e56c890a0eba586cdfd71d9846c0181", "parents": ["7ba4dc5f3fc5f921c57f371b9c19e8934aab56fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072373 [wpt PR 62719] - DOM: tests for event listeners on targets that are not fully active, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDOM: tests for event listeners on targets that are not fully active\n\nCovers skipping an event listener when the event target's or the listener\ncallback's global is a Window whose associated Document is not fully active,\nand how that interacts with adopted nodes, event handler attributes, and\ndocuments without a browsing context.\n\nPR: https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1085 & https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12944\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 443da5ac58a504e644df1b83a817f83129f61648\nwpt-pr: 62719\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/events/event-listener-not-fully-active-adopted-node.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/events/event-listener-not-fully-active-callback.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/events/event-listener-not-fully-active-navigated.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/events/event-listener-not-fully-active-target.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/events/resources/not-fully-active-frame.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/events/resources/not-fully-active-helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/webappapis/scripting/events/event-handler-no-browsing-context.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/webappapis/scripting/events/event-listener-sandboxed-scripts.html"], "git_node": "aa1d063bff00ae98011bf9bf590c6942d38aa79f", "git_parents": ["01182ff133ac65c819265840fb079e735772977d"], "node": "31d76ef8af549eb19325afda577acdcd370d00b3", "parents": ["b5f9c63b8e56c890a0eba586cdfd71d9846c0181"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072373 [wpt PR 62719] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62719\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/events/event-listener-not-fully-active-adopted-node.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/events/event-listener-not-fully-active-navigated.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/events/event-listener-not-fully-active-target.html.ini"], "git_node": "1a3776ca9940f7bacb65e2644f43aef1b8e6d069", "git_parents": ["aa1d063bff00ae98011bf9bf590c6942d38aa79f"], "node": "c5ab39cc280c9ddeee8d7f909db87e550acfefce", "parents": ["31d76ef8af549eb19325afda577acdcd370d00b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Pieters \u003czcorpan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071487 [wpt PR 62516] - HTML: test CORS and the \u003clink\u003e stylesheet MIME type quirk, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nHTML: test CORS and the \u003clink\u003e stylesheet MIME type quirk\n\nNo test set the `crossorigin` attribute on a style sheet with a bad MIME\ntype, so nothing distinguished the quirk's same-origin condition from its\nCORS-same-origin condition. A CORS-enabled cross-origin style sheet is\nCORS-same-origin, but its response's URL is not same origin with the\ndocument, so the quirk must not apply to it, and a redirect that crosses\norigins in either direction decides whether it applies.\n\nAlso add a `cors` knob to `resources/css.py`, and trim the spec text quoted\nin two existing tests.\n\nFor https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12468.\n\n--\nCSS: test the @import MIME type quirk with cross-origin responses\n\nSafari applies the quirk to a cross-origin redirect to a same-origin\nresponse, which is not CORS-same-origin.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a7a59f41e4aa84bed8a634c75e1d041bbb1dc4e6, 04180c9d23fbc63b5aa26ed1aa107493a10365f8\nwpt-pr: 62516\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-cascade/import-mime-type-quirks.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-cascade/resources/quirks-mime-type.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/stylesheet-cross-origin-redirect-quirks.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/document-metadata/the-link-element/link-style-data-url-quirks.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/document-metadata/the-link-element/link-style-quirks-crossorigin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/document-metadata/the-link-element/resources/css.py"], "git_node": "66279f83d8d193f006914c3191d639bebfcc76c4", "git_parents": ["1a3776ca9940f7bacb65e2644f43aef1b8e6d069"], "node": "27f659003247cd09f47943b6881069cce020c3aa", "parents": ["c5ab39cc280c9ddeee8d7f909db87e550acfefce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075115 [wpt PR 62929] - Fix duplicated and malformed attributes in WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix duplicated and malformed attributes in WPTs (#62929)\n\nRemove duplicate attributes ignored by the HTML parser, merging class\nand style values where both are intended.\n\nFix an unterminated metadata quote that consumes the viewport tag,\nremove stray attributes from the grid-gap test and its reference, and\ncorrect quoting in XHR test metadata.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: I66d4610ca2b8b910be2c66a2b3899eb240da49ce\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8220791\nReviewed-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Jacques Newman \u003cjanewman@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703956}\n\nCo-authored-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d0e58242b68ca8513bb2375e2d00c147cd7481b9\nwpt-pr: 62929\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-try-cascade.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/flex-aspect-ratio-img-column-011.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/grid-gap-decorations-067-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/grid-gap-decorations-067.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-items/grid-intrinsic-maximums-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-multicol/getclientrects-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-multicol/getclientrects-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-multicol/getclientrects-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollable-overflow-transform-005.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollable-overflow-transform-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollable-overflow-transform-010.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/nth-child-when-sibling-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/nth-last-child-when-sibling-changes.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/presentation-markup/mrow/inferred-mrow-baseline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/compat/pointerevent_touch-action-verification.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/shadow-dom/focus-navigation/reading-flow/tentative/grid-order-with-slots.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/shadow-dom/focus-navigation/reading-flow/tentative/grid-order.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/geometry/reftests/circle-calc-dynamic-viewport-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/send-redirect-post-upload.htm"], "git_node": "535451658a92a6458bbef926570da964709f1d0f", "git_parents": ["66279f83d8d193f006914c3191d639bebfcc76c4"], "node": "19977d75ebc552a94fd08adee506249f7cb020d0", "parents": ["27f659003247cd09f47943b6881069cce020c3aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071479 [wpt PR 62626] - Make ContainerQueryListController a Document supplement, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake ContainerQueryListController a Document supplement\n\nFollow-up to [1]. Attach the controller to Document instead of\nLocalDOMWindow, so null check no longer need.\n\nAdded tests cover that matches and change events stay correct\nafter the target is adopted into another document.\n\n[1] https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8255022/comment/616642a6_cd704fd3/\n\nBug: 40887402\nChange-Id: I33ea44db6d58776112dc37c0d8320af777940e66\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8374242\nCommit-Queue: Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1701551}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 761562aa00bda23a23e67198a7a2dce561297af1\nwpt-pr: 62626\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/match-container-change-event.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/match-container.tentative.html"], "git_node": "9f18f92df61907f171f7ad486badfed6a5a6b8ac", "git_parents": ["535451658a92a6458bbef926570da964709f1d0f"], "node": "1df84f89ad10b6e32c404ce4e06fa81d2eedd365", "parents": ["19977d75ebc552a94fd08adee506249f7cb020d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071479 [wpt PR 62626] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62626\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/whitespace-update-after-removal.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/match-container-change-event.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/match-container.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "b50b09b8a99466a32cb8f5eaf9d3be069600174d", "git_parents": ["9f18f92df61907f171f7ad486badfed6a5a6b8ac"], "node": "b0d8978ea9bf0a8a0ec1eccea855ebdfe0d65409", "parents": ["1df84f89ad10b6e32c404ce4e06fa81d2eedd365"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075173 [wpt PR 62934] - Add missing closing angle brackets to CSS WPT tags, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd missing closing angle brackets to CSS WPT tags\n\nA number of exported tests have a start or end tag whose \"\u003e\" was left\nout. The tokenizer keeps consuming past the end of the line, so the\nfollowing element is absorbed into the unterminated tag as a bogus\nattribute and never appears in the DOM.\n\nTerminate the offending tags so the parsed DOM matches the source.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: Ie2a51a1502b7443738129eb2e8862156fe058341\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8226467\nReviewed-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Javier Fernandez \u003cjfernandez@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1704425}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7efa3ab5de117cfd01ac23b65a7ab58d43397238\nwpt-pr: 62934\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/text/bidi-span-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/contain-inline-size-grid-indefinite-height-min-height-flex-row.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/alignment/flex-align-baseline-column-rtl-direction.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/anonymous-flex-item-restyle.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/abspos/grid-abspos-staticpos-align-self-end-large-border-padding.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/abspos/grid-abspos-staticpos-align-self-end.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-stop-002-nested.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-stop-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-atomic-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/trailing-ideographic-space-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/trailing-ideographic-space-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/trailing-ideographic-space-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/trailing-ideographic-space-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/trailing-ideographic-space-009.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/trailing-ideographic-space-010.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transforms/transform-containing-block-and-scrolling-area-for-fixed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transforms/transform-containing-block-dynamic-1a.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transforms/transform-containing-block-dynamic-1b.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/reference/viewport-page-print-no-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/reference/viewport-page-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/viewport-page-print.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/svg-aliasing-002.html"], "git_node": "cd512686317c205308631779455116b1114b68ce", "git_parents": ["b50b09b8a99466a32cb8f5eaf9d3be069600174d"], "node": "9694a89c004f35721a44c2f5905a8f6f30fe3572", "parents": ["b0d8978ea9bf0a8a0ec1eccea855ebdfe0d65409"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075173 [wpt PR 62934] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62934\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/text/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/text/crashtests/bidi-inline-fragment-oof-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-contain/contain-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-values/if-invalidation.html.ini"], "git_node": "c449e377c4e68df45f3284f9fa2dc39f0bcebc4f", "git_parents": ["cd512686317c205308631779455116b1114b68ce"], "node": "1c74f8da6f7ca811b4b0343a36ece24678d1a25b", "parents": ["9694a89c004f35721a44c2f5905a8f6f30fe3572"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075476 [wpt PR 62954] - Implement ContainerQueryList move to another document's controller, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement ContainerQueryList move to another document's controller\n\nA ContainerQueryList is associated only with its element, and the\nspec's change steps run per Document:\n\n\u003e As part of [=update the rendering=], for each [=fully active=]\n\u003e {{Document}},\n\u003e ...\n\u003e for each {{element}} \u003cvar\u003eele\u003c/var\u003e in the {{Document}}, in\n\u003e [=tree order=],\n\u003e that has one or more associated {{ContainerQueryList}} objects\n\u003e ...\n\nWhen an element is adopted into another document (e.g. via\nappendChild()), its ContainerQueryLists currently remain in the old\ndocument's controller and are never evaluated by the new document's\nlifecycle, which is where the element now lives. They should move with\nthe element.\n\nThis CL adds that transfer in Element::DidMoveToNewDocument(). Since a\nlist's element can now always reach its current document's controller,\nthe no-controller check is no longer needed.\n\nSpec PR: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/13551\n\nBug: 40887402\nChange-Id: Id152e56c671c500e0b02981bfc29874c97fa3fdf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8424265\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702558}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 681ceb45b1ca9591f81b4235c46631268ae08c12\nwpt-pr: 62954\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/match-container-change-event.tentative.html"], "git_node": "0c4633f8cf647e545d9cbddbc103da205bc71878", "git_parents": ["c449e377c4e68df45f3284f9fa2dc39f0bcebc4f"], "node": "8978e3a41bd48b106e4f4a1ae0f9944db587a133", "parents": ["1c74f8da6f7ca811b4b0343a36ece24678d1a25b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075476 [wpt PR 62954] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62954\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/match-container-change-event.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "e2d928a120784caa88ef2cb3a42efaf2d9c29280", "git_parents": ["0c4633f8cf647e545d9cbddbc103da205bc71878"], "node": "85ba7d3c823e80411718a3d970808f11fed54609", "parents": ["8978e3a41bd48b106e4f4a1ae0f9944db587a133"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Pieters \u003czcorpan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074092 [wpt PR 62828] - Test that loading=lazy videos don't delay load in either attribute order, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest that loading=lazy videos don't delay load in either attribute order\n\nFor whatwg/html#12854.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9885bf6ce60809d94a2929ec0a5529f582f9d805\nwpt-pr: 62828\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-below-viewport-load-event.html"], "git_node": "8589bec158fab76014a3ecab746baafa165fc52d", "git_parents": ["e2d928a120784caa88ef2cb3a42efaf2d9c29280"], "node": "37f60f247ac6d239c115fe138b47935a2fc314b3", "parents": ["85ba7d3c823e80411718a3d970808f11fed54609"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074092 [wpt PR 62828] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62828\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-below-viewport-load-event.html.ini"], "git_node": "38d2711fcc2050b41b0f42666ad8b7dcbf662e8b", "git_parents": ["8589bec158fab76014a3ecab746baafa165fc52d"], "node": "db096268ebb04949af19d0e4081840372f454bbc", "parents": ["37f60f247ac6d239c115fe138b47935a2fc314b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoavweiss@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075541 [wpt PR 62959] - Import map - avoid redefining exact match, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImport map - avoid redefining exact match\n\nBug: 502299325\nChange-Id: I0b4718a1f427579fd4124967ba425a5518bef4bf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8025358\nCommit-Queue: Yoav Weiss (@Shopify) \u003cyoavweiss@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kouhei Ueno \u003ckouhei@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1704687}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a26cbebef096de4ad58c73c706f57a53829dc691\nwpt-pr: 62959\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/import-maps/multiple-import-maps/exact-url-scope-immu