orian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076785 - Run the periodic mochitest-timings test-info task on b-linux-docker-amd for more CPU cores. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329958\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/file-metadata.yml"], "git_node": "3c294c0c64fc19d4f1aae49e61cc270cdf9ec2e8", "git_parents": ["dcbcd5e200815cf5bdcd647dfcf88b23de35ab31"], "node": "65e8129f882f77eb2015cd3bf11f4ba1fbbe9293", "parents": ["9086ecb31a1f823977111654f9e9ea170abb0519"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jaron Kramer \u003cinfo@jkramertech.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069726 - Scope the remote control stripe to the address bar. r=dao,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330152\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "777b69ee13d08899a6f25542f9a0c17261816908", "git_parents": ["3c294c0c64fc19d4f1aae49e61cc270cdf9ec2e8"], "node": "09a1bbe0dd1dd9bd7dda0469b37631d149865e9a", "parents": ["65e8129f882f77eb2015cd3bf11f4ba1fbbe9293"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075647 - Make clientInfo in RemoteWorkerData non-optional. r=dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329245\n", "files": ["dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerPrivate.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerChild.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerTypes.ipdlh", "dom/workers/sharedworkers/SharedWorker.cpp"], "git_node": "3f72179d7f2cbdb9212b98ca6b68e740b868dde0", "git_parents": ["777b69ee13d08899a6f25542f9a0c17261816908"], "node": "61331ff765b1234c0247355a8059ce0450cf67d6", "parents": ["09a1bbe0dd1dd9bd7dda0469b37631d149865e9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045402 - Testcase. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305278\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/test_selection_cross_shadow_boundary_offset_after_mutation.html"], "git_node": "a3f0f2c9388dee724bc79851bc868929966cb89d", "git_parents": ["3f72179d7f2cbdb9212b98ca6b68e740b868dde0"], "node": "092eb589445d3754da704e696d48d2221bdb7492", "parents": ["61331ff765b1234c0247355a8059ce0450cf67d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076537 - Install pyyaml in the python toolchains. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nWith MACH_BUILD_PYTHON_NATIVE_PACKAGE_SOURCE=system, as used in\nautomation builds, mach doesn't install packages from PyPI, so pyyaml\nfalls back to the vendored copy, which doesn't have the libyaml bindings.\nLoading YAML with the pure Python loader is several times slower: e.g.\nparsing the Glean metrics.yaml files takes ~5s instead of \u003c1s. Install\npyyaml alongside psutil and zstandard in the python toolchains so builds\nget the native loader.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329814\n", "files": ["build/pyyaml_requirements.in", "build/pyyaml_requirements.txt", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/python.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-cpython.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/pack-cpython.sh"], "git_node": "e164a1600461b5e95ec97a056377c8fa380992c0", "git_parents": ["a3f0f2c9388dee724bc79851bc868929966cb89d"], "node": "4006728424a349ea0981461a34a6a17462f34e88", "parents": ["092eb589445d3754da704e696d48d2221bdb7492"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076954 - Remove the expiring aboutprivatebrowsing click telemetry. r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330112\n", "files": ["browser/actors/AboutPrivateBrowsingChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.js", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "5f9b0ada4240b04519c382cab4c75a0f824cd18d", "git_parents": ["e164a1600461b5e95ec97a056377c8fa380992c0"], "node": "b39b306e1debaba0d082f87f78f8575118c61823", "parents": ["4006728424a349ea0981461a34a6a17462f34e88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074213 - r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330064\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp"], "git_node": "2ac695e9e8a5cc1a9c703cbf975b53c70951892d", "git_parents": ["5f9b0ada4240b04519c382cab4c75a0f824cd18d"], "node": "8ee8732bdad41b73700e829ebae455ad63a43bf6", "parents": ["b39b306e1debaba0d082f87f78f8575118c61823"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077170 - Remove legacy masonry syntax. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,dholbert,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330156\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/animation-type-longhand.js", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/style/ServoBindings.toml", "layout/style/nsStyleStruct.cpp", "layout/style/nsStyleStruct.h", "layout/style/test/property_database.js", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/position.rs", "servo/components/style/values/generics/grid.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/grid.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/position.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/masonry/__dir__.ini", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "a7825fd3129f7d9f3b17203b3c1c359eae07594a", "git_parents": ["2ac695e9e8a5cc1a9c703cbf975b53c70951892d"], "node": "d2c1d82b55551311f3974e689f8562e405962571", "parents": ["8ee8732bdad41b73700e829ebae455ad63a43bf6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1977950 - Add --enable-isolated-process to run unit tests with isolated process modde, not using build options. r=jmaher,geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nCurrently, MOZ_ANDROID_CONTENT_SERVICE_ISOLATED_PROCESS is used for test\nrunner. I would like to replace it with test runner's option that is\n`--enable-isolated-process`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265098\n", "files": ["layout/tools/reftest/manifest.sys.mjs", "layout/tools/reftest/reftestcommandline.py", "layout/tools/reftest/remotereftest.py", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/util/Environment.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/util/RuntimeCreator.java", "mobile/android/test_runner/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test_runner/TestRunnerActivity.java", "mobile/android/test_runner/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test_runner/XpcshellTestRunnerService.java", "testing/mochitest/mochitest_options.py", "testing/mochitest/runjunit.py", "testing/mochitest/runtests.py", "testing/mochitest/runtestsremote.py", "testing/mozbase/mozinfo/mozinfo/platforminfo.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/android_emulator_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/web_platform_tests.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/browsers/firefox.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/browsers/firefox_android.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/wptcommandline.py", "testing/xpcshell/remotexpcshelltests.py", "testing/xpcshell/runxpcshelltests.py", "testing/xpcshell/xpcshellcommandline.py"], "git_node": "77c91f0bb115699affdbec9d09c8a6c3f121b961", "git_parents": ["a7825fd3129f7d9f3b17203b3c1c359eae07594a"], "node": "65a9f07e3b634883286e6971cf76cb20889e0928", "parents": ["d2c1d82b55551311f3974e689f8562e405962571"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1977950 - Add isolated-process variants to taskcluster tasks. r=geckoview-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,ohall,ahal\n\nRemove debug-isolated-process build type, then add isolated-process\nvariants like the following:\n\n- geckoview-isolated-process\n- geckoview-isolated-process+no-fission\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265099\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/other.py", "taskcluster/kinds/build/android.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/reftest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/misc.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/xpcshell.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/os-integration.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/test-platforms.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/variants.yml"], "git_node": "607ca057c5ac12d887917728b2c5a7a525607c38", "git_parents": ["77c91f0bb115699affdbec9d09c8a6c3f121b961"], "node": "7e1aa9e77df90e2cc6bf6b01d07724b609963fab", "parents": ["65a9f07e3b634883286e6971cf76cb20889e0928"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1977950 - Get rid of MOZ_ANDROID_CONTENT_SERVICE_ISOLATED_PROCESS. r=geckoview-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,nalexander,jmaher\n\nThis build config option is no longer needed since we move this to\nGeckoRuntimeSettings.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265100\n", "files": ["mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/android-x86_64/debug-isolated-process", "mobile/android/geckoview/build.gradle", "mobile/android/moz.build", "mobile/android/moz.configure", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/test/xpcshell/test_GeckoViewAppConstants.js", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mozinfo.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/builds/releng_sub_android_configs/64_x86_64_debug_isolated_process.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/building/buildbase.py", "toolkit/modules/AppConstants.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/moz.build", "tools/@types/subs/AppConstants.sys.d.mts"], "git_node": "d411ccbb5c3df440435fa68341c182bb7bb102a4", "git_parents": ["607ca057c5ac12d887917728b2c5a7a525607c38"], "node": "f47c31f6f64c37765b63cb95154b36fd76901555", "parents": ["7e1aa9e77df90e2cc6bf6b01d07724b609963fab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1977950 - Read `MOZ_ANDROID_CONTENT_SERVICE_ISOLATED_PROCESS` on GeckoRuntime instead of TestRunnerActivity. r=geckoview-reviewers,tcampbell\n\nWhen running WPT's WebDriver tests, it uses config.yaml to pass\nparameters instead of `--es` arguments. But currently,\n`TestRunnerActivity` cannot handle this file.\n\nSo I would like to move reading `MOZ_ANDROID_CONTENT_SERVICE_ISOLATED_PROCESS`\nenvironment variable from `TestRunnerActivity` to `GeckoRuntime` to remove\nduplicated code.\n\nIf this variable is set, GeckoRuntime will start the content process\nin an isolated process even if application doesn't set isolated process\nsetting.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309994\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoThread.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoRuntime.java", "mobile/android/test_runner/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test_runner/TestRunnerActivity.java", "mobile/android/test_runner/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test_runner/XpcshellTestRunnerService.java"], "git_node": "d4abcbed97953eba641278c2b6fc4abcfe630830", "git_parents": ["d411ccbb5c3df440435fa68341c182bb7bb102a4"], "node": "83a41e365f3407ff489668e69aeddd8ec368c3c4", "parents": ["f47c31f6f64c37765b63cb95154b36fd76901555"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074819 - Don't consider speculative loads on link changes when there are no rulesets. r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nIn the spec, when a document has no speculation rule sets, consider speculative\nloads only cancels and discards any existing prefetch records. This\nshould only happen when the last existing rule set is unregistered.\nTherefore, we can avoid considering loads entirely for changes to link\nelements when we have no rulesets registered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330134\n", "files": ["dom/base/SpeculationRules.cpp"], "git_node": "9c6a2d132543860247416060f0a9bc1af49cf556", "git_parents": ["d4abcbed97953eba641278c2b6fc4abcfe630830"], "node": "d8446f44368a69dedcc3ae22af4f7eef65bd872d", "parents": ["83a41e365f3407ff489668e69aeddd8ec368c3c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Max Emig \u003cmozilla@emigm.ax\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1869124 - Streamline Windows event sound playback to avoid shutdown hangs. r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329821\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsSound.cpp", "widget/windows/nsSound.h", "widget/windows/nsdefs.h"], "git_node": "26c8e0658280051ff9782f6166f9597e69a069be", "git_parents": ["9c6a2d132543860247416060f0a9bc1af49cf556"], "node": "8279029a549389a5b6e3a2c3682b11ced7b04aa7", "parents": ["d8446f44368a69dedcc3ae22af4f7eef65bd872d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071379 - Destroy PlatformPipeLink on the IO thread, r=gstoll\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329611\n", "files": ["xpcom/io/AsyncPlatformPipes.cpp"], "git_node": "04c91827ac919da802e599fe402b08c4ba0c4d0b", "git_parents": ["26c8e0658280051ff9782f6166f9597e69a069be"], "node": "04cb3cbb5de37bdb9b281f6f86c82f67f749478f", "parents": ["8279029a549389a5b6e3a2c3682b11ced7b04aa7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074605 - Develop floating edge arrow buttons for New Tab Spaces. r=thecount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328233\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/PageLayoutVariants.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamBase/DiscoveryStreamBase.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Spaces/Spaces.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Spaces/_Spaces.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/common/PageLayoutVariants.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Spaces.test.jsx"], "git_node": "e57a248a86122f4bfa29d79af71d9aa5d8192c25", "git_parents": ["04c91827ac919da802e599fe402b08c4ba0c4d0b"], "node": "8029a11e2105f5427333cf82d148aa84871c0b82", "parents": ["04cb3cbb5de37bdb9b281f6f86c82f67f749478f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jared Wein \u003cjwein@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074692 - Fix TypeScript \"cannot find name\" errors (TS2304) in newtab/lib JSDoc r=places-reviewers,maxx\n\n`{obj}`, `{int}`, `{bool}`, `{str}`, `{func}` and `{Integer}` are not types, and two `@returns` tags named a label instead of a type, so tsc resolved each as an\nundeclared name.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328313\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStreamMessageChannel.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStreamPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/FrecencyBoostProvider/FrecencyBoostProvider.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/HighlightsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/InferredModel/FeatureModel.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/InferredPersonalizationFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/NewTabContentPing.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PlacesFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/SmartShortcutsRanker/RankShortcuts.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/SmartShortcutsRanker/RankShortcutsWorkerClass.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/SmartShortcutsRanker/ThomSample.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TopSitesFeed.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "bc52891e3f13665f028ef92dc06fc9214b59de68", "git_parents": ["e57a248a86122f4bfa29d79af71d9aa5d8192c25"], "node": "a79f0ccd635aeedd997cf48dae17dfbbf5205fd9", "parents": ["8029a11e2105f5427333cf82d148aa84871c0b82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jared Wein \u003cjwein@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074692 - Fix TypeScript errors for JSDoc @param tags naming a parameter the function does not have (TS8024) in newtab/lib r=places-reviewers,maxx\n\nEach `@param` named something the function does not take: a stale or misspelled name, a type with the name omitted, or prose where the name belongs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328314\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStreamMessageChannel.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/InferredModel/FeatureModel.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PlacesFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/RemoteRenderer.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/SmartShortcutsRanker/RankShortcuts.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/SmartShortcutsRanker/RankShortcutsWorkerClass.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/RecentSearchesFeed.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "025c42fd3ac53ec231b5fb76c36a6fed74d01e6a", "git_parents": ["bc52891e3f13665f028ef92dc06fc9214b59de68"], "node": "235d30aa970a4017b76b831a4e991cb7062e22a3", "parents": ["a79f0ccd635aeedd997cf48dae17dfbbf5205fd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jared Wein \u003cjwein@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074692 - Fix TypeScript errors for async functions whose @returns is not a Promise (TS1064) in newtab/lib r=maxx\n\nFifteen async functions documented the type they resolve to rather than the promise they return, so each `@returns` is now wrapped in `Promise\u003c\u003e`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328315\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/FrecencyBoostProvider/FrecencyBoostProvider.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/NewTabContentPing.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PersistentCache.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/SmartShortcutsRanker/RankShortcuts.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/SmartShortcutsRanker/ThomSample.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TopSitesFeed.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "ee626a816fed8b2832ebc7ea8e2bc3e8f75eaded", "git_parents": ["025c42fd3ac53ec231b5fb76c36a6fed74d01e6a"], "node": "0ddf4e0060701cda1398985134fc7033a71563fd", "parents": ["235d30aa970a4017b76b831a4e991cb7062e22a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Max Inden \u003cmail@max-inden.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076802 - Update quinn-udp to 0.6.3 r=leggert,supply-chain-reviewers\n\nhttps://github.com/quinn-rs/quinn/releases/tag/quinn-udp-0.6.3\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329964\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/apple_fast.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/cmsg/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/cmsg/unix.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/cmsg/windows.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/linux.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/unix.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/windows.rs"], "git_node": "2eab300a041be281d48e906e81c37237d4163611", "git_parents": ["ee626a816fed8b2832ebc7ea8e2bc3e8f75eaded"], "node": "feb24d53252f2cc7b15aa3db65b184d1bd6d28d8", "parents": ["0ddf4e0060701cda1398985134fc7033a71563fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076903 - Part 1: Make some Symbol fields const and remove unused method r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330140\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/SymbolType.h"], "git_node": "9d30eac90664006fb14c19e8adec87038aaa6643", "git_parents": ["2eab300a041be281d48e906e81c37237d4163611"], "node": "e6fbe8a00e3ec3a840ed827b437fb29647af5b37", "parents": ["feb24d53252f2cc7b15aa3db65b184d1bd6d28d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076903 - Part 2: Tighten assertions for AtomRefRuntime::recordRefToValue r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330141\n", "files": ["js/public/Zone.h", "js/src/gc/AtomMarking.cpp"], "git_node": "2ce2a824cc02dc98a4d9aff33e9d09e5449e2db9", "git_parents": ["9d30eac90664006fb14c19e8adec87038aaa6643"], "node": "7259b209661083bb879669cce94fc2507b0fb21e", "parents": ["e6fbe8a00e3ec3a840ed827b437fb29647af5b37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076903 - Part 3: Move traceIncomingCrossCompartmentEdgesForZoneGC method to GCRuntime r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\n\nThis is already not specific to compartments as it does debugger tracing and\nwill soon be extended to add zone related tracing too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330142\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Compacting.cpp", "js/src/gc/GCEnum.h", "js/src/gc/GCRuntime.h", "js/src/gc/RootMarking.cpp", "js/src/gc/Sweeping.cpp", "js/src/vm/Compartment.cpp", "js/src/vm/Compartment.h"], "git_node": "bc93ce196f177bb85612978c80fd4f9ee4081188", "git_parents": ["2ce2a824cc02dc98a4d9aff33e9d09e5449e2db9"], "node": "ff0fe0344558f824bfd4848a4890327a38ef0846", "parents": ["7259b209661083bb879669cce94fc2507b0fb21e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075780 - jit/arm64: form an unencodable read-modify-write address once. r=iain\n\nadd32(Imm32, Address), addPtr(Imm32, Address), subPtr(Register, Address)\nand incrementInt32Value load, modify and store through toMemOperand. When\nthe offset has no immediate form, the load and the store each materialize\nit into a scratch register and use a register-offset access, so the\nconstant is built twice:\n\n  mov  x17, #0x6974\n  movk x17, #0x2, lsl #16\n  ldr  w16, [x13, x17]\n  add  w16, w16, #1\n  mov  x17, #0x6974\n  movk x17, #0x2, lsl #16\n  str  w16, [x13, x17]\n\ntoSharedMemOperand forms the address once in the second scratch register,\nas an add of the 4KB-aligned part plus an encodable remainder, or failing\nthat as one materialized offset, and both accesses reuse it:\n\n  add  x17, x13, #0x26, lsl #12\n  ldr  w16, [x17, #0x974]\n  add  w16, w16, #1\n  str  w16, [x17, #0x974]\n\nadd32 and addPtr keep the old path when the added immediate itself has no\nadd/sub form, since Add then needs the second scratch register.\n\nThe main emitter is bumpPointerAllocate, which bumps the zone's catch-all\nAllocSite counter at an offset from the nursery position pointer on every\ninline string and BigInt allocation; the rest are the Baseline for-in index\nincrement at deep frame slots. On a JetStream 3 run with an instrumented\nshell the double-materialized shape appears 3,586 times (Ion 3,457,\nBaseline 83, other stubs 46) and is gone afterwards, with every site in\nthe four-instruction form: about 10,600 fewer instructions, or 42 KB of\nJIT code, per run.\n\nFound with armlint.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WsnsqJvQCmPUe3GWmsM77Q\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329359\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.h"], "git_node": "6ec77b637f07f3e21016a654a64fddc8c62cae08", "git_parents": ["bc93ce196f177bb85612978c80fd4f9ee4081188"], "node": "399e682bee18ad06d9c54f0e7a5c45c80412e57e", "parents": ["ff0fe0344558f824bfd4848a4890327a38ef0846"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iulian moraru \u003cimoraru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2076802 - Update quinn-udp to 0.6.3 r=leggert,supply-chain-reviewers\" for causing build bustages.\n\nThis reverts commit 2eab300a041be281d48e906e81c37237d4163611.\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/apple_fast.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/cmsg/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/cmsg/unix.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/cmsg/windows.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/linux.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/unix.rs", "third_party/rust/quinn-udp/src/windows.rs"], "git_node": "f65c9c9afe278940ced4463015f2b6d3bf95ca97", "git_parents": ["6ec77b637f07f3e21016a654a64fddc8c62cae08"], "node": "f4a7d5a9fc02fba6d331d3f4781634c3d8e27c96", "parents": ["399e682bee18ad06d9c54f0e7a5c45c80412e57e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 44c372fa7ae7e8910d39caaafa229035ecab25d8\naf -\u003e 44c372fa7ae7e8910d39caaafa229035ecab25d8\nan -\u003e 44c372fa7ae7e8910d39caaafa229035ecab25d8\nar -\u003e 44c372fa7ae7e8910d39caaafa229035ecab25d8\nast -\u003