 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nsv-SE -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nta -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nte -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nth -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\ntl -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\ntr -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\ntrs -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nuk -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nur -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nuz -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nvi -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nwo -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nxh -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nzam -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nzh-CN -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\nzh-TW -\u003e 533600beb921c78b58b34f78b5bc4c111ca12dfc\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "3b5631f02cf556f6b4a694dc988b32a9a9c43e60", "git_parents": ["3456f8a0433be2fe209a50c442664c20fc961812"], "node": "deb2667a9b69809dbaa862422325b74a2c9f9c22", "parents": ["243a9cdad0e83e922ad0f3d09504a4fe21b38a2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Smith \u003cbrian@smith.berlin\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077187 - Fix description of 3rdparty policy. r=mkaply DONTBUILD\n\nSomewhere it got lost in translation: admins can set some config via this policy, and extensions can read from it using `storage.managed.get(\"some-config\");`.\n\nSee https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/API/storage/managed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330174\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json"], "git_node": "00718e757d9912662fe551b05b4eb429c47c96ed", "git_parents": ["3b5631f02cf556f6b4a694dc988b32a9a9c43e60"], "node": "72b7933d5d2516562fc2c9091908e820cb39ded9", "parents": ["deb2667a9b69809dbaa862422325b74a2c9f9c22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Smith \u003cbrian@smith.berlin\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074395 - Minor copy fixes for DLP panel. r=gstoll,jmendez,fluent-reviewers,flod\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330121\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/contentanalysis/content/ContentAnalysis.sys.mjs", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl"], "git_node": "65393db90a3996a801a4dc4d8de94e84872a1d0c", "git_parents": ["00718e757d9912662fe551b05b4eb429c47c96ed"], "node": "d0095e1eda3348d11ea4988b2a09de63260d4863", "parents": ["72b7933d5d2516562fc2c9091908e820cb39ded9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074385 - Type the closed tab records in SessionStore.sys.mjs. r=sessionstore-reviewers,sfoster\n\n`#getStateForClosedTabsAndClosedGroupTabs` always returns the whole merged list, and `undoCloseTab`, its only caller that passed an index, indexes into it. Dropping the early break is behavior-neutral: every full-list call already writes the same `_originalStateIndex` values on every entry.\n\nNot behavior-neutral: `formatTabStateForSavedGroup` returns null for a tab without an in-range history entry, and its three callers skip it, where the deferred-restore and migration paths used to save `{}` into the group. It also stops writing `pos`, which has been undefined since bug 1948078 and is never read for saved group tabs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329867\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionMigration.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/TabGroupState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/TabState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/test_format_tab_state_for_saved_group.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/types/sessionstore.ts"], "git_node": "83b6c4e20f3b84fe4e869fbeda7d48bb263feaf7", "git_parents": ["65393db90a3996a801a4dc4d8de94e84872a1d0c"], "node": "d3ad76d6adaef185246fde26850e26a4233b83b7", "parents": ["d0095e1eda3348d11ea4988b2a09de63260d4863"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074386 - Type the window and browser handles in SessionStore.sys.mjs. r=Standard8,sfoster,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nThis is behavior-neutral apart from the four no-op methods on SHistoryListener: nsSHistory calls OnHistoryTruncate, OnDocumentViewerEvicted, OnHistoryCommit and OnEntryUpdated on every listener, and each of those calls used to fail in XPConnect because the JS listener lacked the method.\n\nresetBrowserToLazyState now stores a literal 0 for userTypedClear. Only lazy browsers have that property, and the function returns early for them, so the read always yielded the default. selectTab drops parseInt because the session schema declares selected an integer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329885\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "tools/@types/lib.gecko.augmentations.d.ts", "tools/@types/lib.gecko.tweaks.d.ts", "tools/@types/lib.gecko.xpidl.d.ts"], "git_node": "8bc3d39ec62942afc885172fe00a93a1bfc34b76", "git_parents": ["83b6c4e20f3b84fe4e869fbeda7d48bb263feaf7"], "node": "9bd935bc6e4733c82c8915cfe6f581a5e02c20fb", "parents": ["d3ad76d6adaef185246fde26850e26a4233b83b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074389 - Type the window geometry and chrome flags restore in SessionStore.sys.mjs. r=sfoster,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nBehavior-neutral apart from one case: when the restored state has no `sizemodeBeforeMinimized`, the window's state now leaves it unset instead of storing `\"\"`, which the session schema doesn't allow. Its only reader treats both as falsy.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329900\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c1519404d0d75a45d315f84bcf9788c5b69e1430", "git_parents": ["8bc3d39ec62942afc885172fe00a93a1bfc34b76"], "node": "9cb491fc4c2bce6b30b9ef7482028a4a746727af", "parents": ["9bd935bc6e4733c82c8915cfe6f581a5e02c20fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Fern  ndez Garc  a-Boente \u003cjfernandez@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061233 - Clear the ETP allow-list pref the tracker purge test dirties r=dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nPushing network.cookie.cookieBehavior makes ContentBlockingPrefs rewrite\nbrowser.contentblocking.category, and UrlClassifierExceptionListService\nanswers that by setting\nprivacy.trackingprotection.allow_list.hasUserInteractedWithETPSettings as a\nuser pref. pushPrefEnv pops only what the test itself pushed, so that one\noutlived the file and browser-chrome reported it as a changed preference\nwhenever another test file ran first.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328866\n", "files": ["dom/serviceworkers/test/browser_purgeTrackers_serviceWorkers.js"], "git_node": "909d02e93ab815380deea5200543308f48d46609", "git_parents": ["c1519404d0d75a45d315f84bcf9788c5b69e1430"], "node": "26c3ac0f4b848c0a4f27cc8a35dc27af88bff7f8", "parents": ["9cb491fc4c2bce6b30b9ef7482028a4a746727af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067617 - Enable inputConnection_selectionByArrowKey again. r=geckoview-reviewers,owlish\n\nI added another fix to wait keyboard events by bug 2072582. So we should\nturn on this test again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329109\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/TextInputDelegateTest.kt"], "git_node": "6de0adfa0180dba558d653a54fbeeab0e47c3084", "git_parents": ["909d02e93ab815380deea5200543308f48d46609"], "node": "153adcc10507ba42b5a2c042a51d3f61c2f182ed", "parents": ["26c3ac0f4b848c0a4f27cc8a35dc27af88bff7f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Exploding-Joysticks \u003cExplodingJoysticks@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1831048 - Part 1: Fix 64 'misc-unused-parameters' warnings in directories that have the fewest amount of them r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,layout-reviewers,ahochheiden,dshin,nchevobbe,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329450\n", "files": ["caps/BasePrincipal.cpp", "config/external/rlbox_wasm2c_sandbox/rlbox_wasm2c_thread_locals.cpp", "devtools/shared/heapsnapshot/FileDescriptorOutputStream.cpp", "layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp", "memory/build/test/TestMozJemallocUtils.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/tests/gtest/CoseTest.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/tests/gtest/NSSBenchTest.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/tlsserver/cmd/BadCertAndPinningServer.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/tlsserver/cmd/DelegatedCredentialsServer.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/tlsserver/cmd/EncryptedClientHelloServer.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/tlsserver/cmd/FaultyServer.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/tlsserver/cmd/OCSPStaplingServer.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/tlsserver/cmd/SanctionsTestServer.cpp", "storage/mozStorageConnection.cpp", "storage/mozStorageConnection.h", "testing/gtest/mozilla/GTestRunner.cpp", "testing/mochitest/ssltunnel/ssltunnel.cpp", "testing/tools/screenshot/gdk-screenshot.cpp", "uriloader/exthandler/unix/nsOSHelperAppService.cpp"], "git_node": "6492076ca3150a7f4d5425a0e162759d020744d9", "git_parents": ["6de0adfa0180dba558d653a54fbeeab0e47c3084"], "node": "caf73130f8cf6a8c29c56dbc78e36d1e7c1a7854", "parents": ["153adcc10507ba42b5a2c042a51d3f61c2f182ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069846 - part 1 - Show the extensions menu item in browser screen's menu r=android-reviewers,android-addons-reviewers,matt-tighe,robwu\n\nThis allows the user to install, see installed and manage extensions.\nShowing installed extensions page & browser actions are to happen in a separate\ncommit as the changes are bigger.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325052\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/MenuItemIcon.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/MenuListItemCommon.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/ExtensionsMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuSectionConfiguration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuTelemetryMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/store/MenuAction.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/store/MenuStore.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/navigation/nav_graph.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/ExtensionsMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/config/detekt-baseline.xml"], "git_node": "c4e6bbefe4d18f673e815a45a2abcaed5c250880", "git_parents": ["6492076ca3150a7f4d5425a0e162759d020744d9"], "node": "13a5231ea002d1289ca7306532c417c770916404", "parents": ["caf73130f8cf6a8c29c56dbc78e36d1e7c1a7854"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069846 - part 2 - Show installed extensions actions in the menu r=android-reviewers,android-addons-reviewers,matt-tighe,robwu\n\nWebExtensionMenuActions.kt is now the one place that maps BrowserState to what actions do installed\nextensions offer for the current tab:\n- WebExtensionMenuAction - allows passing all details inside menu items and events.\n- Flow\u003cBrowserState\u003e.webExtensionMenuActions combines the browser-level and tab-level flows to get\nwhat extensions actions are available for the current tab. Icons are only loaded when the\nextensions or their tab state actually change.\n- BrowserState.findWebExtensionMenuAction resolves the same action again at click time.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325923\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/ExtensionsMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/WebExtensionMenuAction.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/WebExtensionsMenuBinding.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuTelemetryMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/store/MenuAction.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/store/MenuStore.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/ExtensionsMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "379390674d8f6ec49926171547e4c74e3d9ca235", "git_parents": ["c4e6bbefe4d18f673e815a45a2abcaed5c250880"], "node": "fcccf0097201aae2af1896d2779dc026813dcd05", "parents": ["13a5231ea002d1289ca7306532c417c770916404"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069866 - Show the FXA account menu item in browser screen's menu r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327850\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/data/MenuItem.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/MenuListItemCommon.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/accounts/MozillaAccountMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuSectionConfiguration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/accounts/MozillaAccountMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "4842e16865970719209516db3db6c80d51df6ff2", "git_parents": ["379390674d8f6ec49926171547e4c74e3d9ca235"], "node": "d736c4728b5ade029848e956c00541729c69a3f3", "parents": ["fcccf0097201aae2af1896d2779dc026813dcd05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069867 - Show the settings menu item in browser screen's menu r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327863\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuSectionConfiguration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SettingsMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SettingsMenuItemProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "2887cac8c21a2750c4bcf22dcdfec2214db201a0", "git_parents": ["4842e16865970719209516db3db6c80d51df6ff2"], "node": "495c341443ed5af579d2f897fdc76f170d5d19fc", "parents": ["d736c4728b5ade029848e956c00541729c69a3f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069868 - Show the \"Delete browsing data and quit\" menu item in browser screen's menu r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327864\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/BrowserMenuBuilder.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuSectionConfiguration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/deletebrowsingdata/QuitMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/deletebrowsingdata/QuitMenuItemProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "4bc4faa61e2b3fed36a420e98a675534ed9bf11d", "git_parents": ["2887cac8c21a2750c4bcf22dcdfec2214db201a0"], "node": "59d1849517dd59e813ad102c1e31e05aafe8003e", "parents": ["495c341443ed5af579d2f897fdc76f170d5d19fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2077401 - Remove DCLayerTree::WebRenderOsCompositorKind r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" for causing merge conflicts.\n\nThis reverts commit 38ec93c1dadf76d83e457de0005bfc010de4497d.\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorANGLE.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorANGLE.h"], "git_node": "8003a2271129ff002e694b3814539173084cf995", "git_parents": ["4bc4faa61e2b3fed36a420e98a675534ed9bf11d"], "node": "8f00f8ddda64fbd1317415d30cc1fb9817604ac4", "parents": ["59d1849517dd59e813ad102c1e31e05aafe8003e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "872b70d1ea3abd312c5a938f7f4eee26f5eae063", "git_parents": ["8003a2271129ff002e694b3814539173084cf995", "26a129b91bc2428191eb5b9dbaaab803601fa414"], "node": "8478e49aebc4e1ab9c5f6ece4fd5e71c36a9018e", "parents": ["8f00f8ddda64fbd1317415d30cc1fb9817604ac4", "6ce79a0416258aa1bc3a29e9ccebccdacebf916a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mcarare \u003c48995920+mcarare@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077409 - Use newPrivateTabSearch in IntentProcessor to ensure intent searches open in a private tab. r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330318\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/session/IntentProcessor.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/focus/session/IntentProcessorTest.kt"], "git_node": "339ee6cefe7b09922d5dee6731a23c078894aa08", "git_parents": ["872b70d1ea3abd312c5a938f7f4eee26f5eae063"], "node": "aa8d363467045f9e62dede78005dece712f06b4f", "parents": ["8478e49aebc4e1ab9c5f6ece4fd5e71c36a9018e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1956139 - Switch back to upstream windows-link. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,supply-chain-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nNow that we switched to the windows-gnullvm targets for rust, we can remove the\nworkaround we had for the windows-gnu targets.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330233\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "build/rust/windows-link/Cargo.toml", "build/rust/windows-link/lib.rs", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/windows-link/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/windows-link/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/windows-link/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/windows-link/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/windows-link/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/windows-link/license-apache-2.0", "third_party/rust/windows-link/license-mit", "third_party/rust/windows-link/readme.md", "third_party/rust/windows-link/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "a59e1f66e1237262916b476d4434938a01cb21af", "git_parents": ["339ee6cefe7b09922d5dee6731a23c078894aa08"], "node": "17a7e753d8197ed44a78cb07ad606fb9485a659d", "parents": ["aa8d363467045f9e62dede78005dece712f06b4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1956139 - Remove raw-dylib related workarounds. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330234\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/http3server/src/main.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/client/app/src/main.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/client/app/src/memory_test.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/client/app/src/ui/windows/mod.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper/moz.build", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/appinfo/windows.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/minidump-analyzer/src/windows/mod.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/mozwer-rust/moz.build", "toolkit/library/moz.build", "toolkit/mozapps/pushnotificationhelper/src/lifecycle.rs", "toolkit/mozapps/pushnotificationhelper/src/pushconnection.rs"], "git_node": "eca6e79121e86ad37be98064bc67b1cf577c99fe", "git_parents": ["a59e1f66e1237262916b476d4434938a01cb21af"], "node": "dd703d3abbc098a807234f78786b85512e528b88", "parents": ["17a7e753d8197ed44a78cb07ad606fb9485a659d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Farre \u003csfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076142 - Remove now invalid WPT assertions from the history interface r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nThe language \"remove any tasks queued by the history traversal task source\" seems to have existed in the spec at one point; the same language was found in Gecko but is removed by 2067178.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329584\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/001.html"], "git_node": "e2b3074ae22d0415f4a84c234e3a272575af9c96", "git_parents": ["eca6e79121e86ad37be98064bc67b1cf577c99fe"], "node": "c27032a57e6fee053ef953bd443ed9fa023c6747", "parents": ["dd703d3abbc098a807234f78786b85512e528b88"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790958524, "git_changesets": ["761d0888115ab8ffb191cfc1be5be35923a1e31e", "b69193462d11e1f7ce216098478564356fe549c4", "38ec93c1dadf76d83e457de0005bfc010de4497d", "3456f8a0433be2fe209a50c442664c20fc961812", "3b5631f02cf556f6b4a694dc988b32a9a9c43e60", "00718e757d9912662fe551b05b4eb429c47c96ed", "65393db90a3996a801a4dc4d8de94e84872a1d0c", "83b6c4e20f3b84fe4e869fbeda7d48bb263feaf7", "8bc3d39ec62942afc885172fe00a93a1bfc34b76", "c1519404d0d75a45d315f84bcf9788c5b69e1430", "909d02e93ab815380deea5200543308f48d46609", "6de0adfa0180dba558d653a54fbeeab0e47c3084", "6492076ca3150a7f4d5425a0e162759d020744d9", "c4e6bbefe4d18f673e815a45a2abcaed5c250880", "379390674d8f6ec49926171547e4c74e3d9ca235", "4842e16865970719209516db3db6c80d51df6ff2", "2887cac8c21a2750c4bcf22dcdfec2214db201a0", "4bc4faa61e2b3fed36a420e98a675534ed9bf11d", "8003a2271129ff002e694b3814539173084cf995", "872b70d1ea3abd312c5a938f7f4eee26f5eae063", "339ee6cefe7b09922d5dee6731a23c078894aa08", "a59e1f66e1237262916b476d4434938a01cb21af", "eca6e79121e86ad37be98064bc67b1cf577c99fe", "e2b3074ae22d0415f4a84c234e3a272575af9c96"], "user": "abutkovits@mozilla.com"}, "45474": {"changesets": [{"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Automatic newtab version bump NO BUG a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/manifest.json"], "git_node": "4578f07ce13c6db83454d7bd2b7583fe3d132bc0", "git_parents": ["e2b3074ae22d0415f4a84c234e3a272575af9c96"], "node": "0e3763914a7e7fed00fc85cc95036f3e934fac46", "parents": ["c27032a57e6fee053ef953bd443ed9fa023c6747"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790959637, "git_changesets": ["4578f07ce13c6db83454d7bd2b7583fe3d132bc0"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45475": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740752 - Part 1: Refactor nursery active chunk range r=jonco\n\nWe can't just start allocating in any chunk; we can either start from\nthe beginning, after evicting a space or when switching spaces, or we\ncan continue with the next chunk.\n\n- Refactor to better name the range of chunks used for allocation since\n  the last collection.  Allow a space to have *no* active chunks; this is\n  the case in the promote-only nursery configuration.\n\n- Add a Space::chunk accessor that ensures the chunk is in the active\n  range.\n\n- Don't bother ensuring that fromspace has an current chunk.\n\n- Don't eagerly flip the gckind of a space's allocated but inactive\n  pages; lazily flip them just before allocation.\n\n- Simplify poisoning under generational GC zeal.\n\n- Simplify nursery growth/shrinkage under generational GC zeal.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325424\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.h"], "git_node": "ac56ac22ebf9e291a7b62f217359c762a53c7936", "git_parents": ["e2b3074ae22d0415f4a84c234e3a272575af9c96"], "node": "1727661e3f0b77711ec4dcd688e410c8988706ed", "parents": ["c27032a57e6fee053ef953bd443ed9fa023c6747"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740752 - Part 2: Implement contiguous nursery mode r=jonco\n\nShould speed up chunk acquisition / release and isInside checks.\nEnabled if -DJS_CONTIGUOUS_NURSERY.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325425\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery-inl.h", "js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.h", "js/src/gc/Scheduling.cpp"], "git_node": "09ca6665a70ed65dc22cdc9a93284ae7634616d6", "git_parents": ["ac56ac22ebf9e291a7b62f217359c762a53c7936"], "node": "43735fc8e2683d390be24c6addbadf98376f7bff", "parents": ["1727661e3f0b77711ec4dcd688e410c8988706ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740752 - Part 3: Use contiguous nursery on 64-bit platforms r=jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325427\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery.h"], "git_node": "7ec494fe5caf6a01d1b8b1ff9d771d8cc9d55170", "git_parents": ["09ca6665a70ed65dc22cdc9a93284ae7634616d6"], "node": "b532e961880595aa7812a8b441c2ed4e8b863596", "parents": ["43735fc8e2683d390be24c6addbadf98376f7bff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Farre \u003csfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067647 - Show correct origin for pointerlock warning r=smaug\n\nLike previous changes for Fullscreen warning, the pointer lock warning must also use the top-most origin.\n\nThis patch also removes the use of the deprecated .fullscreen attribute in one place.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329581\n", "files": ["browser/actors/PointerLockParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "db70a958f3f383e4ffcb00209c01857511e88fce", "git_parents": ["7ec494fe5caf6a01d1b8b1ff9d771d8cc9d55170"], "node": "71599d873ff10f85d544778cd9810925c8114f15", "parents": ["b532e961880595aa7812a8b441c2ed4e8b863596"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070879 - Wait for frame construction before considering document speculation rules. r=smaug,dom-core-reviewers\n\nDocument rules can only match against links which are being rendered,\nand we cannot determine this until after their frames have been constructed.\nSo if frames still need to be contructed, delay consider loads until\nafter the next refresh.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330247\n", "files": ["dom/base/SpeculationRuleSet.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRuleSet.h", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.h", "dom/base/speculationrules/lib.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/document-rules.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/inline-speculation-rules-after-stylesheet.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "d0a922ca450b82ed9648079d48c2267a2a7ed734", "git_parents": ["db70a958f3f383e4ffcb00209c01857511e88fce"], "node": "2eaa5c818806cec07f551da03d8cde5b614fb2dd", "parents": ["71599d873ff10f85d544778cd9810925c8114f15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Katherine Ye \u003ckye@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044192 - Remove image.natural-size-fallback.enabled. r=dholbert\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326311\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsImageLoadingContent.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "3425aadd3da99f7876cd4f5d8be186dd813d9dde", "git_parents": ["d0a922ca450b82ed9648079d48c2267a2a7ed734"], "node": "40894a27efe8b647f1d5527076d94a77bf01e473", "parents": ["2eaa5c818806cec07f551da03d8cde5b614fb2dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Katherine Ye \u003ckye@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033633 - Skip density correction for fallback intrinsic height. r=dholbert\n\nTrack whether the natural height came from the fallback concrete object size and skip Y-axis density correction in that case. Remove the WPT failure annotations fixed by the change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326312\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsImageLoadingContent.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/naturalWidth-naturalHeight-width-height.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/svg-img-density-vs-zoom.html.ini"], "git_node": "4840fdcfe70b2d98b826b7bbe94ed7c8c0dfb601", "git_parents": ["3425aadd3da99f7876cd4f5d8be186dd813d9dde"], "node": "8c2312f2b515d6b4c95aaa908192d84c6538b47a", "parents": ["40894a27efe8b647f1d5527076d94a77bf01e473"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052914 part 1: Simplify our code that tracks whether an image's height came from fallback size. r=kye\n\nNo behavioral changes; just iterating on bug 2033633's added code to condense\nit a bit, so that this doesn't end up too verbose after the next patch in this\nseries (which will effectively duplicate that code to perform the same checks\nfor an image's width).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328613\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsImageLoadingContent.cpp"], "git_node": "dbd8236b315729a7c3569d3aacd4a98a64d24c36", "git_parents": ["4840fdcfe70b2d98b826b7bbe94ed7c8c0dfb601"], "node": "67fb4c4fc80968370005ee1ab545019d5b71125f", "parents": ["8c2312f2b515d6b4c95aaa908192d84c6538b47a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052914 part 2: Skip density correction for images' fallback intrinsic height (and update documentation). r=kye\n\nThis is just a logical extension of bug 2033633, to apply to the JS APIs for\nreading image width (as well as height which we fixed up in bug 2033633).\n\nFor *both* dimensions, we need to track whether we're using the fallback size;\nand if we are, we need to **decline to scale it by the image density** (because\nthe fallback dimensions are just there to give the image a reasonable size -\nthey're not a real measure of pixels inside the image that need to scale with\nimage density).\n\nI'm also updating the accompanying documentation to refer to the spec instead\nof describing what we do as a non-standard web-compatibility hack, since the\nspec has now been updated to more-directly call for the behavior that we\nimplement.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328614\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsImageLoadingContent.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/naturalWidth-naturalHeight-width-height.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/svg-img-density-vs-zoom.html.ini"], "git_node": "c3b0688af50aa83e7f691750375af122d95e2666", "git_parents": ["dbd8236b315729a7c3569d3aacd4a98a64d24c36"], "node": "1d4a0afc9e8b01219d2e4aa711adeb2907651c1e", "parents": ["67fb4c4fc80968370005ee1ab545019d5b71125f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052914 part 3: Density-correct image width/height attributes' return values, regardless of whether image is rendered. r=kye\n\nBefore this patch, we *did not* density-correct in this case, because other\nbrowsers did not.  But recently, the HTML spec changed to require\ndensity-correction, and we're not anticipating any webcompat trouble from that\nchange.  This patch implements that change.\n\nI'm updating the nearby comments to reference the (newly-added) spec text.\n(Previously the comments were documenting our at-the-time\nnonnstandard-but-interoperable behavior.)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328615\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsImageLoadingContent.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/naturalWidth-naturalHeight-width-height.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/width-height-attribute-parsing.html.ini"], "git_node": "b6c152c0f6f6af7cae5ebfecac0c5c9df73deecd", "git_parents": ["c3b0688af50aa83e7f691750375af122d95e2666"], "node": "48e001eb0475839bf43dd54441ec6b0d765e8c00", "parents": ["1d4a0afc9e8b01219d2e4aa711adeb2907651c1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077416 - Document how to test the address bar over the message path. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330322\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/docs/testing.md"], "git_node": "c8196439b953afc504d69666ff33bfe4b6cee717", "git_parents": ["b6c152c0f6f6af7cae5ebfecac0c5c9df73deecd"], "node": "3ff477a89fd7df2730142863643ea38a906b5992", "parents": ["48e001eb0475839bf43dd54441ec6b0d765e8c00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077390 - Be a bit more conservative about whether directories are readable. r=edgar\n\nI think this is the smallest change we can make really. I _think_\non windows we don't do this weird stuff...\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330352\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/FilePickerParent.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsFilePicker.cpp", "widget/nsBaseFilePicker.cpp", "widget/nsBaseFilePicker.h"], "git_node": "f7b4bd0e24a82e18fa1befd0970ac8130e0fbb09", "git_parents": ["c8196439b953afc504d69666ff33bfe4b6cee717"], "node": "aa45f4902fe4b68caab6b517ad76173ae70549e8", "parents": ["3ff477a89fd7df2730142863643ea38a906b5992"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077438 - Document how to write address bar code that works over the message path. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330326\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/docs/index.md", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/message-path.md", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/utilities.md"], "git_node": "293687f7509477c5de9c3521c4d0e21f943ce280", "git_parents": ["f7b4bd0e24a82e18fa1befd0970ac8130e0fbb09"], "node": "99317349fe392fa3e284f04c97304ecea8a970e3", "parents": ["aa45f4902fe4b68caab6b517ad76173ae70549e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077445 - Retitle the address bar docs to cover the search bars. r=mbeier,urlbar-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330351\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/docs/index.md", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/lifetime.md", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/message-path.md", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/overview.md", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/testing.md", "browser/docs/overview.md"], "git_node": "313b55efd8519232aac7c2d17ddae445a0e3d8b3", "git_parents": ["293687f7509477c5de9c3521c4d0e21f943ce280"], "node": "52a0aa722928369853bc93d0cb88e510141bcbc5", "parents": ["99317349fe392fa3e284f04c97304ecea8a970e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2067647 - Show correct origin for pointerlock warning r=smaug\" for causing failures at browser_pointerlock_warning.js.\n\nThis reverts commit db70a958f3f383e4ffcb00209c01857511e88fce.\n", "files": ["browser/actors/PointerLockParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "445fdc60697312fe3cd263a0dd0bc41065af8963", "git_parents": ["313b55efd8519232aac7c2d17ddae445a0e3d8b3"], "node": "50777ca22bf9de37d067fd26c9b73b7d9e6fad28", "parents": ["52a0aa722928369853bc93d0cb88e510141bcbc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077285 - Update PDF.js to c33c32aed46637ec6010e9f6c031c72e1c529d31 r=pdfjs-reviewers,calixte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330253\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsVersion.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/wasm/openjpeg.wasm", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/wasm/openjpeg_nowasm_fallback.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "1a98ffcf76e39e32ed08b92cd9de58da3640f744", "git_parents": ["445fdc60697312fe3cd263a0dd0bc41065af8963"], "node": "e521cb67ad5e5e555cd57742f9c3c046ef5dfe79", "parents": ["50777ca22bf9de37d067fd26c9b73b7d9e6fad28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075788 - jit/arm64: build the regexp SIMD table-scan match mask with SHRN. r=iain\n\nEmitSkipUntilBitInTableSimd turns each 16-byte CMEQ result into a scalar\nmask with the wasm bitmaskInt8x16, which on arm64 emulates x86 PMOVMSKB:\nit rematerializes a constant (mov/movk x4, dup), then runs sshr, and, ext,\nzip1, addv and umov, all inside the scan loop:\n\n  mov  x16, #0x201\n  movk x16, #0x804, lsl #16\n  movk x16, #0x2010, lsl #32\n  movk x16, #0x8040, lsl #48\n  dup  v5.2d, x16\n  sshr v31.16b, v4.16b, #7\n  and  v31.16b, v31.16b, v5.16b\n  ext  v5.16b, v31.16b, v31.16b, #8\n  zip1 v5.16b, v31.16b, v5.16b\n  addv h5, v5.8h\n  umov w5, v5.h[0]\n  cbz  w5, \u003cnext chunk\u003e\n\nThe scan only needs to know whether any byte matched and where the first\none is, so a nibble mask does: SHRN narrows each 16-bit pair of all-zeros\nor all-ones lanes to one byte holding four bits per lane, and FMOV moves\nthe 64-bit result to a general register. The match index is the trailing\nzero count divided by four:\n\n  shrn v5.8b, v4.8h, #4\n  fmov x5, d5\n  cbz  x5, \u003cnext chunk\u003e\n  rbit x4, x5\n  clz  x4, x4\n  lsr  x4, x4, #2\n\nThis takes the per-chunk mask from eleven instructions to two. On an\nApple M4 Max, a regexp that reaches the vectorized scan (such as\n/[aeiqwx]/ or /[aeiqwx]\\d{5}/) runs a 1MB Latin-1 search 1.6-1.7x\nfaster, a 64-byte one 1.16x faster, and one with a candidate every 17\nbytes 1.25x faster. x86 keeps PMOVMSKB.\n\nThe new jit-test puts the first match at every lane of several chunks,\nbehind near-miss candidates in the same chunk.\n\nFound with armlint.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WsnsqJvQCmPUe3GWmsM77Q\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329367\n", "files": ["js/src/irregexp/RegExpNativeMacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/regexp/skip-until-bit-in-table-simd.js", "js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.h"], "git_node": "902c9cc537d6e9cc952095dcab68afe49bfd47a4", "git_parents": ["1a98ffcf76e39e32ed08b92cd9de58da3640f744"], "node": "5b960de84e10417ac35e329d3936abf01d347f44", "parents": ["e521cb67ad5e5e555cd57742f9c3c046ef5dfe79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077390 - Fix -Wunreachable-code on macOS\n", "files": ["widget/nsBaseFilePicker.cpp"], "git_node": "c2d14bab92667d9d83fd5a6a487e7b61a2d5012c", "git_parents": ["902c9cc537d6e9cc952095dcab68afe49bfd47a4"], "node": "f0cf5f26f22bd4feecc14fedbabcaf5941e0a5d6", "parents": ["5b960de84e10417ac35e329d3936abf01d347f44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Hynson \u003cmhynson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061871 - Add scrollbar inset for browser content area. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton,akulyk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317586\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css"], "git_node": "f478f12551f1fc4baa145667e0a6bfdc9a87cea6", "git_parents": ["c2d14bab92667d9d83fd5a6a487e7b61a2d5012c"], "node": "fc915a935915c85c3f737c7e454cfa19f0aa3160", "parents": ["f0cf5f26f22bd4feecc14fedbabcaf5941e0a5d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1740752 - Part 3: Use contiguous nursery on 64-bit platforms r=jonco\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 7ec494fe5caf6a01d1b8b1ff9d771d8cc9d55170.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1740752 - Part 2: Implement contiguous nursery mode r=jonco\"\n\nThis reverts commit 09ca6665a70ed65dc22cdc9a93284ae7634616d6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1740752 - Part 1: Refactor nursery active chunk range r=jonco\"\n\nThis reverts commit ac56ac22ebf9e291a7b62f217359c762a53c7936.\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery-inl.h", "js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.h", "js/src/gc/Scheduling.cpp"], "git_node": "37f45facca6278123bdbfc30acbd24eff1fb16fb", "git_parents": ["f478f12551f1fc4baa145667e0a6bfdc9a87cea6"], "node": "81af7fd2296455d913d2092d01b38d9569227975", "parents": ["fc915a935915c85c3f737c7e454cfa19f0aa3160"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071313 - Enable BTP purge telemetry on android. r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325596\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingProtection.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/pings.yaml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/xpcshell/test_bouncetracking_purge_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "ec8c2a35dbe5ca9d2488afd4823dabd1e6c6047e", "git_parents": ["37f45facca6278123bdbfc30acbd24eff1fb16fb"], "node": "30d9ea4621acf27b9700cd2aed077094511840bd", "parents": ["81af7fd2296455d913d2092d01b38d9569227975"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071974 - Implement window.pushManager for Declarative Web Push. r=saschanaz,webidl,tschuster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328914\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/bindings/Bindings.conf", "dom/push/PushManager.cpp", "dom/push/PushManager.h", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerRegistration.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUnregisterJob.cpp", "dom/webidl/PushManager.webidl", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/notifications/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js"], "git_node": "6caa7f8c3706d2892aca0b78841f34c3bd9d3025", "git_parents": ["ec8c2a35dbe5ca9d2488afd4823dabd1e6c6047e"], "node": "abb508cdf98bb1eb48a3e6bf9aba5750d663d581", "parents": ["30d9ea4621acf27b9700cd2aed077094511840bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2070879 - Wait for frame construction before considering document speculation rules. r=smaug,dom-core-reviewers\" for causing wpt failures\n\nThis reverts commit d0a922ca450b82ed9648079d48c2267a2a7ed734.\n", "files": ["dom/base/SpeculationRuleSet.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRuleSet.h", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.h", "dom/base/speculationrules/lib.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/document-rules.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/inline-speculation-rules-after-stylesheet.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "1f1aaf46365e934860556b4b6144ed2fed704d9e", "git_parents": ["6caa7f8c3706d2892aca0b78841f34c3bd9d3025"], "node": "f723b71f4d114ebd4770ce714859b04904893008", "parents": ["abb508cdf98bb1eb48a3e6bf9aba5750d663d581"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077193 - Resolve IsWindowArranged at runtime in nsWindow::OnWindowPosChanged. r=emilio\n\nIsWindowArranged requires Windows 10 1903, and is also missing from Wine\nbefore 10.8 and from VxKex on Windows 7. Calling it through the user32.dll\ndelay-load import crashes there, so treat a missing export as not tiled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330286\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "55aafe5617cf9b9dd34e880d52e1a6f63aa93ec0", "git_parents": ["1f1aaf46365e934860556b4b6144ed2fed704d9e"], "node": "25fce0b8839ae88867beb1c64cb73c96f4774903", "parents": ["f723b71f4d114ebd4770ce714859b04904893008"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077268 - Have spaces arrow buttons variant background panel occupy full page height. r=maxx\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330243\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/Base.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Spaces/_Spaces.scss"], "git_node": "91b7c082495fd66382e0e3d437fa97b27390cf47", "git_parents": ["55aafe5617cf9b9dd34e880d52e1a6f63aa93ec0"], "node": "d393f7255dbf290f8adb8b41dce6deb435285e07", "parents": ["25fce0b8839ae88867beb1c64cb73c96f4774903"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077175 - Add JavaScript Review Skill + Review Context hook r=ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330153\n", "files": [".agents/skills/js-review/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/js-review/SKILL.md", "review-context.toml"], "git_node": "b0b5197fc6a0f8d65bbc3cfdcedf7df9821c750f", "git_parents": ["91b7c082495fd66382e0e3d437fa97b27390cf47"], "node": "42bc296a44b858ce06fae82e83320403640d426b", "parents": ["d393f7255dbf290f8adb8b41dce6deb435285e07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the rlbox and soundtouch compile edges from `recurse.mk` to objdir `LOCAL_INCLUDES` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nObjects now wait for the `pre-compile` step of each directory whose objdir they\ninclude. `layout/build` and `media/libsoundtouch/src` now also wait for\n`security/rlbox`, and `netwerk/build` for `netwerk/dns`. Each includes that\nobjdir and had no edge.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329011\n", "files": ["config/recurse.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/common.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/objdir-local-includes/consumer/consumer.c", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/objdir-local-includes/consumer/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/objdir-local-includes/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/objdir-local-includes/producer/generate.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/objdir-local-includes/producer/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/objdir-local-includes/srcdir-only/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/objdir-local-includes/srcdir-only/srcdir-only.c", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py"], "git_node": "687b4552906e4b3d07e4422196ec2a978ddc32bd", "git_parents": ["b0b5197fc6a0f8d65bbc3cfdcedf7df9821c750f"], "node": "a6a3c3345c442a15458e5893b66e32deb734b736", "parents": ["42bc296a44b858ce06fae82e83320403640d426b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077536: stop running cppunit on macOS 10.15/Catalina r=aryx\n\nWe already run these on Sonoma and Sequoia, which gives us Intel and aarch64 coverage respectively. It seems doubtful that we're getting a lot of value from also running them on an older macOS Intel platform.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330374\n", "files": ["taskcluster/test_configs/test-sets.yml"], "git_node": "49b8e3e7c5a4098c20dbd086c5ebbf666c2ce0e1", "git_parents": ["687b4552906e4b3d07e4422196ec2a978ddc32bd"], "node": "f8e34060f7298028fed226f94aa32b4a228432ca", "parents": ["a6a3c3345c442a15458e5893b66e32deb734b736"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075370 - Make EventUtils drag helpers fail clearly when the drag service is suppressed, r=edgar.\n\nStartDragSessionForTests now throws NS_ERROR_NOT_AVAILABLE while dragging is suppressed instead of creating a session that GetCurrentSession hides, which synthesizeDrop could not end and which reappeared once the suppression was lifted. EventUtils.startDragSession turns that into an error naming the likely cause.\n\nDepends on D329186\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329187\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/EventUtils.js", "testing/mochitest/tests/browser/browser.toml", "testing/mochitest/tests/browser/browser_EventUtils_drag_suppressed.js", "widget/nsBaseDragService.cpp", "widget/nsIDragService.idl"], "git_node": "8b0aa3525257ad862f6f6c88c1d48e8c774f96c7", "git_parents": ["49b8e3e7c5a4098c20dbd086c5ebbf666c2ce0e1"], "node": "f699cc99e1b69ecae8b8187615f2c4d797bf37a4", "parents": ["f8e34060f7298028fed226f94aa32b4a228432ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yulia Startsev \u003cyulia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067720 - Port CopyDataProperties and CopyDataPropertiesUnfiltered to C++. r=jandem\n\nThis patch was initially written by claude, it moves CopyDataProperties and\nCopyDataPropertiesUnfiltered from selfhosted code to two C++\nintrinsics of the same name. As far as my review goes, this looks like a\npretty clean translation. I cross checked the implementation with the\nspec and similar implementations.\n\nPerformance wise there isn't a huge win from this. The slow path is a\nlittle faster, but the fast path is about the same, see the table in\ncomment https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2067720#c3.\n\nThe reason for the flat line is that the self-hosted code was inlined,\nand was already pretty fast. However this is still a nice cleanup and\nworth landing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323669\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Object.cpp", "js/src/builtin/Object.h", "js/src/builtin/Utilities.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/object-spread-slow-path.js", "js/src/vm/SelfHosting.cpp"], "git_node": "5757fe7a1b156da48cae7e49ffa7ed1618a83db4", "git_parents": ["8b0aa3525257ad862f6f6c88c1d48e8c774f96c7"], "node": "fc74756f0ed4024b76595e99a07de7e68e14010f", "parents": ["f699cc99e1b69ecae8b8187615f2c4d797bf37a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yulia Startsev \u003cyulia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067720 - Remove the intrinsics that are now unused. r=jandem\n\nThis was directly authored by claude, but it is just a straightforward\ndeletion. CopyDataPropertiesOrGetOwnKeys existed only to serve the self-hosted\nCopyDataProperties, and std_Object_propertyIsEnumerable only to serve its slow\npath. Both lost their last caller in the previous patch.\n\nobj_propertyIsEnumerable itself stays: it is still\nObject.prototype.propertyIsEnumerable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323765\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/SelfHosting.cpp"], "git_node": "299fb3ea75badb1364269960e51693f152a585ab", "git_parents": ["5757fe7a1b156da48cae7e49ffa7ed1618a83db4"], "node": "d687730e8fc54b84b36b82bafa9325a53463d5c2", "parents": ["fc74756f0ed4024b76595e99a07de7e68e14010f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076675 - Don't reset image sizes=auto width when image is moved with moveBefore. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330380\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLImageElement.cpp"], "git_node": "0516bf56189ef9264d87a57ed8d468b0ddb16f34", "git_parents": ["299fb3ea75badb1364269960e51693f152a585ab"], "node": "6c6b6aee58cf6ba730bc1639d22629f44fc7888f", "parents": ["d687730e8fc54b84b36b82bafa9325a53463d5c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1524251 - [Pointer Event] pointermove will only be detected for one finger with multiple touches when preventDefault is used, r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330349\n", "files": ["dom/events/PointerEventHandler.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/pointerevent_multi_touch_pointerdown_prevented.html"], "git_node": "fa1277c79cf842c5e9bcfed0d5f0dc1eb1c3e801", "git_parents": ["0516bf56189ef9264d87a57ed8d468b0ddb16f34"], "node": "35e398abc7e36a0d42947ef48cf53d667843211b", "parents": ["6c6b6aee58cf6ba730bc1639d22629f44fc7888f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dustin Whisman \u003cdwhisman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052926 - Make urlbarview CSS variable names use consistent case r=urlbar-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,hjones\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327481\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/themes/shared/smartbar.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/dynamic-results.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/variables.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css", "tools/lint/stylelint/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/config.mjs"], "git_node": "fad6d3f049273fc9c66b9bd1e97a393b7da59e2c", "git_parents": ["fa1277c79cf842c5e9bcfed0d5f0dc1eb1c3e801"], "node": "1ae693583c1af9e646d63439c8992ff3bd717d1b", "parents": ["35e398abc7e36a0d42947ef48cf53d667843211b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074509 - Skip HAL calls when the PHal actor cannot be created during content process shutdown. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nGetHal() returns null once the PHal actor is destroyed or could not be\ncreated, e.g. after PContent closed, and callers then skip the message.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330356\n", "files": ["dom/power/moz.build", "dom/power/tests/browser/browser.toml", "dom/power/tests/browser/browser_hal_during_content_shutdown.js", "hal/HalInternal.h", "hal/sandbox/SandboxHal.cpp"], "git_node": "3a91f102855ac1f654de1fe87508da1ddcf52f98", "git_parents": ["fad6d3f049273fc9c66b9bd1e97a393b7da59e2c"], "node": "e5f66341f328e3cf3d71c9bcd5dada9048b667e6", "parents": ["1ae693583c1af9e646d63439c8992ff3bd717d1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077354 - jit/arm64: fold constant shifts into the shifted-register operand of int32 add, sub and bitwise ops. r=iain\n\nIon lowers JavaScript bit math one MIR node at a time, so a hash step such\nas ((h \u003c\u003c 5) + c) | 0 emits the shift and the add separately:\n\n  lsl w2, w2, #5\n  add w2, w4, w2\n\nAArch64 add, sub, and, orr and eor can shift their second register operand\nby a constant for free. When an Int32 shift by a nonzero constant has a\nsingle use, and that use is an Int32 add, sub (as the subtrahend) or\nbitwise op in the same block whose other operand is not a constant, arm64\nlowering now defers the shift with emitAtUses and the consumer lowers to a\nnew LShiftedOpI:\n\n  add w2, w4, w2, lsl #5\n\nFallible adds and subs use adds/subs and keep their overflow bailout. A\nfallible \u003e\u003e\u003e is never folded. Other platforms get an empty hook.\n\nIn a JetStream 3 run the fold applies at roughly 600 Ion sites.\nIn 10 interleaved JetStream 3 runs on an Apple M4 Max,\nstanford-crypto-pbkdf2 improves by 2.2% and 8bitbench-wasm by 0.5%, with\nno overlap between base and fix runs. The overall score is unchanged\nwithin noise.\n\nFound with armlint.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330296\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/shifted-operand.js", "js/src/jit/LIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/CodeGenerator-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/Lowering-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/Lowering-arm64.h", "js/src/jit/shared/Lowering-shared.h"], "git_node": "836068be179a6816dbeaa78628180835e5ad76b1", "git_parents": ["3a91f102855ac1f654de1fe87508da1ddcf52f98"], "node": "895a983cfc2266fc0da8eba5b3a01746b37f295f", "parents": ["e5f66341f328e3cf3d71c9bcd5dada9048b667e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge autoland to mozilla-central\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/naturalWidth-naturalHeight-width-height.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/inline-speculation-rules-after-stylesheet.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "4f030eadb8e64c07761f6693645e6a961c15915e", "git_parents": ["4578f07ce13c6db83454d7bd2b7583fe3d132bc0", "836068be179a6816dbeaa78628180835e5ad76b1"], "node": "ffa0ef5229bff8f30bfb976e1a12229db49a6bd2", "parents": ["0e3763914a7e7fed00fc85cc95036f3e934fac46", "895a983cfc2266fc0da8eba5b3a01746b37f295f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790975779, "git_changesets": ["ac56ac22ebf9e291a7b62f217359c762a53c7936", "09ca6665a70ed65dc22cdc9a93284ae7634616d6", "7ec494fe5caf6a01d1b8b1ff9d771d8cc9d55170", "db70a958f3f383e4ffcb00209c01857511e88fce", "d0a922ca450b82ed9648079d48c2267a2a7ed734", "3425aadd3da99f7876cd4f5d8be186dd813d9dde", "4840fdcfe70b2d98b826b7bbe94ed7c8c0dfb601", "dbd8236b315729a7c3569d3aacd4a98a64d24c36", "c3b0688af50aa83e7f691750375af122d95e2666", "b6c152c0f6f6af7cae5ebfecac0c5c9df73deecd", "c8196439b953afc504d69666ff33bfe4b6cee717", "f7b4bd0e24a82e18fa1befd0970ac8130e0fbb09", "293687f7509477c5de9c3521c4d0e21f943ce280", "313b55efd8519232aac7c2d17ddae445a0e3d8b3", "445fdc60697312fe3cd263a0dd0bc41065af8963", "1a98ffcf76e39e32ed08b92cd9de58da3640f744", "902c9cc537d6e9cc952095dcab68afe49bfd47a4", "c2d14bab92667d9d83fd5a6a487e7b61a2d5012c", "f478f12551f1fc4baa145667e0a6bfdc9a87cea6", "37f45facca6278123bdbfc30acbd24eff1fb16fb", "ec8c2a35dbe5ca9d2488afd4823dabd1e6c6047e", "6caa7f8c3706d2892aca0b78841f34c3bd9d3025", "1f1aaf46365e934860556b4b6144ed2fed704d9e", "55aafe5617cf9b9dd34e880d52e1a6f63aa93ec0", "91b7c082495fd66382e0e3d437fa97b27390cf47", "b0b5197fc6a0f8d65bbc3cfdcedf7df9821c750f", "687b4552906e4b3d07e4422196ec2a978ddc32bd", "49b8e3e7c5a4098c20dbd086c5ebbf666c2ce0e1", "8b0aa3525257ad862f6f6c88c1d48e8c774f96c7", "5757fe7a1b156da48cae7e49ffa7ed1618a83db4", "299fb3ea75badb1364269960e51693f152a585ab", "0516bf56189ef9264d87a57ed8d468b0ddb16f34", "fa1277c79cf842c5e9bcfed0d5f0dc1eb1c3e801", "fad6d3f049273fc9c66b9bd1e97a393b7da59e2c", "3a91f102855ac1f654de1fe87508da1ddcf52f98", "836068be179a6816dbeaa78628180835e5ad76b1", "4f030eadb8e64c07761f6693645e6a961c15915e"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45476": {"changesets": [{"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2071974 - Implement window.pushManager for Declarative Web Push. r=saschanaz,webidl,tschuster\" for causing wpt failures @push-api.\n\nThis reverts commit 6caa7f8c3706d2892aca0b78841f34c3bd9d3025.\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/bindings/Bindings.conf", "dom/push/PushManager.cpp", "dom/push/PushManager.h", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerRegistration.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUnregisterJob.cpp", "dom/webidl/PushManager.webidl", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/notifications/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js"], "git_node": "bf9757d91e2e53b8ab836f2a08bf4c0275fdcd23", "git_parents": ["4f030eadb8e64c07761f6693645e6a961c15915e"], "node": "dfc77f7a6d716f1a20a2576597638d4fc21cd916", "parents": ["ffa0ef5229bff8f30bfb976e1a12229db49a6bd2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1790975933, "git_changesets": ["bf9757d91e2e53b8ab836f2a08bf4c0275fdcd23"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45477": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074584 - Wake the timer thread for a timer due before the end of its wakeup window. r=jlink,xpcom-reviewers,nika\n\nThe timer thread hands the monitor a wakeup time and a tolerance and, where\nthe monitor honours the tolerance, may sleep until the end of that window.\nAddTimer only compared a new timer against the start of the window, so a\ntimer due inside it did not wake the thread and fired late by the remaining\ntolerance.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328224\n", "files": ["xpcom/threads/TimerThread.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TimerThread.h"], "git_node": "0df88970c79b1cae3bd7954c72c8b7b27a0cc0e1", "git_parents": ["836068be179a6816dbeaa78628180835e5ad76b1"], "node": "d3ec54a8f93f598bdcb79dcb76709382b7a05d50", "parents": ["895a983cfc2266fc0da8eba5b3a01746b37f295f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051892 - Add TimerThreadMonitor and use it for the timer thread. r=xpcom-reviewers,nika,jlink\n\nThe timer thread needs a precise wakeup when the timers it waits for have a\nsmall tolerance. Only Windows got one, from HiResWindowsMonitor in\nTimerThread.h. Elsewhere it waits on a condvar, which on macOS is subject to\nwakeup coalescing, most aggressively when the machine is idle.\n\nMove that monitor into TimerThreadMonitor, one file per platform, and give\nmacOS a kqueue backend: an EVFILT_TIMER carrying the tolerance as NOTE_LEEWAY,\nplus NOTE_CRITICAL when it is small, and an EVFILT_USER for Notify(). Other\nplatforms, and iOS where the content sandbox blocks kevent64, use a condvar\nthat waits for the end of the budget.\n\nThe tolerance now stays a TimeDuration down to each backend, which moves the\nprecise/tolerant boundary on Windows from \"below 17ms\" to \"at most 16ms\".\n\nThe monitor supports a single waiter, as HiResWindowsMonitor already did\nimplicitly; this is now documented and debug-asserted. Notify() requires the\nmonitor to be held, which every caller already did.\n\nThis hands the backends the whole residual tolerance of a bundle, up to an\neighth of a timer's delay. D326430 takes it away from timers that did not ask\nfor slack.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320396\n", "files": ["xpcom/tests/gtest/TestTimerThreadMonitor.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/moz.build", "xpcom/threads/TimerThread.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TimerThread.h", "xpcom/threads/TimerThreadMonitor.h", "xpcom/threads/TimerThreadMonitor_darwin.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TimerThreadMonitor_posix.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TimerThreadMonitor_windows.cpp", "xpcom/threads/moz.build"], "git_node": "79c06516482e66be0c07daaeb82f362dd5f89336", "git_parents": ["0df88970c79b1cae3bd7954c72c8b7b27a0cc0e1"], "node": "966a3c23d5dafcd768e31af0a4774579fcb689b6", "parents": ["d3ec54a8f93f598bdcb79dcb76709382b7a05d50"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051892 - Let a timer compute how late it may fire. r=jlink,xpcom-reviewers,nika\n\nThe timer thread derived the acceptable firing delay from the entry's copy of\nthe delay, on every wakeup and every insertion. Let the timer compute it under\nits own mutex and copy the result into the entry, like the delay. No behaviour\nchange.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326429\n", "files": ["xpcom/threads/TimerThread.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TimerThread.h", "xpcom/threads/nsTimerImpl.cpp", "xpcom/threads/nsTimerImpl.h"], "git_node": "001cece2002bd96dafefa7b0b374f8125cb2546b", "git_parents": ["79c06516482e66be0c07daaeb82f362dd5f89336"], "node": "72079ce570150f31db635cb413db2709eddcab6c", "parents": ["966a3c23d5dafcd768e31af0a4774579fcb689b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051892 - Fire one-shot and precise timers on their deadline. r=jlink,xpcom-reviewers,nika\n\nEvery timer accepted an eighth of its delay, and at least a millisecond, of\nlateness. The timer thread wakes up for the last timer of a bundle, so the\nearlier ones fire late, and hands what is left of the tolerance to the monitor,\nwhich may wait for it. Keep that tolerance for slack and low priority timers,\nwhich asked for it, and give every other timer none: it fires on its deadline,\nsharing a wakeup only with timers due at the same instant or slack timers\ndelayed to join it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326430\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "xpcom/threads/nsTimerImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "2ef6b97f7ba8e727485b17c9a62799ae56ca7c40", "git_parents": ["001cece2002bd96dafefa7b0b374f8125cb2546b"], "node": "34d729a940ed1526975e7f7c9bfe25b81446f742", "parents": ["72079ce570150f31db635cb413db2709eddcab6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hannajones \u003chjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059669 - Add gradient for sun theme preview in dark mode r=desktop-theme-reviewers,hjones\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329974\n", "files": ["browser/themes/ThemesList.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e8de3ef60a32770d33a1dab5f1a0710b61ae1544", "git_parents": ["2ef6b97f7ba8e727485b17c9a62799ae56ca7c40"], "node": "df415cab9a3d3eeeea2cda184515913389926579", "parents": ["34d729a940ed1526975e7f7c9bfe25b81446f742"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rob Wu \u003crob@robwu.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077557 - Disable webcompat logging by default r=webcompat-reviewers,twisniewski\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330395\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/logging.js", "devtools/client/framework/test/allocations/browser_allocations_browser_console.toml"], "git_node": "0d082e44e09cb2a971f6ab8aa70f7ebb8c4b81c5", "git_parents": ["e8de3ef60a32770d33a1dab5f1a0710b61ae1544"], "node": "8b8983ddaae9ce0781641ed3f531bac7288ab879", "parents": ["df415cab9a3d3eeeea2cda184515913389926579"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059669 - Add gradient for sun theme preview in dark mode r=desktop-theme-reviewers,hjones\" for causing xpc failures @test_ThemesList.js.\n\nThis reverts commit e8de3ef60a32770d33a1dab5f1a0710b61ae1544.\n", "files": ["browser/themes/ThemesList.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "cca997ccabcad40b48cafa27269d86bbb92f4967", "git_parents": ["0d082e44e09cb2a971f6ab8aa70f7ebb8c4b81c5"], "node": "d0e035f5bd2ffa69d439e956bb5e1e1c17208b45", "parents": ["8b8983ddaae9ce0781641ed3f531bac7288ab879"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2071974 - Implement window.pushManager for Declarative Web Push. r=saschanaz,webidl,tschuster\" for causing wpt failures @push-api.\n\nThis reverts commit 6caa7f8c3706d2892aca0b78841f34c3bd9d3025.\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/bindings/Bindings.conf", "dom/push/PushManager.cpp", "dom/push/PushManager.h", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerRegistration.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUnregisterJob.cpp", "dom/webidl/PushManager.webidl", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/notifications/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js"], "git_node": "861666401b573a565999697a1f398a593a94b119", "git_parents": ["cca997ccabcad40b48cafa27269d86bbb92f4967"], "node": "c698120df2ed0b9094f9b70bb2c2533962f69a1f", "parents": ["d0e035f5bd2ffa69d439e956bb5e1e1c17208b45"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1971509 - Disable panel opacity transition on non-mac when reduced motion is enabled. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330354\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/popup.css"], "git_node": "85b95fd9647eaa77a3eb60224441db91de1f9b34", "git_parents": ["861666401b573a565999697a1f398a593a94b119"], "node": "506ff54f68115155b638fc2070941e05ff4b74fd", "parents": ["c698120df2ed0b9094f9b70bb2c2533962f69a1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\naf -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nan -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nar -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nast -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\naz -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nbe -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nbg -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nbn -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nbo -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nbqi -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nbr -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nbrx -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nbs -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nca -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nca-valencia -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\ncak -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nckb -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\ncs -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\ncy -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nda -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nde -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\ndsb -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nel -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nen-CA -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nen-GB -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\neo -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nes-AR -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nes-CL -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nes-ES -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nes-MX -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\net -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\neu -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nfa -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\nff -\u003e 4a