nzh-TW -\u003e 4a2612cd2f4d9e740fe0c3faaa2d0134534346e6\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "0bb2385dae40a53b1400a610f23636281e818795", "git_parents": ["6461e05a698df14b6b86f329f8e9462c55643235"], "node": "558ab04d1cad8295fcfd861cfe7dc53435d54eca", "parents": ["d53b1c23b9afa74ed74c5b01eb98e5a6f2239a94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060167 - Don't report a shutdown hang profile for a crash a test requested. r=xpcom-reviewers,emilio\n\ntest_crash_terminator.js makes the terminator crash on purpose. In profiled CI\nruns its crash printed the TEST-UNEXPECTED-FAIL line naming the hang profile,\nwhich failed the job whenever the test's output ended up in the log.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328766\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/terminator/nsITerminatorTest.idl", "toolkit/components/terminator/nsTerminator.cpp"], "git_node": "504ad9dcfd794270336ba2591002bf4758c84a84", "git_parents": ["0bb2385dae40a53b1400a610f23636281e818795"], "node": "d12a82b61986e6a388d0168abc65a29d83b38d9a", "parents": ["558ab04d1cad8295fcfd861cfe7dc53435d54eca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072840 - Remove security protections popup telemetry r=webcompat-reviewers,timhuang,twisniewski\n\nSmart block embeds have been shipped for a while, the telemetry has been looked at and there are no plans to unship. Therefore remove the telemetry collection.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329194\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-siteProtections.js", "browser/base/content/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/webcompat/data/shims.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/experiment-apis/trackingProtection.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/experiment-apis/trackingProtection.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/shims.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/smartblock_embeds_helper.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/tests/browser/browser_smartblockembeds.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/tests/browser/head.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.glean.d.ts"], "git_node": "d618d7f534eb61a4ee0b0fbe07d1cba2dd5a321c", "git_parents": ["504ad9dcfd794270336ba2591002bf4758c84a84"], "node": "427b783c279026fa723db0ed369c38ac123022e5", "parents": ["d12a82b61986e6a388d0168abc65a29d83b38d9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077099 - Get rid of unreferenced set_config(...) entries r=ahochheiden\n\nThe approach is quite stupid and has a lot of false negative, but no\nfalse positive: call all set_config entries and grep for the variable\nname in the whole directory. If the count is only 1, it should be safe to\nremove them. And indeed:\n\n- TARGET_RAW_{CPU,OS} references were removed in commit 8c0d445b9db1d02086015c20bfe7728e30048dc1\n- MOZ_PGO_RUST and PGO_PROFILE_PATH references were removed in commit a83a8eebd30db1b6763c7e13c93ffe49ff02f8a4\n- FMA_FLAGS reference was removed in commit 45f9203b1f963c40ed4c5013a5c1a750c013f3ba\n- HOST_LINKER_LIBPATHS_BAT reference was removed in commit d061aa5e737200b099343ccfd1e66d702488abd0\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330113\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/init.configure", "build/moz.configure/lto-pgo.configure", "build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure", "build/moz.configure/windows.configure"], "git_node": "80115621bd633ce37812500a3d40aab1a765f78e", "git_parents": ["d618d7f534eb61a4ee0b0fbe07d1cba2dd5a321c"], "node": "dce15822320e8f960a3dfb3f1927b05b792a59e6", "parents": ["427b783c279026fa723db0ed369c38ac123022e5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update HSTS HPKP - r=release-managers,dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330446\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": "8ff566ff5c7796233c2f1afa2f12715b5a5a5f8a", "git_parents": ["80115621bd633ce37812500a3d40aab1a765f78e"], "node": "979fb16840227bbc653d79a416e803db8287f64b", "parents": ["dce15822320e8f960a3dfb3f1927b05b792a59e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068761 - Create a richer MicroTask API & prepare for microtasks by value r=arai,smaug\n\nThe most important piece of this is that we're now using a class with explicit kind to store\nMicroTasks.\n\nThis patch has a few component pieces to call out:\n\nSpiderMonkey:\n\n1. We adopt an explicit empty representation via Maybe\u003c\u003e; this way we avoid\n   representing silly states, like \"What if the queue had an empty task in it\".\n\n2. The JS engine now exports a JSMicroTaskRef API for JS microtasks. This\n   external interface can only be used as a temporary. This is a\n   deliberate design decision -- in LTO builds this should be basically free,\n   but it avoids having long lived views which can go out of sync as we\n   manipulate the underlying task\n\n3. Embedders can enqueue a raw pointer directly with FromEmbedderPtr, and\n   retrieve it with embedderPtr, rather than wrapping it in a PrivateValue\n   themselves.\n\nGecko:\n\n1. Using JSMicroTaskRef, we've split the management of MicroTasks in Gecko into\n   two halves: Lifetime (May/Must/Wont)ConsumeMicrotask, and Query (AsJSMicroTask).\n\n   This reduces duplication while having the same level of safety as\n   JSMicroTaskRef doesn't leak raw microtasks either.\n\n2. To make the rooting more clear we use free functions that take handles. This\n   documents and enforces the rooting issues.\n\nSome other notable changes:\n\n- maybeGetHostDefinedData now bakes in the behaviour that Gecko had been using rather than\n  having two stage unwrap.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326708\n", "files": ["js/public/friend/MicroTask.h", "js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/moz.build", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testMicroTask.cpp", "js/src/shell/js.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSContext.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSContext.h", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSContext.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSContext.h"], "git_node": "e1a85f887ba6b2f14e976e856c6c894ea8543e94", "git_parents": ["8ff566ff5c7796233c2f1afa2f12715b5a5a5f8a"], "node": "75c5857e6972d75bc208010ee2726b59db779ba7", "parents": ["979fb16840227bbc653d79a416e803db8287f64b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068761 - Start creating private Kinds for specialized microtasks r=arai\n\nSince embedders only care about `isJS()` vs `isEmbedder()` we begin to\nbe able to carve out space for engine specialization.\n\nThe current patch allocates a range of 16 as I believe that will be sufficient\nfor the final state.\n\nThis commit also forces `EnqueueJob` callers to declare the kind of job, which\nis preparation for alternative task shapes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326709\n", "files": ["js/public/friend/MicroTask.h", "js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSContext.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSContext.h"], "git_node": "3c7aefc6651ba39c12089dfc850ff1ba11ed1562", "git_parents": ["e1a85f887ba6b2f14e976e856c6c894ea8543e94"], "node": "a73044306bd4ef372739b536eafb3226dff6690f", "parents": ["75c5857e6972d75bc208010ee2726b59db779ba7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068761 - Dispatch JS microtasks on their element kind r=arai\n\nMake use of our ability to encode task type\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326710\n", "files": ["js/public/friend/MicroTask.h", "js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSContext.h"], "git_node": "b8c2195feaf64f084ef794615d1c35dde6024fa4", "git_parents": ["3c7aefc6651ba39c12089dfc850ff1ba11ed1562"], "node": "82fcec0375b7a5ca3ce0ff899d173df1d01876c9", "parents": ["a73044306bd4ef372739b536eafb3226dff6690f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068761 - Drop ThenableJob::TargetFunction in favour of js::MicroTaskQueueElement::Kind r=arai\n\nThe previous work has made this enum redundant.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326711\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp"], "git_node": "53bce4abe7ca49f3451c217a133f8c996ba6ade5", "git_parents": ["b8c2195feaf64f084ef794615d1c35dde6024fa4"], "node": "cd7bb8cc5ceea913fb0ba683b59661c5558b7ed3", "parents": ["82fcec0375b7a5ca3ce0ff899d173df1d01876c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mathew Hodson \u003cmathew.hodson@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011408 - Remove GDI font table loading code r=gfx-reviewers,TravisLong,bradwerth\n\nRemove pref gfx.font_rendering.directwrite.use_gdi_table_loading\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315774\n", "files": ["gfx/metrics.yaml", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.h", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json"], "git_node": "78dd6eb3e8ae918dcf4ea33dba5dee4af1419caa", "git_parents": ["53bce4abe7ca49f3451c217a133f8c996ba6ade5"], "node": "29b94e6e5e03f9050e30b5731081c147cb14836d", "parents": ["cd7bb8cc5ceea913fb0ba683b59661c5558b7ed3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mathew Hodson \u003cmathew.hodson@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011408 - Fix clang warnings in gfxDWriteFontList.cpp r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nmodernize-loop-convert: use range-based for loop instead\nmodernize-use-equals-delete: deleted member function should be public\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315775\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp"], "git_node": "0c956e7b241ab370c9006a24a62a5a3c6e830767", "git_parents": ["78dd6eb3e8ae918dcf4ea33dba5dee4af1419caa"], "node": "6417abb0603d51b4168972375cf2539d725cdafb", "parents": ["29b94e6e5e03f9050e30b5731081c147cb14836d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mathew Hodson \u003cmathew.hodson@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011408 - Remove some duplicated code used for debug asserts r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315843\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp"], "git_node": "0e7e6c4ff39dfdaf87f2d439a973435f1d8e0cb0", "git_parents": ["0c956e7b241ab370c9006a24a62a5a3c6e830767"], "node": "d23fa3afde2dbc18239a29d59a46c2c1872f237c", "parents": ["6417abb0603d51b4168972375cf2539d725cdafb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhinav Singh \u003cabhinavsingh717073@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070629 - Implement zero-copy DMABuf VideoFrame import to remote Canvas2D on Linux r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327325\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/DrawTargetWebgl.cpp", "dom/canvas/TexUnpackBlob.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLTypes.h", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.h", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.h", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "a1ce6fdd651399726adcbab9ff7a933c205df385", "git_parents": ["0e7e6c4ff39dfdaf87f2d439a973435f1d8e0cb0"], "node": "f7c591a105d9323d1ae7e48a36deda0a7cfe5daf", "parents": ["d23fa3afde2dbc18239a29d59a46c2c1872f237c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075811 - Don't blame the frame element for clicks that land in a remote document in the a11y checks, r=accessibility-frontend-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,Jamie,nchevobbe.\n\nA click into a remote browser or iframe is dispatched to the frame element in\nthe parent process, so the a11y checks reported the frame element as not\naccessible, while the node the user clicked lives in another process where\nthe checks don't run. Log that the check could not run instead, like for hidden\nnodes, and remove the fail-if annotations this fixes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329406\n", "files": ["devtools/client/framework/browser-toolbox/test/browser.toml", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_al.toml", "devtools/client/responsive/test/browser/browser.toml", "testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/AccessibilityUtils.js", "toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "7660e17c1c1a6eac93854c0e4a8d976477aea7af", "git_parents": ["a1ce6fdd651399726adcbab9ff7a933c205df385"], "node": "66b5149977cbef4a7a40959c46db14d020b8f6ab", "parents": ["f7c591a105d9323d1ae7e48a36deda0a7cfe5daf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075369 - Click instead of only pressing the mouse button in browser_toTopLevelWidgetRect.js, r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,Gijs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329170\n", "files": ["toolkit/modules/tests/browser/browser_toTopLevelWidgetRect.js"], "git_node": "db5e5365d05646ad77667ac4f3e1d51d5348d247", "git_parents": ["7660e17c1c1a6eac93854c0e4a8d976477aea7af"], "node": "47201503b58b61280f642ad6477610ae7f9611bb", "parents": ["66b5149977cbef4a7a40959c46db14d020b8f6ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075369 - Use real clicks in markup view tests that dispatched a lone mousedown, r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe.\n\nbrowser_markup_links_07.js followed attribute links by dispatching a trusted mousedown, and browser_markup_tag_edit_long-classname.js dispatched one on the selected container. Neither sent a mouseup, which left the mouse button pressed after the test.\n\nSynthesize real middle and accel clicks on the links, and use the clickContainer helper on the container.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329175\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/markup/test/browser_markup_links_07.js", "devtools/client/inspector/markup/test/browser_markup_tag_edit_long-classname.js"], "git_node": "9acd5741101879fc1f2cdc52c77ad1ed8aea5676", "git_parents": ["db5e5365d05646ad77667ac4f3e1d51d5348d247"], "node": "3880c7ed1846ce8af1f4b30deee66cfc1dcd0a5b", "parents": ["47201503b58b61280f642ad6477610ae7f9611bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075369 - Release the mouse button after the gutter shift-click in browser_editor_cursor.js, r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe,bomsy.\n\nThe test dispatched a trusted shift+mousedown on the editor gutter without a mouseup, which left the mouse button pressed after the test. Dispatch the matching mouseup.\n\nA synthesized click at the gutter coordinates would not work here without waiting for a paint: the editor frame has just loaded, and until it paints the click targets its iframe element instead of the gutter.\n\nDepends on D329175\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329176\n", "files": ["devtools/client/shared/sourceeditor/test/browser_editor_cursor.js"], "git_node": "226e4d65874b4e372613de2813c3914d7d7d16c7", "git_parents": ["9acd5741101879fc1f2cdc52c77ad1ed8aea5676"], "node": "e235b007769546ad4a1e8675b12a37a82a26d4a6", "parents": ["3880c7ed1846ce8af1f4b30deee66cfc1dcd0a5b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075369 - Release the mouse button after synthesized mousedowns in urlbar tests, r=urlbar-reviewers,mbeier.\n\nkeep_view_open_on_context_menu_mousedown now completes the click on \"Open in new tab\", so it adds a history visit to make the first result a local URL; otherwise the click opens a web search and the harness fails on a non-local connection.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329178\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_urlbar_contextmenu.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-search/browser_speculative_connect.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_strip_on_share.js"], "git_node": "c8787a03dc8ff66ce1227ff06581ffd8d47b72dd", "git_parents": ["226e4d65874b4e372613de2813c3914d7d7d16c7"], "node": "0a6388bfd224a0b83a62cd98323225338a549682", "parents": ["e235b007769546ad4a1e8675b12a37a82a26d4a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075369 - Release the mouse button after opening a tab on mousedown in browser_tabswitch_window_focus.js, r=tabbrowser-reviewers,sclements.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329180\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tabswitch_window_focus.js"], "git_node": "2580fa33c2316aaa471020099be4b1ceb09668e8", "git_parents": ["c8787a03dc8ff66ce1227ff06581ffd8d47b72dd"], "node": "6696591558494c1f7c3bb82ddd3c154cc69ff177", "parents": ["0a6388bfd224a0b83a62cd98323225338a549682"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075369 - Release the mouse button after the container menu opens from the new tab button in browser_newtabButton.js, r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,Gijs.\n\nThe container menu opens on mousedown. On macOS it is a native menu activated with activateItem, so the test never sent a mouseup and left the mouse button pressed. Keep the press that opens the menu and release the button once it is shown, as a user does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329183\n", "files": ["browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser_newtabButton.js"], "git_node": "ecd06a6b0d4488a254288a7d253613dfdca22643", "git_parents": ["2580fa33c2316aaa471020099be4b1ceb09668e8"], "node": "4818f78a25ab9f7c9d7eeddcde821e3624740fe7", "parents": ["6696591558494c1f7c3bb82ddd3c154cc69ff177"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1775706 - Wait for the sidebar animation before right-clicking the vertical tabs new tab button in browser_newtabButton.js, and re-enable it on macOS opt, r=sidebar-reviewers,sclements.\n\nWhile the sidebar expand animation runs, the content area overlaps the button and the synthesized contextmenu opens the content context menu instead. This was the macOS opt failure, so the skip-if is removed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329184\n", "files": ["browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser_newtabButton.js"], "git_node": "e1ab694d2ea62b92b5588b1aa1ea59632487e427", "git_parents": ["ecd06a6b0d4488a254288a7d253613dfdca22643"], "node": "7a1e313818a1ae931fe9f9db87264f96946fc231", "parents": ["4818f78a25ab9f7c9d7eeddcde821e3624740fe7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075521 - Consider the mouse button released when a drag session ends, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug.\n\nA drag can end without a dragend, for example when tabbrowser recovers from a stale drag session or when the drag service was suppressed during the drag. The platform drag loop swallows the button release, so nsGlobalWindowInner::sMouseDown stayed set, and the next window move or resize suppressed drag and drop until the next mouseup.\n\nDepends on D329184\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329185\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/events/test/browser.toml", "dom/events/test/browser_dragsession_end_without_dragend.js", "widget/nsBaseDragService.cpp"], "git_node": "ab9464e8f597b53cbda01ced14f888c66559cb3a", "git_parents": ["e1ab694d2ea62b92b5588b1aa1ea59632487e427"], "node": "e050437edda55af65aae8a93e7d6958e8c6dc42b", "parents": ["7a1e313818a1ae931fe9f9db87264f96946fc231"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071974 - Implement window.pushManager for Declarative Web Push. r=saschanaz,webidl,tschuster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328914\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/bindings/Bindings.conf", "dom/push/PushManager.cpp", "dom/push/PushManager.h", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerRegistration.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUnregisterJob.cpp", "dom/webidl/PushManager.webidl", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/notifications/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js"], "git_node": "a4e5ab76206becb92e6cad077cad408e24ac4960", "git_parents": ["ab9464e8f597b53cbda01ced14f888c66559cb3a"], "node": "6aaaff420e889a5e3a613db226b217914dde3a74", "parents": ["e050437edda55af65aae8a93e7d6958e8c6dc42b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075436. r=gfx-reviewers,ahale\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330454\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/PathRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/PathRecording.h"], "git_node": "5727a14a786818f54b5ce9d45c0c5262b39bdc98", "git_parents": ["a4e5ab76206becb92e6cad077cad408e24ac4960"], "node": "918d4d801d10e271875a754c092ebc5b71ef5cdd", "parents": ["6aaaff420e889a5e3a613db226b217914dde3a74"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059179 - Fix TimeUnit overflow when converting MSE duration to microseconds. r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers\n\nFor the crash recorded in\nhttps://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2059179#c0 and\nhttps://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2017567#c2.  Even if the\nparser-level fix https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D284050?id=1208302\nwere in place, this guards the two call sites that would crash if a\nnear-INT64_MAX timestamp ever reached them.\n\nmGroupEndTimestamp can hold a large TimeUnit (e.g. 8.82e18 ticks at 44100Hz).\nConverting to microseconds via ToBase(USECS_PER_S) overflows INT64_MAX\nin both DurationChangeOnEndOfStream and SetMediaSourceDuration. The original\ncode then called Invalid().ToSeconds() which hits a MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT\nin CheckedInt::value(). MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT fires in debug builds and\nNightly (where MOZ_DIAGNOSTIC_ASSERT_ENABLED is set).\n\nFix: check IsValid() after ToBase(USECS_PER_S) in both call sites.\nDurationChangeOnEndOfStream returns early; SetMediaSourceDuration, which\nhas a second caller (MediaSource::SetDuration with an internal TimeUnit),\nfalls back to seconds precision rather than crashing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D284048\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediasource/MediaSource.cpp", "dom/media/mediasource/MediaSourceDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/test/crashtests/2014870.html"], "git_node": "324701cfc2d4ffffa867b97468d2462a6354ea3c", "git_parents": ["5727a14a786818f54b5ce9d45c0c5262b39bdc98"], "node": "5f0a7e22c8a218a97e5c143bbcf434021bb8a564", "parents": ["918d4d801d10e271875a754c092ebc5b71ef5cdd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075420: Add early-exit for non-permanent atoms in LookupStdName r=spidermonkey-reviewers,yulia\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329345\n", "files": ["js/src/jsapi.cpp"], "git_node": "3e51e450d497a08d939d66c15003cb6578ad37e2", "git_parents": ["324701cfc2d4ffffa867b97468d2462a6354ea3c"], "node": "5bd97510c4cd2097146b60007add3286067264cb", "parents": ["5f0a7e22c8a218a97e5c143bbcf434021bb8a564"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2070629 - Implement zero-copy DMABuf VideoFrame import to remote Canvas2D on Linux r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" for causing bustages on GLBlitHelper.\n\nThis reverts commit a1ce6fdd651399726adcbab9ff7a933c205df385.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/DrawTargetWebgl.cpp", "dom/canvas/TexUnpackBlob.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLTypes.h", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.h", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.h", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "1af0d7a63a869f87c3a39ad4753063eb1c56d094", "git_parents": ["3e51e450d497a08d939d66c15003cb6578ad37e2"], "node": "4c513dda5acaa148d1a89ef14b9d56c3fbac19cb", "parents": ["5bd97510c4cd2097146b60007add3286067264cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Oberhauser \u003cj.git@obez.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076859 - Adding android automotive glean metric r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330041\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FenixApplication.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FenixApplicationTest.kt"], "git_node": "7ab2715773a3b8ad3734f8736691f0eaf5f1a13d", "git_parents": ["1af0d7a63a869f87c3a39ad4753063eb1c56d094"], "node": "f2accb53cf270667535e6475917270ac7cb536e6", "parents": ["4c513dda5acaa148d1a89ef14b9d56c3fbac19cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077517: Pass undefined for missing argument in fun_SymbolHasInstance r=spidermonkey-reviewers,yulia\n\nThe [spec text](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-function.prototype-%symbol.hasinstance%) here is:\n```\nFunction.prototype [ %Symbol.hasInstance% ] ( value )\n1. Let thisValue be the this value.\n2. Return ? OrdinaryHasInstance(thisValue, value).\n```\nIf no arguments are passed, `value` is undefined, but we still have to call OrdinaryHasInstance.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330398\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/function/bug2077517.js", "js/src/vm/JSFunction.cpp"], "git_node": "b6682f6dc3c26774a1713016c6e91d36e5e32dca", "git_parents": ["7ab2715773a3b8ad3734f8736691f0eaf5f1a13d"], "node": "c3b585e733e894c123dbb9b1169715dab926d13c", "parents": ["f2accb53cf270667535e6475917270ac7cb536e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076917: Prevent unexpected magic values in ArgumentsObject r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330059\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineCodeGen.cpp", "js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/vm/ArgumentsObject-inl.h", "js/src/vm/ArgumentsObject.h", "js/src/vm/EnvironmentObject-inl.h", "js/src/vm/EnvironmentObject.h"], "git_node": "4d189d6c3505c6c6d3757d9f7acbfb6cb56eec1d", "git_parents": ["b6682f6dc3c26774a1713016c6e91d36e5e32dca"], "node": "4ba179119ae8090320c0607f77e0791fd543428c", "parents": ["c3b585e733e894c123dbb9b1169715dab926d13c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076917: Use stronger assertions for some isMagic checks r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330060\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineJIT.cpp", "js/src/jit/Jit.cpp", "js/src/jit/TrampolineNatives.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpOracle.cpp"], "git_node": "335af0bf8b4475c8ae971a7ac29163520ed46902", "git_parents": ["4d189d6c3505c6c6d3757d9f7acbfb6cb56eec1d"], "node": "94a9e014dd91c350acde70a04e0899a96fde3432", "parents": ["4ba179119ae8090320c0607f77e0791fd543428c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2071974 - Implement window.pushManager for Declarative Web Push. r=saschanaz,webidl,tschuster\" for causing merge back conflicts.\n\nThis reverts commit a4e5ab76206becb92e6cad077cad408e24ac4960.\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/bindings/Bindings.conf", "dom/push/PushManager.cpp", "dom/push/PushManager.h", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerRegistration.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUnregisterJob.cpp", "dom/webidl/PushManager.webidl", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/notifications/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js"], "git_node": "445cb22943f2b0d16798ccb7201269234d022aa3", "git_parents": ["335af0bf8b4475c8ae971a7ac29163520ed46902"], "node": "5a4b5a8c2338b7bd14af72e97ef6297101567e93", "parents": ["94a9e014dd91c350acde70a04e0899a96fde3432"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "261cafaf9f5485884ee0a4c4e679e19e674cbb7e", "git_parents": ["445cb22943f2b0d16798ccb7201269234d022aa3", "bf9757d91e2e53b8ab836f2a08bf4c0275fdcd23"], "node": "c1e42646d59fc998e9fca7dab9d4985b39d44329", "parents": ["5a4b5a8c2338b7bd14af72e97ef6297101567e93", "dfc77f7a6d716f1a20a2576597638d4fc21cd916"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071974 - Implement window.pushManager for Declarative Web Push. r=saschanaz,webidl,tschuster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328914\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/bindings/Bindings.conf", "dom/push/PushManager.cpp", "dom/push/PushManager.h", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerRegistration.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUnregisterJob.cpp", "dom/webidl/PushManager.webidl", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/notifications/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js"], "git_node": "e37d96eb8d95d722205810bf3aa69b318c033ff6", "git_parents": ["261cafaf9f5485884ee0a4c4e679e19e674cbb7e"], "node": "801be7d174065e5fd19176ad7ede98741259a361", "parents": ["c1e42646d59fc998e9fca7dab9d4985b39d44329"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2071974 - Implement window.pushManager for Declarative Web Push. r=saschanaz,webidl,tschuster\" for causing wpt failures @push-api.\n\nThis reverts commit e37d96eb8d95d722205810bf3aa69b318c033ff6.\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/bindings/Bindings.conf", "dom/push/PushManager.cpp", "dom/push/PushManager.h", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerRegistration.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerUnregisterJob.cpp", "dom/webidl/PushManager.webidl", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/notifications/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/push-sw.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js"], "git_node": "b796074e28ccd19d6e4ca402c75acc9674126ba5", "git_parents": ["e37d96eb8d95d722205810bf3aa69b318c033ff6"], "node": "1fc2feb3feac032e49aade1c162e378680274bd1", "parents": ["801be7d174065e5fd19176ad7ede98741259a361"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dmitry Gozman \u003cdgozman@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076389 - Set the target of coalesced PointerEvents only after duplicating their private data. r=dom-core-reviewers,masayuki\n\nPointerEvent::GetCoalescedEvents() creates a DOM event that aliases an entry\nof the shared WidgetPointerEventHolder, assigns mTarget on it, and only then\ncalls DuplicatePrivateData(). The assignment therefore lands on the\nWidgetPointerEvent inside the holder, a plain ref-counted object shared by\nevery copy of the outer WidgetPointerEvent and never traversed by the cycle\ncollector. When a page keeps the pointermove event alive (hCaptcha samples\npointer events and calls getCoalescedEvents()), the target element and its\nwhole document are kept alive forever through that untraversed edge.\n\nSet mTarget after DuplicatePrivateData(), so the strong reference lives on the\ninternal copy that the cycle collector traverses. mWidget and mPresContext\nmust stay before it, since MouseEvent::DuplicatePrivateData() needs them to\ncache the event coordinates.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329732\n", "files": ["dom/events/PointerEvent.cpp", "dom/events/test/pointerevents/file_getCoalescedEvents_retained_event_leak.html", "dom/events/test/pointerevents/mochitest.toml", "dom/events/test/pointerevents/test_getCoalescedEvents_retained_event_leak.html"], "git_node": "da1688c62468c554f6593456cff80f3886dc21b8", "git_parents": ["b796074e28ccd19d6e4ca402c75acc9674126ba5"], "node": "2d2c60880f5c674975f66e07760e9fd6b09c6360", "parents": ["1fc2feb3feac032e49aade1c162e378680274bd1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2051892, Bug 2074584 - Fire one-shot and precise timers on their deadline. r=jlink,xpcom-reviewers,nika\" for causing multiple failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 2ef6b97f7ba8e727485b17c9a62799ae56ca7c40.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2051892 - Let a timer compute how late it may fire. r=jlink,xpcom-reviewers,nika\"\n\nThis reverts commit 001cece2002bd96dafefa7b0b374f8125cb2546b.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2051892 - Add TimerThreadMonitor and use it for the timer thread. r=xpcom-reviewers,nika,jlink\"\n\nThis reverts commit 79c06516482e66be0c07daaeb82f362dd5f89336.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2074584 - Wake the timer thread for a timer due before the end of its wakeup window. r=jlink,xpcom-reviewers,nika\"\n\nThis reverts commit 0df88970c79b1cae3bd7954c72c8b7b27a0cc0e1.\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestTimerThreadMonitor.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/moz.build", "xpcom/threads/TimerThread.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TimerThread.h", "xpcom/threads/TimerThreadMonitor.h", "xpcom/threads/TimerThreadMonitor_darwin.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TimerThreadMonitor_posix.cpp", "xpcom/threads/TimerThreadMonitor_windows.cpp", "xpcom/threads/moz.build", "xpcom/threads/nsTimerImpl.cpp", "xpcom/threads/nsTimerImpl.h"], "git_node": "0f07a80c07d7c863508a28086d4fc8c119148e6d", "git_parents": ["da1688c62468c554f6593456cff80f3886dc21b8"], "node": "b142254fbfc0b7105b059b2f93efb1c167edebaa", "parents": ["2d2c60880f5c674975f66e07760e9fd6b09c6360"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1324602 - Ship Scroll-driven Animations. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,dshin\n\nShip Scroll-driven Animations on Fx159 since the major features have been\nimplemented and most of the wpt are passed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330194\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "dc3622e7d15b6a1ddbe83e63b3a6f13a4e3f5604", "git_parents": ["0f07a80c07d7c863508a28086d4fc8c119148e6d"], "node": "f08b67071821effeaade3cfbaf7434e1ce0cee10", "parents": ["b142254fbfc0b7105b059b2f93efb1c167edebaa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhinav Singh \u003cabhinavsingh717073@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070629 - Implement zero-copy DMABuf VideoFrame import to remote Canvas2D on Linux r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327325\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/DrawTargetWebgl.cpp", "dom/canvas/TexUnpackBlob.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLTypes.h", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelper.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.h", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.h", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "a3c328e4aff34a383827dc4b23f96001a3975428", "git_parents": ["dc3622e7d15b6a1ddbe83e63b3a6f13a4e3f5604"], "node": "5a7ebbc00c274bef04f894324c648548929ffce0", "parents": ["f