5dc281cf6ab68188a1fedf5d56a5b27f9d\nxh -\u003e ddf6cc5dc281cf6ab68188a1fedf5d56a5b27f9d\nzam -\u003e ddf6cc5dc281cf6ab68188a1fedf5d56a5b27f9d\nzh-CN -\u003e ddf6cc5dc281cf6ab68188a1fedf5d56a5b27f9d\nzh-TW -\u003e ddf6cc5dc281cf6ab68188a1fedf5d56a5b27f9d\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "5eabb9704b01cdc6374964b15ecd6e620a04dd0b", "git_parents": ["0ed3dffd376745b62d38cb149bdd2f3805bdd66b"], "node": "082b3c64824e94539e933ab482b093906a63cdf2", "parents": ["e56c0c30fae73888b1db2560d3db02f86a195478"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076837 - Run reftests and crashtests on GeckoView with fission. r=geckoview-reviewers,necko-reviewers,valentin,owlish\n\nRight now, Fenix runs with fission, but both reftests and crashtests\ndon't run with fission.\n\nAlso, non-fission should be moved to mozilla-central only and change\ntier to 2, like linux tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330133\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/crashtests/crashtests.list", "taskcluster/kinds/reftest/kind.yml"], "git_node": "7727a8c1dc0ea918bc4e4af8f17c87797a87786b", "git_parents": ["5eabb9704b01cdc6374964b15ecd6e620a04dd0b"], "node": "95f7a5de1ecafb7e0b7c561666a15527dfe56305", "parents": ["082b3c64824e94539e933ab482b093906a63cdf2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073538 - Update AGP to version 9.4.1. r=android-reviewers,adhingra\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327403\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml"], "git_node": "b0a432ee92b8b84151e4d56072041620df95bb64", "git_parents": ["7727a8c1dc0ea918bc4e4af8f17c87797a87786b"], "node": "4dd98cdcc64ead52f38971b29fbdb9f718a42983", "parents": ["95f7a5de1ecafb7e0b7c561666a15527dfe56305"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1998616 - Wait for the IME and the dynamic toolbar to settle before InteractiveWidgetTest goes on. r=geckoview-reviewers,m_kato\n\nensureKeyboardOpen returns as soon as the visual viewport has shrunk, which happens while the IME's insets\nanimation is still running, and bug1994311 then hides the keyboard about 300 ms after the show request, inside\nthat animation. Android cancels the show animation, reports the IME as hidden so the viewport grows back, and\nthen completes the original show and re-applies the keyboard insets, so the viewport shrinks again shortly\nafter the test saw it restored. Every test in the file also hides the keyboard on its way out without waiting,\nso the next test's show can land inside that hide animation the same way.\n\nTrack the ime insets animations with a WindowInsetsAnimation callback on the root view, and have showKeyboard\nand hideKeyboard wait until the ime has the requested visibility and no ime animation is running. The\nshowSoftInput and hideSoftInputFromWindow ResultReceiver overloads are not enough: they report once the IME\nhas handled the request, a few tens of milliseconds in, while the animation runs for a few hundred\nmilliseconds more.\n\nThe dynamic toolbar hides race too: setVerticalClipping reaches content through an async PBrowser message that\nthe test-support flushes do not order against. Wait for the window resize event after the toolbar hide, as the\nDynamicToolbarTest hit tests do. overlaysContent keeps the bare setVerticalClipping call: its\ninteractive-widget=overlays-content page gets no resize event from the toolbar hide, so the wait times out\nthere.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327718\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/InteractiveWidgetTest.kt"], "git_node": "9fe49371caf63b6192901f006b61769fdcee38a2", "git_parents": ["b0a432ee92b8b84151e4d56072041620df95bb64"], "node": "3be6a36487f2f5b6a4675dbd9367d08cb2f6ac66", "parents": ["4dd98cdcc64ead52f38971b29fbdb9f718a42983"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791061683, "git_changesets": ["5b33955c67800b8cc5b83e40d04f2d45d5a4cc03", "3a3255e6473d76b068618fb52cfb0c457f5f55dd", "44f70b6e77d3d76c56442ee5d21dc286ebbe4ca1", "5320dd8219adbb66b61cb429956d9aa1de286b92", "f7ed3cf856ffef2bc0051e92a132eb88c1885f17", "0ed3dffd376745b62d38cb149bdd2f3805bdd66b", "5eabb9704b01cdc6374964b15ecd6e620a04dd0b", "7727a8c1dc0ea918bc4e4af8f17c87797a87786b", "b0a432ee92b8b84151e4d56072041620df95bb64", "9fe49371caf63b6192901f006b61769fdcee38a2"], "user": "nfay@mozilla.com"}, "45479": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077683 - Update test_interfaces.js now that ScrollTimeline and ViewTimeline ship on all channels. r=webidl,emilio\n\nBug 1324602 shipped scroll-driven animations in Fx159: `layout.css.scroll-driven-animations.enabled` now defaults to `true` on every channel. ScrollTimeline and ViewTimeline are gated only by that pref, but test_interfaces.js still marks them as `nightly: true`. So when 159 merges to beta, the beta simulation fails with \"DANGER ... expose the new interface ViewTimeline\".\n\nThis patch drops `nightly: true` from both entries.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330566\n", "files": ["dom/tests/mochitest/general/test_interfaces.js"], "git_node": "f5fc27ce1f865968194fad55b733ac4e4b48ea87", "git_parents": ["9fe49371caf63b6192901f006b61769fdcee38a2"], "node": "b89bcf1a9226456794c45b4775daab3fae3ca3b4", "parents": ["3be6a36487f2f5b6a4675dbd9367d08cb2f6ac66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings tld-suffixes ct-logs - r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330569\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/to