r=necko-reviewers,nika,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305263\n", "files": ["netwerk/ipc/NeckoChannelParams.ipdlh", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelParent.h"], "git_node": "7692db72ce07889a181da1228f8c5607af0fc7e9", "git_parents": ["9938d16c743a2298fe1bf137ee9a57a0f38db28a"], "node": "6e8048c834d5aa0d5d614b53cdfadbc7f0ec1bd8", "parents": ["30a45f6e386020f884414ab1d477a25ee1c4c675"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2045704: Validate LoadInfoArgs and HTTP channel flags r=necko-reviewers,nika,valentin\" for causing dt failures @browser_webconsole_network_messages_resend_request.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 7692db72ce07889a181da1228f8c5607af0fc7e9.\n", "files": ["netwerk/ipc/NeckoChannelParams.ipdlh", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelParent.h"], "git_node": "00a4d527cdb9807ecb561c9fcf7d211e7e568ddf", "git_parents": ["7692db72ce07889a181da1228f8c5607af0fc7e9"], "node": "4dc52174287d433a83e0ee56aeb76a69c266af06", "parents": ["6e8048c834d5aa0d5d614b53cdfadbc7f0ec1bd8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791187314, "git_changesets": ["94403844fcb51919804117d60c9896dfe95caf1d", "d60ebb90570b5148c9566dd1eb57d718af7dc8f6", "4e130ec94bdde34b4de4bce8f3e90de0cc29ca4c", "0021f5957690a5daab41c4a852265cd10101c4cb", "5eb3311b6e5dda740912e3503b112a891a7b8a2d", "8e719975da54c26616b76dc4479d04105be7a92d", "e93e62096b88edccccd78449fb4cacf7916ccbe1", "1309c4cfe0f45332e16669fffaa9377a28a1bff6", "8f1d523454550cda03cc5220ba8c284d810d7536", "4a115dd896d86611afabe888423ec6d6acadbdf1", "4878e77256a2744ef1429246a23a40a18188a96e", "be32552acda4a03ee240e82005b0458a70fe41e3", "e22cf72e6ce3381ba345e1986a89d7371d552de0", "63f1a659b30d8827af728e325031411db4ff34cc", "9b17359563517ea6dca4d12badaa88dba1f4b601", "f044f1e0e704e387779a181ebf53942f81038e77", "eb9c3600a6bf46148e09f94946c7bd6037cf55c5", "9938d16c743a2298fe1bf137ee9a57a0f38db28a", "7692db72ce07889a181da1228f8c5607af0fc7e9", "00a4d527cdb9807ecb561c9fcf7d211e7e568ddf"], "user": "csabou@mozilla.com"}, "45482": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 9872e53cf08d45c2a502b3ea45150534c4a0a09e with FIREFOX-ANDROID_158_0b4_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "4fb76d4fc2fb87ad5d60957988da84a820d37efc", "git_parents": ["86b0d1d285678a58dc4eb1985d1fc4c413faa532"], "node": "37bb2c2138b54857ebeab81cf14d0dec4b1e41b6", "parents": ["dec48190f2dec95365653d755ba04ab23037eab4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791205622, "git_changesets": ["4fb76d4fc2fb87ad5d60957988da84a820d37efc"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45483": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 9872e53cf08d45c2a502b3ea45150534c4a0a09e with DEVEDITION_158_0b4_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "2ab061fd80d583353b0f3238a31ab94f73e5a60c", "git_parents": ["4fb76d4fc2fb87ad5d60957988da84a820d37efc"], "node": "19b2c376c7aabaa8849a305a6648b3b6238f3969", "parents": ["37bb2c2138b54857ebeab81cf14d0dec4b1e41b6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791205720, "git_changesets": ["2ab061fd80d583353b0f3238a31ab94f73e5a60c"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45484": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 9872e53cf08d45c2a502b3ea45150534c4a0a09e with FIREFOX_158_0b4_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "e5978fdb35fe29ab9514216ccab29f49eaad22b7", "git_parents": ["2ab061fd80d583353b0f3238a31ab94f73e5a60c"], "node": "7554c335ff25a94cf79bd276fecece2900b6fec9", "parents": ["19b2c376c7aabaa8849a305a6648b3b6238f3969"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791205800, "git_changesets": ["e5978fdb35fe29ab9514216ccab29f49eaad22b7"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45485": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 9872e53cf08d45c2a502b3ea45150534c4a0a09e with FIREFOX-ANDROID_158_0b4_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "2b1df7fcf48f11bdc92f418dd947932060f6bed9", "git_parents": ["e5978fdb35fe29ab9514216ccab29f49eaad22b7"], "node": "19679c7175ce5efa6c1d3fc13c4711e9c22ede19", "parents": ["7554c335ff25a94cf79bd276fecece2900b6fec9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791207320, "git_changesets": ["2b1df7fcf48f11bdc92f418dd947932060f6bed9"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45486": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mayank Bansal \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1961720 - Remember where GetKey left off instead of rescanning mValues. r=dom-storage-reviewers,asuth,jari\n\nLSSnapshot::GetKey(n) started a fresh mValues iteration on every call and\ncounted live entries until it reached n. Walking the whole storage with\nlocalStorage.key(i) was therefore O(N^2): with N=500000 the testcase in\nthe bug spends 21 minutes with ~95% of the content process' CPU time\ninside PLDHashTable::Iterator::MoveToNextLiveEntry.\n\nKeep the iterator alive between calls instead, along with the index it\nrefers to, so that walking the keys in order costs one step per call.\nThe iterator only moves forward, so a request before the cursor\nrestarts from the beginning; that keeps repeated key(0) cheap as well.\n\nThis doesn't change what any call returns. The keys still come out in\nmValues' arbitrary hashtable order, which is all we owe callers: the\nspecification's storage reorder operation lets an implementation\nreshuffle the map on insertion of a new key or removal of an existing\none, so the order only has to be self-consistent while nothing is\nmutated. Every mutation of mValues therefore invalidates the cursor\nfirst, which is also required for a different reason - a live iterator\nholds the table in a read state and PLDHashTable's checker, enabled in\nDEBUG and FUZZING builds, release-asserts on writes while one is\noutstanding.\n\nPure reads deliberately don't invalidate, so the key(i)/getItem(key)\nloop in the testcase keeps the cursor across the getItem call.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312889\n", "files": ["dom/localstorage/LSSnapshot.cpp", "dom/localstorage/LSSnapshot.h"], "git_node": "411db8361ab260b0556604f9fd2d873c1d815e8c", "git_parents": ["00a4d527cdb9807ecb561c9fcf7d211e7e568ddf"], "node": "c71d54e897dd54e1e837da76a1628bda17ea301f", "parents": ["4dc52174287d433a83e0ee56aeb76a69c266af06"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mayank Bansal \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1961720 - Sort write infos once instead of inserting each into place. r=dom-storage-reviewers,jari\n\nGetSortedWriteInfos() built its result with InsertElementSorted() per\nwrite info. Each insertion binary searches and then shifts the tail of\nthe array, so building the list of N writes is O(N^2) memmove work.\n\nCheckpointing the 500000 setItem() calls from the testcase in the bug\nmakes this the dominant cost on both sides of the IPC boundary: it is\n82% of the parent's IPDL Background thread time (via\nDatastoreWriteOptimizer::ApplyAndReset) and 62% of the content process'\nmain thread time (via SnapshotWriteOptimizer::Enumerate), essentially\nall of it inside memcpy.\n\nAppend everything and sort once instead. Serial numbers are drawn from a\nmonotonically incremented counter, so the comparator induces a total\norder with no ties and the result is unchanged.\n\nSessionStorageCache::GetWriteInfos() shares this helper and gets the\nsame improvement.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312926\n", "files": ["dom/localstorage/LSWriteOptimizer.cpp"], "git_node": "93a4761cc864dbbd34c356dbce9363d5851a07b8", "git_parents": ["411db8361ab260b0556604f9fd2d873c1d815e8c"], "node": "e36419b8a20332f0df877cea0be47003babc2d2b", "parents": ["c71d54e897dd54e1e837da76a1628bda17ea301f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mayank Bansal \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1961720 - Transfer the serial number counter in LSWriteOptimizerBase's move constructor. r=dom-storage-reviewers,jari\n\nThe move constructor moved mTruncateInfo and swapped mWriteInfos, but\nleft mLastSerialNumber to default-construct to 0 on the destination.\nThis was latent: nothing observed the destination's counter unless it\nwas written to after the move, and its only use (Connection::Flush\nmoving mWriteOptimizer into a FlushOp, which is only Perform()'d and\nReset()) never adds writes post-move.\n\nIt matters now because GetSortedWriteInfos()'s previous commit relies\non serial numbers being unique to guarantee nsTArray::Sort (unstable)\nreproduces the same order as the old per-element InsertElementSorted.\nA moved-to optimizer that resumed accumulating writes would restart\nnumbering from 0 and collide with the higher serials it already holds,\nsilently corrupting replay order. Copy the counter across so the\ninvariant holds structurally instead of by the accident of no current\ncaller reusing a moved-to optimizer.\n\nThe source keeps its own counter unchanged, so Connection::mWriteOptimizer\ncorrectly continues numbering forward for writes queued after the flush.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312927\n", "files": ["dom/localstorage/LSWriteOptimizer.cpp"], "git_node": "9a8f4584ad74908a6e3c1b59bf9de1c9b9101b25", "git_parents": ["93a4761cc864dbbd34c356dbce9363d5851a07b8"], "node": "67dc7d7fd808baea4f52c534298bf5b571388908", "parents": ["e36419b8a20332f0df877cea0be47003babc2d2b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivier Mehani \u003comehani@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072023 - workflows: remove path limitation in pr-handler DOT_GITHUB_OVERRIDE r=conduit-reviewers,sheehan,zeid DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329110\n", "files": [".github/workflows/pr-handler.yml"], "git_node": "3b2f615e6a3075a18eefae3b0e1e31cab6605974", "git_parents": ["9a8f4584ad74908a6e3c1b59bf9de1c9b9101b25"], "node": "fe95d2e2589f62b7fb15cbe6b57b073907e657a2", "parents": ["67dc7d7fd808baea4f52c534298bf5b571388908"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077283 - Enable network.trr.preserve_on_background on all channels. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330249\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "355addff1aeb57cf26961123ce7c36deb35d9947", "git_parents": ["3b2f615e6a3075a18eefae3b0e1e31cab6605974"], "node": "afe44e0615fae86f95efb25eea71cddb8923f0f4", "parents": ["fe95d2e2589f62b7fb15cbe6b57b073907e657a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077283 - Enable network.trr.allow_default_http3_first on all channels. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330250\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "5a84a6db12629156fcc910dbdb0ca4d0e47a7078", "git_parents": ["355addff1aeb57cf26961123ce7c36deb35d9947"], "node": "0476d0fede6b807846d1aedbebdf92a8e3516266", "parents": ["afe44e0615fae86f95efb25eea71cddb8923f0f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077283 - Enable network.tcp.user_timeout on all channels. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330251\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "f63149eeef0b61329e582539b66ecef61428ecce", "git_parents": ["5a84a6db12629156fcc910dbdb0ca4d0e47a7078"], "node": 