\nThis practice is already adopted by some distros, like Arch Linux RISC-V\nand openRuyi.\n\nLink: https://github.com/felixonmars/archriscv-packages/blob/2662cf75438febc6ea993b5ecd6a2c747e8942bb/firefox/xptcstubs-riscv64-tail.patch\nLink: https://github.com/openRuyi-Project/openRuyi/blob/ef71a3c657919f7fdffe5ce5c7782abbf8d7549a/SPECS/firefox/2000-riscv64-Use-long-tail-jump-for-xptcall-stubs.patch\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330581\n", "files": ["xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcstubs_riscv64.cpp"], "git_node": "95e0ef3dd433cf7179235b00c3ffb3162dd85751", "git_parents": ["b59c8abfb9a3d107c2686b14ef3d570cefa2ec3c"], "node": "c91776e1c87f3f4401cff838f81ee3c4f6356365", "parents": ["94611f0155afaab95904121f820b7af1b011405f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hubert B Manilla \u003chmanilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077519 - [devtools] Show \"prefetch\" in the initiator column for prefetch requests r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nThis covers both link prefetch and speculative rules prefetch requests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330451\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_initiator.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_speculation-rules-prefetch-requests.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/html_cause-test-page.html", "devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c5de76cbcc6d8f97c782f054a10cfff0c3c3051b", "git_parents": ["95e0ef3dd433cf7179235b00c3ffb3162dd85751"], "node": "33239a7fd77889b5c2ad98fcd697083b6cc78f1b", "parents": ["c91776e1c87f3f4401cff838f81ee3c4f6356365"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077820 - [loongarch64] Part 1: Use `TAIL36` instead of `B` when tail-calling SharedStub. r=xpcom-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330582\n", "files": ["xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcstubs_loongarch64.cpp"], "git_node": "b5db03a4b5f018d53e4e5026bb778fd7f41e2d83", "git_parents": ["c5de76cbcc6d8f97c782f054a10cfff0c3c3051b"], "node": "dcb34d6a3303d5e9f1bcde3c469860ed121a1aff", "parents": ["33239a7fd77889b5c2ad98fcd697083b6cc78f1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077820 - [loongarch64] Part 2: Use `CALL36` instead of `BL` in _NS_InvokeByIndex and SharedStub. r=xpcom-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330586\n", "files": ["xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcinvoke_asm_loongarch64.S", "xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcstubs_asm_loongarch64.S"], "git_node": "714b5cd86ba71216b2838249d3f0ec0d5e10cede", "git_parents": ["b5db03a4b5f018d53e4e5026bb778fd7f41e2d83"], "node": "6566f7dfebb83ad81da6099cd5a2268cc1a9ad9c", "parents": ["dcb34d6a3303d5e9f1bcde3c469860ed121a1aff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077820 - [loongarch64] Part 3: (Drive-by) Use `RET` alias instead of raw `JIRL $zero, $ra, 0` in assembly. r=xpcom-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis is purely hygiene and should have no runtime effects.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330587\n", "files": ["xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcinvoke_asm_loongarch64.S", "xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/xptcstubs_asm_loongarch64.S"], "git_node": "03809552a72c66eabca8cd367d6d789487560d81", "git_parents": ["714b5cd86ba71216b2838249d3f0ec0d5e10cede"], "node": "cd0e1bfd7ee118124d7a52e8f4beec01e1b0b1b4", "parents": ["6566f7dfebb83ad81da6099cd5a2268cc1a9ad9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073889 - Don't require an accesskey on a menuitem without a label. r=tgiles,reusable-components-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329565\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/chrome/test_menu_accesskey_conflicts.xhtml", "toolkit/content/widgets/accesskey-check.mjs"], "git_node": "25e86fd80bf707fd7eabb36eac8ea507b2b65cfb", "git_parents": ["03809552a72c66eabca8cd367d6d789487560d81"], "node": "f5cd3532a83116876b063657b16cfe2f32139105", "parents": ["cd0e1bfd7ee118124d7a52e8f4beec01e1b0b1b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073889 - Drop the accesskeys of the content context menu's navigation items. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,fluent-reviewers,places-reviewers,daisuke,flod,mossop\n\nBack, Forward, Reload, Stop and Bookmark Page are icon buttons with no label to show an accesskey, and each has a window-level keyboard shortcut. Their hidden B and F collided with Bookmark Link and Full Screen.\n\nThe toolbar button messages copy their text instead of referencing the renamed context menu messages, since a reference shows the message id in locales that lack the target.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329566\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-context.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/base/content/browser-places.js", "browser/base/content/navigator-toolbox.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/nsContextMenu.sys.mjs", "browser/base/content/test/browser-general/browser_bug624734.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browserContext.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2073889_navigation_context_menu_accesskeys.py"], "git_node": "d599e23ea9391308d9cdc7420c1957500f1591e1", "git_parents": ["25e86fd80bf707fd7eabb36eac8ea507b2b65cfb"], "node": "c354e669619e11795bb47b11a3d9500d41ebe743", "parents": ["f5cd3532a83116876b063657b16cfe2f32139105"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073889 - Skip the accesskey check on a menu that macOS shows natively. r=reusable-components-reviewers,akulyk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329780\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/chrome/test_menu_accesskey_conflicts.xhtml", "toolkit/content/widgets/accesskey-check.mjs"], "git_node": "e15fa23b0c09ed4d08dd18875b326c59fcfadd75", "git_parents": ["d599e23ea9391308d9cdc7420c1957500f1591e1"], "node": "3f335ab3036f4a7978717538f6ba598a48a4f532", "parents": ["c354e669619e11795bb47b11a3d9500d41ebe743"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brendan Birdsong \u003cbbirdsong@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075410 - Add SponsoredTopSitesScoreProvider function to sum configured domain visits per day. r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329330\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/SponsoredTopSitesScoreProvider/SponsoredTopSitesScoreProvider.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/SponsoredTopSitesScoreProvider/SponsoredTopSitesScoreProvider.test.js"], "git_node": "c850f51bd50badf566dc1a42324d78faee1e2c62", "git_parents": ["e15fa23b0c09ed4d08dd18875b326c59fcfadd75"], "node": "e70564fefc3f2c70a9229c75ace2d706f427d990", "parents": ["3f335ab3036f4a7978717538f6ba598a48a4f532"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070841 - Discard a speculation-rules prefetch record whose final response is not an ok status. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329898\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp"], "git_node": "004caa70b1ad5b44e21337caf4df47b570a25f74", "git_parents": ["c850f51bd50badf566dc1a42324d78faee1e2c62"], "node": "22a912036ff61debcfec63aeff968041772fc518", "parents": ["e70564fefc3f2c70a9229c75ace2d706f427d990"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070841 - Skip cache validation when serving a navigation activated from a speculation-rules prefetch record. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329899\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/browser_prefetch_delivery_type.js", "dom/base/test/file_pageload_prefetch_target.sjs", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/clear-prefetch-cache-after-clear-site-data-cache.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/initiators-a-element.sub.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/mutate-rules.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/navigation-timing-delivery-type.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/navigation-timing-requestStart-responseStart.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-vary-search/prefetch-single.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/prefetch-single.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/prefetch-status.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/prefetch-traverse-reload.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/redirect-url.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/referrer-policy-from-rules.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/referrer-policy-not-accepted.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/referrer-policy.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/same-origin-cookies.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/tentative/service-worker/basic.sub.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/tentative/service-worker/redirect.sub.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/user-pass.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/storage-access-api/storage-access-headers.tentative.https.sub.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "e9a55ea084a1caba7fb4447a04814ee39b210ff5", "git_parents": ["004caa70b1ad5b44e21337caf4df47b570a25f74"], "node": "68e651c855bd23585ffe0c14c817b4e0550eb0a8", "parents": ["22a912036ff61debcfec63aeff968041772fc518"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078225 - Make MediaFormatReader::ResetDecode reset audio track correctly. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nIt was previously resetting the video's mFirstFrameTime instead of\nthe audio's when the audio track was reset.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330752\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaFormatReader.cpp"], "git_node": "4c30cece1da4ccfd706652ede8d0eec7a339e48c", "git_parents": ["e9a55ea084a1caba7fb4447a04814ee39b210ff5"], "node": "9b3d8e262fea127963b29bfdbb73fdbd0db0dbe8", "parents": ["68e651c855bd23585ffe0c14c817b4e0550eb0a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075853 - Probe HSTS hosts with a sliding-window pool and retry failures once. r=keeler,releng-reviewers,jcristau\n\ngetHSTSPreloadList.js probed hosts in batches of 500 and waited for the slowest request of each batch, so most\nbatches took the full 30 second timeout. The bursts of 500 lookups also overwhelmed the container's DNS\nresolver and produced tens of thousands of false connection failures, which kept live Chromium-listed hosts\noff the list.\n\nA pool of 250 requests now starts the next one as soon as one completes. Every connection failure, TLS errors\nincluded, is then retried once in a second pass with the same concurrency and timeout. This replaces\nMAX_RETRIES, which at 1 never retried. Hosts reached on the retry are marked rescued in\nhsts-probe-results.json.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329494\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getHSTSPreloadList.js"], "git_node": "5807cfa561bec3d51ba6bf8df36ee112cbddfd70", "git_parents": ["4c30cece1da4ccfd706652ede8d0eec7a339e48c"], "node": "68a7ad40fb311555b6186fe696c612d40cbecf0b", "parents": ["9b3d8e262fea127963b29bfdbb73fdbd0db0dbe8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075853 - Keep HSTS preload entries whose host answers 4xx or 5xx without the header. r=keeler\n\nA 403 or 429 bot-blocking page or a 5xx error page usually lacks the Strict-Transport-Security header that the\nsite otherwise sends, so whether a live site stayed on the preload list depended on the timing of the probe.\nSuch a response now keeps the entry like one that could not be reached, the same rule the failure streak in\nhsts-probe-results.json uses. A 2xx or 3xx response without the header still removes the entry, as does a\nheader whose max-age is below the minimum, whatever the status. The streak no longer counts the latter as a\nfailed run either.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329495\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getHSTSPreloadList.js"], "git_node": "bf1c47e98ce0a2214a54018c065e34105199a6da", "git_parents": ["5807cfa561bec3d51ba6bf8df36ee112cbddfd70"], "node": "adae5c525c2502a9b2f76219a4992f3c7e9c9bbc", "parents": ["68a7ad40fb311555b6186fe696c612d40cbecf0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075853 - Probe HSTS preload hosts in random order and retry 429 responses. r=keeler,releng-reviewers,jcristau\n\nChromium's list holds thousands of domains of one hosting operator in a contiguous block, all served from two\naddresses. Probing in list order sent nearly every request in flight to those two addresses at once, and the\noperator answered with 429 for thousands of hosts that otherwise send a valid header, which kept them off the\npreload list. Shuffling the probe order spreads them over the whole run. The operator still limits the rate\nover the run as a whole, so this recovers only part of the entries it kept off the list. It also shortens the\nmain pass by about a third, mostly because that block answers slowly when probed all at once.\n\n429 responses without the header also join the connection failures in the retry pass, which runs after the\nmain pass and is spread out the same way. A second retry pass was considered and left out: it would cost about\nas long as the first, mostly in 30 second timeouts, while the first reaches under 1% of the hosts it retries.\n\nThis is an addition to the plan in bug 1891052, which did not cover rate limiting.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329496\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getHSTSPreloadList.js"], "git_node": "263339295e4694a4b9363552c6160184c69cca60", "git_parents": ["bf1c47e98ce0a2214a54018c065e34105199a6da"], "node": "60b705c83f21f98f6ff1aa1213b6699377631c03", "parents": ["adae5c525c2502a9b2f76219a4992f3c7e9c9bbc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075432 - Ensure table continuations use consistent border-collapse model. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330808\n", "files": ["layout/tables/nsTableFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-tables/table-continuation-border-model-crash-print.html"], "git_node": "14ceedd5e0f1695d1145a09d288bae3ed9c2f3b0", "git_parents": ["263339295e4694a4b9363552c6160184c69cca60"], "node": "9dee6e8aff14c48df396591e9437834e7e434f55", "parents": ["60b705c83f21f98f6ff1aa1213b6699377631c03"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Borondo \u003caborondo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078338 - Remove aborondo from the Firefox::Profile Backup triage owners list r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330826\n", "files": ["browser/components/backup/triage.json"], "git_node": "b16b93dcb2e79f07d654002d9787632c3b2ce5ef", "git_parents": ["14ceedd5e0f1695d1145a09d288bae3ed9c2f3b0"], "node": "eaaeeb8f1267d708669be9168c3cbe3689962f35", "parents": ["9dee6e8aff14c48df396591e9437834e7e434f55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "acreskeyMoz \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073257 - Add an in-flight activation subtest to the browsertime-speculation-rules raptor test r=perftest-reviewers,aglavic\n\nClicks before the prefetch completes so the navigation must wait for the ongoing prefetch, which the existing subtests never exercise.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327459\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/desktop.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md", "testing/raptor/browsertime/speculation-rules-prefetch.js", "testing/raptor/browsertime/support-scripts/speculation_rules.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/perfdocs/config.yml", "testing/raptor/raptor/tests/custom/browsertime-speculation-rules.toml"], "git_node": "715d5c0083d73dfb1378e7805c57d20836986826", "git_parents": ["b16b93dcb2e79f07d654002d9787632c3b2ce5ef"], "node": "96ff07070a26a1591952a34ba0783b0ac3d70b73", "parents": ["eaaeeb8f1267d708669be9168c3cbe3689962f35"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073647; r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329143\n", "files": ["dom/media/webcodecs/AudioData.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/EncodedAudioChunk.cpp", "dom/media/webcodecs/ImageDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "25decc525a7bcd40e090d754a3972c713699a1e8", "git_parents": ["715d5c0083d73dfb1378e7805c57d20836986826"], "node": "8cf5d778ab0e141b2a5b1a28507e76e14116a4ce", "parents": ["96ff07070a26a1591952a34ba0783b0ac3d70b73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068902 - Use __builtin_prefetch for absl::PrefetchToLocalCacheForWrite on x86-64. r=sergesanspaille,firefox-build-system-reviewers\n\nWithout PRFCHW, abseil emits a hard-coded prefetchw on the assumption that CPUs lacking it treat the opcode as\na no-op. 64-bit NetBurst CPUs (Pentium 4 / Xeon family 15) raise #UD instead, crashing protobuf at startup.\nLet the compiler pick the instruction: prefetcht0 by default, prefetchw when the target guarantees it. The\nnon-GNU SSE fallback gets the same treatment. Written in the shape intended for upstream.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330758\n", "files": ["third_party/abseil-cpp/absl/base/prefetch.h", "third_party/abseil-cpp/moz-patch-stack/0004.patch"], "git_node": "0f49952df11d9d3b4452a01d48e6333bedc9ec2f", "git_parents": ["25decc525a7bcd40e090d754a3972c713699a1e8"], "node": "e3cdcb6db73cd3ca3281059a336e66a251845922", "parents": ["8cf5d778ab0e141b2a5b1a28507e76e14116a4ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078243 - Bump taskcluster-taskgraph to v24.4.0, r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330791\n", "files": ["taskcluster/requirements.in", "taskcluster/requirements.txt"], "git_node": "1f7fd88b92b98ca807c30326d76809da4139e75c", "git_parents": ["0f49952df11d9d3b4452a01d48e6333bedc9ec2f"], "node": "05330a883f8d2f48c6fd05814f5970d4c2d7af7b", "parents": ["e3cdcb6db73cd3ca3281059a336e66a251845922"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ted Campbell \u003ctcampbell@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068239 - Use 4 shards for gv-junit tests. r=geckoview-reviewers,nalexander\n\nOur harness already allows this already. I picked 4 shards to aim for about 11\nminutes per job. The chunk distribution is decided by the JUnitRunner on device\nrather than harness so there is no support for dynamic chunking.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330834\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/test/misc.yml"], "git_node": "368041ef8e8ecaecc92170775c54763e31ab5248", "git_parents": ["1f7fd88b92b98ca807c30326d76809da4139e75c"], "node": "236ec1aeec3f03f7eaaccdc1f2863b66ddda17f2", "parents": ["05330a883f8d2f48c6fd05814f5970d4c2d7af7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072610 - Add a ubsan_error structured log action and a shared parser r=ahal\n\nUndefinedBehaviorSanitizer reports only exist in test logs as raw\nprocess_output lines: a \"\u003cfile\u003e:\u003cline\u003e:\u003ccol\u003e: runtime error: \u003cmessage\u003e\"\nheader, the stack the runtime prints, and a \"SUMMARY:\nUndefinedBehaviorSanitizer: undefined-behavior \u003clocation\u003e\" line, which is\nthe only one Treeherder's failure summary shows. The kind there is always\n\"undefined-behavior\" (report_error_type is off), so nothing downstream\nsees the actual message, the source location or the stack.\n\nAdd a ubsan_error structured log action carrying the kind, message, source\nlocation, and the stack as profiler-format\nframes, and a shared UBSanErrorParser in moztest, modelled on the TSan\nparser, that harnesses feed with their process output. The parser keys\nin-progress reports by the emitting stream, understands symbolized and\nunsymbolized frames, tolerates the note and hex-dump lines some checks\nprint, and can be told to discard a report a structured action already\ncovers.\n\nThe mach formatter renders the action on one line; the tbpl formatter\ndeliberately does not, so the task log and Treeherder's failure summary\nkeep showing the original lines only. TestSummaryFormatter keeps the\naction, with its stack like crash, so summary.jsonl carries the report.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326481\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/machformatter.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/testsummary.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/structuredlog.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_formatters.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_structured.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_testsummary.py", "testing/mozbase/moztest/moztest/ubsan.py", "testing/mozbase/moztest/tests/manifest.toml", "testing/mozbase/moztest/tests/test_ubsan.py"], "git_node": "4434c26bf66fcd3ed466618e43c1abac3da52fc6", "git_parents": ["368041ef8e8ecaecc92170775c54763e31ab5248"], "node": "ee4e52fd21dfabaa9ca86b25ab08dfbfea2724f4", "parents": ["236ec1aeec3f03f7eaaccdc1f2863b66ddda17f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072610 - Record UBSan reports as markers in resource usage profiles r=ahal\n\nDispatch the ubsan_error action from both the local ResourceHandler and\nthe CI StructuredOutputParser to a new SystemResourceMonitor handler, so\neach UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer report becomes a \"UBSan Error\" marker\ncarrying the message, source location and the stack the\nruntime printed.\n\nThe monitor used to turn every line of a report (header, frames and\nSUMMARY) into a generic output marker. Keep a line-based path for\nharnesses that do not emit the action yet, but drive it with the shared\nUBSanErrorParser: the lines are folded into one marker instead of\nproducing output markers, and a pending line-based report is dropped when\nthe structured action for the same report arrives, so wired harnesses get\nexactly one marker per report. Without moztest the lines keep their\nprevious treatment.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326482\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/handlers/resourcehandler.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/mozsystemmonitor/resourcemonitor.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/tests/test_resource_monitor.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/structuredlog.py"], "git_node": "b729a8402bc1b1110e6004d19d3b9f54c612dfbb", "git_parents": ["4434c26bf66fcd3ed466618e43c1abac3da52fc6"], "node": "c85452721119b8ae54c1e9757bd68ecb6de8a521", "parents": ["ee4e52fd21dfabaa9ca86b25ab08dfbfea2724f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072610 - mochitest/xpcshell: emit ubsan_error from process output r=ahal\n\nFeed the process output of mochitest (OutputHandler, keyed by the\nemitting GECKO stream) and xpcshell (each test's lines as they are logged,\nlive or replayed) to the shared UBSanErrorParser, so the ubsan_error\naction follows the raw lines in the structured log and the resource usage\nprofile gets a marker with the real stack.\n\nThe parser runs unconditionally, like the assertion parser bug 2070642\nlanded in both harnesses: it is inert until a \"runtime error:\" header, and\nthe xpcshell selftest must pass on every build type.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326483\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/runtests.py", "testing/xpcshell/runxpcshelltests.py", "testing/xpcshell/selftest.py"], "git_node": "8d662ced02a4b84bd5feac13842c767efaa7d6fe", "git_parents": ["b729a8402bc1b1110e6004d19d3b9f54c612dfbb"], "node": "d8dc8661bfca3ec5d93be3887a2ac0ea87f6aafe", "parents": ["c85452721119b8ae54c1e9757bd68ecb6de8a521"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Remove the dead `installer` and `deb` targets from `mobile/android/build.mk` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,sylvestre,owlish\n\n`mobile/android/installer/Makefile.in` defines neither target, so both recipes\nfailed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328997\n", "files": ["mobile/android/build.mk"], "git_node": "1227f22b18063d1cb6fb95423f71b48204f4b012", "git_parents": ["8d662ced02a4b84bd5feac13842c767efaa7d6fe"], "node": "5433df782c4f01c710e6fb262ff6a8491a0cb3b3", "parents": ["d8dc8661bfca3ec5d93be3887a2ac0ea87f6aafe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Remove the dead test harness targets from `testsuite-targets.mk`, `build.mk` and `rules.mk` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,sergesanspaille,owlish\n\n`mach` runs each of these harnesses directly and nothing invokes the Make\ntargets. `mochitest-browser-chrome` also expanded `RUN_MOCHITEST`, which is\ndefined nowhere.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329465\n", "files": ["browser/build.mk", "build/binary-location.mk", "config/rules.mk", "mobile/android/build.mk", "testing/testsuite-targets.mk"], "git_node": "ea097b3dd34ad01f599d4238b53cb79ab26d08f1", "git_parents": ["1227f22b18063d1cb6fb95423f71b48204f4b012"], "node": "c33cd3a13330a26af469b1e40c88c78dd4572976", "parents": ["5433df782c4f01c710e6fb262ff6a8491a0cb3b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Remove the dead `wget-en-US` forwards from `build.mk` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,sergesanspaille,owlish\n\nNeither `browser/locales` nor `mobile/android/locales` defines the target they\nforward to.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329466\n", "files": ["browser/build.mk", "mobile/android/build.mk"], "git_node": "d9bd37a266f436fe5558d22f76594ef2ae16d143", "git_parents": ["ea097b3dd34ad01f599d4238b53cb79ab26d08f1"], "node": "d1fffcd8d9da0bd4ba53e00d7e743a0c1baaaa27", "parents": ["c33cd3a13330a26af469b1e40c88c78dd4572976"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the XPIDL export traversal from `xpcom/xpidl/Makefile.in` to the backend r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,shtrom,sylvestre\n\nThe traversal runs `export` in `config/makefiles/xpidl`, where the removed\nsubmake ran `xpidl`, so `config/makefiles/xpidl/Makefile.in` now makes `export`\nbuild `xpidl`. The directory is traversed only when XPIDL modules exist.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329012\n", "files": ["config/makefiles/xpidl/Makefile.in", "mots.yaml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py", "toolkit/toolkit.mozbuild", "xpcom/xpidl/Makefile.in", "xpcom/xpidl/moz.build"], "git_node": "c6eac23759463c1ce1d279174df72c657636be52", "git_parents": ["d9bd37a266f436fe5558d22f76594ef2ae16d143"], "node": "cbe35c5275a5c70a94fb548cd48cd848ff77fc63", "parents": ["d1fffcd8d9da0bd4ba53e00d7e743a0c1baaaa27"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the XPIDL `COMPILE_ENVIRONMENT` condition from `config/makefiles/xpidl/Makefile.in` to the emitter r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nA build without a compile environment no longer writes the XPIDL Makefile,\ninstall manifest and Rust summary. The `xpidl` target already built nothing in\nsuch a build.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329013\n", "files": ["config/makefiles/xpidl/Makefile.in", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/common.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/emitter.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/common.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py"], "git_node": "91c42f66588ef00264c8b0ad002d5bf3f6ffa4a2", "git_parents": ["c6eac23759463c1ce1d279174df72c657636be52"], "node": "5e206a6880f15b5fab181461a5caf83a72ef79ad", "parents": ["cbe35c5275a5c70a94fb548cd48cd848ff77fc63"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the source package `buildid.h` build from `_run_make` to `mach build` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329018\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "61efc67b9f2eb4c3566d23678a4b3f6f026cf568", "git_parents": ["91c42f66588ef00264c8b0ad002d5bf3f6ffa4a2"], "node": "0bf0dae9916aeeac7d42960e70aab41675c68a95", "parents": ["5e206a6880f15b5fab181461a5caf83a72ef79ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077669 - Ignore the `braces` advisory GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm in pnpm-audit r=mconley\n\nNo braces release fixes the advisory. Every sass version that drops\nbraces changes the compiled newtab CSS, and the newest ones fail to\ncompile it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330577\n", "files": ["tools/lint/pnpm-audit.yml"], "git_node": "45d42a77bc4cff6cd01bc8474d78643589fb19da", "git_parents": ["61efc67b9f2eb4c3566d23678a4b3f6f026cf568"], "node": "6d599cd8fbbdd71ecbd259121681c954d0a78bba", "parents": ["0bf0dae9916aeeac7d42960e70aab41675c68a95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057112: Backed out 4 changesets for causing crashes r=win-reviewers,necko-reviewers,chutten,gstoll\n\nConsolidated backout:\n\nBacked out changeset b15f195b6f9f\nBacked out changeset 800b21b1dbee\nBacked out changeset 476da53d95d8\nBacked out changeset 75b4e31ffc30\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330458\n", "files": ["browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/DllBlocklist.cpp", "browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/ModuleLoadFrame.cpp", "browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/ModuleLoadFrame.h", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPPlatform.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPPlatform.h", "dom/media/gmp/PGMP.ipdl", "dom/media/ipc/PRDD.ipdl", "dom/media/ipc/RDDChild.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RDDChild.h", "ipc/glue/PUtilityProcess.ipdl", "ipc/glue/UtilityProcessParent.cpp", "ipc/glue/UtilityProcessParent.h", "mozglue/misc/NativeNt.h", "netwerk/ipc/PSocketProcess.ipdl", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.h", "toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/obsolete/collection/third-party-modules-ping.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/other/UntrustedModules.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/other/UntrustedModulesDataSerializer.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_ThirdPartyModulesPing.js", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/ModuleVersionInfo.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesData.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/ModuleLoadInfo.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/TestModuleFileValidation.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/TestUntrustedModules.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "a80e787cc2419f8abdaaa5e0b97eaaec633bdec7", "git_parents": ["45d42a77bc4cff6cd01bc8474d78643589fb19da"], "node": "3f16800cb007ce9718eda84454dedbd1433813de", "parents": ["6d599cd8fbbdd71ecbd259121681c954d0a78bba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057112: Part 1 - Rename ModulePaths to ModuleIdentifiers r=win-reviewers,necko-reviewers,gstoll\n\nRename-only, since ModuleIdentifiers will be used in later parts, instead of\njust paths.  No substantive changes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330459\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPPlatform.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPPlatform.h", "dom/media/gmp/PGMP.ipdl", "dom/media/ipc/PRDD.ipdl", "dom/media/ipc/RDDChild.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RDDChild.h", "ipc/glue/PUtilityProcess.ipdl", "ipc/glue/UtilityProcessParent.cpp", "ipc/glue/UtilityProcessParent.h", "netwerk/ipc/PSocketProcess.ipdl", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesData.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.h"], "git_node": "719e3ed6024bb4cbed8ae555be9649b2b626b69c", "git_parents": ["a80e787cc2419f8abdaaa5e0b97eaaec633bdec7"], "node": "31673754bc3ee28cf758d55c590c5165a2dd5923", "parents": ["3f16800cb007ce9718eda84454dedbd1433813de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057112: Part 2 - Pass child process's module list by file handle r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nChild processes now report loaded DLLs to the parent by file HANDLE instead\nof by filename.  In child processes, the DLL blocklist now hooks\nNtCreateSection and duplicates the file handle that the loader passes it.\nThat is the only point where the handle is available, since the loader closes\nit once the section is created.  The NtMapViewOfSection hook attaches it to\nthe ModuleLoadInfo for the load.  The parent identifies the module from the\nHANDLE with GetFinalPathNameByHandleW.  This is based on the abandoned\nrevision D321122.\n\nA handle cannot be forged into a reference to a different file and a child can\nonly send one it holds.  ValidateAndResolveModuleFile sanity checks:\n\n1. The handle must be for a file on a disk.\n2. The file must not be on a remote device.\n3. The file must not carry a mandatory integrity label below medium.\n\nThese checks replicate the checks of the MITIGATION_IMAGE_LOAD_NO_REMOTE and\nMITIGATION_IMAGE_LOAD_NO_LOW_LABEL child sandbox behaviors.  A child can open\na file without loading it, so what it hands us is not bounded by the\nimage-load policy.  The checks avoid considering such files at all.  This\ncurrently applies to all child processes: content, gpu, RDD, socket, utility\n(all kinds), and GMP.  All have these sandbox mitigations.\n\nA file handle cannot be duplicated with more access than the loader's handle\nhas, and that lacks READ_CONTROL, so the duplicate is given no access to the\nfile at all.  The parent reopens the file from the handle to read its label.\n\nHolding a file handle does not prevent the file's deletion, so a module that\nis quickly unloaded and then deleted, before the parent processes the batch,\nstill cannot be evaluated.  These patches do not fix that problem.\n\nAlso fixes a couple of ways that a version resource could misuse VerQueryValueW's\noutput in the parent: a zero length underflowing to SIZE_MAX in\nQueryStringValue and a too-short buffer dereference in GetFromImage.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330460\n", "files": ["browser/app/winlauncher/DllBlocklistInit.cpp", "browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/DllBlocklist.cpp", "browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/DllBlocklist.h", "browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/ModuleLoadFrame.cpp", "browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/ModuleLoadFrame.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/GMPPlatform.h", "mozglue/misc/NativeNt.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/ModuleVersionInfo.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesData.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/ModuleLoadInfo.h"], "git_node": "80b0d6fe58300b3b21e4b962ce7baec172533e1d", "git_parents": ["719e3ed6024bb4cbed8ae555be9649b2b626b69c"], "node": "e6d5a7a65cc6b3136b6a89f36e7210800be29e18", "parents": ["31673754bc3ee28cf758d55c590c5165a2dd5923"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057112: Part 3 - Test that UntrustedModulesProcessor rejects invalid modules r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nCheck that ValidateAndResolveModuleFile rejects descriptors that are not for\nfiles on a disk or are for below-medium-integrity modules.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330461\n", "files": ["toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/TestModuleFileValidation.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "359cec75d456bfb094d9b14347f41cc57016cd73", "git_parents": ["80b0d6fe58300b3b21e4b962ce7baec172533e1d"], "node": "78336dde3f8aed14d99d2b7d30462486333d3e41", "parents": ["e6d5a7a65cc6b3136b6a89f36e7210800be29e18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057112: Part 4 - Add DLL-reporting failures to the third-party-modules ping r=win-reviewers,chutten,gstoll\n\nNow that the parent identifies a child process's modules from the file handle\nthe child sends, and silently skips any handle it cannot identify, we will\nneed telemetry for how often that skipping happens. This patch adds a counter\nfor that.\n\nrejectedFiles: the number of module file handles a child process sent to the\nparent that it refused as invalid module file handles.\n\nThe counter is per-process and is only ever incremented for child processes,\nso the browser process reports zero. The counter is reported by the process\nusing the module, so its accuracy depends on trusting the process itself.\nThis is how the UntrustedModulesProcessor has always worked, and is by design\n(for performance reasons).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330462\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/other/UntrustedModules.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/other/UntrustedModulesDataSerializer.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_ThirdPartyModulesPing.js", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesData.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesData.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/TestUntrustedModules.cpp"], "git_node": "34afc58d1565aa867f0f640ca957aab2c9062f94", "git_parents": ["359cec75d456bfb094d9b14347f41cc57016cd73"], "node": "6c34161b74704093695e2f08dfc4d441c1234991", "parents": ["78336dde3f8aed14d99d2b7d30462486333d3e41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1987001 - Improve draining in FFmpegVideoDecoder and FFmpegAudioDecoder on Android. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nWhen draining, Android MediaCodec can still hold frames while\navcodec_receive_frame returns EAGAIN, for example because it reported an\noutput format change before its first frame, or because it has no free output\nbuffer until the compositor releases one. Completing the drain at that point\nloses those frames, and for short videos, such as those in our mochitests, no\nframe is ever returned.\n\nThe video decoder could already defer a drain, but only while it held frames\nwhose release would resume it. Now it can also be resumed by a timer polling\nuntil MediaCodec reports EOS or we exceed our maximum attempts. This\ncode is shared with the audio decoder.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329595\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegAudioDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegAudioDecoder.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDataDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDataDecoder.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.h"], "git_node": "5cf346157068a285144cfb2f0409e81a2796ac59", "git_parents": ["34afc58d1565aa867f0f640ca957aab2c9062f94"], "node": "9c731d12bc6782e7ce290f7648f04c26e25786e4", "parents": ["6c34161b74704093695e2f08dfc4d441c1234991"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2077519 - [devtools] Show \"prefetch\" in the initiator column for prefetch requests r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\" for causinf devtools failures at network_events\n\nThis reverts commit c5de76cbcc6d8f97c782f054a10cfff0c3c3051b.\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_initiator.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_speculation-rules-prefetch-requests.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/html_cause-test-page.html", "devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "4805bdbc63bec6743c62a257fefb77cac6a1c5e5", "git_parents": ["5cf346157068a285144cfb2f0409e81a2796ac59"], "node": "c1ad49e3744cd9985058b5f8e7897baee94c6c7b", "parents": ["9c731d12bc6782e7ce290f7648f04c26e25786e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2075432 - Ensure table continuations use consistent border-collapse model. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\" for causing web platform tests failures at css-tables\n\nThis reverts commit 14ceedd5e0f1695d1145a09d288bae3ed9c2f3b0.\n", "files": ["layout/tables/nsTableFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-tables/table-continuation-border-model-crash-print.html"], "git_node": "2ef394c5eecdb9f2d1594d43f0ef557beff6d2b9", "git_parents": ["4805bdbc63bec6743c62a257fefb77cac6a1c5e5"], "node": "315dc672f161b89297e5fb605a02835c05f27687", "parents": ["c1ad49e3744cd9985058b5f8e7897baee94c6c7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077992 - Set the artifact download progress callback before the download starts r=RyanVM\n\nThe download thread can finish before a later `set_progress` call,\nwhich leaves the progress log and the\n`test_artifact_cache_content_encoding` assertion empty.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330747\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifact_cache.py"], "git_node": "04eb1545e7b2b0aafb3dae349ae08519c213458a", "git_parents": ["2ef394c5eecdb9f2d1594d43f0ef557beff6d2b9"], "node": "caa0670f02968cac7c50274579a91d00ad724e80", "parents": ["315dc672f161b89297e5fb605a02835c05f27687"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075147 - Hide Reveal Password context menu items when DisablePasswordReveal is set. r=jmendez,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328911\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/nsContextMenu.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/content/aboutPolicies.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_disable_password_reveal.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/policies/policies-descriptions.ftl", "toolkit/content/editMenuOverlay.js"], "git_node": "62092bb7ebf49c1cddff44ed2429372f3cae318f", "git_parents": ["04eb1545e7b2b0aafb3dae349ae08519c213458a"], "node": "8f49e4a6e604112eddc3458f753b4b1dfcb8932a", "parents": ["caa0670f02968cac7c50274579a91d00ad724e80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075147 - Respect DisablePasswordReveal in the passwords sidebar. r=credential-management-reviewers,mtigley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328912\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/aggregator/datasources/LoginDataSource.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/content/components/login-form/login-form.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/content/components/login-line/login-line.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/content/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/content/tests/browser/browser_passwords_policy_disable_reveal.js"], "git_node": "10488f0dd43ecaad11614e3c2ac8bc6396b1a8f2", "git_parents": ["62092bb7ebf49c1cddff44ed2429372f3cae318f"], "node": "4a28e98094ae0eb1dea86367e9e93ed1a113060a", "parents": ["8f49e4a6e604112eddc3458f753b4b1dfcb8932a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fabio Kaminski \u003cfabiokaminski@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1735401 - EXT_texture_norm16 webgl feature - remove obsolete guards and don't accept unsized RGBA r=lsalzman,gfx-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330803\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLExtensions.cpp", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/generated/generated-mochitest-webgl2-core-conformance2.toml", "gfx/gl/GLContextFeatures.cpp"], "git_node": "6588d85910cdddc0c801b2da250da3db0694fe6c", "git_parents": ["10488f0dd43ecaad11614e3c2ac8bc6396b1a8f2"], "node": "7ba1dbf5b9eb5a467e2524bb8e2f27631c0e7590", "parents": ["4a28e98094ae0eb1dea86367e9e93ed1a113060a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075369 - Release the mouse button after the long press in browser_link_preview.js, r=omarg.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329169\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_link_preview.js"], "git_node": "672f6f308e38a34e373cdc82280a3a5efea1424e", "git_parents": ["6588d85910cdddc0c801b2da250da3db0694fe6c"], "node": "d38176cd8145bebb2b01f07c4fbfe075b9db64b4", "parents": ["7ba1dbf5b9eb5a467e2524bb8e2f27631c0e7590"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075369 - Dispatch a mouseup after the synthetic mousedowns in AI window tests, r=omarg.\n\nDepends on D329176\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329177\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button_tab_management.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_focus.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_suggestions.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_resume_card.js"], "git_node": "6ba0106eb5cf8350074c927acf8ffec9dd5ce8d0", "git_parents": ["672f6f308e38a34e373cdc82280a3a5efea1424e"], "node": "10b57165d97f4bcc2583e0a67f4f7b2996f25eb0", "parents": ["d38176cd8145bebb2b01f07c4fbfe075b9db64b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073976 - Pt 5 - Write the follower stores and builder map into captures r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nA capture holds one build's delta, but the display lists in it can reference\nhandles interned by earlier builds, so replaying needs the store contents\nrather than a delta. The render backend now writes DlStores with the frame,\nbeside data-stores, and the scene builder writes its DlBuilderMap and\nSceneDlStores with the scene, beside interners. On load the render backend\nrestores its stores and sends the other two to the scene builder ahead of\nLoadScenes, so the rebuilt scene finds the namespaces its pipelines had\ninstead of being handed fresh ones; the fresh allocation stays as the\nfallback for a pipeline the map does not know.\n\nThe two snapshots are taken by different threads at different moments, the\nsame skew DataStores::reconcile_from_interners papers over for the interners.\nOnly the namespaces can be reconciled here, since the entries' keys live in\nthe content process: DlStore::reconcile opens and closes namespaces to match\nthe restored map and takes its generations, so a later Open or Close from the\nreplayed stream lands on the state the map describes.\n\nWith the type lists still empty every store is a struct with no fields, so\nthe captures gain three near-empty files and nothing renders differently;\nwrench's rawtest round-trips a capture through the new path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329663\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/dl_interner.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs"], "git_node": "03dd099393e0a528e472238af751e86acbd933cb", "git_parents": ["6ba0106eb5cf8350074c927acf8ffec9dd5ce8d0"], "node": "012a059561fc18a6b9bfbbee8ab1fa6885dd8301", "parents": ["10b57165d97f4bcc2583e0a67f4f7b2996f25eb0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073987 - Enable -Wthread-safety-pointer warnings. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nclang's -Wthread-safety-pointer warning warns when passing or returning\npointers to guarded data:\n\nhttps://releases.llvm.org/21.1.0/tools/clang/docs/DiagnosticsReference.html#wthread-safety-pointer\n\nIt was added in clang 21 and will be enabled by default under\n-Wthread-safety in a future clang release:\n\nhttps://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/127396\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329366\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/warnings.configure"], "git_node": "393199dfbacb5eaa0da7862037c0936217642ebf", "git_parents": ["03dd099393e0a528e472238af751e86acbd933cb"], "node": "ec7777ed09ed92c46bf8988e0be7cc48a1182c70", "parents": ["012a059561fc18a6b9bfbbee8ab1fa6885dd8301"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050211 - Make test 1780191-1.svg not rely on WebRender's incorrect snapping of SVG rectangles. r-#gfx-reviewers r=layout-reviewers,tnikkel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326213\n", "files": ["layout/reftests/bugs/1780191-1-ref.svg", "layout/reftests/bugs/1780191-1.svg", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list"], "git_node": "99954a8b51e8a932e81425474b6d7f1b3aa224f3", "git_parents": ["393199dfbacb5eaa0da7862037c0936217642ebf"], "node": "96b6b06c941437f6f589f5521655b7a980f4a3f0", "parents": ["ec7777ed09ed92c46bf8988e0be7cc48a1182c70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050211 - Wire up AA for primitives that have the ANTIALIASING flag. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThis used to work and got lost at some point.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310361\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs"], "git_node": "b2ee5d72aa069e32591882ef738e5569973480a6", "git_parents": ["99954a8b51e8a932e81425474b6d7f1b3aa224f3"], "node": "9cfb809e3696a75f232096d6b6c166bd8048569f", "parents": ["96b6b06c941437f6f589f5521655b7a980f4a3f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050211 - Dont't snap anti-aliased primitives. r=gw\n\nAn anti-aliased SVG shape keeps its exact sub-pixel edges instead of\nlanding on the device pixel grid, so an edge that used to be crisp is\nresolved by the shader. Where the reference draws the same geometry at\na snapped position, what is left is a seam one pixel wide along that\nedge. Fuzz the web-platform tests where that shows up. The ranges start\nat 0, so they also hold where the edge still falls on a whole pixel.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310363\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-position-svg-001e.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-position-svg-001o.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-position-svg-002e.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-position-svg-002o.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/painting/inline-svg-resize-viewport-dependent-mask.html.ini"], "git_node": "69939a86f564760c7d6ba6e3993e16b64a79da4f", "git_parents": ["b2ee5d72aa069e32591882ef738e5569973480a6"], "node": "6f946494774fff7adb0f09a122b44881226edd43", "parents": ["9cfb809e3696a75f232096d6b6c166bd8048569f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050211 - Add a wrench test. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310362\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/antialiased-ref.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/antialiased.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs"], "git_node": "f7467f88e7c87cf763779fbdcf566a45a64d1f1f", "git_parents": ["69939a86f564760c7d6ba6e3993e16b64a79da4f"], "node": "c2d3281571304ae974d7b3ff442e2d0a14a3df87", "parents": ["6f946494774fff7adb0f09a122b44881226edd43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050211 - Quantize reference frame origins in device space, not local space. r=gw\n\nThe 1/128 px quantization of reference frame origins (added to keep float\nnoise from the external scroll offset round-trip off the device-pixel snap\ntie) was applied to origin_in_parent_reference_frame at scene build time, in\nthe parent frame's local units. Under a scaled ancestor those units are not\ndevice pixels: SVG content sits under the outer \u003csvg\u003e's viewBox transform,\nso a rect with a CSS transform gets a nested reference frame whose origin\nis quantized to 1/128 of a user unit, i.e. scale/128 device pixels. With\nanti-aliased primitives no longer snapped, that error becomes visible.\n\nMove the quantization to the places where a device-space offset is about to\nbe rounded to a device pixel: snap_offset(), and the should_snap round of\nthe accumulated ScaleOffset in update_transform(). That keeps the snap-tie\nprotection while leaving unsnapped content at its exact position.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326214\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/spatial_node.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reference-frame-origin-scaled-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reference-frame-origin-scaled.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reftest.list"], "git_node": "7e1f5b7ab007a1015eca8cd27ba453721515f0b9", "git_parents": ["f7467f88e7c87cf763779fbdcf566a45a64d1f1f"], "node": "ce3486c8f05a2034361cc8961433cd12954b02f7", "parents": ["c2d3281571304ae974d7b3ff442e2d0a14a3df87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050211 - Honour shape-rendering: crispEdges for WebRender SVG rects. r=firefox-svg-reviewers,longsonr\n\nwhen crispEdges is used the primitive should not be anti-aliased.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326215\n", "files": ["layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "9968267c7a661cde857d5c8673312dbc7eae2d16", "git_parents": ["7e1f5b7ab007a1015eca8cd27ba453721515f0b9"], "node": "42eda121b0f550c915da644dc897500dffc2d238", "parents": ["ce3486c8f05a2034361cc8961433cd12954b02f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050211: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "d3351290b8fbdcc496eea75f2b94d2109977c061", "git_parents": ["9968267c7a661cde857d5c8673312dbc7eae2d16"], "node": "f495ab9bf02da74ae2fa21cc57fac75a838d5abf", "parents": ["42eda121b0f550c915da644dc897500dffc2d238"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078285 - allow afterEach to run if test body fails and added tests r=beth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330842\n", "files": ["testing/modules/Mochia.js", "testing/modules/tests/xpcshell/test_mochia.js", "testing/modules/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "6b6ba0c8a308f2cae7ea8ba256b1f5a8e84fec72", "git_parents": ["d3351290b8fbdcc496eea75f2b94d2109977c061"], "node": "8a407c325955d034044f906dc24d4ddbdf62401c", "parents": ["f495ab9bf02da74ae2fa21cc57fac75a838d5abf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078331 Part 1 - Move compensatingForScroll closer to its first usage. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330816\n", "files": ["layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "836f7859ab9053895abd843346ca38fdaa657c57", "git_parents": ["6b6ba0c8a308f2cae7ea8ba256b1f5a8e84fec72"], "node": "9d754005e5d24aae0209258b5346381cee6401be", "parents": ["8a407c325955d034044f906dc24d4ddbdf62401c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078331 Part 2 - Remove the redundant UpdateOverflow() call in UpdateScrollShift(). r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nA frame's overflow areas are relative to the frame itself, so moving the frame\nvia `SetPosition()` doesn't change them. Only its parent's overflow areas change,\nwhich is already handled by existing code.\n\nUsing `TRANSFORM_CHANGED` on `aPositioned` does not work, because it can trigger\n\"InitialOverflowProperty must be set first.\" assertion in\n`OverflowChangedTracker::Flush()` when `aPositioned` doesn't have any\ntransforms.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330817\n", "files": ["layout/base/AnchorPositioningUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "a5a033561ba2f12f47751b23a923edecc9149ddd", "git_parents": ["836f7859ab9053895abd843346ca38fdaa657c57"], "node": "4611b473fd1f4004b8d35a4eb68da439a01eab53", "parents": ["9d754005e5d24aae0209258b5346381cee6401be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2016487 - Cap gradient stop count so quad gradient data fits in one GPU buffer row. r=nical\n\nQuad gradient patterns write their parameters, colors and offset tree into a\nsingle GPU buffer row, which overflows at 721 stops. The shaders (including\nSWGL's span path) rely on the data being contiguous within a row, so subsample\nthe stops down to MAX_GRADIENT_STOPS when building the gradient templates.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329824\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/gradient.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/crash/gradient-many-stops.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/crash/reftest.list"], "git_node": "6601eefda92fa5bc2d669cf44d94bdda58760730", "git_parents": ["a5a033561ba2f12f47751b23a923edecc9149ddd"], "node": "fba2264fb2831ca776d186264dbcd569cf41a85b", "parents": ["4611b473fd1f4004b8d35a4eb68da439a01eab53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072379 - Add test; r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324886\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/fullscreen/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/fullscreen/test_fullscreen_iframe_multiple.html"], "git_node": "d123a65eb415d8155b98c71d7a16ea94488a982a", "git_parents": ["6601eefda92fa5bc2d669cf44d94bdda58760730"], "node": "95b1e9ed969cee17aadc2d8e3bfe7ba2debe6868", "parents": ["fba2264fb2831ca776d186264dbcd569cf41a85b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078261 - Update gleam to upstream 0.16. r=gfx-reviewers,supply-chain-reviewers,gw\n\nBug 2059717 switched us to a fork of gleam in order to include\nhttps://github.com/servo/gleam/pull/235. This has now been merged and\ngleam 0.16.0 has been released, so this patch switches back to the\nlatest crates.io version.\n\nNote we also switched to a fork of gl_generator at the same time, in\norder to avoid pathologically slow arm PGO compile times with the\ngleam update. This issue has not yet been resolved so we must continue\nusing the fork of gl_generator.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330779\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "gfx/webrender_bindings/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/Cargo.toml", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "supply-chain/config.toml", "third_party/rust/gleam/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/gleam/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/gleam/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/gleam/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/gleam/Cargo.toml.orig"], "git_node": "c19dcdbbe0b10f65302f68c6b9848249c1489241", "git_parents": ["d123a65eb415d8155b98c71d7a16ea94488a982a"], "node": "1485456273f5d62d9a86549328b69a53afd50db1", "parents": ["95b1e9ed969cee17aadc2d8e3bfe7ba2debe6868"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077978 - Update intellij-markdown to version 0.7.16. r=android-reviewers,adhingra\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330623\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml"], "git_node": "c2e3a28751ef0b8e4750da022664cfa738f6737f", "git_parents": ["c19dcdbbe0b10f65302f68c6b9848249c1489241"], "node": "9793770a009d07a037b34b0c501d4fcd28ba403d", "parents": ["1485456273f5d62d9a86549328b69a53afd50db1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2050211: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing wrench tests failures at reftests/border\n\nThis reverts commit d3351290b8fbdcc496eea75f2b94d2109977c061.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2050211 - Honour shape-rendering: crispEdges for WebRender SVG rects. r=firefox-svg-reviewers,longsonr\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9968267c7a661cde857d5c8673312dbc7eae2d16.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2050211 - Quantize reference frame origins in device space, not local space. r=gw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7e1f5b7ab007a1015eca8cd27ba453721515f0b9.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2050211 - Add a wrench test. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\"\n\nThis reverts commit f7467f88e7c87cf763779fbdcf566a45a64d1f1f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2050211 - Dont't snap anti-aliased primitives. r=gw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 69939a86f564760c7d6ba6e3993e16b64a79da4f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2050211 - Wire up AA for primitives that have the ANTIALIASING flag. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\"\n\nThis reverts commit b2ee5d72aa069e32591882ef738e5569973480a6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2050211 - Make test 1780191-1.svg not rely on WebRender's incorrect snapping of SVG rectangles. r-#gfx-reviewers r=layout-reviewers,tnikkel\"\n\nThis reverts commit 99954a8b51e8a932e81425474b6d7f1b3aa224f3.\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/spatial_node.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/antialiased-ref.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/antialiased.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reference-frame-origin-scaled-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reference-frame-origin-scaled.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs", "layout/reftests/bugs/1780191-1-ref.svg", "layout/reftests/bugs/1780191-1.svg", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list", "layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-position-svg-001e.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-position-svg-001o.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-position-svg-002e.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-position-svg-002o.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/painting/inline-svg-resize-viewport-dependent-mask.html.ini"], "git_node": "6ceb77c688a97b68486058ad468bfd23b349a769", "git_parents": ["c2e3a28751ef0b8e4750da022664cfa738f6737f"], "node": "104960ec3e34908619299c6c8dfa987047628090", "parents": ["9793770a009d07a037b34b0c501d4fcd28ba403d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Caleb Chan \u003ccachan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077358 - Show the calculator snake game overlay in the top layer above the results dropdown. r=urlbar-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,adw,dao\n\nSince bug 2022527 only the view is a popover, so the overlay's z-index can no longer lift it above the view. Make the overlay its own popover, anchored to the input container.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330306\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css"], "git_node": "aea0b77f44b1089107882a1fb63e90e5494b1545", "git_parents": ["6ceb77c688a97b68486058ad468bfd23b349a769"], "node": "2e59583a41bbbc38967af6cf96fb21a2fdc6ab31", "parents": ["104960ec3e34908619299c6c8dfa987047628090"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1735401 - EXT_texture_norm16 webgl feature - remove obsolete guards and don't accept unsized RGBA r=lsalzman,gfx-reviewers\" for causing mochitest core-nofis failures at EXT_texture_norm16\n\nThis reverts commit 6588d85910cdddc0c801b2da250da3db0694fe6c.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLExtensions.cpp", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/generated/generated-mochitest-webgl2-core-conformance2.toml", "gfx/gl/GLContextFeatures.cpp"], "git_node": "e4aa43167c5ab3ccee6466f934bf579a5b44b9ad", "git_parents": ["aea0b77f44b1089107882a1fb63e90e5494b1545"], "node": "15f703446e44c744031043f755fe71f58521c25e", "parents": ["2e59583a41bbbc38967af6cf96fb21a2fdc6ab31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076484 - Move Chrome bookmark tree merging into ChromeMigrationUtils and add unit tests. r=migration-reviewers,Gijs\n\nThis moves the `mergeChromeBookmarkChildren` helper from ChromeProfileMigrator.sys.mjs into\n`ChromeMigrationUtils.mergeBookmarkChildren`, so thatit can be unit tested directly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330893\n", "files": ["browser/components/migration/ChromeMigrationUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/ChromeProfileMigrator.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/tests/unit/test_ChromeMigrationUtils.js"], "git_node": "c960d3b26ddbc4bffab4b907fd04f921b798eb3f", "git_parents": ["e4aa43167c5ab3ccee6466f934bf579a5b44b9ad"], "node": "65c6b9c2a57ad0ef5e2995538aa0ba6c962384a0", "parents": ["15f703446e44c744031043f755fe71f58521c25e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070177 - Make Show all / Show less shortcut button announce state change r=android-reviewers,gl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325130\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/topsites/TopSites.kt"], "git_node": "418e91ca1d8f313848905edf46a093c7431a5848", "git_parents": ["c960d3b26ddbc4bffab4b907fd04f921b798eb3f"], "node": "134d7f17d18ea098ddf7a6867b48c6484407fd26", "parents": ["65c6b9c2a57ad0ef5e2995538aa0ba6c962384a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078392 - Remove the unused cursor variable from MasonryLayout (Coverity CID 1702489) r=layout-reviewers,TYLin\n\nIts only read went away with the legacy masonry syntax in bug 2077170.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330905\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "74cb6bcb3b3419b27734340c1d3799f5b0da23b2", "git_parents": ["418e91ca1d8f313848905edf46a093c7431a5848"], "node": "edb5701be228781b1c9c9ad591330f74110616ea", "parents": ["134d7f17d18ea098ddf7a6867b48c6484407fd26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077974 - Drop the Python bytes repr from xz-embedded's moz.yaml r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe revision was written as b'...' by a mach vendor that has since been fixed, and the SBOM carried it into the component version and purl.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330614\n", "files": ["modules/xz-embedded/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "a7a467e6c19b71a430a271ea7c36e0550a7a2de0", "git_parents": ["74cb6bcb3b3419b27734340c1d3799f5b0da23b2"], "node": "ac4f9aed52b9ca2bfa5d2842a4edbdb32abc6bd6", "parents": ["edb5701be228781b1c9c9ad591330f74110616ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077975 - Turn Cargo's legacy MIT/Apache-2.0 license syntax into an SPDX expression in the SBOM r=ahochheiden,mach-reviewers\n\nSixty-seven vendored crates still use it, and the SBOM recorded each as a free-text license name nobody can match.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330615\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_cargo.py"], "git_node": "686bdc12e52f004771326a1a9bb82cbe14d2d69f", "git_parents": ["a7a467e6c19b71a430a271ea7c36e0550a7a2de0"], "node": "d17118bbc4414734cb506e6dfeceb523bd777f4b", "parents": ["ac4f9aed52b9ca2bfa5d2842a4edbdb32abc6bd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077976 - License an SBOM notice component by its title when it has no SPDX id r=ahochheiden,mach-reviewers\n\nThe JPNIC notice has no SPDX id, so its component was emitted with no license at all.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330616\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom.py"], "git_node": "500dbe3af9fb94ef65a9e0d72bfdd398b9ed5f85", "git_parents": ["686bdc12e52f004771326a1a9bb82cbe14d2d69f"], "node": "9cb34487165f7c168ae5536ec109ea9bb95ec01a", "parents": ["d17118bbc4414734cb506e6dfeceb523bd777f4b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077977 - Map unambiguous Python license names to SPDX ids in the build tooling SBOM r=ahochheiden,mach-reviewers\n\nValues such as \"APL 2\" and \"MPL2\" each name one license, but were recorded as free text nobody can match.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330617\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_python.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_python.py"], "git_node": "dddd1229fc7067c211af7f46f8b41d4804636586", "git_parents": ["500dbe3af9fb94ef65a9e0d72bfdd398b9ed5f85"], "node": "4e0f01fd843255b5163811104f536182877d06a1", "parents": ["9cb34487165f7c168ae5536ec109ea9bb95ec01a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076267 - Ensure proper node iteration. r=keithamus\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330606\n", "files": ["dom/base/NodeIterator.cpp", "dom/base/NodeIterator.h"], "git_node": "26da06ebb689a513d38cb6a8d373c6f85c01db68", "git_parents": ["dddd1229fc7067c211af7f46f8b41d4804636586"], "node": "c8640d4ec4c2ba7c35479dfd55f005fdf6224c92", "parents": ["4e0f01fd843255b5163811104f536182877d06a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075248 - Set MOZ_GENERATE_SBOM on linux64-reproduced/opt to match linux64-shippable/opt r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe reproducible-linux64 diffoscope task compares build-linux64-shippable/opt with build-linux64-reproduced/opt. The shippable build now sets MOZ_GENERATE_SBOM=1 but the reproduced build does not. Because MOZ_GENERATE_SBOM is an env configure option, it is recorded in the configure options in chrome/toolkit/content/global/buildconfig.html, so omni.ja differs (only by that 20-byte string, as the diff in comment 1 shows).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328851\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/build/linux.yml"], "git_node": "256fec0a0f0f1749c819749bfc240f6b20299a10", "git_parents": ["26da06ebb689a513d38cb6a8d373c6f85c01db68"], "node": "1d362276e8b38e446dc0b1803ba9e452baf4a177", "parents": ["c8640d4ec4c2ba7c35479dfd55f005fdf6224c92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073555 - Teach jsdoc the TypeScript type syntax our comments use r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nOur JSDoc comments are type-checked by TypeScript, so they are written in\nTypeScript type syntax. jsdoc parses a type expression with catharsis,\nwhich only understands Closure syntax and rejects a type predicate\n(`element is MozTabbrowserTab`), a generic (`Values\u003ctypeof X\u003e`), an\nindexed access (`Foo[keyof Foo]`), a tuple, an arrow type, an `import()`\ntype and a postfix `[]`.\n\nEach rejection logs a build ERROR -- 627 of them -- and makes jsdoc drop\nthe whole tag, name and description along with the type, so the parameter\nor return value the comment documented is missing from the rendered page\nentirely.\n\nAnything is a valid Closure type name once quoted, so this plugin wraps\nthe expressions catharsis rejects before it sees them and unwraps them\nagain on the doclet, leaving the page showing the type the author wrote.\nA multi-line expression is padded back out to the number of lines it took\nup so that nothing else in the file is renumbered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327414\n", "files": ["docs/jsdoc-plugins/accept-typescript-types.mjs", "docs/jsdoc.json"], "git_node": "98757c184cbabb56ba4f66749ebb7d35b40b115d", "git_parents": ["256fec0a0f0f1749c819749bfc240f6b20299a10"], "node": "3b9e0413eaecbf8e8e77dc7a2dd09a6373327a11", "parents": ["1d362276e8b38e446dc0b1803ba9e452baf4a177"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Katherine Ye \u003ckye@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043007 - Continue display-list traversal after line clamping for visible out-of-flow descendants. r=dshin,layout-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325472\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-013.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-014.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-016.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-013.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-014.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/webkit-line-clamp-abspos-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-024.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-025.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-026.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-popover-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-abspos-024-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-popover-001-ref.html"], "git_node": "48a357a3441b76487e859d94b734dcdce1eb7874", "git_parents": ["98757c184cbabb56ba4f66749ebb7d35b40b115d"], "node": "1d2868a0480c0d1757b7f8c53d89334209d6b653", "parents": ["3b9e0413eaecbf8e8e77dc7a2dd09a6373327a11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erich Gubler \u003cerichdongubler@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078159 - fix(wpt): point accidentally duped `tests/webgl` component entry to `webgpu` r=webgpu-reviewers,jimb\n\nWhen it was introduced in D209467, this dupe entry accidentally regressed the classification of `webgl` tests to point to `webgpu`, with `webgpu` tests simply never being classified correctly. Fix it with `s/webgl/webgpu` in the path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330712\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/moz.build"], "git_node": "57281d0c889206a39db4510aca87fa6a862a2111", "git_parents": ["48a357a3441b76487e859d94b734dcdce1eb7874"], "node": "223c1dc3a1987a7743e00f776d8878e3fbc66ef3", "parents": ["1d2868a0480c0d1757b7f8c53d89334209d6b653"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074227 - Part 1: Accept a default top sites provider in DefaultTopSitesStorage r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\n- The default top sites backfill the slots that are left over once the pinned and frecent top sites have been added, and are skipped when they are already present.\n- Nothing passes a provider yet, so there is no behaviour change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327993\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/top-sites/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/top/sites/DefaultTopSitesStorage.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/top-sites/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/top/sites/DefaultTopSitesStorageTest.kt"], "git_node": "c1a9883baa0a79d11bec8a4f0654df7891dc5209", "git_parents": ["57281d0c889206a39db4510aca87fa6a862a2111"], "node": "289c1d6c1b8c7c17ea43f88c7398df919c8e48d7", "parents": ["223c1dc3a1987a7743e00f776d8878e3fbc66ef3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076356 - Fail NotifyChildCreated in ContentCompositorBridgeParent like the other child layer tree messages. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe handler was only used by nested content processes, which were removed in\nbug 1522579; the message is now only sent by the parent process. Also remove\nCompositorBridgeParent::ForEachLayerTreeStateUnderLock, which has no other\ncaller.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330629\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/ContentCompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/ContentCompositorBridgeParent.h"], "git_node": "a7c93bd80447d14e65994f1bacf37aba83d51399", "git_parents": ["c1a9883baa0a79d11bec8a4f0654df7891dc5209"], "node": "cab510e04fd68710f28fe0c4bef059e9367f1434", "parents": ["289c1d6c1b8c7c17ea43f88c7398df919c8e48d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1751335: Select the clicked word or link when opening the context menu. r=masayuki,extension-reviewers,search-reviewers,layout-reviewers,pdahiya,robwu\n\nThe original patch is Nishu Sheth's work, relanded here with the four causes of its backout fixed.\n\nDeciding this on mouse down cannot work for links, because MoveCaretToEventPoint() returns early for draggable non-editable content and every link with a URI is draggable. Doing it on the contextmenu event puts the word and link cases behind one set of checks, and keeps a click inside an existing selection from replacing it. The selection is made after the page has handled the event, and not at all if the page cancels it.\n\nThe test changes turn ui.mouse.right_click.select_under_cursor off where a test asserts context menu contents that the new selection would change on macOS.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327973\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser_contextmenu.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser_copy_link_to_highlight.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser_right_click_select.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser_view_image.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-sync/browser_contextmenu_sendpage.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_browserAction_contextMenu.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_menus_events.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_menus_incognito.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_menus_replace_menu.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_menus_targetElement_shadow.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_pageAction_contextMenu.js", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_page.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/browser_contentContextMenu.js", "dom/events/test/test_selection_after_right_click.html", "layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.h", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_editing_contextmenu.js"], "git_node": "9799184a5acae0dc0b3c9f4df4f6cc3bddf0c978", "git_parents": ["a7c93bd80447d14e65994f1bacf37aba83d51399"], "node": "f99caa7fce2d7f52cbc54187c70be4b3ba5dd9d7", "parents": ["cab510e04fd68710f28fe0c4bef059e9367f1434"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078004 - Skip polling a process for WebRTC stats history while its previous reply is outstanding. r=webrtc-reviewers,ng,jib\n\nGatherHistory requested stats from the parent and from every content process\nthat has created an RTCPeerConnection on each tick of its repeating timer,\nwithout waiting for the replies to the previous request. When handling the\nreplies took longer than the poll interval, requests piled up and kept the\nparent main thread busy.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330625\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/WebrtcGlobalInformation.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/WebrtcGlobalParent.h"], "git_node": "1bc3ef9fb160da072d311a127096ad32fd58c27f", "git_parents": ["9799184a5acae0dc0b3c9f4df4f6cc3bddf0c978"], "node": "66eefa34c095478b1310c9d384232a5050fd1bfd", "parents": ["f99caa7fce2d7f52cbc54187c70be4b3ba5dd9d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066931 - Drop QR scan results that arrive after QrFeature has stopped. r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nQrFeature.stop() clears the scan listener, but a result that was already on\nits way still went to the old listener. Results now check the listener when\nthey arrive and are dropped if it has been cleared.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329047\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/qr/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/qr/QrFragment.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/qr/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/qr/QrFragmentTest.kt"], "git_node": "20aa94eda50449c553d044fc4163b71a45ac0df7", "git_parents": ["1bc3ef9fb160da072d311a127096ad32fd58c27f"], "node": "56998f27cc5835c78d41ab5bb4f8406b490571ff", "parents": ["66eefa34c095478b1310c9d384232a5050fd1bfd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2077977, Bug 2077976, Bug 2077975, Bug 2077974 - Map unambiguous Python license names to SPDX ids in the build tooling SBOM r=ahochheiden,mach-reviewers\" for causing vendor tests failures at xz-embedded\n\nThis reverts commit dddd1229fc7067c211af7f46f8b41d4804636586.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2077976 - License an SBOM notice component by its title when it has no SPDX id r=ahochheiden,mach-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 500dbe3af9fb94ef65a9e0d72bfdd398b9ed5f85.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2077975 - Turn Cargo's legacy MIT/Apache-2.0 license syntax into an SPDX expression in the SBOM r=ahochheiden,mach-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 686bdc12e52f004771326a1a9bb82cbe14d2d69f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2077974 - Drop the Python bytes repr from xz-embedded's moz.yaml r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\"\n\nThis reverts commit a7a467e6c19b71a430a271ea7c36e0550a7a2de0.\n", "files": ["modules/xz-embedded/moz.yaml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_vendor_sbom_python.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/sbom_python.py"], "git_node": "d80de4102341ad6c59d9f6193605666006d2a8ca", "git_parents": ["20aa94eda50449c553d044fc4163b71a45ac0df7"], "node": "ea9c8db4dec50963be09ba7da23bf885437f1f02", "parents": ["56998f27cc5835c78d41ab5bb4f8406b490571ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harrison Oglesby \u003coglesby.harrison@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074588 - Part 1: Let Google Lens callers decode an image before uploading it. r=android-reviewers,Roger\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328264\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/LensImageUploader.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/LensImageUploaderTest.kt"], "git_node": "00210a4ed26d9a5f5447ef33d9889ffc9dbfabbd", "git_parents": ["d80de4102341ad6c59d9f6193605666006d2a8ca"], "node": "689996f20378943ffdd1bebc6e57bcf57e0e7fd7", "parents": ["ea9c8db4dec50963be09ba7da23bf885437f1f02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harrison Oglesby \u003coglesby.harrison@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074588 - Part 2: Let Google Lens hosts open a result the camera screen already uploaded. r=android-reviewers,Roger\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328265\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/LensFeature.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensCameraActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensImageSearch.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/widget/LensSearchActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/LensFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensCameraActivityTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensImageSearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/widget/LensSearchActivityTest.kt"], "git_node": "94f3e79e824b08c8e7d2be1fa60159e96dcfaaae", "git_parents": ["00210a4ed26d9a5f5447ef33d9889ffc9dbfabbd"], "node": "00caaba338a39d113c0ea840d28aeeff795e6e68", "parents": ["689996f20378943ffdd1bebc6e57bcf57e0e7fd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harrison Oglesby \u003coglesby.harrison@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074588 - Part 3: Add the Google Lens upload loading screen. r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,Roger\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328266\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensUploadLoadingScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensUploadLoadingScreenTest.kt"], "git_node": "d28e11099ab319780b0bcc69fb6f34614bb42534", "git_parents": ["94f3e79e824b08c8e7d2be1fa60159e96dcfaaae"], "node": "0ddf0b28b3f6bf64efd8b9aedce88da875faba23", "parents": ["00caaba338a39d113c0ea840d28aeeff795e6e68"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harrison Oglesby \u003coglesby.harrison@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074588 - Part 4: Show the loading screen while a photo picker image uploads to Google Lens. r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,Roger\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328267\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/GoogleLensSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/GoogleLensSearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensCameraActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensImageSearch.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensUploadOverlay.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensUploadViewModel.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/widget/LensSearchActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/activity_lens_camera.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/LensFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensCameraActivityTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensImageSearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensUploadViewModelTest.kt"], "git_node": "388aa63114a683e4ed1694af74e8c84f163084b6", "git_parents": ["d28e11099ab319780b0bcc69fb6f34614bb42534"], "node": "f49234787ff1473f7cbd9e81efe60e8db816b9ca", "parents": ["0ddf0b28b3f6bf64efd8b9aedce88da875faba23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078227 - Run the l10n bumper weekly on mozilla-esr153. r=releng-reviewers,bhearsum DONTBUILD\n\nSame Sunday schedule and l10n-bump config as mozilla-release.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330843\n", "files": [".cron.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/l10n-bump/kind.yml"], "git_node": "a2b2d1201a9f0f472f08fb0428ee894003d92f45", "git_parents": ["388aa63114a683e4ed1694af74e8c84f163084b6"], "node": "2f165291fd3e407f8bd323c137144201d9d4e04f", "parents": ["f49234787ff1473f7cbd9e81efe60e8db816b9ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069729 - Expect PassedNoHardwareEncoder from the sanity test when GPU encoding is off. r=gfx-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nHardware H.264 encoding is only available through the GPU process encoder, which is gated on\nmedia.use-remote-encoder.video.platform and media.gpu-process-encoder. Both default to on only in Nightly, so\non Beta and Release the sanity test correctly reports PassedNoHardwareEncoder.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330917\n", "files": ["dom/media/test/test_gfx_sanity_gpu.html"], "git_node": "928ea37dc30ffeff7e30cb591c558d684b5688f7", "git_parents": ["a2b2d1201a9f0f472f08fb0428ee894003d92f45"], "node": "70f90e0980c52e57dbfdbc2c1d7b6d26bafff5b7", "parents": ["2f165291fd3e407f8bd323c137144201d9d4e04f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maile Lucks \u003cmaile.lucks@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073300 - update viewer url to use about:smartpage, allow about:smartpage URLs to render in chat assistant r=rrando,mlucks\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328645\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/AITab.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/aitab_viewer_stub.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab_generation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_aitab_viewer.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AIChatContentParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AITabParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-message/ai-chat-message.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/TrustedInternalURLs.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_open_link.js"], "git_node": "db8841b21c23bd36e0ec34ac8f7130809af41eea", "git_parents": ["928ea37dc30ffeff7e30cb591c558d684b5688f7"], "node": "568aae5fbeca26f2dd82e7ed4c10477bbf723ace", "parents": ["70f90e0980c52e57dbfdbc2c1d7b6d26bafff5b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075619 - Allow skipping checksum verification when mozinstall attaches a DMG. r=mozbase-reviewers,whimboo\n\nAdd a `verify` parameter to mozinstall.install() and a matching\n--no-verify command line option. mozharness already checks the download\nsize, and the checksum pass roughly doubles the install time on macOS\ntest tasks, so pass --no-verify from mozharness when installing a DMG.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329221\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozinstall/mozinstall/mozinstall.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/testbase.py"], "git_node": "a3538e0169a65150c6082ac86ff9afca048d61a4", "git_parents": ["db8841b21c23bd36e0ec34ac8f7130809af41eea"], "node": "c9dd2ec4425b738b961a392691d10c4a6ef7bb53", "parents": ["568aae5fbeca26f2dd82e7ed4c10477bbf723ace"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078057 - Use a pre-indexed store for the RegExp backtrack push on arm64. r=iain\n\nSMRegExpMacroAssembler::Push decremented the backtrack stack pointer\nand stored in two steps, which on arm64 emits sub + str. On arm64, emit\na single pre-indexed str instead.\n\nThis removes 1240 instructions on Octane (4.9 KB, ~1.8% of the RegExp\ncode Octane generates). A 12-run interleaved Octane A/B on an M4 was\nflat: the RegExp benchmark median moved -0.05% and every other\nper-benchmark median was within noise.\n\nFound with armlint.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330642\n", "files": ["js/src/irregexp/RegExpNativeMacroAssembler.cpp"], "git_node": "d4d7604f0e7c2bb4c4ff0f5e035b605a05742a88", "git_parents": ["a3538e0169a65150c6082ac86ff9afca048d61a4"], "node": "07010077ac8cdb591f2294733668d61fbea1ae18", "parents": ["c9dd2ec4425b738b961a392691d10c4a6ef7bb53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078356 - Update NSS to f96edd30a0ed38bb955bbe7a0927ee2780afd2be. UPGRADE_NSS_RELEASE r=jschanck\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330840\n", "files": ["security/nss/cpputil/freebl_scoped_ptrs.h", "security/nss/gtests/cryptohi_gtest/cryptohi_mldsa_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/cryptohi_gtest/cryptohi_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/freebl_gtest/aes_ctr_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/freebl_gtest/freebl_gtest.gyp", "security/nss/gtests/freebl_gtest/manifest.mn", "security/nss/gtests/smime_gtest/smime_unittest.cc", "security/nss/lib/cryptohi/seckey.c", "security/nss/lib/cryptohi/secvfy.c", "security/nss/lib/freebl/ctr.c", "security/nss/lib/freebl/ctr.h", "security/nss/lib/freebl/intel-aes-x64-masm.asm", "security/nss/lib/freebl/intel-aes-x86-masm.asm", "security/nss/lib/freebl/intel-aes.h", "security/nss/lib/freebl/rijndael.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12d.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs7/p7decode.c", "security/nss/lib/pki/cryptocontext.c", "security/nss/lib/pki/nsspki.h", "security/nss/lib/pki/pki.h", "security/nss/lib/pki/pki3hack.c", "security/nss/lib/pki/pki3hack.h", "security/nss/lib/pki/pkim.h", "security/nss/lib/pki/tdcache.c", "security/nss/lib/pki/trustdomain.c", "security/nss/lib/smime/cmsauthenvdata.c", "security/nss/lib/smime/cmscinfo.c", "security/nss/lib/smime/cmsenvdata.c", "security/nss/lib/smime/cmsrecinfo.c", "security/nss/lib/smime/cmssigdata.c", "security/nss/lib/smime/cmssiginfo.c", "security/nss/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "fc183fe98673d8ab3862295f7de81871e4414f44", "git_parents": ["d4d7604f0e7c2bb4c4ff0f5e035b605a05742a88"], "node": "329286c4b06f56a11a193fa8f56f29e650feabfe", "parents": ["07010077ac8cdb591f2294733668d61fbea1ae18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078337 - Add newer fuzzing builds to the mocked bugbug known tasks. DONTBUILD\n\nSince bug 1649416, bugbug selects fuzzing builds in mach try auto, and tasks\nunknown to bugbug are always scheduled, so the stale known_tasks list in the\ntest data caused newer fuzzing builds to be scheduled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330946\n", "files": ["taskcluster/test/data/bugbug-push-schedules.json"], "git_node": "532a018b0cd1ff4c9fe1cdc5b62922b23dc070b0", "git_parents": ["fc183fe98673d8ab3862295f7de81871e4414f44"], "node": "fbf52e465c7d2988ef078955a1b483802d8a940d", "parents": ["329286c4b06f56a11a193fa8f56f29e650feabfe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shane Hughes \u003cshughes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078309 - Add subcategory attribute to importBrowserData prefs pane. r=settings-reviewers,Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330802\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/config/LegacyPaneMappings.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/config/account-sync.mjs"], "git_node": "b71df51f63d1203ccd2365889f0c2db071905111", "git_parents": ["532a018b0cd1ff4c9fe1cdc5b62922b23dc070b0"], "node": "832728607498803fbd5a4659f2a724e5afebe09c", "parents": ["fbf52e465c7d2988ef078955a1b483802d8a940d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070592 - Fix GMP plugin shutdown race assertions causing intermittent failures in CI. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nNo functional change besides correcting the assertions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329630\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/ChromiumCDMChild.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.cpp"], "git_node": "0ee43ba3dfc90da69ee01f8f32029434a28adf07", "git_parents": ["b71df51f63d1203ccd2365889f0c2db071905111"], "node": "a9ab013779d03c2e3035a27d59938693f747d355", "parents": ["832728607498803fbd5a4659f2a724e5afebe09c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2043007 - Continue display-list traversal after line clamping for visible out-of-flow descendants. r=dshin,layout-reviewers\" for causing web platform tests failures at line-clamp-auto-025.html\n\nThis reverts commit 48a357a3441b76487e859d94b734dcdce1eb7874.\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-013.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-014.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-016.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-013.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-fixed-pos-014.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/webkit-line-clamp-abspos-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-024.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-025.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-abspos-026.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-popover-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-abspos-024-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-with-popover-001-ref.html"], "git_node": "23cd63d8cab2b6cd9a532ec6e16b34c698336716", "git_parents": ["0ee43ba3dfc90da69ee01f8f32029434a28adf07"], "node": "b713375861ba9a343cef431ff2d466eead1ada89", "parents": ["a9ab013779d03c2e3035a27d59938693f747d355"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069154 - Add a dropdown affordance to the AI action in the selection menu. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,Mardak,sthompson,kcochrane,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nFor background on the new Highlight to Search project, here is [[ https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lpprhnIKYbXSNnVE-OSmVcE1Vpm9_vBBIKIOjW8_0lE/edit?tab=t.os3nbc21wjhe | the current spec ]].\n\nTo test this out manually, use `./mach run --setpref browser.ml.chat.provider='https://chatgpt.com'`. Then run `for (const id of [\"search-action-button\", \"copy-action-button\", \"more-actions-button\"]) { document.getElementById(id).hidden = false; }` in the browser toolbox to show the other action buttons that are part of the new Highlight to Search menu. (Those other buttons will have their behavior hooked up in later patches.) The menu appears when you select some text on a webpage.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328339\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css"], "git_node": "1c60cd9c430d6f4db38edc6cac1427a88fa68483", "git_parents": ["23cd63d8cab2b6cd9a532ec6e16b34c698336716"], "node": "da0cc238e055c01918631a4df8bf621f194c12db", "parents": ["b713375861ba9a343cef431ff2d466eead1ada89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077088: Gracefully handle races where an iframe embedder has died, but a content process hasn't caught up yet, so the parent process still receives accessibility messages related to the discarded embedder. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330319\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserBridgeParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp"], "git_node": "69384598c4b6311621a370f2d90fd281e3716f10", "git_parents": ["1c60cd9c430d6f4db38edc6cac1427a88fa68483"], "node": "74fb3aa43073dd566d3b8f4361ad3221fe3d24b2", "parents": ["da0cc238e055c01918631a4df8bf621f194c12db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077022: Ignore DOM attribute changes before the initial accessibility tree is constructed. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nAfter bug 2051694, UpdateAccessibleOnAttrChange (called by AttributeChanged) calls UpdateDocRoleMapEntry if the role attribute changes on the body or root element.\nA DOM attribute change can occur before the initial accessibility tree is constructed, since tree construction is triggered by the refresh driver.\nIn that case, mContent will still be null, which means we have an ARIA role on an Accessible with no mContent.\nLocalAccessible::ContainerWidget assumes (reasonably) that mContent must be set if there is an ARIA role.\nThus, if a client happened to query the state of a parent process DocAccessible after the role of the body/root mutated but before the tree was constructed, LocalAccessible::ContainerWidget would dereference null.\n\nThe simplest fix would be to have LocalAccessible::ContainerWidget null check mContent.\nHowever, expecting mContent when there is an ARIA role seems like a pretty reasonable assumption and there may be other code that assumes the same.\n\nAnother fix would be to have UpdateDocRoleMapEntry return early if mContent is null.\nIn that case, UpdateRootElement would be called soon thanks to DoInitialUpdate and UpdateDocRoleMapEntry would be called then.\n\nMore generally, though, it really doesn't make sense for AttributeChanged to do anything at all if the tree hasn't been constructed yet.\nIn that case, there's nothing in the tree, so there's nothing to mutate.\nThus, there's no point wasting cycles on checks that will all fail, nor potentially breaking normally reasonable assumptions like the one which triggers this crash.\nSo, AttributeChanged now returns early if the tree hasn't been constructed yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330103\n", "files": ["accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "170af7005c334708db68c558f2cfe9f23d932984", "git_parents": ["69384598c4b6311621a370f2d90fd281e3716f10"], "node": "d4b3f3354549520ee1c146ba60e46222fbf85ab8", "parents": ["74fb3aa43073dd566d3b8f4361ad3221fe3d24b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elissa Cha \u003cecha@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067868 - implement 'open tabs' action for Smart Window resume activity cards r=pdahiya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329111\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-resume-card/smartwindow-resume-card.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ToolUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_resume_card.js"], "git_node": "90f75e1e0d676a2d92b266230ac7b60c852a8257", "git_parents": ["170af7005c334708db68c558f2cfe9f23d932984"], "node": "99e2773a34ce34b98ac1df2ef04aa0aca8943770", "parents": ["d4b3f3354549520ee1c146ba60e46222fbf85ab8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076227: Fix RecvRequestAckMutationEvents on Android. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329696\n", "files": ["accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp"], "git_node": "b9d206bc5f77efed37d981df17ef86f5224c8c63", "git_parents": ["90f75e1e0d676a2d92b266230ac7b60c852a8257"], "node": "5a32650a39f58122412c9f0756ea1a5b8cfd8907", "parents": ["99e2773a34ce34b98ac1df2ef04aa0aca8943770"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2077022: Ignore DOM attribute changes before the initial accessibility tree is constructed. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\" for causing junit-nofis3 tests failures at DocAccessible.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 170af7005c334708db68c558f2cfe9f23d932984.\n", "files": ["accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "2d4413c3fac2ffa14589654d4ff17f52751b5c6d", "git_parents": ["b9d206bc5f77efed37d981df17ef86f5224c8c63"], "node": "5f678eecb37d9ff4eab03458f0480cd78eaf7cf7", "parents": ["5a32650a39f58122412c9f0756ea1a5b8cfd8907"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2072379 - Add test; r=smaug\" for causing failures at fullscreen_meta_viewport\n\nThis reverts commit d123a65eb415d8155b98c71d7a16ea94488a982a.\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/fullscreen/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/fullscreen/test_fullscreen_iframe_multiple.html"], "git_node": "14423035d6d768a75fbb1d8f4af2eb388909618c", "git_parents": ["2d4413c3fac2ffa14589654d4ff17f52751b5c6d"], "node": "48f51d4aa9fe75208b3b713626944a0e70e336f8", "parents": ["5f678eecb37d9ff4eab03458f0480cd78eaf7cf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atharva Wadodkar \u003catharva.wadodkar2003@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1999073 - Remove unused GeckoSession.Window.nativeTransfer(). r=m_kato,geckoview-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330565\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoSession.java"], "git_node": "87775f65623bd459ee2f0ecd013197041c8d2a13", "git_parents": ["14423035d6d768a75fbb1d8f4af2eb388909618c"], "node": "7adf07e54928231ba02b9b32486bb0d5755e4fba", "parents": ["48f51d4aa9fe75208b3b713626944a0e70e336f8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791259801, "git_changesets": ["b6a0839267a604c8db68a4d8d1dd497ba24887cb", "4d428444ce9c438810cbcc1695eac03121e2fe3a", "30011c7bc9d8acd6532511c41a55cede32a86adf", "61632478aac612c80f87a987f13ac0cd5bebb56b", "941f7be8a3ea57c446aeb13e40dd7451a3a1ff3b", "4375673ea1a5c9bd614366acb6d920070c2a18ca", "5fa77b923dd863e3570cf08f1c065561120abd35", "517979bee7e6d2734aae493866f4ff37bfe6e063", "9a77bf0ae132f9e52097301c853d868a44be9547", "b59c8abfb9a3d107c2686b14ef3d570cefa2ec3c", "95e0ef3dd433cf7179235b00c3ffb3162dd85751", "c5de76cbcc6d8f97c782f054a10cfff0c3c3051b", "b5db03a4b5f018d53e4e5026bb778fd7f41e2d83", "714b5cd86ba71216b2838249d3f0ec0d5e10cede", "03809552a72c66eabca8cd367d6d789487560d81", "25e86fd80bf707fd7eabb36eac8ea507b2b65cfb", "d599e23ea9391308d9cdc7420c1957500f1591e1", "e15fa23b0c09ed4d08dd18875b326c59fcfadd75", "c850f51bd50badf566dc1a42324d78faee1e2c62", "004caa70b1ad5b44e21337caf4df47b570a25f74", "e9a55ea084a1caba7fb4447a04814ee39b210ff5", "4c30cece1da4ccfd706652ede8d0eec7a339e48c", "5807cfa561bec3d51ba6bf8df36ee112cbddfd70", "bf1c47e98ce0a2214a54018c065e34105199a6da", "263339295e4694a4b9363552c6160184c69cca60", "14ceedd5e0f1695d1145a09d288bae3ed9c2f3b0", "b16b93dcb2e79f07d654002d9787632c3b2ce5ef", "715d5c0083d73dfb1378e7805c57d20836986826", "25decc525a7bcd40e090d754a3