ataEncoder GetFrame, r=media-playback-reviewers,chunmin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328204\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "33f0b2b5d2efe2c70076c9ab810395c2a7f728f2", "git_parents": ["87775f65623bd459ee2f0ecd013197041c8d2a13"], "node": "a8d1eb56b6a1bd3364a41929927cef177388b918", "parents": ["7adf07e54928231ba02b9b32486bb0d5755e4fba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070256 - Resolve A2UI data to renderable data and set up component renderers r=mlucks\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328395\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AITabParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-page.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/A2UI.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/moz.build", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_actions.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_page.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_store_integration.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head_aitab.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_A2UI.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "ac51238f68670848d89e2cd5ab870764fc0f8058", "git_parents": ["33f0b2b5d2efe2c70076c9ab810395c2a7f728f2"], "node": "df0c74a9a0a49ebbd631aa3c6147658f9d556f60", "parents": ["a8d1eb56b6a1bd3364a41929927cef177388b918"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074672 - Open mini windows clear of other always-on-top windows. r=mconley\n\nmostly mimics how pip handles tiling - i have a bug on file to eventually make a shared\nspace for these sorts of windows so the helpers aren't duplicated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328870\n", "files": ["browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_overlap.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_telemetry.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/head.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/xpcshell/test_MiniWindowUtils.js"], "git_node": "068a6c63a707f1cfa4093aa71bfe9b0dfd406c0c", "git_parents": ["ac51238f68670848d89e2cd5ab870764fc0f8058"], "node": "4d7a2c95e81e298acdc02f2df5db03ed945445b5", "parents": ["df0c74a9a0a49ebbd631aa3c6147658f9d556f60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074671 - Update toolbar hiding behavior and make urlbar editable on full tab mini windows. r=mconley,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328891\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "5991fb35343f738894e312018918062da6bfffad", "git_parents": ["068a6c63a707f1cfa4093aa71bfe9b0dfd406c0c"], "node": "b791cf1192286d0ed162ff55bddb256c0b741227", "parents": ["4d7a2c95e81e298acdc02f2df5db03ed945445b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074199 - Make ScrollToCSSPixelsForApz report whether the scroll frame is still alive. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330644\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/util/APZCCallbackHelper.cpp", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.h"], "git_node": "7f97c05f47fcb80d42a36438d0cb94c5f4ee7179", "git_parents": ["5991fb35343f738894e312018918062da6bfffad"], "node": "27497e2260dcf91c2e33c5abad9f5b0033d1c322", "parents": ["b791cf1192286d0ed162ff55bddb256c0b741227"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077022: Ignore DOM attribute changes before the initial accessibility tree is constructed. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nAfter bug 2051694, UpdateAccessibleOnAttrChange (called by AttributeChanged) calls UpdateDocRoleMapEntry if the role attribute changes on the body or root element.\nA DOM attribute change can occur before the initial accessibility tree is constructed, since tree construction is triggered by the refresh driver.\nIn that case, mContent will still be null, which means we have an ARIA role on an Accessible with no mContent.\nLocalAccessible::ContainerWidget assumes (reasonably) that mContent must be set if there is an ARIA role.\nThus, if a client happened to query the state of a parent process DocAccessible after the role of the body/root mutated but before the tree was constructed, LocalAccessible::ContainerWidget would dereference null.\n\nThe simplest fix would be to have LocalAccessible::ContainerWidget null check mContent.\nHowever, expecting mContent when there is an ARIA role seems like a pretty reasonable assumption and there may be other code that assumes the same.\n\nAnother fix would be to have UpdateDocRoleMapEntry return early if mContent is null.\nIn that case, UpdateRootElement would be called soon thanks to DoInitialUpdate and UpdateDocRoleMapEntry would be called then.\n\nMore generally, though, it really doesn't make sense for AttributeChanged to do anything at all if the tree hasn't been constructed yet.\nIn that case, there's nothing in the tree, so there's nothing to mutate.\nThus, there's no point wasting cycles on checks that will all fail, nor potentially breaking normally reasonable assumptions like the one which triggers this crash.\nSo, AttributeChanged now returns early if the tree hasn't been constructed yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330103\n", "files": ["accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "f2981b7fbf816625a72bbe35028e48993d57b76f", "git_parents": ["7f97c05f47fcb80d42a36438d0cb94c5f4ee7179"], "node": "277b390d16266c0e826d2a6723982e0afca3c6cf", "parents": ["27497e2260dcf91c2e33c5abad9f5b0033d1c322"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067689 - Part 1. Add decode/encode masking for MediaCodecsSupported to MCSInfo. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nThis will prove useful in a later patch in this series.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329317\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/MediaCodecsSupport.h"], "git_node": "89d19e3585d6bcafe62dbc30f3f46b20febce784", "git_parents": ["f2981b7fbf816625a72bbe35028e48993d57b76f"], "node": "9a2965da5906c488724a778c3cd94c0635f80504", "parents": ["277b390d16266c0e826d2a6723982e0afca3c6cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067689 - Part 2. Teach HardwareCodecCapabilityUtils to return both decoder and encoder info. r=geckoview-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,owlish,azebrowski\n\nAndroidDecoderModule only needs the decoder info right now, but\nwhen we refactor this into a set of gfxVars, we want to be able to\npull the encoders as well in one Java call.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329318\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/android/AndroidDecoderModule.cpp", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/util/HardwareCodecCapabilityUtils.java"], "git_node": "483481759fc57790bb29edf773f113aa731cb645", "git_parents": ["89d19e3585d6bcafe62dbc30f3f46b20febce784"], "node": "9e3c44539fbbff252e8054297bd8463a33ba904c", "parents": ["9a2965da5906c488724a778c3cd94c0635f80504"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067689 - Part 3. Add gfxVars containing summary of what Android platform supports. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nThis patch makes it so that we advertise what the platform supports\ninside a gfxVar. This is not to be confused with that the decoder\nand encoder modules on Android will advertise. For example, while\nthe platform may support Opus/Vorbis/FLAC, we won't generally use\nthose implementations as we prefer ffvpx. But we do need to know\nfor the purposes of EME decrypt and decode support, because we will\nuse what the MediaCodec NDK provides in that specific case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329319\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/MediaCodecsSupport.h", "gfx/config/gfxVars.h", "gfx/ipc/GfxMessageUtils.h", "gfx/ipc/GraphicsMessages.ipdlh", "gfx/thebes/gfxAndroidPlatform.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxAndroidPlatform.h"], "git_node": "1f0f1a842b9b959534fd30ad77a104018e535006", "git_parents": ["483481759fc57790bb29edf773f113aa731cb645"], "node": "6696ce640257ff60d4dee4d658cc1ffcb3fa958e", "parents": ["9e3c44539fbbff252e8054297bd8463a33ba904c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067689 - Part 4. Make AndroidDecoder/EncoderModule use the new gfxVars. r=ipc-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nThis will reduce the amount of caching we need to do in the content,\nutility and/or RDD processes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329320\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/android/AndroidDecoderModule.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/android/AndroidDecoderModule.h", "dom/media/platforms/android/AndroidEncoderModule.cpp", "ipc/glue/UtilityMediaServiceParent.cpp"], "git_node": "8b665026f16a1e5f7e1a2a3bac4fc34b9d26dff7", "git_parents": ["1f0f1a842b9b959534fd30ad77a104018e535006"], "node": "a947c039841e083bb60ae2aa15dc9a0b86089748", "parents": ["6696ce640257ff60d4dee4d658cc1ffcb3fa958e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067689 - Part 5. Make KeySystemConfig/MediaKeySystemAccess use the new gfxVars. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nThis mirrors the work done in AndroidDecoderModule, but removes the\ndependencies on Java for EME. This allows EME to work with isolated\nprocesses, as well as makes the reporting accurate. We used to\nadvertise support for decrypt only, for FLAC/AV1/etc regardless of\nwhat the platform supported. Now it accurately only supports\ndecrypt and decode for codecs supplied by the MediaCodec NDK.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329321\n", "files": ["dom/media/eme/KeySystemConfig.cpp", "dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccess.cpp", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/media/MediaDrmProxy.java"], "git_node": "4bd4a611230706960409dfc7f2edb8eaaa40dd9b", "git_parents": ["8b665026f16a1e5f7e1a2a3bac4fc34b9d26dff7"], "node": "b2eec49cebe0dd090085e4f637c988c6285d2332", "parents": ["a947c039841e083bb60ae2aa15dc9a0b86089748"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078357 - Make the bug-filing skill open the prefilled form when asked to file a bug, never submit it. r=ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330841\n", "files": [".agents/skills/bug-filing/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/bug-filing/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "4f90c1bdf4facd512f5c98d815f4d0776185c9df", "git_parents": ["4bd4a611230706960409dfc7f2edb8eaaa40dd9b"], "node": "40b1fdd35749f7a7a097dc851ab49c7fe26163f8", "parents": ["b2eec49cebe0dd090085e4f637c988c6285d2332"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077485 - Remove the dead AltSvcCache replacement on profile-change-net-restore and lock the test alt-svc map in nsHttpHandler. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nNothing has sent profile-change-net-restore since widget/qt was removed in bug 1285554; the original profile manager sender went away in bug 389671.  Replacing the cache would have destroyed an instance the TRR thread can be using, and the new instance would never have had storage because AltSvcCache::EnsureStorageInited only initializes once per process, so just remove the code.  The test mapping table is written on the main thread and read on the TRR thread, so move it into a DataMutex.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330418\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.h"], "git_node": "f99cff631d638ffc876dd128fcecf041b6ea07d2", "git_parents": ["4f90c1bdf4facd512f5c98d815f4d0776185c9df"], "node": "c2faa79c9ea72a80f4605be4dad4b1320f293fd4", "parents": ["40b1fdd35749f7a7a097dc851ab49c7fe26163f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077567 - Remove the dead profile-change-net-restore observers from nsIOService and nsHttpHandler. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nNothing has sent profile-change-net-restore since widget/qt was removed in bug 1285554; the original profile manager sender went away in bug 389671.  profile-change-net-teardown is still sent by AppShutdown and stays.  mOfflineForProfileChange is kept: it is still set at net teardown and read by IsNetTearingDown and the SetOffline guards, it just can no longer be cleared.\n\nThis is based on the bug 2077485 patch because both touch the same branch of nsHttpHandler::Observe.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330419\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsIOService.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "3e9719acdbff5e1262a48da805b74b9e1fa44cf9", "git_parents": ["f99cff631d638ffc876dd128fcecf041b6ea07d2"], "node": "88d8398b540c15ac51b03a9626499c09c2f698b5", "parents": ["c2faa79c9ea72a80f4605be4dad4b1320f293fd4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075163 - Rename SessionStore's updateSessionStoreFromTablistener to updateSessionStoreFromChild. r=sthompson,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328805\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStoreFunctions.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "425d671058cb0e8a6f076723d7f5e56ba57a4bfe", "git_parents": ["3e9719acdbff5e1262a48da805b74b9e1fa44cf9"], "node": "73b2f6121e81c9959f1e3036b593686614c9d3b6", "parents": ["88d8398b540c15ac51b03a9626499c09c2f698b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075556 - Paint the split onboarding screen's secondary section with --background-color-box-info. r=omc-reviewers,aminomancer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329288\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css"], "git_node": "79bfde6b576a7beab4d9b53f7f493e539e0f0089", "git_parents": ["425d671058cb0e8a6f076723d7f5e56ba57a4bfe"], "node": "e609cad036c11ba953e0bb38a577732a413b199b", "parents": ["73b2f6121e81c9959f1e3036b593686614c9d3b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075556 - Add panel footer color tokens for the downloads summary and the UITour tooltip buttons, and remove the dimmed background tokens. r=hjones,desktop-theme-reviewers,reusable-components-reviewers,extension-reviewers,robwu\n\nThunderbird still uses --panel-background-color-dimmed until bug 2075611 lands.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329289\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-static/browser_parsable_css.js", "browser/themes/shared/UITour.css", "browser/themes/shared/downloads/downloads.inc.css", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_themes_sanitization.js", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-platform.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/base/background.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/panel.tokens.json"], "git_node": "913f1b0d39545d35df052e949e6f8cb34fc94d3e", "git_parents": ["79bfde6b576a7beab4d9b53f7f493e539e0f0089"], "node": "61a3053315b85a6dbccb1aa73966b5aa01f65c30", "parents": ["e609cad036c11ba953e0bb38a577732a413b199b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078489 - Allow Layers.TextureYCbCrSerialization gtest to run standalone. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nWithout this, the ImageBridgeChild::InitSameProcess call crashes\nbecause of uninitialized mutexes and missing threads, when running\nthe test via `./mach gtest 'Layers.TextureYCbCrSerialization'`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330992\n", "files": ["gfx/tests/gtest/TestTextures.cpp"], "git_node": "92ead482b5a92ffdd7b3133379af072f8a6f3140", "git_parents": ["913f1b0d39545d35df052e949e6f8cb34fc94d3e"], "node": "889d168146bff3345f0c0f296ae20563e0c16f86", "parents": ["61a3053315b85a6dbccb1aa73966b5aa01f65c30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070276 - Create a standardized title typography for all widgets. r=nina-py\n\nCrossword, Picture of the Day and Weather Forecast headers used the root font size, which made them bigger than every other widget header. This adds a shared `newtab-widget-title` class in `_Widgets.scss` at the small font size, puts it on each widget's header and deletes the per-widget copies. A new widget now gets the right header by adding one class. The Recent searches title named in the bug has been hidden since bug 2063718, so nothing visible changes there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329628\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Crossword/Crossword.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Crossword/_Crossword.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Lists/Lists.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Lists/_Lists.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/PictureOfTheDay/PictureOfTheDay.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/PictureOfTheDay/_PictureOfTheDay.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/RecentSearches/RecentSearches.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/RecentSearches/_RecentSearches.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/Stocks.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/_Stocks.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Weather/Weather.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Weather/_Weather.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/WeatherForecast/WeatherForecast.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/WeatherForecast/WeatherForecast.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_Widgets.scss"], "git_node": "d78335c873aa2e887c06fb25811e297840bd2399", "git_parents": ["92ead482b5a92ffdd7b3133379af072f8a6f3140"], "node": "70c51831292b6223eb5105b3f20fbb472d4267b6", "parents": ["889d168146bff3345f0c0f296ae20563e0c16f86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076276 - Fix comment in DebianBootstrapper._check_packages_installed. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330987\n", "files": ["python/mozboot/mozboot/debian.py"], "git_node": "119f3897aff216fed093423041feaa02bcd03620", "git_parents": ["d78335c873aa2e887c06fb25811e297840bd2399"], "node": "299962f644e9f5b2233343aa8e711549607487a0", "parents": ["70c51831292b6223eb5105b3f20fbb472d4267b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074924 - Keep the Clocks widget's Add Clock form open when focus leaves it. r=nina-py\n\nTabbing out of Add Clock used to close the form and discard what you typed. I removed the blur handler, so it now closes only with Escape or Cancel, like Edit Clocks.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329790\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Clocks/AddClockForm.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/AddClockForm.test.jsx"], "git_node": "d4f0f741358396e00fa332f9720096dc4bef4344", "git_parents": ["119f3897aff216fed093423041feaa02bcd03620"], "node": "1adedb7943076df6122baa521e394da9f4803556", "parents": ["299962f644e9f5b2233343aa8e711549607487a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077412 - Make `TSFTextStore` not notify the layout changes immediately if the document is locked r=m_kato\n\nIIRC, we notify TSF of only the layout changes immediately for keeping\nthe behavior as far as possible with the e10s world. However, this\nmay cause we return error for the document lock requests if TSF and/or\nTIP wants to retrieve the new layout immediately and that may cause\nthey stop handling something.\n\nIf the focused element is in a content process, we won't do this because\n`ContentCacheInParent` flushes the notifications only when all things\nare handled in the remote process and it never happens while we're\nhandling a native keyboard and IME event.\n\nSo, the new delay should be safe because we don't have bug reports\nonly happens with web content in a remote process.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330630\n", "files": ["widget/windows/TSFTextStore.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFTextStore.h"], "git_node": "f454dcce0e8c4b685662205788acc11b544f28e3", "git_parents": ["d4f0f741358396e00fa332f9720096dc4bef4344"], "node": "3e352e869661e7f7de5831d893431d0d9527246a", "parents": ["1adedb7943076df6122baa521e394da9f4803556"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075809 - Expose the network monitor request and message lists as listboxes of selectable options, r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329402\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/messages/MessageListContent.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/messages/MessageListItem.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/request-list/RequestListContent.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/request-list/RequestListItem.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_al.toml", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_mz.toml", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_server_timings.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_service-worker-timings.js"], "git_node": "17205393ca7aec710881ee609bb1628b278f95df", "git_parents": ["f454dcce0e8c4b685662205788acc11b544f28e3"], "node": "03e2f61344e355f68c3f97f3162d02953e17ee19", "parents": ["3e352e869661e7f7de5831d893431d0d9527246a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075820 - Select network monitor requests and messages on click instead of mousedown, r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329405\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/messages/MessageListContent.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/messages/MessageListItem.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/request-list/RequestListContent.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/request-list/RequestListItem.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_server_timings.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_service-worker-timings.js"], "git_node": "0e07800efeef1710e5d1cb4d182a2f9a414bea04", "git_parents": ["17205393ca7aec710881ee609bb1628b278f95df"], "node": "03da9cb5e0b39638ed7115d91c20bbcc7ebcd84f", "parents": ["03e2f61344e355f68c3f97f3162d02953e17ee19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075369 - Select requests with real clicks in netmonitor tests, r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nNetmonitor tests selected requests with EventUtils.sendMouseEvent({ type: \"mousedown\" }), which dispatches a trusted mousedown from chrome without a mouseup. That left nsGlobalWindowInner::sMouseDown set after the test, which suppresses drag and drop in later tests once a window moves or resizes.\n\nReplace these calls with real clicks (mousedown, mouseup, click). The new clickOnRequestRow helper clicks the file cell of the row, which has no mouse handler of its own. It clicks the cell rather than the file name: a long file name overflows the cell, and at some window sizes its center is over another column or a column resizer. The new clickInView helper scrolls the target to the center of the list first: rows can be scrolled out of view, and the sticky column headers cover a row scrolled only to the top edge. Clicks aimed at specific targets (the waterfall, initiator, security tab, WebSocket messages and search results) still click those targets. The initiator is clicked near its start, as it overflows into the next column once the side panel is open.\n\nIn browser_net_security-tab-deselect.js, the mousedown on the security tab did nothing, because tabs are selected on click. The click now selects the tab as the test intended.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329162\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/src/har/test/browser_net_har_import_no-mime.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/har/test/head.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_accessibility-02.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_block-before-network.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_block-draganddrop.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_block-pattern.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_block.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_cause_redirect.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_cause_source_map.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_complex-params.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_cookies_sorted.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_copy_as_curl.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_copy_as_fetch.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_copy_as_powershell.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_copy_headers.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_copy_image_as_data_uri.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_copy_params.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_copy_response.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_copy_svg_image_as_data_uri.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_copy_url.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_cyrillic-01.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_cyrillic-02.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_decode-params.js", "devtoo