author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071998 - Fix stale-while-revalidate refreshes for HTTP redirects r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328941\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_stale-while-revalidate_redirect.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "netwerk/test/unit_ipc/child_stale-while-revalidate_redirect.js", "netwerk/test/unit_ipc/test_stale-while-revalidate_redirect.js", "netwerk/test/unit_ipc/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "425077b3ee5bf610a1216853370ed147733dc60d", "git_parents": ["0a663c2511915210918dc86255360d7d28220c1c"], "node": "643856a53fc14f08b1bbfa60eef61eaf8e578382", "parents": ["0dd4fea36300c30a4d0902fb5a57020fcb4e1851"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075770 [wpt PR 62977] - [masonry] Add RTL tests for decoration assignments in grid-lanes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] Add RTL tests for decoration assignments in grid-lanes\n\nWe don't have any RTL coverage for decoration assignents in grid-lanes\nso this test adds it\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: I0d3143accccb6cda24962898476b7bc679c831e0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8465648\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705038}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3e9f4164067f53861a39946edbf51d2fb67063c7\nwpt-pr: 62977\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-list-rtl-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-list-rtl-track-reverse-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-list-rtl-track-reverse.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-list-rtl.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-list-rtl-fill-reverse-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-list-rtl-fill-reverse.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-list-rtl-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-list-rtl.html"], "git_node": "e4f3b56db5f0e68105d36799fa7b8975f05741d4", "git_parents": ["425077b3ee5bf610a1216853370ed147733dc60d"], "node": "0996af20e575aa17fb8224a8e5b46cf108c44b52", "parents": ["643856a53fc14f08b1bbfa60eef61eaf8e578382"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075770 [wpt PR 62977] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62977\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-list-rtl-track-reverse.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-list-rtl.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-list-rtl-fill-reverse.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-list-rtl.html.ini"], "git_node": "4f06962bc88ca225b69749fcc8610d4388d9de53", "git_parents": ["e4f3b56db5f0e68105d36799fa7b8975f05741d4"], "node": "5b8a2681260b2b9fb78a17bc47045e3b97bf3d8e", "parents": ["0996af20e575aa17fb8224a8e5b46cf108c44b52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075758 [wpt PR 62970] - [gap-decorations] Fix column rule not extending when columns overflow, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[gap-decorations] Fix column rule not extending when columns overflow\n\nThis CL fixes a bug where column rules in a wrapped multicol don't\nextend past the end of the container, even when columns overflow.\n\nIn `column-wrap` scenarios where `column-height` is set, we make the\ndecorations stretch to the end of the row, even if that row overflows\nthe container. This is consistent with the spec, since in the spec we\ndefine rules to span the gutters, and in this case the gutters are\nconfined within each row.\n\nA unit test had to be updated to reflect this, it was incorrectly\nspanning the rules to the end of the container, beyond the end of the\nrow.\n\nChange-Id: Ib51c6ae1106c208226c016a8b7430a151309711a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8444947\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705060}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c6a653b0614d87618fd720d9c6c71a4b16b6e77a\nwpt-pr: 62970\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-column-rule-final-row-overflow-fragmentation-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-column-rule-final-row-overflow-fragmentation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-column-rule-fixed-row-shorter-than-container-fragmentation-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-column-rule-fixed-row-shorter-than-container-fragmentation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/multicol-column-rule-final-row-overflow-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/multicol-column-rule-final-row-overflow.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/multicol-column-rule-fixed-row-shorter-than-container-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/multicol/multicol-column-rule-fixed-row-shorter-than-container.html"], "git_node": "bc5dcfbc33e8a47441ae1829a94d3c0bf32fe72e", "git_parents": ["4f06962bc88ca225b69749fcc8610d4388d9de53"], "node": "3ef676c27d4636fbff157cd7f3c34087e235cca9", "parents": ["5b8a2681260b2b9fb78a17bc47045e3b97bf3d8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075758 [wpt PR 62970] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62970\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-column-rule-final-row-overflow-fragmentation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/multicol/fragmentation/multicol-column-rule-fixed-row-shorter-than-container-fragmentation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/multicol/multicol-column-rule-final-row-overflow.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/multicol/multicol-column-rule-fixed-row-shorter-than-container.html.ini"], "git_node": "af5756358434aa0629339dbb3c1f1bac2a2f7a43", "git_parents": ["bc5dcfbc33e8a47441ae1829a94d3c0bf32fe72e"], "node": "a8388c43bc8e0220a1c7a749327039ceec2b244f", "parents": ["3ef676c27d4636fbff157cd7f3c34087e235cca9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075764 [wpt PR 62973] - [gap-decorations] Fix rule between grid spans, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[gap-decorations] Fix rule between grid spans\n\nA bug was found where `rule` would disappear between two adjacent\nspanning grid items.\n\nThe reason for this is that currently, we mark a segment as `blocked`\nwhen the cells adjacent to it are marked as occupied as spanners.\n\nHowever, this missed the case of where the segment was flanked by two\ndifferent spanners, since both cells were still marked as occupied by\nspanners.\n\nThis CL fixes this by recording the furthest end line of an item\ncovering each cell, then block a gap only if an item extends past its\nboundary. Taking the maximum also preserves crossings when items\noverlap.\n\nFixed: 564789128\nChange-Id: I7793be1cb98aef1e741ffd2255182e9a2ffd89e2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8451626\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705080}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d6e2a6ae7bde004bc098145a011980455e5630c7\nwpt-pr: 62973\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/grid-gap-decorations-column-rule-between-spanning-items-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid/grid-gap-decorations-column-rule-between-spanning-items.html"], "git_node": "b71c70193ac01c458792e832926cc4427120a2d4", "git_parents": ["af5756358434aa0629339dbb3c1f1bac2a2f7a43"], "node": "935ed70c9ea57678a49808fdf15b806d277b2a81", "parents": ["a8388c43bc8e0220a1c7a749327039ceec2b244f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075764 [wpt PR 62973] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62973\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid/grid-gap-decorations-column-rule-between-spanning-items.html.ini"], "git_node": "268499520b874ca70099af64d332b5153e38185e", "git_parents": ["b71c70193ac01c458792e832926cc4427120a2d4"], "node": "41d41b53442278586049f84a0ebd5d8bb6f22c88", "parents": ["935ed70c9ea57678a49808fdf15b806d277b2a81"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mark a. foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075464 [wpt PR 62950] - [actor] Prevent UAF in ScriptTool and ModelContext, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[actor] Prevent UAF in ScriptTool and ModelContext\n\nWhen executing or cancelling a WebMCP tool, ScriptTool::Execute() and\nScriptTool::Cancel() previously passed execution_id_.value() by const\nreference down to ModelContext::ExecuteTool() / CancelTool().\n\nBecause ModelContext::ExecuteV8Tool() (via tool_function-\u003eInvoke()) and\nModelContext::CancelTool() (via abort_controller-\u003eabort()) synchronously\nexecute page JavaScript, the handler can destroy ToolExecutor and\nScriptTool while ModelContext is still on the call stack and holding a\ndangling reference to ScriptTool::execution_id_.\n\nThis CL:\n\n1. Copies execution_id_ onto the stack in ScriptTool::Execute()\n   and ScriptTool::Cancel() before calling into ModelContext.\n2. Passes base::UnguessableToken invocation_id by value across\n   ModelContext::ExecuteTool(), CancelTool(), ExecuteDeclarativeTool(),\n   and ExecuteV8Tool().\n3. Adds browser tests in ActorUafRegressionScriptToolBrowserTest\n   verifying synchronous frame detachment during ScriptTool::Execute()\n   and ScriptTool::Cancel().\n4. Adds web platform tests for synchronous frame detachment during\n   executeTool(), both directly and through the signal handler.\n\nFixed: 513147880\nChange-Id: I70c08e3afe425a278ce00bf4b25cb9a4a804906a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8430470\nReviewed-by: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dave Tapuska \u003cdtapuska@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705139}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 19c83fb5e314f6dbe9c5ce3a89c0f5ddac4956b2\nwpt-pr: 62950\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-target-detachment.https.html"], "git_node": "eab6e2b7a90f0d7e311b55e55d57919c7112d4fc", "git_parents": ["268499520b874ca70099af64d332b5153e38185e"], "node": "2b9f2eb9d386a98dda6a1b6d23646f0481e74cdf", "parents": ["41d41b53442278586049f84a0ebd5d8bb6f22c88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075464 [wpt PR 62950] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62950\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-target-detachment.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "80b9c6a5af5e1a22e34d4481dff9f9f7276ac402", "git_parents": ["eab6e2b7a90f0d7e311b55e55d57919c7112d4fc"], "node": "51bb9428150af0fb32c323ff70cc5249711577b9", "parents": ["2b9f2eb9d386a98dda6a1b6d23646f0481e74cdf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075776 [wpt PR 62981] - Avoid losing focus when closing submenu with Escape key., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAvoid losing focus when closing submenu with Escape key.\n\nBug: 406566432\nChange-Id: Id4190150013f62ea83086f7a55366895e6b1f7f8\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8451952\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705157}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 59e94f7725ac14eb56a92e6a33528cbb06cef206\nwpt-pr: 62981\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/focus-menu-elements-nested-arrowoperations.html"], "git_node": "0c22f8ec05a733c7797dd61ef0b0d72961d14f19", "git_parents": ["80b9c6a5af5e1a22e34d4481dff9f9f7276ac402"], "node": "5963ad68c8453fe6d21dd9e7f87204867b136d3d", "parents": ["51bb9428150af0fb32c323ff70cc5249711577b9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075776 [wpt PR 62981] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62981\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/focus-menu-elements-nested-arrowoperations.html.ini"], "git_node": "ddbf2330d85d860841c77dbc3839dc70b8a4fc29", "git_parents": ["0c22f8ec05a733c7797dd61ef0b0d72961d14f19"], "node": "d0aa5b063aaff0b93bfd87a31d5427eddfabc186", "parents": ["5963ad68c8453fe6d21dd9e7f87204867b136d3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sky Debreuil \u003cskydebreuil@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075762 [wpt PR 62972] - [css-overflow] Fix crash when scroll-marker-group position changes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-overflow] Fix crash when scroll-marker-group position changes\n\nChanging scroll-marker-group between 'before' and 'after' should replace\nthe corresponding ::scroll-marker-group pseudo-element. Blink did not\nrecognize this as a pseudo-element change, so the old group remained.\nDuring layout-tree rebuilding, both groups could try to attach the same\nmarkers.\n\nThis hits DCHECK(!GetLayoutObject()) in\nPseudoElement::AttachLayoutTree().\n\nTreat position changes as pseudo-element style changes so the old group\nis removed before the new one is attached.\n\nToggling whether the element is a scroll container also changes which\npseudo-elements exist. That is more involved and will be fixed in a\nfollow-up CL.\n\nBug: 564557265, 500793607\nChange-Id: Idfc661a8e5a9f4653c2f2c2fe0a445769d31cc48\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8395609\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Sky Debreuil \u003cskydebreuil@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705258}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 59b2b203ace9c36378a12d16dbd84312b9fb1e85\nwpt-pr: 62972\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-group-position-change-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-group-position-change-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-group-position-change-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-group-position-change-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-group-position-change-003.html"], "git_node": "29b4c77feed6691abf171ae42cbe5a87edc39e2c", "git_parents": ["ddbf2330d85d860841c77dbc3839dc70b8a4fc29"], "node": "6ada8e5f11892b9d84cfdeec3ef38497dee78b66", "parents": ["d0aa5b063aaff0b93bfd87a31d5427eddfabc186"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075762 [wpt PR 62972] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62972\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-group-position-change-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-group-position-change-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-group-position-change-003.html.ini"], "git_node": "6b436874ba0d32ecefbcf466c90e58e054418a68", "git_parents": ["29b4c77feed6691abf171ae42cbe5a87edc39e2c"], "node": "a1f52fd03e03ac64b140d39255475e4bcf16d053", "parents": ["6ada8e5f11892b9d84cfdeec3ef38497dee78b66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075773 [wpt PR 62979] - [align] output `flow-start/end` for `flex-start/end` serialization behind a flag, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[align] output `flow-start/end` for `flex-start/end` serialization behind a flag\n\nWe should be returning `flow-start/end` as the serialized value for\n`flex-start/end`. We want to gate this behind the\n`CSSFlowStartAndEndSerialization` flag in the case of compatibility\nissues.\n\nWe don't set `CSSFlowStartAndEndSerialization` as an experimental\nfeature because there are 39 existing tests which use the computed\nserialization of `flex-start/end`.\n\nThere is an upcoming change to enable `CSSFlowStartAndEndSerialization`\nthrough the `experiment` flag which updates the WPT tests checking for\n`flex-start/end` serialized value to check for `flow-start/end` instead.\n\nBug: 555299635\nChange-Id: I539c1b74b1784bd8809667ac011603f9c7fd816f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8422704\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705259}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 84b89a5fbbcd285f1ab112b74c14cb423c74c8fb\nwpt-pr: 62979\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/flow-start-and-end-serialization.html"], "git_node": "ff7c77e2d82551de7d1cffb44f57cd8f9d4eb33a", "git_parents": ["6b436874ba0d32ecefbcf466c90e58e054418a68"], "node": "673890e0bba0553905ff99414bc25c81025d93a8", "parents": ["a1f52fd03e03ac64b140d39255475e4bcf16d053"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075773 [wpt PR 62979] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62979\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/flow-start-and-end-serialization.html.ini"], "git_node": "51bf545362665adeccd49d32198430e40276a625", "git_parents": ["ff7c77e2d82551de7d1cffb44f57cd8f9d4eb33a"], "node": "520090b369ed981f83e727c1987b84526b9d587d", "parents": ["673890e0bba0553905ff99414bc25c81025d93a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075793 [wpt PR 62985] - [HiC] Rename UpdateElementGeometryOption clip to canvasClip, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Rename UpdateElementGeometryOption clip to canvasClip\n\nFor consistency that name should be canvasClip rather than clip.\nUpdate the IDL, test files and internal access methods.\n\nFixed: 565837685\nChange-Id: I582b5398018d7f7010f6b679593e645b8da81424\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8466544\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705333}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d270c14bf440a3a1912b5b25253a10e567fd77d8\nwpt-pr: 62985\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-update-element-geometry-offscreen.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-update-element-geometry.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/update-element-geometry-get-bounding-client-rect.tentative.html"], "git_node": "6d8b9732eb336abce327866c192408e4b115c2d7", "git_parents": ["51bf545362665adeccd49d32198430e40276a625"], "node": "039a2a3d74fab614b1938b1d99c4f65bc67e45ac", "parents": ["520090b369ed981f83e727c1987b84526b9d587d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075791 [wpt PR 62984] - [html-in-canvas] Add tests for reverse shadow-including paint order, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Add tests for reverse shadow-including paint order\n\nCanvas paint events fire in reverse shadow-including tree order so that\ndescendant canvases fire paint events before their ancestors.\n\nThis patch adds a test that paint events fire in reverse\nshadow-including tree order with shadow dom. Existing tests have been\nupdated to use the term \"reverse shadow-including tree order\". Also, a\ndisplay: none test has been added.\n\nChange-Id: I4ea42ab2b18e693a9679997291edb593340d5d9b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8443825\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705345}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 454c92d351cd7f54f8e7aa5373fdfffd12afe0dc\nwpt-pr: 62984\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-display-none.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-iframe-post-tree-order.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-post-tree-order-shadow-dom.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-post-tree-order.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/lint.ignore"], "git_node": "053fb6defeaf48d36ca4ae5502874f4c79f27513", "git_parents": ["6d8b9732eb336abce327866c192408e4b115c2d7"], "node": "53549365b0f4f13e1ce1d4f168714cb81bee63db", "parents": ["039a2a3d74fab614b1938b1d99c4f65bc67e45ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075791 [wpt PR 62984] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62984\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-display-none.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-iframe-post-tree-order.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-post-tree-order-shadow-dom.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-post-tree-order.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "cef56d4bd2d987f5623d999e81cd7be41c4229e1", "git_parents": ["053fb6defeaf48d36ca4ae5502874f4c79f27513"], "node": "21fab52f0189b44445f65060d63aaa9a313f4c42", "parents": ["53549365b0f4f13e1ce1d4f168714cb81bee63db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075775 [wpt PR 62980] - [Prompt API] Default samplingMode to balanced when omitted, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Prompt API] Default samplingMode to balanced when omitted\n\nWhen AIPromptAPIParams is enabled and neither samplingMode nor legacy\ntopK/temperature options are provided to LanguageModel.create(), default\nthe session's samplingMode to \"balanced\". When legacy topK/temperature\nparameters are provided, session.samplingMode remains null.\n\nAligns Chromium with https://github.com/webmachinelearning/prompt-api/pull/218.\n\nBug: 561753033\nChange-Id: Id446cffbe2c21c8c28df2cffeee60ada052d5fbd\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8448521\nReviewed-by: Reilly Grant \u003creillyg@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Isaac Ahouma \u003ciahouma@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike Wasserman \u003cmsw@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705408}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f4fa35a5bd45480664287981490d8018ee1136f9\nwpt-pr: 62980\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/ai/language-model/language-model-availability-sampling-mode.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/language-model/language-model-create-sampling-mode.tentative.https.window.js"], "git_node": "d8ee40c1769d79e31afa1f202a92a82b31ec2a02", "git_parents": ["cef56d4bd2d987f5623d999e81cd7be41c4229e1"], "node": "2d3d257129138612e4fc70cba8c35e7ff206ebf0", "parents": ["21fab52f0189b44445f65060d63aaa9a313f4c42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075775 [wpt PR 62980] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62980\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/ai/language-model/language-model-create-sampling-mode.tentative.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "04444a1a1fb034a3b901dfad40d88efef01f0afd", "git_parents": ["d8ee40c1769d79e31afa1f202a92a82b31ec2a02"], "node": "56249b435d251cb09136ff1a7d9038af3d913a3c", "parents": ["2d3d257129138612e4fc70cba8c35e7ff206ebf0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075795 [wpt PR 62986] - [HiC] Disallow external SVG content referenced by href, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Disallow external SVG content referenced by href\n\nSeveral SVG elements support href attributes to obtain the\nimplementation of the element from a template. When the\nreferencing element is inside the canvas subtree, and the\nreferenced element is outside we must disallow the outer\nelement because it does not have privacy protections in\nplace for style-based privacy control, such as visited link\ncolor.\n\nFix the problem for \u003cpattern\u003e, \u003clinearGradient\u003e and \u003cradialGradient\u003e\nand add tests. Other elements that support this form of referencing\nhave been audited. A test has been added for chained \u003cuse\u003e elements,\nwhich is not a problem due to the implementation of \u003cuse\u003e cloning\nthe external content into the subtree. The \u003cset\u003e element uses the\nattribute changed pathway so changes to href through that mechanism\nare also protected.\n\nFinally, the number of SVG privacy tests is large enough to justify\nmoving them to a sub-directory.\n\nFixed: 553147154\nChange-Id: I91d780134a32454ef4fb1adf7c03548a3a54dc23\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8455562\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705420}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a0500266d90b600fb09336409c4006ff48c516f1\nwpt-pr: 62986\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-images-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-linear-gradient-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-marker-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-mask-filter.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-mask-nested-filter.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-mask-visited.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-pattern-cross-origin-image.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-pattern-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-pattern-with-feImage-cross-origin-image.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-radial-gradient-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-use-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg-use-outside-subtree-images-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-images-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-linear-gradient-href-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-linear-gradient-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-marker-outside-subtree-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-mask-filter.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-mask-nested-filter.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-mask-visited.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-pattern-cross-origin-image.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-pattern-href-outside-subtree-ignor