- [Extensions][Chrome] Actually fix Windows path handling and errors, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Extensions][Chrome] Actually fix Windows path handling and errors\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9eb176d2fcc2c869c815debe208bb123eaa4bdca\nwpt-pr: 62534\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/resources/testharness.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/browsers/chrome.py"], "git_node": "5a34e28b6abc0bfbcdb37a9961060dfd84ba504b", "git_parents": ["ccc335bb8103ffc3c4333b52df46889fb608cc35"], "node": "167da259f0d7b36d502ac19a3c7df019ba0698bb", "parents": ["cd2eee5e0180d80099c777bbd3ffb6288400e839"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076106 [wpt PR 62242] - More \u003cselectedcontent\u003e coverage, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMore \u003cselectedcontent\u003e coverage\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12263.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b08095447cc5207285244b0b462f2367c9b64cac\nwpt-pr: 62242\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/reactions/HTMLOptionElement.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/reactions/HTMLOptionsCollection.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/reactions/HTMLSelectElement.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/selectedcontent-attribute-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/selectedcontent-nested-select.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/selectedcontent-option-insertion.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/selectedcontent-subtree-mutations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/select-ancestor-subtree-removal.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/select-attribute-change-reset.html"], "git_node": "dbd63375bc231fe5a411e02f8b59c8211c40e128", "git_parents": ["5a34e28b6abc0bfbcdb37a9961060dfd84ba504b"], "node": "76d8f0c0b80e431846c4d84e2d30c103f827f083", "parents": ["167da259f0d7b36d502ac19a3c7df019ba0698bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076106 [wpt PR 62242] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62242\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/reactions/HTMLOptionElement.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/reactions/HTMLOptionsCollection.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/reactions/HTMLSelectElement.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/nested-select-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-listitems-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-listitems-hr-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/selectedcontent-attribute-change.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/select-attribute-change-reset.html.ini"], "git_node": "b3f5aebf5b99013714fe328e392c11082072c392", "git_parents": ["dbd63375bc231fe5a411e02f8b59c8211c40e128"], "node": "c2644e8b823e216e83299e05e974bfd60a056804", "parents": ["76d8f0c0b80e431846c4d84e2d30c103f827f083"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Francois Daoust \u003cfd@tidoust.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074345 [wpt PR 62848] - Adjust URLs of ARIA specs in META files, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdjust URLs of ARIA specs in META files\n\nThe Editor's Drafts of the specs developed by the ARIA WG have moved to the\ncommon `w3c/aria` repository. This adjusts the URLs accordingly so that tools\ncan continue to map the tests with the right specification.\n\nNote: The tests themselves would also benefit from an update since they also\ntarget the former URLs. Not done here. There are redirects in place in any\ncase.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 239ed2624c287ffaa0f6917305a6bbc141d43a84\nwpt-pr: 62848\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/accname/META.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/core-aam/META.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/dpub-aam/META.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/dpub-aria/META.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/graphics-aam/META.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/graphics-aria/META.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/html-aam/META.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg-aam/META.yml"], "git_node": "2c6741f14b8fe725b3829b79cb4f10fd12cd7244", "git_parents": ["b3f5aebf5b99013714fe328e392c11082072c392"], "node": "3097f4757ea25c5633f989985a123db59fc4e79f", "parents": ["c2644e8b823e216e83299e05e974bfd60a056804"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antoine Quint \u003cgraouts@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076132 [wpt PR 63008] - [scroll-animations] make ViewTimelineOptions.subject a required member, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[scroll-animations] make ViewTimelineOptions.subject a required member (#63008)\n\nApply the IDL changes made to the scroll-animations-1 spec in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/commit/d1232f978ae92d4b4c04c9b4d5fe82cd0f5ddf86.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 088871600cd6b24f550a4b6a0b1987e8f3327db9\nwpt-pr: 63008\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/scroll-animations.idl"], "git_node": "616614caf373a46297746f10abe8665b2e76954d", "git_parents": ["2c6741f14b8fe725b3829b79cb4f10fd12cd7244"], "node": "8fd6c916aae9d42f0d8567e9f4fd7358f47eaa54", "parents": ["3097f4757ea25c5633f989985a123db59fc4e79f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076132 [wpt PR 63008] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63008\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/idlharness.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "171b3ef75fa2fa82e160d8f9fd338e0f838df281", "git_parents": ["616614caf373a46297746f10abe8665b2e76954d"], "node": "a980ec26a5fdda49093775c110cb089e93ccb0ef", "parents": ["8fd6c916aae9d42f0d8567e9f4fd7358f47eaa54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Kron \u003ckron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076099 [wpt PR 63006] - [blink] Enable Region Capture on cloned MediaStreamTracks, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[blink] Enable Region Capture on cloned MediaStreamTracks\n\nEnable dynamic sub-capture target tracking and per-track cropping on\ncloned MediaStreamTrack instances:\n\n- Update MediaStreamVideoSource::GetNextCaptureVersion() and\n  ApplySubCaptureTarget() to take SubCaptureTargetType and\n  MediaStreamVideoTrack* respectively.\n- Add OnTrackCloned()/OnTrackRemoved() hooks and protected Tracks()/\n  SetTrackSubCaptureTarget() helpers to MediaStreamVideoSource, so\n  subclasses can manage per-track targets without accessing\n  VideoTrackAdapter directly.\n- Track sub-capture targets for individual MediaStreamVideoTrack\n  instances in MediaStreamVideoCapturerSource.\n- Use the single-target GPU crop path when all active tracks share the\n  same crop target.\n- Switch to full-frame capture on GPU when tracks target different\n  regions or when uncropped tracks coexist, allowing VideoTrackAdapter\n  to crop per-track.\n- Stop delivering GPU-cropped frames to tracks that have no sub-capture\n  target. Now that the capturer alternates between the single-target\n  GPU crop path and full-frame capture, an untargeted track can observe\n  a frame that was physically cropped to another track's target, which\n  it must not be given. VideoTrackAdapter treats the presence of\n  metadata.region_capture_rect as the signal that such cropping\n  occurred.\n- Propagate crop targets to cloned tracks during track cloning.\n- Allow cloned BrowserCaptureMediaStreamTrack instances to invoke\n  cropTo() independently while preserving rejection for Element Capture\n  (restrictTo) when clones exist, and reject cropTo() while a\n  restriction target is active.\n- Add unit tests verifying independent sub-capture on clones.\n- Update Web Platform Tests and browser tests to verify independent\n  cropTo() on cloned tracks while ensuring restrictTo() continues to be\n  rejected when clones exist. The WPT subtests now stop their tracks so\n  that later getDisplayMedia() calls can start.\n\nBug: 555826257\nChange-Id: I7d4028360bac4cd110b011010819fa784164f4f2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8344692\nReviewed-by: Tove Petersson \u003ctovep@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705919}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f16736c26d98279ba50db457b2615cf032c75181\nwpt-pr: 63006\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mediacapture-streams/BrowserCaptureMediaStreamTrack-cropTo.https.html"], "git_node": "bd914ca77a8ca8580984131438db394e2eed647d", "git_parents": ["171b3ef75fa2fa82e160d8f9fd338e0f838df281"], "node": "f4e9253e3df77ac75fad6e2b39d67d2765e20e04", "parents": ["a980ec26a5fdda49093775c110cb089e93ccb0ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076099 [wpt PR 63006] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63006\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-streams/BrowserCaptureMediaStreamTrack-cropTo.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "03399ba91e58056f94cd615b21c90f2767d7996e", "git_parents": ["bd914ca77a8ca8580984131438db394e2eed647d"], "node": "4407e223b448478ee957f3f75965942fbcbae688", "parents": ["f4e9253e3df77ac75fad6e2b39d67d2765e20e04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Barry Pollard \u003cbarrypollard@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074869 [wpt PR 62872] - Set WEB_FEATURES from html-setters and html-streaming-setters, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSet WEB_FEATURES from html-setters and html-streaming-setters (#62872)\n\n* Set WEB_FEATURES from html-setters and html-stream-setters\n\n* Correct streaming name\n\n* Linting\n\n* Another linting fix\n\n* Add tentative directory\n\n* Move to tentative folder\n\n* Create WEB_FEATURES.yml in tentative folder\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b2262ae8441692882643097c07dbbeb66f83e0d4\nwpt-pr: 62872\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/WEB_FEATURES.yml"], "git_node": "ae4bc76647fe6b351bcb672c52ce03af8f235799", "git_parents": ["03399ba91e58056f94cd615b21c90f2767d7996e"], "node": "827b2ccf711f4245948daf3879908cc3df9a623f", "parents": ["4407e223b448478ee957f3f75965942fbcbae688"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076083 [wpt PR 63004] - [web-animations] Test easing on a keyframe with no value for the property, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[web-animations] Test easing on a keyframe with no value for the property (#63004)\n\n* [web-animations] Test easing on a keyframe with no value for the property\n\nTest for w3c/csswg-drafts#14492.\n\n* Use assert_equals\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 80b14d35f8f27b45666c2382aa93bfa26d017026\nwpt-pr: 63004\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/keyframe-effects/effect-value-easing-on-keyframe-without-property.html"], "git_node": "e9e7436e6a0be761ee1f5f5ce1226c2ae7c9df76", "git_parents": ["ae4bc76647fe6b351bcb672c52ce03af8f235799"], "node": "72d1e95e2be219ed13119f2039cdd03810dbf4a3", "parents": ["827b2ccf711f4245948daf3879908cc3df9a623f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076112 [wpt PR 63007] - Don't keep reference to attribute AtomicString during style resolution, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon't keep reference to attribute AtomicString during style resolution\n\nAttribute synchronization may change internal attribute storage during\nstyle resolution. Keep a local AtomicString for ShadowPseudoId() instead\nof a reference pointing into the internal attribute storage.\n\nFixes UAF crasher.\n\nBug: 565742178\nChange-Id: I00f0d4fc35594254939ad74a1734c8eda37bd2f2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8469947\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705920}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b7d7cc8a567592206dd16f6588f65da49db12bad\nwpt-pr: 63007\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/crashtests/chrome-bug-565742178.html"], "git_node": "d003404883db3af6f4864d9b43e96c97d4f4d01a", "git_parents": ["e9e7436e6a0be761ee1f5f5ce1226c2ae7c9df76"], "node": "dfb22e4a96fa5dc94babb770759bacbafb943a05", "parents": ["72d1e95e2be219ed13119f2039cdd03810dbf4a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072003 [wpt PR 62682] - layout: Stop reusing a box that has gone out of flow, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Stop reusing a box that has become absolutely positioned\n\nSigned-off-by: mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\nlayout: Assert the offsets take effect in the dynamic abspos test\n\nSigned-off-by: mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\nlayout: Stop reusing a box that has become floated\n\nSigned-off-by: mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\nlayout: Improve wording\n\nSigned-off-by: mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 792e49c1d04f35eac00ce9dda211dcc2a0217a0f, ccaaf1295bab4fc24050ac168338ca8bc4fbccfd, 954f98ac47e3979950ca9c9cbef76243db3d52cd, b48a5c3fb57854fd217421e247a4f4a0149951a7\nwpt-pr: 62682\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/floats/float-dynamic-formatting-context.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-position/position-absolute-dynamic-formatting-context.html"], "git_node": "03676d8cd34b807e2298665dcbcdef4fddb3fa1f", "git_parents": ["d003404883db3af6f4864d9b43e96c97d4f4d01a"], "node": "6a844c33397a8889418d428a1e45515ce4f38fb8", "parents": ["dfb22e4a96fa5dc94babb770759bacbafb943a05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072003 [wpt PR 62682] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62682\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/floats/crashtests/firefox-bug-1904409.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/floats/crashtests/firefox-bug-1904419.html.ini"], "git_node": "18f6c608d7f5e67cc8229da80b9c850c2fdd28c7", "git_parents": ["03676d8cd34b807e2298665dcbcdef4fddb3fa1f"], "node": "44219327379696469aa43a0f4fca98c4cde6d800", "parents": ["6a844c33397a8889418d428a1e45515ce4f38fb8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Diego Frias \u003cmail@dzfrias.dev\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073729 [wpt PR 62777] - script: Do not perform `EditingAction`s in `EditingContext`s that do not have layout boxes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Do not write to text controls if they are hidden\n\nSigned-off-by: Diego Frias \u003cmail@dzfrias.dev\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3634ba2b729fef46f8fb42b78a5cf9ba345c8639\nwpt-pr: 62777\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/editing/other/edit-in-textcontrol-immediately-after-hidden.tentative.html"], "git_node": "93a216a01243438b87b90963c9e191d1fec90e50", "git_parents": ["18f6c608d7f5e67cc8229da80b9c850c2fdd28c7"], "node": "022ad908f8eaf023a5219d627ad7e6a2be5534b4", "parents": ["44219327379696469aa43a0f4fca98c4cde6d800"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076118 [wpt PR 62999] - webgl: Return the stencil masks from getParameter as unsigned integers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebgl: Return the stencil masks from getParameter as unsigned integers\n\nSigned-off-by: mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bcd4134d88e8f9aa9abbed792bd15f6984f928d9\nwpt-pr: 62999\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webgl/getParameter-stencil-masks.html"], "git_node": "43cae91d4c4a68bb0f250247cf15789b6279efac", "git_parents": ["93a216a01243438b87b90963c9e191d1fec90e50"], "node": "a33f1583f1a61b0104b1ee82994ee64d6071a4f7", "parents": ["022ad908f8eaf023a5219d627ad7e6a2be5534b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076192 [wpt PR 63017] - Fix crash when XPath step predicate is a variable reference, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix crash when XPath step predicate is a variable reference\n\nWhen a step predicate is a variable reference (e.g. \"any[$any]\"),\nStep::Optimize() calls Predicate::IsContextPositionSensitive(), which\ncalls VariableReference::ResultType(). Previously, ResultType() hit\nNOTREACHED().\n\nSince VariableReference::Evaluate() always returns a string Value,\nreturn Value::kStringValue from VariableReference::ResultType().\n\nFixed: 564353354\nChange-Id: Ib6a77d71bc9ee48fef2bce6f8eb15fd69e2e8124\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8470028\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706173}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: afb141b9f7e9dd0f7047bce05b5a93ccf576a567\nwpt-pr: 63017\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domxpath/variables-in-expression-crash.html"], "git_node": "66991975b8326b4bf0c5d8ed2cbf4187e878609e", "git_parents": ["43cae91d4c4a68bb0f250247cf15789b6279efac"], "node": "23256f266dd49937259ae770fdbf630b039c6d98", "parents": ["a33f1583f1a61b0104b1ee82994ee64d6071a4f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076255 [wpt PR 63022] - Add Payment Method Manifest WPTs for Web App Manifest ingestion, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd Payment Method Manifest WPTs for Web App Manifest ingestion\n\nAdd Web Platform Tests covering Web App Manifest (WAM) fetching,\ndefault_applications ingestion, WAM redirect handling, and Payment\nMethod Manifest HTTP error status handling. Tests added:\n\n   - Web App Manifest (WAM) fetching end-to-end success\n   - Multiple default_applications web app manifests are fetched\n   - Duplicate URLs in default_applications are handled gracefully and\n     deduplicated\n   - Relative default_applications URL resolves against payment method\n     manifest URL\n   - Payment method manifest with non-array default_applications fails\n     parsing cleanly and does not fetch WAM\n   - Web App Manifest GET request omits credentials (cookies and\n     authorization)\n   - Non-HTTPS Web App Manifest URL in default_applications is not\n     fetched\n   - Non-HTTPS URL in default_applications fails entire manifest\n     validation without fetching valid HTTPS WAM\n   - Web App Manifest GET request with redirect aborts\n   - HTTP 404 response on Payment Method Manifest GET request aborts\n     ingestion and does not fetch WAM\n   - HTTP 500 response on Payment Method Manifest GET request aborts\n     ingestion and does not fetch WAM\n\nBug: 552832440\nChange-Id: Ia6fea5e54da652df6e931ebfb68336de7f0223c8\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8339948\nReviewed-by: Xuehui Chen \u003cxuehuichen@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706219}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 62d90b5ff1e7ac93c0e75bde48fd6ff66dadfda7\nwpt-pr: 63022\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/pmm-http-status.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/resources/web-app-manifest.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/wam-ingestion.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/wam-non-https.https.sub.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/wam-redirect-disallowed.https.window.js"], "git_node": "dc713c1bf95448748bbee4801f0dbe351eef104b", "git_parents": ["66991975b8326b4bf0c5d8ed2cbf4187e878609e"], "node": "3bb1d6c8f967c67051024253f3ace6fea8da31e9", "parents": ["23256f266dd49937259ae770fdbf630b039c6d98"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076255 [wpt PR 63022] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63022\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/pmm-http-status.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/wam-ingestion.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/wam-non-https.https.sub.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/wam-redirect-disallowed.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "1f9083c24f2c39544638525005c970fcd2a019a9", "git_parents": ["dc713c1bf95448748bbee4801f0dbe351eef104b"], "node": "52a0ef404bf93737bff6fa86931cf2e807c1014d", "parents": ["3bb1d6c8f967c67051024253f3ace6fea8da31e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075747 [wpt PR 62969] - Remove void element end tags in WPTs in css-contain css-sizing selectors, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove void element end tags in WPTs in css-contain css-sizing selectors\n\nimg and input have no end tag. Writing \u003c/img\u003e or \u003c/input\u003e anyway is a\nparse error, and the parser drops the tag. This CL removes those end\ntags from wpt/css/css-contain, wpt/css/css-sizing and wpt/css/selectors.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: I4db35c16d8b269ca55248f48af8baae5518d8afd\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8222124\nReviewed-by: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706268}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9e56f92d788601dea29caed2fd379f19c3c8ddc4\nwpt-pr: 62969\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/contain-layout-baseline-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-021.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-024-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-024.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-047.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-auto-selection-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/detach-locked-slot-children-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/reference/contain-layout-baseline-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/contain-intrinsic-size/contain-intrinsic-size-012-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/contain-intrinsic-size/contain-intrinsic-size-012.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/contain-intrinsic-size/contain-intrinsic-size-017-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/contain-intrinsic-size/contain-intrinsic-size-017.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/contain-intrinsic-size/contain-intrinsic-size-020-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/contain-intrinsic-size/contain-intrinsic-size-020.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/replaced-aspect-ratio-intrinsic-size-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/replaced-aspect-ratio-intrinsic-size-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/focus-visible-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/focus-visible-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/focus-visible-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/focus-visible-014.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/enabled-disabled.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/invalidation/has-with-pseudo-class.html"], "git_node": "21a908de9f4002f42622dc95851a0e70d13e162d", "git_parents": ["1f9083c24f2c39544638525005c970fcd2a019a9"], "node": "9cb2b5e825f68fb9cc0c8d2d83b8942baaaca701", "parents": ["52a0ef404bf93737bff6fa86931cf2e807c1014d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076162 [wpt PR 63014] - layout: Respect `text-wrap-mode` around atomic during inline content size calculation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Respect `text-wrap-mode` around atomic during inline content size calculation\n\nWhether or not there is a line break around an atomic depends on the\n`text-wrap-mode` of the containing box's style. This change makes it so\nthat the sizing code tracks that wrap mode and uses it to determine if a\nline break opportunity exists.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d394ec38cc11dc14279f5fe2b48dd978af7dee5c\nwpt-pr: 63014\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-atomic-nowrap-002.html"], "git_node": "efb133be0e9f504c66bfc2281e80302acbd331e1", "git_parents": ["21a908de9f4002f42622dc95851a0e70d13e162d"], "node": "96ee60d249f641042c4c3e9172d18e0efbc57a1c", "parents": ["9cb2b5e825f68fb9cc0c8d2d83b8942baaaca701"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076352 [wpt PR 63032] - Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAvoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\n\nFixed: 565674529\nChange-Id: Ia3248d945dc01328e8f354ec28d7cfcadafb87f3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464608\nAuto-Submit: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706396}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4beb3990d4ae38e77dc483e026f9c2434ec06f47\nwpt-pr: 63032\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/navigate-to-javascript-url-009-crash.html"], "git_node": "e9428c6ffee14e7cfeb49ff85433cf67b03a0003", "git_parents": ["efb133be0e9f504c66bfc2281e80302acbd331e1"], "node": "5dacf1e0d2d44b455734497135f42015cbd06caf", "parents": ["96ee60d249f641042c4c3e9172d18e0efbc57a1c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christian Biesinger \u003ccbiesinger@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076373 [wpt PR 63036] - Install cryptography for commands that serve tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nInstall cryptography for commands that serve tests (#63036)\n\nPython handlers in the test tree run inside wptserve, so they can only\nimport packages present in the venv that the serving command set up.\n/fedcm/support/delegation-issuance.py imports cryptography, which no\nrequirements file lists; it happens to be installed as a transitive\ndependency of aioquic in tools/wptrunner/requirements.txt.\n\nThat makes it work for `wpt run`, but not for `wpt serve`, which had no\nunconditional requirements at all. Because the venv is shared and\ninstalls are cumulative, `wpt serve` then succeeds or fails depending on\nwhether that checkout has ever run `wpt run` -- so the handler returns\n500 only on a fresh checkout.\n\nAdd tools/serve/requirements.txt for packages that test handlers need,\nand install it from every command that serves tests: `wpt serve`,\n`wpt serve-wave` and `wpt run`.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9ee707c850996c8d124809570c3ff855d67301b9\nwpt-pr: 63036\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/serve/commands.json", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/serve/requirements.txt", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/commands.json"], "git_node": "e242db53c08f87bc22d1b2525c8c494fa443a3ab", "git_parents": ["e9428c6ffee14e7cfeb49ff85433cf67b03a0003"], "node": "d84c9c530491ee7b6b770c9c0ab27eb9a8fbb73f", "parents": ["5dacf1e0d2d44b455734497135f42015cbd06caf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076190 [wpt PR 63016] - webgl: Update both stencil writemasks for FRONT_AND_BACK, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebgl: Update both stencil writemasks for FRONT_AND_BACK\n\nSigned-off-by: mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 913ae6e0493356df04fb44c939dd2d7d2c388929\nwpt-pr: 63016\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webgl/stencilMaskSeparate-front-and-back.html"], "git_node": "cf7e7231e8c82cdd9cbcf5201f3fc6e0d15ba0d3", "git_parents": ["e242db53c08f87bc22d1b2525c8c494fa443a3ab"], "node": "0d3866b3bd559cbe18006382b8c2adc8dfd5df20", "parents": ["d84c9c530491ee7b6b770c9c0ab27eb9a8fbb73f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076384 [wpt PR 63038] - [layout] Change ContainingBlock to return LayoutBox., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[layout] Change ContainingBlock to return LayoutBox.\n\nThe difference between LayoutBlock and LayoutBox has been minimal for a\nwhile now.\n\nWe have things like \"ContainingNGBox\" which we use to correctly\ninvalidate up the LayoutBox chain when we need it.\n\nThe latest issue was triggered by a LayoutReplaced object being allowed\nto have CanContainFixedPositionObjects return true, but\nContainingBlock() would skip over any LayoutReplaced objects.\n\nThis resulted in an incorrect layout invalidation (leaving the tree\nstale) during an anchor position style update.\n\nIn a previous patch we changed the return type of ContainingBlock to a\nLayoutBox - but not changing its functionality.\n\nThis patch completes the change, by allowing LayoutBoxes to be\n(actually) returned from ContainingBlock.\n\nBug: 564720399\nChange-Id: Ia7d120a691097f35cbc8053c62ad61583e1d5779\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8469756\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706438}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 27f97e5079f050286ee1b4e3f6729963c7042979\nwpt-pr: 63038\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/chrome-564720399-crash.html"], "git_node": "ce2e97fef48c2c4e37ba48efb8dd98d53306f561", "git_parents": ["cf7e7231e8c82cdd9cbcf5201f3fc6e0d15ba0d3"], "node": "f948e863bcd7a903077f0e6407827a9e19716c84", "parents": ["0d3866b3bd559cbe18006382b8c2adc8dfd5df20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076319 [wpt PR 63028] - [WebCodecs] Fix Vorbis setup in audioDecoder-codec-specific WPT, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebCodecs] Fix Vorbis setup in audioDecoder-codec-specific WPT\n\nPer the Vorbis I spec, decoders return no audio for the first packet,\nwhich is only used to prime the decoder. This also applies after a\nflush. The test didn't account for this, so two Vorbis subtests failed\neven though the decoder behaves correctly.\n\nChunks can now set their own duration. The first Vorbis chunk is given\na duration of 128 samples, and `discard_padding` is set to match, so the\nnegative timestamp test expects the correct first output timestamp. The\nflush test now queues the first chunk again after flushing when\n`packet_delay` \u003e 0, to prime the reset decoder.\n\nAll Vorbis subtests now pass, so the Vorbis -expected.txt files are\nremoved.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=a052d893-0771-4c56-a3f3-001e81510bc5\n\nBug: 512772321\nTest: external/wpt/webcodecs/audioDecoder-codec-specific.https.any.js\nChange-Id: I50cabd735d0235e0cc62f0bf662f41734b991e03\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464346\nCommit-Queue: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706488}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7da29ce14d03f5a356bd94bc67d1ada78075eb42\nwpt-pr: 63028\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/audioDecoder-codec-specific.https.any.js"], "git_node": "afd2a41887a3e47c06caedd46c563e0deac26c82", "git_parents": ["ce2e97fef48c2c4e37ba48efb8dd98d53306f561"], "node": "20596a2dbdd4183780575c21783fd08fe58c51c3", "parents": ["f948e863bcd7a903077f0e6407827a9e19716c84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joone Hur \u003cjoonehur@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076144 [wpt PR 63012] - Redact opaque script positions in LoAF promise attribution, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRedact opaque script positions in LoAF promise attribution\n\nRedact character, line, and column positions when capturing source\nlocations for opaque scripts.\n\nRequires a companion V8 change providing StackFrame::IsScriptOpaque():\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8422987\n\nBug: 562158081, 502251640\nChange-Id: Ic64040f8663b26c6ace883cc47a1e405a94e5ef4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8421802\nReviewed-by: Michal Mocny \u003cmmocny@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joone Hur \u003cjoonehur@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706573}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3b5f16ed8f1afd1fa59b27fec1d807398b41c286\nwpt-pr: 63012\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/loaf-source-location-redirect.html"], "git_node": "462ed08be8092239db542ab477eebff655c98b4c", "git_parents": ["afd2a41887a3e47c06caedd46c563e0deac26c82"], "node": "8cac0bcc217a78fb42e4e150f32f0e20167acac3", "parents": ["20596a2dbdd4183780575c21783fd08fe58c51c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Minseop Choi \u003cminsubb13@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076355 [wpt PR 63034] - [WebCrypto] Fix supports() for exportKey and wrapKey, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebCrypto] Fix supports() for exportKey and wrapKey\n\nsupports() is specified to accept \"exportKey\" as an operation, and to\nreturn false for \"wrapKey\" when additionalAlgorithm does not support the\nexport key operation. Blink returned false for every \"exportKey\" query,\nand returned true for \"wrapKey\" with an HKDF or PBKDF2\nadditionalAlgorithm even though wrapKey() rejects such keys with a\nNotSupportedError:\n\nhttps://wicg.github.io/webcrypto-modern-algos/#SubtleCrypto-method-supports\n\nMap \"exportKey\" to kWebCryptoOperationExportKey and add the wrapKey\ncheck, using the export key operation info added in\nhttps://crrev.com/c/8312049. Add WPTs for both cases.\n\nFixed: 41264071\nChange-Id: If0e60ecfc2c52ac7b2fcbbfdfbc2855c00524853\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8471207\nReviewed-by: David Benjamin \u003cdavidben@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Minseop Choi \u003cminsubb13@gmail.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Daniel Cheng \u003cdcheng@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706614}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3127c3a492e63578ed2bf76e3d4bda805183b5a3\nwpt-pr: 63034\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/WebCryptoAPI/supports.tentative.https.any.js"], "git_node": "f50984107bc57720b9eb718db53d248b396eb37c", "git_parents": ["462ed08be8092239db542ab477eebff655c98b4c"], "node": "e768b2529656622d7d6a16b804cd258493cf4ad0", "parents": ["8cac0bcc217a78fb42e4e150f32f0e20167acac3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076355 [wpt PR 63034] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63034\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/supports.tentative.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "458dbfbc7af2ce68625a6b19aa08184b30ce43d9", "git_parents": ["f50984107bc57720b9eb718db53d248b396eb37c"], "node": "b4b907cc3ca201abd6873a5d228ec0adb04795e4", "parents": ["e768b2529656622d7d6a16b804cd258493cf4ad0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eriko Kurimoto \u003celkurin@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076401 [wpt PR 63043] - Revert \"Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRevert \"Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\"\n\nThis reverts commit 280ca3161bda00f116803a7064aba3ce91a7d59e.\n\nReason for revert: Causing a failure on linux-blink-leak-rel due to\nexternal/wpt/trusted-types/navigate-to-javascript-url-009-crash.html\n\nFailure Link: https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/ci/Mac13%20Tests/42984/overview\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\n\u003e\n\u003e Fixed: 565674529\n\u003e Change-Id: Ia3248d945dc01328e8f354ec28d7cfcadafb87f3\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464608\n\u003e Auto-Submit: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706396}\n\nBug: 565674529\nNo-Presubmit: true\nNo-Tree-Checks: true\nNo-Try: true\nChange-Id: Id6e28582a83f7405347ab0ecd207748885599fbf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8482891\nAuto-Submit: Eriko Kurimoto \u003celkurin@chromium.org\u003e\nBot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nOwners-Override: Eriko Kurimoto \u003celkurin@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706622}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8e0cd746af87162610047b989c9ddf211478b009\nwpt-pr: 63043\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/navigate-to-javascript-url-009-crash.html"], "git_node": "2ff493c3dbcf6065c458318993ed215ce07a21d5", "git_parents": ["458dbfbc7af2ce68625a6b19aa08184b30ce43d9"], "node": "8b3fb5b4922c5819059e811fb7d1e8df4598e0e9", "parents": ["b4b907cc3ca201abd6873a5d228ec0adb04795e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Pieters \u003czcorpan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074138 [wpt PR 62832] - Test that inserting a source into a lazy video doesn't delay load, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest that inserting a source into a lazy video doesn't delay load (#62832)\n\nFor whatwg/html#12971.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8b6e09b0fe80243092050c92ff430a47c2d30b77\nwpt-pr: 62832\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-source-inserted-load-event.html"], "git_node": "fa2e3e11bc8ec6f21508039a23e62849bf520698", "git_parents": ["2ff493c3dbcf6065c458318993ed215ce07a21d5"], "node": "31a29ed0879f33f5e1b188804d5df5f7d6d06247", "parents": ["8b3fb5b4922c5819059e811fb7d1e8df4598e0e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074138 [wpt PR 62832] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62832\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-source-inserted-load-event.html.ini"], "git_node": "ee142766e9bec48bf4f096bde59e6694c7733284", "git_parents": ["fa2e3e11bc8ec6f21508039a23e62849bf520698"], "node": "f9369a2bbc99faf084efdb4a9dae8fae690ac3e6", "parents": ["31a29ed0879f33f5e1b188804d5df5f7d6d06247"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stalgia Grigg \u003cstalgiag@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066646 [wpt PR 62198] - [testdriver] Add test_driver.navigate(), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[testdriver] Add test_driver.navigate\n\nAdd a testdriver method matching the WebDriver classic\nNavigate To command which navigates a top-level browsing context to a URL.\n\nA context may now be given as a WebDriver window handle as well as a WindowProxy. This allows windows created by test_driver.create_window() to be navigated. Contexts were previously resolved only from a WindowProxy.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: aa7c3e6a2e4138d576fd4859f7d62bc9323ec0e3\nwpt-pr: 62198\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/docs/writing-tests/testdriver.md", "testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/testdriver/navigate.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/testdriver/navigate_target.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resources/testdriver.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/executors/actions.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/executors/protocol.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/testdriver-extra.js"], "git_node": "0df58711df5c885854e96b81cf1500825cc13a63", "git_parents": ["ee142766e9bec48bf4f096bde59e6694c7733284"], "node": "44871f1af4f198dd647aa33791402f8c99ecf7b2", "parents": ["f9369a2bbc99faf084efdb4a9dae8fae690ac3e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "wpt-pr-bot \u003cwpt-pr-bot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075994 [wpt PR 63001] - Update Test262 tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUpdate Test262 tests\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5235c9f5e8caa2e5d199ba5194093cef444d45e7\nwpt-pr: 63001\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/filter/BigInt/callbackfn-detachbuffer-kept-undefined.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/filter/BigInt/callbackfn-detachbuffer.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/filter/BigInt/callbackfn-shrink-kept-undefined.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/filter/callbackfn-detachbuffer.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/with/BigInt/index-coercion-shrinks.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/with/BigInt/negative-index-resize-to-out-of-bounds.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/with/BigInt/value-coercion-shrinks.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/with/index-coercion-shrinks.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/built-ins/TypedArray/prototype/with/value-coercion-shrinks.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/intl402/DateTimeFormat/prototype/format/german-weekday-no-year.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/intl402/Locale/constructor-unicode-extension-uvalue-true.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/intl402/Locale/constructor-unicode-extension-uvalue-yes.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/intl402/NumberFormat/prototype/format/format-significant-digits-rounding-magnitude.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/test/intl402/NumberFormat/prototype/formatToParts/significant-digits-rounding-magnitude-en-US.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/vendored.toml"], "git_node": "20d6cc7a7e2e689d22f2d45340e4d521f2101147", "git_parents": ["0df58711df5c885854e96b81cf1500825cc13a63"], "node": "0b34ba8de427465d08a508edadcea4c9902edf82", "parents": ["44871f1af4f198dd647aa33791402f8c99ecf7b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076433 [wpt PR 62505] - [wpt] Add CSP style policy enforcement tests for MathML elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Add CSP style policy enforcement tests for MathML elements\n\nAdds tests to ensure CSP style-src-attr and style-src directives are\ncorrectly checked and enforced across all MathML elements.\n\nBug: 541711729\nChange-Id: Ic6de9e6cb0beaa05d1afb9940d82df02cd24fee0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8181776\nReviewed-by: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706748}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7a8d143bce12c1142109d27a8de4b0b26f9f5a47\nwpt-pr: 62505\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/style-src-attr-meta.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/style-src-elem-meta.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/support/csp-test-helper.js"], "git_node": "72eab02bfd9c8b1cac13ca40a143d0bec691c024", "git_parents": ["20d6cc7a7e2e689d22f2d45340e4d521f2101147"], "node": "272f6159c01bd9cd660e48e1fa9ffc00a5f6fe5d", "parents": ["0b34ba8de427465d08a508edadcea4c9902edf82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luke Warlow \u003clwarlow@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075743 [wpt PR 62968] - Test moving sources within a video element, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest moving sources within a video element\n\nThis covers a case where the old parent and new parent of the source element is the same media element.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8719b8fdacb5cf56e3774f1544ecebebe936eba4\nwpt-pr: 62968\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/loading-the-media-resource/resource-selection-invoke-move-source-same-parent.html"], "git_node": "a0c9183682f989eda7db8889d1a97650ce61d576", "git_parents": ["72eab02bfd9c8b1cac13ca40a143d0bec691c024"], "node": "01e754ca13edb22cb9dfd0df2c8d1835eef5490e", "parents": ["272f6159c01bd9cd660e48e1fa9ffc00a5f6fe5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075743 [wpt PR 62968] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62968\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/loading-the-media-resource/resource-selection-invoke-move-source-same-parent.html.ini"], "git_node": "a6b6dc2b0c678f14f9f00e2ae84fa54d881217b4", "git_parents": ["a0c9183682f989eda7db8889d1a97650ce61d576"], "node": "b7e3dfbddc05f3aadafc693e4bc3b02dde70a88d", "parents": ["01e754ca13edb22cb9dfd0df2c8d1835eef5490e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antoine Quint \u003cgraouts@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076455 [wpt PR 63049] - [scroll-animations] make ViewTimelineOptions.subject a required member (take 2), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[scroll-animations] make ViewTimelineOptions.subject a required member (take 2) (#63049)\n\nA mistake was made in the previous attempt for this in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/commit/088871600cd6b24f550a4b6a0b1987e8f3327db9.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: aa5aba84dd056671c29ba7e7b41f8234673b4dbd\nwpt-pr: 63049\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/scroll-animations.idl"], "git_node": "7f34240663ac258d6e97bf0f8f9a9748bfc22914", "git_parents": ["a6b6dc2b0c678f14f9f00e2ae84fa54d881217b4"], "node": "bf7c2e943e1ca01a2b2befcc4edf71f120ded0a0", "parents": ["b7e3dfbddc05f3aadafc693e4bc3b02dde70a88d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076455 [wpt PR 63049] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63049\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/idlharness.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "2ab36bdf33c1117cdf55cc00f7ff848a27e1530d", "git_parents": ["7f34240663ac258d6e97bf0f8f9a9748bfc22914"], "node": "2878b598cdd6880820b74a6df2a07b687eafbbf1", "parents": ["bf7c2e943e1ca01a2b2befcc4edf71f120ded0a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076344 [wpt PR 63029] - carousel: Make the parameter case insensitive, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncarousel: Make the parameter case insensitive\n\nCSS keywords are case insensitive, so should be the scroll button\narguments\n\nR=flackr@chromium.org\n\nChange-Id: Idb32490c560808b1eef2a0320c373d084ce722e4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8466185\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707025}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 33836fd8a89da9fa76eb6f99754c166e85dd164c\nwpt-pr: 63029\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-button-argument-case-insensitive.html"], "git_node": "c94dc5626bd4fac9c15966ce480242a88383a300", "git_parents": ["2ab36bdf33c1117cdf55cc00f7ff848a27e1530d"], "node": "2029510ae48794903277c22fde66511f1fde07cf", "parents": ["2878b598cdd6880820b74a6df2a07b687eafbbf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076344 [wpt PR 63029] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63029\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-button-argument-case-insensitive.html.ini"], "git_node": "2ee6b03569272a5cf083dde5187a031242806aea", "git_parents": ["c94dc5626bd4fac9c15966ce480242a88383a300"], "node": "61c1e9e0f781af5badb052e7e152567a94283ca9", "parents": ["2029510ae48794903277c22fde66511f1fde07cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076436 [wpt PR 63048] - Implement position-visibility: anchor-valid, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement position-visibility: anchor-valid\n\nAccording to CSS Anchor Positioning 1, when an element references the\ndefault anchor box (via position-area, anchor() or anchor-size()\nwithout an anchor name, or align-self/justify-self: anchor-center) and\nthe default anchor box cannot be resolved, the box's visibility\nproperty computes to force-hidden.\n\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position-1/#position-visibility\n\nThis CL implements this behavior:\n- Adds runtime flag CSSPositionVisibilityAnchorValid (experimental).\n- Adds PositionVisibility::kAnchorValid and tracks default anchor\n  references through CSS length resolution and style building.\n- Sets PaintLayer::SetInvisibleForPositionVisibility(kAnchorValid)\n  during out-of-flow layout if the default anchor cannot be resolved.\n- Updates WPT baselines and adds test coverage for anchor-valid.\n\nBug: 333421963\nChange-Id: I20f1e78866d7f644a42b34c58f63aa37338f6f8a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8453827\nCommit-Queue: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707046}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 781b65691872bbbec4c7fbd26dbce0229521363e\nwpt-pr: 63048\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-visibility-anchor-valid-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-visibility-anchor-valid-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-visibility-anchor-valid-dynamic-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-visibility-anchor-valid-dynamic.html"], "git_node": "9dc440357cbf33f971a0371dd1eb2f8736646b02", "git_parents": ["2ee6b03569272a5cf083dde5187a031242806aea"], "node": "db0498adf4104ed6a18d59260b0e1942e311bf17", "parents": ["61c1e9e0f781af5badb052e7e152567a94283ca9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076436 [wpt PR 63048] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63048\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/position-visibility-anchor-valid-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/position-visibility-anchor-valid-dynamic.html.ini"], "git_node": "59e45101fb23b362d6205b68809ff3d5ff9f9aab", "git_parents": ["9dc440357cbf33f971a0371dd1eb2f8736646b02"], "node": "09015244f3fae4da172fa9163be41a9ed0f523d3", "parents": ["db0498adf4104ed6a18d59260b0e1942e311bf17"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kate Lee \u003cklee@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076091 [wpt PR 63005] - [css-conditional] Wait for the scroll to end in scroll-state-scrolled\u2026, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-conditional] Wait for the scroll to end in scroll-state-scrolled-keyboard-scroll-on-body (#63005)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2d7d6f28a5e94c4b563b1d5af84542c86bf730d8\nwpt-pr: 63005\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/container-queries/scroll-state/scroll-state-scrolled-keyboard-scroll-on-body.html"], "git_node": "3a5dfacc1e64b85d10cdaa74754c246621fd0849", "git_parents": ["59e45101fb23b362d6205b68809ff3d5ff9f9aab"], "node": "6e3b384be9daa67b3677c3943f3497d640790b76", "parents": ["09015244f3fae4da172fa9163be41a9ed0f523d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076390 [wpt PR 63040] - WebMCP: Treat missing and explicit undefined as object, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebMCP: Treat missing and explicit undefined as object\n\nThis CL implements `NativeValueTraits\u003cIDLOptional\u003cIDLObject\u003e\u003e` as a\nfollow-up to https://crrev.com/c/8250826/comment/478e5f2a_3a3851ec/,\nallowing `optional object foo` with no default value.\n\nThe WebIDL specification's overload resolution algorithm, step 11.4.2\n[1] supports this, by appending the special value \"missing\" to an\ninvocation's arguments list in this case.\n\nThe closest thing we have to that in our bindings world is an \"empty\"\n`ScriptObject`. So this CL introduces a circumstance where bindings will\nemit an *empty* ScriptObject, representing a \"missing\" optional `object`\nargument with no default. I believe this is novel behavior.\n\nConsumers, like `ModelContext` in this CL, must check the \"emptiness\" of\nsuch objects and handle it accordingly.\n\n[1]:\nhttps://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#js-overloads:~:text=any%20entry%20in%20S.-,If%20optionality%20is%20%E2%80%9Coptional%E2%80%9D%20and%20V%20is%20undefined%2C%20then,-%3A\n\nR=beaufort.francois@gmail.com, caseq\n\nBug: 489045948\nChange-Id: Icdcf34374b4016ed2065bd3409dbd9ec18de37e4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8461705\nReviewed-by: Andrey Kosyakov \u003ccaseq@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fr \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707117}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0c7a6c61ffc3e1d4eab65b7a8a6b1281aaa7c703\nwpt-pr: 63040\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/object-arguments.https.html"], "git_node": "5c48981de914736a85b36f653a4b36fb6ada562a", "git_parents": ["3a5dfacc1e64b85d10cdaa74754c246621fd0849"], "node": "ce06864152e45c4bd742660d32b1fd21ac7727cf", "parents": ["6e3b384be9daa67b3677c3943f3497d640790b76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aadharsh Pannirselvam \u003caadharsh2010@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075802 [wpt PR 62987] - [wptrunner] Disable Chrome's known-root requirement for compression dictionaries, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wptrunner] Disable Chrome's known-root requirement for compression dictionaries (#62987)\n\n* [wptrunner] Disable Chrome's known-root requirement for compression dictionaries\n\nChromium only sends Available-Dictionary when the certificate chains to a\nknown root, or when the host is localhost\n(kCompressionDictionaryTransportRequireKnownRootCert, enabled by default).\nThe wpt test CA is trusted through --ignore-certificate-errors-spki-list, so\nit is never a known root, and every fetch/compression-dictionary/ test that\nexpects the header fails. Edge's daily run on wpt.fyi scores 0/16 on\ndictionary-registration.tentative.https.html for this reason.\n\nThe feature goes into the existing --disable-features flag rather than a\nsecond one, since a later --disable-features would replace the earlier value.\n\n* Update tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/browsers/chrome.py\n\nCo-authored-by: Jonathan Lee \u003cjonathan-j-lee@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n* Drop the comment line the suggestion left behind\n\nThe applied suggestion moved the ScrollbarAnimations comment into the\nlist but kept the original above it, plus a whitespace-only line that\nflake8 flags as W293.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aadharsh Pannirselvam \u003c19518661+oddharsh@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\nCo-authored-by: Jonathan Lee \u003cjonathan-j-lee@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fcc730cd4fa6b28c233adbcebbb3fb6768f799de\nwpt-pr: 62987\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/browsers/chrome.py"], "git_node": "e374e5414b847082dd7ae927dce3113f709404a1", "git_parents": ["5c48981de914736a85b36f653a4b36fb6ada562a"], "node": "b9c05fb6e78aa7055da6d42a9d173f6a18dbd5fe", "parents": ["ce06864152e45c4bd742660d32b1fd21ac7727cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Viktoriya Bryhider \u003cvbryhider@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076431 [wpt PR 63046] - WebTransport: add WPT test for anticipated concurrent incoming streams, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebTransport: add WPT test for anticipated concurrent incoming streams\n\nVerify omitted and explicit null defaults, constructor reflection,\nsetter behavior, unsigned short boundary values, and rejection of\nout-of-range values without modifying the existing hint.\n\nBug: 514531767\nChange-Id: I179a55fa941db04b7ed797e2037a23141bf30fef\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8459544\nCommit-Queue: Viktoriya Bryhider \u003cvbryhider@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707134}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bbbfd159132c7397f0adb1dafc9dc6c91a7f6f5f\nwpt-pr: 63046\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/anticipated-concurrent-incoming-streams.https.any.js"], "git_node": "4a948c4afe3aa11098c424f774ae3ece03d4046f", "git_parents": ["e374e5414b847082dd7ae927dce3113f709404a1"], "node": "7688ca792da9732650273722c0f44c8fa97f9e28", "parents": ["b9c05fb6e78aa7055da6d42a9d173f6a18dbd5fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076431 [wpt PR 63046] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63046\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/anticipated-concurrent-incoming-streams.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "27686be058267b936128f6d580ef2a0fed36a453", "git_parents": ["4a948c4afe3aa11098c424f774ae3ece03d4046f"], "node": "c4403e72b213e8cf68aebddb9dcacedc831b2f6c", "parents": ["7688ca792da9732650273722c0f44c8fa97f9e28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076312 [wpt PR 63026] - webgl: Ignore UNPACK_ALIGNMENT for texImage2D from a TexImageSource, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebgl: Ignore UNPACK_ALIGNMENT for texImage2D from a TexImageSource\n\nSigned-off-by: mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 52110495e3b415aad0b3b95f60273ddea24d4cb6\nwpt-pr: 63026\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webgl/texImage2D-source-ignores-unpack-alignment.html"], "git_node": "84e06f01775d97478415ab019f122fcbcb82d8a4", "git_parents": ["27686be058267b936128f6d580ef2a0fed36a453"], "node": "ab349101cb03daac543fcd4d6b010fde9185780b", "parents": ["c4403e72b213e8cf68aebddb9dcacedc831b2f6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hojeong Park \u003cparkhj062@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076498 [wpt PR 63054] - [css-pseudo] Support 'quotes' property in ::marker, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-pseudo] Support 'quotes' property in ::marker\n\nFollow the CSSWG resolution [1].\n\n[1]: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5265#issuecomment-3531669680\n\nBug: 40110559\nTest: external/wpt/css/css-lists/marker-quotes.html\nTest: external/wpt/css/css-pseudo/parsing/marker-supported-properties.html\nTest: external/wpt/css/css-pseudo/parsing/marker-supported-properties-in-animation.html\nChange-Id: I352407f10fdca79e3303be6f018be60e8c53ab57\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8425980\nCommit-Queue: Hojeong Park \u003cparkhj062@gmail.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707180}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9eac644ddfadefbbcb4d99780c82465d4dd33db7\nwpt-pr: 63054\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/parsing/marker-supported-properties-in-animation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/parsing/marker-supported-properties.html"], "git_node": "05289adbe74949aa5f51f541a9376fa649bc6154", "git_parents": ["84e06f01775d97478415ab019f122fcbcb82d8a4"], "node": "acfb3243f00712af50257b62be575d3ae704aa49", "parents": ["ab349101cb03daac543fcd4d6b010fde9185780b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076521 [wpt PR 63059] - carousel: mark scroll-* pseudos as tree abiding., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncarousel: mark scroll-* pseudos as tree abiding.\n\nThis seems to only affected slotted so it also adds the parsing tests\nthere.\n\nR=flackr@chromium.org\n\nChange-Id: Ife9add8d1d705c29d9da8bb3a40b759394fbdb6b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8481559\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707217}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1f2bc9dd74a2e67d7b6132bef3def6247a0b5f61\nwpt-pr: 63059\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shadow/slotted-parsing.html"], "git_node": "f56990561f45878187c26be4f3d703f7425b5e77", "git_parents": ["05289adbe74949aa5f51f541a9376fa649bc6154"], "node": "15417aaad8253427b6198435d78f346032993a2b", "parents": ["acfb3243f00712af50257b62be575d3ae704aa49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076521 [wpt PR 63059] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63059\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-shadow/slotted-parsing.html.ini"], "git_node": "c83608396dbe81c1c52dc0c9b017e428cc9a1b23", "git_parents": ["f56990561f45878187c26be4f3d703f7425b5e77"], "node": "df3c6eccc6f235f71833dcdd8e96e160011cee22", "parents": ["15417aaad8253427b6198435d78f346032993a2b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075789 [wpt PR 62982] - [align] Update WPT tests to check for `flow-start/end` instead of `flex-start/end`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[align] Update WPT tests to check for `flow-start/end` instead of `flex-start/end`\n\nUpdate WPT tests to check for `flow-start/end` instead of\n`flex-start/end` so that we can enable `flow-start/end` serialization\nthrough the experimental flag. This allows us to remove the virtual test\nsuite that was enabling `CSSFlowStartAndEndSerialization` specifically.\n\nBug: 555299635\nChange-Id: I1056bb0c3a204361a27af3665185ef157fced51d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8444297\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707230}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7584ae4d0599a442ff9f1e624f5bdf1a1fe0b092\nwpt-pr: 62982\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/content-distribution/parse-align-content-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/content-distribution/parse-align-content-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/content-distribution/parse-justify-content-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/content-distribution/parse-justify-content-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/content-distribution/place-content-shorthand-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/default-alignment/parse-align-items-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/default-alignment/parse-align-items-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/default-alignment/parse-justify-items-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/default-alignment/parse-justify-items-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/default-alignment/place-items-shorthand-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-content-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-items-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/align-self-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-content-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-items-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/justify-self-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/place-content-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/place-items-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/parsing/place-self-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/resources/alignment-parsing-utils.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/self-alignment/parse-align-self-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/self-alignment/parse-align-self-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/self-alignment/parse-justify-self-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/self-alignment/parse-justify-self-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/self-alignment/place-self-shorthand-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-content-flex-end.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-content-flex-start.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-items-flex-end.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-items-flex-start.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-self-flex-end.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-self-flex-start.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_justify-content-flex-end.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_justify-content-flex-start.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/property-list.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/animation-model/keyframe-effects/effect-value-iteration-composite-operation.html"], "git_node": "1d7d7c162578942188070eda72ebd941e3c8eaba", "git_parents": ["c83608396dbe81c1c52dc0c9b017e428cc9a1b23"], "node": "982338e19dbae64f2d424b33d8a886a09623550c", "parents": ["df3c6eccc6f235f71833dcdd8e96e160011cee22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075789 [wpt PR 62982] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62982\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/content-distribution/parse-align-content-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/content-distribution/parse-align-content-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/content-distribution/parse-justify-content-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/content-distribution/parse-justify-content-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/content-distribution/place-content-shorthand-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/default-alignment/parse-align-items-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/default-alignment/parse-align-items-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/default-alignment/parse-justify-items-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/default-alignment/parse-justify-items-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/default-alignment/place-items-shorthand-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-content-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-items-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/align-self-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-content-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-items-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/justify-self-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/place-content-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/place-items-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/parsing/place-self-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/self-alignment/parse-align-self-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/self-alignment/parse-align-self-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/self-alignment/parse-justify-self-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/self-alignment/parse-justify-self-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/self-alignment/place-self-shorthand-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-content-flex-end.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-content-flex-start.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-items-flex-end.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-items-flex-start.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-self-flex-end.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_align-self-flex-start.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_justify-content-flex-end.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/getcomputedstyle/flexbox_computedstyle_justify-content-flex-start.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/accumulation-per-property-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/addition-per-property-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/animation-types/interpolation-per-property-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/animation-model/keyframe-effects/effect-value-iteration-composite-operation.html.ini"], "git_node": "44d5513387c15ac00a0d0f953350053339f284ef", "git_parents": ["1d7d7c162578942188070eda72ebd941e3c8eaba"], "node": "4cbb742d608a5b42ae20a6e747b516284b4f82df", "parents": ["982338e19dbae64f2d424b33d8a886a09623550c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076379 [wpt PR 63037] - [WPT] Fix stale expectations in script execution-timing tests 083, 128, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WPT] Fix stale expectations in script execution-timing tests 083, 128\n\n128.html: Since script execution moved from the DOM insertion steps to\nthe post-connection steps (whatwg/html#8730), atomically inserting a\nfragment into an empty, connected script element first runs the outer\nscript's children changed steps (executing its concatenated Text node\nchildren) and only then runs the post-connection steps of the inserted\ninner script. The HTML spec now documents exactly this scenario in a\nnote under \"script processing model\". Chrome and Safari already produce\nthe new order; Firefox has not implemented post-connection script\nexecution yet (it also fails the companion test 148.html for the same\nreason).\n\n083.html: Setting frames[0].location starts an asynchronous navigation,\nso the fireFooEvent() call in the immediately following script block\nruns while the iframe's original document is still fully active and must\ninvoke the listener a second time. Only once the navigation completes is\nthe listener suppressed, because its callback's realm belongs to a\nWindow whose associated document is no longer fully active (DOM's \"inner\ninvoke\", step 2.4). The test assumed the navigation deactivates the\ndocument synchronously and expected only one \"event: foo\" entry; Chrome,\nFirefox and Safari all produce identical output with two entries,\nmatching the spec. The interesting assertion is preserved: the final\nfireFooEvent() after the navigation completes must not fire the\nlistener.\n\nUpdate both expectations and remove the stale Blink FAIL baselines.\n\nBug: 40781537\nChange-Id: I81d48902a406eaf7d3ab58972dfedcb503660bbc\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8462267\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706418}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f9194d13616b54754ef0e7eea4b82a54cee90866\nwpt-pr: 63037\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/execution-timing/083.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/execution-timing/128.html"], "git_node": "321c88615ea58c32583f11e6819f55b3b2148a3a", "git_parents": ["44d5513387c15ac00a0d0f953350053339f284ef"], "node": "5a84850f48d424d3af9a93a7acf40a4cc0a01f98", "parents": ["4cbb742d608a5b42ae20a6e747b516284b4f82df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076379 [wpt PR 63037] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63037\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/execution-timing/083.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/execution-timing/128.html.ini"], "git_node": "e22dd8550c85539a584ad827633d8e9872894c39", "git_parents": ["321c88615ea58c32583f11e6819f55b3b2148a3a"], "node": "b249971921de2d4cb641340fbb4ca38214648d3f", "parents": ["5a84850f48d424d3af9a93a7acf40a4cc0a01f98"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Pieters \u003czcorpan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076398 [wpt PR 63042] - Test `TrustedHTML` with parser options that need vetting, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest `TrustedHTML` with parser options that need vetting\n\nFor w3c/trusted-types#616.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 43681d686ca43bfb9ae5e0bb9e775dc25246d9c4\nwpt-pr: 63042\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/support/trustedhtml-parser-options.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options-default-createHTML.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options-default-createParserOptions.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options-no-enforcement.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options-report-only.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options-report-only.tentative.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options.tentative.html"], "git_node": "8bcace96c99faf3b001d236e345c575666a39885", "git_parents": ["e22dd8550c85539a584ad827633d8e9872894c39"], "node": "645b0ff0dd44d7d2047661b168d39ced6f413cb2", "parents": ["b249971921de2d4cb641340fbb4ca38214648d3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076398 [wpt PR 63042] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63042\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options-default-createHTML.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options-default-createParserOptions.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options-no-enforcement.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options-report-only.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/trustedhtml-unvetted-parser-options.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "edcc49adf7b1ddb6b022974d6fee379a617453b0", "git_parents": ["8bcace96c99faf3b001d236e345c575666a39885"], "node": "2c2340eac0d2560f29d19f3223f5d4f388676ff3", "parents": ["645b0ff0dd44d7d2047661b168d39ced6f413cb2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076354 [wpt PR 63033] - Remove \u003c/img\u003e from css-grid/grid-lanes WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove \u003c/img\u003e from css-grid/grid-lanes WPTs\n\nimg has no end tag. Writing \u003c/img\u003e is a parse error and the parser drops\nthe tag, so the source suggests a structure the document never had. This\nCL removes all the \u003c/img\u003es from\nthird_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/*.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: If75f9d197e51f029c7f9b682096dea4121b54b2f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8224723\nReviewed-by: Brandon Walderman \u003cbrwalder@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707275}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f1c79523f6bbf72d5fd1b2fa2f0be92026e006ee\nwpt-pr: 63033\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/intrinsic-sizing/grid-lanes-contain-intrinsic-size-010.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-027-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-027.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-auto-023-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-auto-023.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-auto-024.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-auto-025-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-auto-025.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-auto-026-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-auto-026.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/column-auto-repeat-auto-027.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-auto-023-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-auto-023.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-auto-024.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-auto-025-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-auto-025.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-auto-026-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-auto-026.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-auto-027-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/intrinsic-auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-auto-027.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-025-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/track-sizing/auto-repeat/row-auto-repeat-025.html"], "git_node": "3691809e5d5fc73b7764c5cc745de6d1fcc65874", "git_parents": ["edcc49adf7b1ddb6b022974d6fee379a617453b0"], "node": "af25a08f16d107343a1e4129688039029ae69cbf", "parents": ["2c2340eac0d2560f29d19f3223f5d4f388676ff3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076544 [wpt PR 63060] - [HiC] Fix rasterization scale for nested canvas snapshots, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Fix rasterization scale for nested canvas snapshots\n\nFixed: 540532973\nChange-Id: Ifcf78c0fa9d531cdbc95b8eaab465d585d437303\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8474440\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707287}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8b289ba13fbff34b8ecc1b1d2fd7c5d738bcd58f\nwpt-pr: 63060\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/nested-canvas-scale-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/nested-canvas-scale.tentative.html"], "git_node": "976d857b5f9471e343ce88d94f90cdf87e153714", "git_parents": ["3691809e5d5fc73b7764c5cc745de6d1fcc65874"], "node": "69731d39078a5fb5a9290335084509544d5700ff", "parents": ["af25a08f16d107343a1e4129688039029ae69cbf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Kardell \u003cbkardell@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076578 [wpt PR 63066] - add subdirectory files to feature, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nadd subdirectory files to feature (#63066)\n\nThese aren't currently showing up when you query by feature, we  should add them.  Because of where this clip is and the history of mathml, we'd like them to show up in that implementation report as well\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 948960f00d9b2a75fb4a81757d0ec62e09fd2fbd\nwpt-pr: 63066\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/css-styling/WEB_FEATURES.yml"], "git_node": "ef6b7c00b09f7b6cf55c06808c2039167e479bb5", "git_parents": ["976d857b5f9471e343ce88d94f90cdf87e153714"], "node": "6a17fc401a437020014dadd012be1c16c1268655", "parents": ["69731d39078a5fb5a9290335084509544d5700ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076553 [wpt PR 63062] - Reland \"Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReland \"Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\"\n\nThis is a reland of commit 280ca3161bda00f116803a7064aba3ce91a7d59e\nwith the addition of a new change to LeakExpectations.\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\n\u003e\n\u003e Fixed: 565674529\n\u003e Change-Id: Ia3248d945dc01328e8f354ec28d7cfcadafb87f3\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464608\n\u003e Auto-Submit: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706396}\n\nFixed: 565674529\nBug: 567487270\nChange-Id: I3011a6ac54d8228f8a52601b324b7054a4aa2c9e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8480519\nAuto-Submit: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707303}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: afe89a5df4dcc7c6bcb317b07d6eee31a383c466\nwpt-pr: 63062\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/navigate-to-javascript-url-009-crash.html"], "git_node": "eb40ad763dc17fd8a94b1fa356a5f8ea58c6b0b2", "git_parents": ["ef6b7c00b09f7b6cf55c06808c2039167e479bb5"], "node": "418777f3d6079222d9daedd51d6944681d0f86aa", "parents": ["6a17fc401a437020014dadd012be1c16c1268655"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Kardell \u003cbkardell@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076587 [wpt PR 63072] - Add mathml html tree feature mappings, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd mathml feature mappings (#63072)\n\nThese too need to be included in the web-feature report, similar to #63066\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c0adb76317058ef97624ecda9e1ce451cf701b49\nwpt-pr: 63072\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/WEB_FEATURES.yml"], "git_node": "6cef347243cef733137a5b20d3172847337e2ee0", "git_parents": ["eb40ad763dc17fd8a94b1fa356a5f8ea58c6b0b2"], "node": "1adc29c89a1ccd08b4e09caa32bf4e2d2f5444e3", "parents": ["418777f3d6079222d9daedd51d6944681d0f86aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076550 [wpt PR 63061] - [HiC] Adjust fuzzy on WPT tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Adjust fuzzy on WPT tests\n\nThe two tests changed have more fuzziness on WPT infra. Increase\nthe fuzzy allowance a little.\n\nBug: 519494301\nChange-Id: Ic07316bb4700e0e19a704ecad2b1fa5acbc7c7ff\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8466364\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707372}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e8c1ce3a4616078ae6156de77267e022c95127aa\nwpt-pr: 63061\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-transform-on-div.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/scale-worker.tentative.html"], "git_node": "801856250fc5968feb95355e246080b30795f468", "git_parents": ["6cef347243cef733137a5b20d3172847337e2ee0"], "node": "66ab623097028a71c26236e4edcb28335dbaf854", "parents": ["1adc29c89a1ccd08b4e09caa32bf4e2d2f5444e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Harrelson \u003cchrishtr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076589 [wpt PR 63073] - Remove WPT tests for input-security, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove WPT tests for input-security\n\nThis feature has been removed from the css-ui spec.\n\nBug: 40793945\n\nChange-Id: Iea10d00ca3384ee08b6f91866327fc8e940ef06b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8487165\nCommit-Queue: Chris Harrelson \u003cchrishtr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip J\u00e4genstedt \u003cfoolip@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707442}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a1180baf863c466a39971291d91af1aa97a7dc83\nwpt-pr: 63073\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/input-security-auto-sensitive-text-input-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/input-security-auto-sensitive-text-input.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/input-security-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/input-security-non-sensitive-elements-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/input-security-non-sensitive-elements.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/input-security-none-sensitive-text-input-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/input-security-none-sensitive-text-input.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/input-security-parsing.html"], "git_node": "ebbef318c73becee3fa4d8d9ee6cc26910f1c655", "git_parents": ["801856250fc5968feb95355e246080b30795f468"], "node": "d46fc7dc6436a98660efafc34cae617f5523d5da", "parents": ["66ab623097028a71c26236e4edcb28335dbaf854"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076575 [wpt PR 63065] - CSSPseudoElement: Propagate VT name when selecting VT elements., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCSSPseudoElement: Propagate VT name when selecting VT elements.\n\nThis patch ensures we propagate the vt argument when creating a pseudo\nelement. This is used in pseudoTarget on events, and a test verifies\nthat this works correctly.\n\nR=flackr@chromium.org, kevers@chromium.org\n\nChange-Id: Ie081f58c205d54f224ff1bf289997a61eaf05e7c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8466391\nCommit-Queue: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707453}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 51ef5ebce5d9c73417219b71204edb1bf78b5b5e\nwpt-pr: 63065\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/events-on-view-transition-pseudos.tentative.html"], "git_node": "9b9eef0669c9b53310a4ce805db25f56ab308e04", "git_parents": ["ebbef318c73becee3fa4d8d9ee6cc26910f1c655"], "node": "e4f2f39f6a1ba6b7f559997a5bf7e96ab57757d9", "parents": ["d46fc7dc6436a98660efafc34cae617f5523d5da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076575 [wpt PR 63065] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63065\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/events-on-view-transition-pseudos.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "268e30b0ae7969d30fcf7efd43da54d02bb177a1", "git_parents": ["9b9eef0669c9b53310a4ce805db25f56ab308e04"], "node": "3617ac28bca42d623d3ccfe04429c1f6db8e49c8", "parents": ["e4f2f39f6a1ba6b7f559997a5bf7e96ab57757d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076582 [wpt PR 63069] - [blink] Input client rect excludes inline padding, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[blink] Input client rect excludes inline padding\n\nA text field clips its text at the content box in the inline axis, so\nmeasure clientLeft, clientWidth and scrollWidth from there instead of\nthe padding box. The block axis keeps the padding box, and vertical\nwriting modes swap the axes. This matches Firefox and the CSSWG\nresolution in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13502.\n\nAdd Element::PhysicalClientRect(), shared by the client* getters and\nHTMLInputElement's scrollWidth and scrollHeight.\n\nGuarded by the InputClientRectWithoutInlinePadding kill switch.\nApplying overflow-clip-margin to scroll containers is left to\ncrbug.com/501216032.\n\nWiden a 15px input in autofill's IsWebElementVisibleTest to 20px so it\nstays above the 10px visibility floor.\n\nFixed: 507830640\nChange-Id: I696f6cbc8d76a0a4ce26fba3e1c966b634d9d3d1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8432242\nReviewed-by: Jihad Hanna \u003cjihadghanna@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707468}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 42105f7d205d44330d6fd25cd592ebe2530cc861\nwpt-pr: 63069\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/client-scroll-props-input.html"], "git_node": "a33c0f989f93aaef60ddff1544ac4ebb1a6f4cbf", "git_parents": ["268e30b0ae7969d30fcf7efd43da54d02bb177a1"], "node": "1ed3301d81cbbc1a2f6bc408ab62f67f03321d09", "parents": ["3617ac28bca42d623d3ccfe04429c1f6db8e49c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Pieters \u003czcorpan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1999936 [wpt PR 56009] - Avoid ERROR result when customizable select parsing is not supported, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAvoid ERROR result when customizable select parsing is not supported\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 49484dbc1bbfa528e9b985d8063a790ad879a4a1\nwpt-pr: 56009\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-base-appearance-computed-style.html"], "git_node": "5f34004ca2986e81c73dbb3c5f81b7b890e80a8e", "git_parents": ["a33c0f989f93aaef60ddff1544ac4ebb1a6f4cbf"], "node": "64168a9264ccdcba408babd7bde376c45fc01eb9", "parents": ["1ed3301d81cbbc1a2f6bc408ab62f67f03321d09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Pieters \u003czcorpan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2005753 [wpt PR 56715] - HTML: event handlers are null when there's no browsing context, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nHTML: event handlers are null when there's no browsing context\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11441\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e6ba3d7abea784a1f03347bccaad76e7a6347eae\nwpt-pr: 56715\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/webappapis/scripting/events/event-handler-attributes-no-bc.html"], "git_node": "9049ae2f773e89083283e243131c6106d0ce993d", "git_parents": ["5f34004ca2986e81c73dbb3c5f81b7b890e80a8e"], "node": "9ac455f3a899bf49e4b8bd6e2310c95b9707bc15", "parents": ["64168a9264ccdcba408babd7bde376c45fc01eb9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2005753 [wpt PR 56715] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 56715\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/webappapis/scripting/events/event-handler-attributes-no-bc.html.ini"], "git_node": "2e0fd661ac2d5381c870becf5694638219cde11b", "git_parents": ["9049ae2f773e89083283e243131c6106d0ce993d"], "node": "d50b9fbf0260c64873d92b07ac6cf46766a30298", "parents": ["9ac455f3a899bf49e4b8bd6e2310c95b9707bc15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075137 [wpt PR 62930] - layout: Restrict `::first-letter` to the first formatted line, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Restrict `::first-letter` to the first formatted line\n\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cob