atform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-changedElements.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-css-animation.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-fires-post-intersection-observation-steps.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-fires-post-resize-observer.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-iframe-nested-invalidation.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-iframe.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-invalidation-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-outside-invalidation-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-post-tree-order.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-scroll-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-zindex.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/percent-sizing.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/requestPaint.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/ruby-canvas-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/scale.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/scroller-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/triple-nested-content-drawable-canvas.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/video.tentative.html"], "git_node": "6e30c97ca1c75607c3789b132c390d2b402417c4", "git_parents": ["3013753da5a966788eec15feb8b60a661c57eb2a"], "node": "8f4d2f0b2a51bb9ecac24b14e72133f7e6890fe9", "parents": ["d3078bb1e1891d7eeb33f62d4c0e9a39c8fe598b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076472 [wpt PR 63051] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325616, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nmoveBefore() updates id and name maps of shadow trees inside the moved subtree against the wrong tree scope\n\nElement::movingSteps() used the old parent's tree scope to update the id and\nname maps of every shadow-including inclusive descendant of the moved node. For\nelements in a shadow tree inside the moved subtree that is the wrong tree scope,\nas their own does not change. They were removed from the old parent's maps,\nwhere they were never registered, and registered a second time in their own.\nThis happens when moving a \u003cselect\u003e or \u003cdetails\u003e, whose user agent shadow trees\ncontain a named \u003cslot\u003e, or any shadow host whose shadow tree has an element with\nan id or name.\n\nThe moving steps now receive whether the old and the new tree scope changed,\nworked out as for the insertion and removal steps: from whether the old and the\nnew parent are in a tree scope, and false for shadow trees inside the moved\nsubtree. Element::movingSteps() then does the id and name bookkeeping of the\nremoval steps for the old parent and that of the insertion steps for the new\none, sharing the code with those steps. Neither parent is in a tree scope when\nmoving inside a disconnected tree, so the document's maps are no longer touched\nthen, which fixes bug 324715.\n\nisInTreeScope() and isInDocumentTree() rely on the IsInShadowTree flag, which\nthe moving steps did not update. It was stale after moving a node into or out of\na shadow tree, so changing the id or name of that node later updated the wrong\nmaps, which could crash. Node::movingSteps() now updates it, as the insertion\nand removal steps do.\n\nselectedcontent-subtree-mutations.html no longer needs to be skipped.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325616\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 939d537f69683aa26db1eadbacc50dda44e115a9\nwpt-pr: 63051\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-disconnected-id-map.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-shadow-boundary-id-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-shadow-host-id-map.html"], "git_node": "76dbf7c72e425cc72504065eb97fdbcbec454472", "git_parents": ["6e30c97ca1c75607c3789b132c390d2b402417c4"], "node": "f16cd1d471a90ca841310fe5b5bd93d79ba487d0", "parents": ["8f4d2f0b2a51bb9ecac24b14e72133f7e6890fe9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076472 [wpt PR 63051] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63051\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-iframe-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "9b60c2a04af91147f031084e3979df23d4c17e12", "git_parents": ["76dbf7c72e425cc72504065eb97fdbcbec454472"], "node": "054d372e83cd3ab2f6b20cc4680db46516ba71cc", "parents": ["f16cd1d471a90ca841310fe5b5bd93d79ba487d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Wonik Choi \u003cchoiwonik91@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075808 [wpt PR 62420] - Recognize *+xml MIME types behind SpecCompliantXmlMimeTypes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRecognize *+xml MIME types behind SpecCompliantXmlMimeTypes\n\nMatch WHATWG mimesniff XML MIME types (*+xml) when the experimental\nflag is enabled; keep legacy application/*+xml matching otherwise.\nFollows the SpecCompliantJsonMimeTypes approach.\n\nAdd WPT coverage for non-application structured XML MIME types through\nPerformanceResourceTiming.contentType.\n\nChromeStatus entry: https://chromestatus.com/feature/5092584283308032\n\nIntent-to-Prototype:\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/HoHP5xZmw1o\n\nBug: 362282752\nChange-Id: I23189ab573fbd1cea4440f0e48c7b2ebbd1c0f43\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8301932\nReviewed-by: mmenke \u003cmmenke@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dmitry Gozman \u003cdgozman@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: mmenke \u003cmmenke@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1692490}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0f195499f06d0833e768b01a1a8ce942b8622fc8\nwpt-pr: 62420\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mimesniff/mime-types/resources/mime-types-minimized.json"], "git_node": "47bd3178448e36baf259e7381b8904e1d661eea8", "git_parents": ["9b60c2a04af91147f031084e3979df23d4c17e12"], "node": "cfec61bc867d94c3aea928e5e11aa8a3a54237d0", "parents": ["054d372e83cd3ab2f6b20cc4680db46516ba71cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075808 [wpt PR 62420] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62420\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/content-type-minimization.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/delivery-type.tentative.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "598b2933fff6a774a1cb16838d8f166e170d8e44", "git_parents": ["47bd3178448e36baf259e7381b8904e1d661eea8"], "node": "6f010003a98f519063dba5f83ec2ddd862e7d85e", "parents": ["cfec61bc867d94c3aea928e5e11aa8a3a54237d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076519 [wpt PR 63058] - [css] Reuse cached implicit scopes in parent frames, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css] Reuse cached implicit scopes in parent frames\n\nImplicit @scope traversal is cached via seen_implicit_scopes_, but this\nwasn't being looked at when traversing parent frames. This adds some\nlogic to take this into account during parent frame traversal.\n\nNo behavioral changes are expected, just optimization:\n\nImplicitAtScopeInsertion -7.7%\n\nImplicitAtScope -2.7%\n\nA WPT was added for sibling stylesheet @scope invalidation, which wasn't\ncurrently covered.\n\nChange-Id: Id7d8a4814b4bdd7de8b5bee70b1d94ca599028de\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8421208\nCommit-Queue: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707633}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3619c4c0ed0dfc67ae0f6c3cc85d4fbddaa7fb7e\nwpt-pr: 63058\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-cascade/scope-implicit-sibling-mutations.html"], "git_node": "b05d39a0e1852d963840a00c900f96dd7ff42511", "git_parents": ["598b2933fff6a774a1cb16838d8f166e170d8e44"], "node": "81f1738aeae93b8a42c0f998ff86e55bbe11dede", "parents": ["6f010003a98f519063dba5f83ec2ddd862e7d85e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "zcorpan \u003czcorpan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1982602 [wpt PR 54266] - Quirks: Apply percentage height quirk to position: sticky, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nQuirks: Apply percentage height quirk to position: sticky\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/quirks/pull/88\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: eed8aea45725da5b002ee8778400d14148d0ebfe\nwpt-pr: 54266\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/quirks/percentage-height-calculation.html"], "git_node": "2aac63b4cfa469d7b356c34c42e5be1ccd62e354", "git_parents": ["b05d39a0e1852d963840a00c900f96dd7ff42511"], "node": "8269b1a328c2036d60c57be3a5d2f8406f20a2eb", "parents": ["81f1738aeae93b8a42c0f998ff86e55bbe11dede"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076605 [wpt PR 63079] - [HiC] Base ElementImage width/height getters on live canvas size, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Base ElementImage width/height getters on live canvas size\n\nBug: 456097302\nChange-Id: I5e1de416750a4c24d0c8040e09af7baef9edda34\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8477854\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707704}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a6e66db3709bfebb764502d55f6d501a25059448\nwpt-pr: 63079\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/captureElementImage.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/element-image-fractional-size.tentative.html"], "git_node": "c127426490facaf236d22d3ebd649a5ff2f658cf", "git_parents": ["2aac63b4cfa469d7b356c34c42e5be1ccd62e354"], "node": "ce8422d136d4fabd69de8fbae2d48402014901e8", "parents": ["8269b1a328c2036d60c57be3a5d2f8406f20a2eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076620 [wpt PR 63082] - [html-in-canvas] Update CSS, transform, shadow, and hit-test WPTs to use drawable, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Update CSS, transform, shadow, and hit-test WPTs to use drawable\n\nThis patch updates the html-in-canvas CSS, filter, compositing,\ntransform, shadow DOM, SVG, and hit-testing WPT tests to explicitly add\nthe `drawable` attribute to canvas child elements.\n\nBug: 565840012\nChange-Id: Iba6d49cf8de3dde832c858ec4d8845511c1c4e0d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8488207\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707703}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1b81534c42533f63bf293db63359