"testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/selection.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/z-index.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/opacity-animation.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/position-anchor-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/resources/CanvasWidget.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-basic.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slot-canvas-child.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slotted-moveBefore.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slotted.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-non-opaque-element.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/svg-foreign-object.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/svg-rect.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/top-layer-not-painted-in-canvas.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/update-element-geometry-get-bounding-client-rect.tentative.html"], "git_node": "7c39e5406a89c6ec61f8d048da7ed1480c691760", "git_parents": ["c127426490facaf236d22d3ebd649a5ff2f658cf"], "node": "f23a2ea523522fecfb6458d1db56094af958672c", "parents": ["ce8422d136d4fabd69de8fbae2d48402014901e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Issac Roy \u003c69167197+TheBoyRoy05@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076559 [wpt PR 63063] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323382, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Flex Wrap Balance] flex-flow shorthand has no test coverage for the balance value (#63063)\n\nI had claude-opus-5.5 draft these changes and had it model them on the existing\nflex-wrap-*.html balance tests, checked the shortest-form serialization\nconvention against parsing/flex-flow-valid.html, and ran ./wpt lint and\n./wpt run chrome (Chrome 153 stable: 24/24 subtests pass). As a negative\ncontrol, it changed the expected serialization of row balance to row balance,\nand that case failed as expected. I reviewed every case and take responsibility\nfor the change.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323382\n\nCo-authored-by: Issac Roy \u003cissacroy@amazon.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: da9e329017b22ee787d336e5b0daf8dee146e241\nwpt-pr: 63063\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/balance/flex-flow-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/balance/flex-flow-shorthand.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/balance/flex-flow-valid.html"], "git_node": "4976aa32cdbca38e3fb3ed20a2adc58314abc5fe", "git_parents": ["7c39e5406a89c6ec61f8d048da7ed1480c691760"], "node": "2c6cdbcc8ee26b0567fa1e09e5abc625900d8b55", "parents": ["f23a2ea523522fecfb6458d1db56094af958672c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076559 [wpt PR 63063] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63063\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/balance/flex-flow-shorthand.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-flexbox/balance/flex-flow-valid.html.ini"], "git_node": "e6b34a490c559a5966869b383ccae91c9218a081", "git_parents": ["4976aa32cdbca38e3fb3ed20a2adc58314abc5fe"], "node": "0dbda1c53fa65f2a884e49293a8fe395d256e6a3", "parents": ["2c6cdbcc8ee26b0567fa1e09e5abc625900d8b55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076614 [wpt PR 63080] - Don't rebuild date-time edit fields when layout parameters are unchanged., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon't rebuild date-time edit fields when layout parameters are unchanged.\n\nThe primary change here is changing DateTimeEditElement::GetLayout to\nreturn early if the layout parameters are unchanged.  However, this\nchange has a number of prerequisites that are also included here:\n\n* Adds default comparison operators to make it possible to compare\n  LayoutParameters objects.\n\n* Moves the needs-millisecond-field information into the\n  LayoutParameters.\n\n* Recompute style when changing values (in cases where, previously,\n  elements were reconstructed, plus SetValueAsDateTimeFieldsState which\n  was likely buggy) so that GetCustomStyleForLayoutObject will rerun\n  when the value changes, since it depends on the value (e.g., setting a\n  different width for 5-digit years).\n\n* Clear cached type-ahead buffers when changing the values (which\n  reconstructing the elements previously did, except in the\n  SetValueAsDateTimeFieldsState case).\n\nFixed: 565838017\nChange-Id: Ic248053b6731c83db92ba99e110a652acfb1ace0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464610\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707763}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b1f77737e8a4fd98867b320bdc1ed0022f3d7d5b\nwpt-pr: 63080\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/date-input-slot-assignment-crash.tentative.html"], "git_node": "61c5e2ec04445419338dedb1d0fe593014878079", "git_parents": ["e6b34a490c559a5966869b383ccae91c9218a081"], "node": "12a3e710def842ded92f66eb6fb9a598e7707530", "parents": ["0dbda1c53fa65f2a884e49293a8fe395d256e6a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076628 [wpt PR 63083] - [HiC] Read from WebGL back buffer for nested canvas snapshots, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Read from WebGL back buffer for nested canvas snapshots\n\nA nested canvas with a WebGL context will stop producing front buffers\nbecause it doesn't get a cc::Layer and doesn't display directly. We\nshould be reading from the back buffer.\n\nFixed: 563000233\nChange-Id: I671352b35060e45278fabc9d9e3d4813a7af9738\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8428142\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707787}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 77e428d85779a6602d1ff782b252435188e40c89\nwpt-pr: 63083\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/moved-webgl-canvas.tentative.html"], "git_node": "d38613aa8a94485e1216b3c066d2248529438041", "git_parents": ["61c5e2ec04445419338dedb1d0fe593014878079"], "node": "96cf733e8ce952fc5889f4fa691c0fa04b6e69d1", "parents": ["12a3e710def842ded92f66eb6fb9a598e7707530"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076628 [wpt PR 63083] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63083\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/moved-webgl-canvas.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "b2e95cacafd0286301c6bb8f85c04bdcaa6e3fdf", "git_parents": ["d38613aa8a94485e1216b3c066d2248529438041"], "node": "fdb175d01a81b114b855998c24f92d4f864353bd", "parents": ["96cf733e8ce952fc5889f4fa691c0fa04b6e69d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076685 [wpt PR 63089] - Add a few test cases recommended by the I2S thread, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd a few test cases recommended by the I2S thread\n\nSee conversation:\n\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/2NYLp-Jcff0?e=48417069\n\nBug: 333421963\nChange-Id: I96dd21bd78bd306cc1e8c3bf7fdcdf711f1b09ec\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8487385\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707844}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e6e7aca2489afb339d8cf615e5b3ea6c22021a3d\nwpt-pr: 63089\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-visibility-anchor-valid-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-visibility-anchor-valid-001.html"], "git_node": "738c40db0c97ca698becd969a9f6feda364a584c", "git_parents": ["b2e95cacafd0286301c6bb8f85c04bdcaa6e3fdf"], "node": "26eda4d76a7af7e552da4799b611f391572d9d81", "parents": ["fdb175d01a81b114b855998c24f92d4f864353bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076599 [wpt PR 63077] - Sync interfaces/ with @webref/idl 3.85.0- #63013, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSync interfaces/ with @webref/idl 3.85.0- #63013 (#63077)\n\n* Sync interfaces/ with @webref/idl 3.85.0\n\n* Update tests for IDL file renames\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: wpt-pr-bot \u003cwpt-pr-bot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4604834dd43c9f1c40e3e166f19c8a70888b7dcc\nwpt-pr: 63077\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/bluetooth/bidi/idl/idlharness.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/bluetooth-scanning.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/bluetooth.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/hid.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/html.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/prompt-api.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/speech-api.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/usb.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/web-bluetooth-scanning.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/web-bluetooth.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webhid.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webidl.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webmcp.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webrtc-diagnostic-logging.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webusb.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/webhid/idlharness.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webusb/idlharness.https.any.js"], "git_node": "6d1e8c37c5e4b1f22d708ba8cb1bc5e0386b2254", "git_parents": ["738c40db0c97ca698becd969a9f6feda364a584c"], "node": "19aace0d2f00f0f58e6c66e419ff32137786196d", "parents": ["26eda4d76a7af7e552da4799b611f391572d9d81"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076599 [wpt PR 63077] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63077\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/delivery-type.tentative.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-unconnected-outputs.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/idlharness.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-close.html.ini"], "git_node": "61989ddba04f8d7f779a6d14a6327cb6cafd1d1f", "git_parents": ["6d1e8c37c5e4b1f22d708ba8cb1bc5e0386b2254"], "node": "66ec23dea09f119681c304c767d0624b219569e4", "parents": ["19aace0d2f00f0f58e6c66e419ff32137786196d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076728 [wpt PR 63090] - [block-in-inline] Skip opaque boxes in inline CB, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] Skip opaque boxes in inline CB\n\nWhen an inline containing block contains a block-in-inline, an\nopaque `PhysicalBoxFragment` (`IsOpaque()`) is generated for\nthe inline box on the block-in-inline line box.\n\nBefore this change, `GatherInlineContainerFragmentsFromItems`\ndid not skip opaque fragments. Because a block-in-inline line\nbox is not marked as `IsEmptyLineBox()`, the opaque fragment's\nrect (which has the inline size of the block child) was used\nto update the inline containing block's geometry when there\nwere no non-empty inline lines after the block-in-inline.\n\nThis patch skips opaque box fragments when gathering inline\ncontaining block fragments.\n\nChanges are guarded by the `InlineContainingBlockSkipOpaque`\nkill-switch flag.\n\nFixed: 40910996\nChange-Id: I565c7536b796cd6ad90b84d83f7693895a4975e3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8491871\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707892}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 08b84ff820e69f6a7b397b236a881c1c1fac84ac\nwpt-pr: 63090\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/abspos/abspos-in-block-in-inline-in-relpos-inline-002.html"], "git_node": "95826c1759bc49253c84b10958b7462475648c00", "git_parents": ["61989ddba04f8d7f779a6d14a6327cb6cafd1d1f"], "node": "7ae578cada7df34d9c5ce65d7f69509dd22908ec", "parents": ["66ec23dea09f119681c304c767d0624b219569e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076728 [wpt PR 63090] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63090\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/abspos/abspos-in-block-in-inline-in-relpos-inline-002.html.ini"], "git_node": "7e53034443fc8518ec519bfcff61862092aced0a", "git_parents": ["95826c1759bc49253c84b10958b7462475648c00"], "node": "5aba08f9ca4262c5bef67ceb2131817fce1c4661", "parents": ["7ae578cada7df34d9c5ce65d7f69509dd22908ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076656 [wpt PR 63088] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324993, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSubgrid implicit grid-area line name is matched by first substring instead of suffix (#63088)\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\nImplicit grid line names are formed as \"\u003carea\u003e-start\" / \"\u003carea\u003e-end\". When\nresolving such a name for a subgrid, StyleGridPositionsResolver located the\nsuffix with String::find(), which matches the first occurrence anywhere in\nthe name. For an area whose own name ends in \"-end\" (e.g. \"x-end\"), the line\nname \"x-end-end\" matched the leading \"-end\" and was attributed to area \"x\"\ninstead of \"x-end\", placing the item on the wrong line.\n\nMatch the \"-start\"/\"-end\" suffix with endsWith() and strip it from the end of\nthe name so the correct area name is recovered.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324993\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/322238@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a71908392a6c6ee4536bb457905e601375d5b84e\nwpt-pr: 63088\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/subgrid/placement-implicit-area-line-name-suffix.html"], "git_node": "6622f47c2263a44795ce37df46983fa3667b0bc5", "git_parents": ["7e53034443fc8518ec519bfcff61862092aced0a"], "node": "deadb4263699421fe6ad54196f06ca022783efe0", "parents": ["5aba08f9ca4262c5bef67ceb2131817fce1c4661"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076739 [wpt PR 63094] - [blink] Recalc colors derived from parent color, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[blink] Recalc colors derived from parent color\n\nElement::PropagateInheritedProperties (the independent inheritance fast\npath) either kept an element's color or copied its parent's computed\ncolor. Colors resolved from the parent's color were therefore not\nupdated when only the parent's color changed:\n\n - color-mix(), relative colors or other color functions using\n   currentColor in the color property, which Color::ApplyValue resolves\n   against the parent's color.\n - forced-color-adjust: preserve-parent-color, which inherits the\n   parent's used (possibly forced) color rather than its computed color.\n\nMark these elements with ColorIsDerivedFromParent and skip the fast path\nfor them; their plain descendants still use it. Every Color apply\nfunction sets the flag, since incremental style starts from a copy of\nthe old style.\n\nBug: 492536576\nChange-Id: Ia0a0736416bf1c7edc3d50df9bc6ce0df5606190\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8484577\nAuto-Submit: Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707915}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b0ae16efde6407041a439de88025a3845e850214\nwpt-pr: 63094\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/color-mix-currentcolor-parent-change.html"], "git_node": "ec32acb255949be56163ad1076fde64912ea1346", "git_parents": ["6622f47c2263a44795ce37df46983fa3667b0bc5"], "node": "06047da78bb05aa3dd6fb6139912ad2549bd47b5", "parents": ["deadb4263699421fe6ad54196f06ca022783efe0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Kardell \u003cbkardell@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076780 [wpt PR 63103] - Add WEB_FEATURES.yml for math related subdirectory of CSS, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd WEB_FEATURES.yml for math related subdirectory of CSS (#63103)\n\nrelated: w3c/mathml-core#283 (comment)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1881d7f39d889b523c1b56ecce6c90eb8f7ddfb7\nwpt-pr: 63103\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/math-script-level-and-math-style/WEB_FEATURES.yml"], "git_node": "bb1481f4894d8038e6ec06a73988d29347658c47", "git_parents": ["ec32acb255949be56163ad1076fde64912ea1346"], "node": "7b4786be4581bf4b39942b21d6ba84789ffeb058", "parents": ["06047da78bb05aa3dd6fb6139912ad2549bd47b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fran\u00e7ois Beaufort \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076896 [wpt PR 63114] - [WebMCP] Remove origin-keyed agent cluster requirement, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebMCP] Remove origin-keyed agent cluster requirement\n\nPreviously, document.modelContext's registerTool(), getTools() and\nexecuteTool() rejected with a SecurityError, and declarative tools were\nsilently not registered, when the document was not in an origin-keyed\nagent cluster (i.e. when document.domain could be used). The spec no\nlonger has this requirement, so remove the check.\n\nThis also removes the tests that asserted the old behavior, including\nthe --disable-web-security exception test, which is now moot.\n\nSpec PR: https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/pull/330\n\nBug: 489045948\nChange-Id: I8ab7fcacd73f879e9bdb73f9eaf3ea9a21cada75\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8479638\nReviewed-by: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708220}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fe52996d4465f23617bce91927bdd58e6ce8f541\nwpt-pr: 63114\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/document-domain-enabled.sub.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/resources/document-domain-enabled-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/resources/document-domain-enabled-iframe.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/document-domain-enabled.sub.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/document-domain-enabled-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/document-domain-enabled-iframe.html.headers"], "git_node": "3a9cd03291033272320b8ee1f73196dc3acd24ad", "git_parents": ["bb1481f4894d8038e6ec06a73988d29347658c47"], "node": "d22ac7f07f01a9f7def16e97a094f5af3b0c86f3", "parents": ["7b4786be4581bf4b39942b21d6ba84789ffeb058"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Kardell \u003cbkardell@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076801 [wpt PR 63107] - Add display-math rule to WEB_FEATURES.yml, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd display-math rule to WEB_FEATURES.yml (#63107)\n\nrelated: https://github.com/w3c/mathml-core/issues/283\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3b65f0831bd93f71052a46eff58095ab7ec9900e\nwpt-pr: 63107\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/WEB_FEATURES.yml"], "git_node": "0fa473e89501c132bc2ece97804a2590be68587a", "git_parents": ["3a9cd03291033272320b8ee1f73196dc3acd24ad"], "node": "98a33c2efc0f50bb7d7ff8f54b0b140492c332c7", "parents": ["d22ac7f07f01a9f7def16e97a094f5af3b0c86f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076760 [wpt PR 63101] - Account for script \u003cscript is=\"...\"\u003e in streaming sanitizer, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAccount for script \u003cscript is=\"...\"\u003e in streaming sanitizer\n\nThis prevents a situation where \u003cscript is=\"custom-el\"\u003e would invoke custom-el's constructor despite scripts being forbidden by sanitizer.\n\nBug: 562404384\nChange-Id: I5fc3dc36371ce470a77d32f7ddeb10b6b48b5e29\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8486086\nReviewed-by: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708032}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b41f54d32d4efa254ebf629300776aed0bca63eb\nwpt-pr: 63101\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-custom-element-sanitizer.html"], "git_node": "c71b5820ab6434bb4b88665a491ce7679be55b5e", "git_parents": ["0fa473e89501c132bc2ece97804a2590be68587a"], "node": "1efe6e257bf4e21e8e07702778982941686646f7", "parents": ["98a33c2efc0f50bb7d7ff8f54b0b140492c332c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076760 [wpt PR 63101] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63101\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/move-head-during-prepend-before-close-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-custom-element-sanitizer.html.ini"], "git_node": "0e1d2cef264e1f86062134e41aa79139356a732d", "git_parents": ["c71b5820ab6434bb4b88665a491ce7679be55b5e"], "node": "13d904da4c6fa3a85a19db04fa4bbc9247b1d204", "parents": ["1efe6e257bf4e21e8e07702778982941686646f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076865 [wpt PR 63112] - Move single-axis scroll snap tests to external WPT, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMove single-axis scroll snap tests to external WPT\n\nMove single-axis-001.html through single-axis-009.html from\nwpt_internal/css/css-scroll-snap/ to external/wpt/css/css-scroll-snap/\nso they are upstreamed to web-platform-tests.\n\nWhile moving them, this patch also:\n- Points the help links at #scroll-snap-type and #snap-scope instead of\n  the spec root.\n- single-axis-003: adds a help link to css-multicol-2 #column-pseudo.\n- single-axis-007: adds a help link to css-scroll-snap-2 #snap-events.\n- single-axis-009: adds a help link to #re-snap and replaces the\n  Chromium-internal \"old_target_ids.y\" wording in the assertion and\n  test descriptions.\n\nBug: 473576119\nChange-Id: Ica3f81e199f01ce56f5d81dbccb523f8d3bd3f95\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8484053\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708152}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a189abf0056e76e28e7835b274507a37578d7bd6\nwpt-pr: 63112\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-009.html"], "git_node": "169f0007369f2c91f95467f2a76db02a26b2b120", "git_parents": ["0e1d2cef264e1f86062134e41aa79139356a732d"], "node": "0af86f8b4cc229fc132bf1a17b688bd3989e8573", "parents": ["13d904da4c6fa3a85a19db04fa4bbc9247b1d204"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076865 [wpt PR 63112] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63112\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/single-axis-009.html.ini"], "git_node": "5b95a4442af08516002ee5c9ca7e05811d169e11", "git_parents": ["169f0007369f2c91f95467f2a76db02a26b2b120"], "node": "e5108f13cdcf3e5acce5fccb7782ca6178d6f7a9", "parents": ["0af86f8b4cc229fc132bf1a17b688bd3989e8573"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Celeste \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076904 [wpt PR 63115] - Fix typo in name of `checkPlaceShorhand` to `checkPlaceShorthand`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix typo in name of `checkPlaceShorhand` to `checkPlaceShorthand`\n\nThere were a couple of methods using `checkPlaceShorhand` which seems to\nbe a typo, so this CL changes those instances to use\n`checkPlaceShorthand` instead.\n\nChange-Id: I094dca83cee000b3c5fce1d84283d2b16fd932f0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8487449\nCommit-Queue: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708223}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7b205c0606c8578a3a3d437db2236858cb9c284f\nwpt-pr: 63115\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/content-distribution/place-content-shorthand-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/content-distribution/place-content-shorthand-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/content-distribution/place-content-shorthand-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/default-alignment/place-items-shorthand-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/default-alignment/place-items-shorthand-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/default-alignment/place-items-shorthand-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/resources/alignment-parsing-utils.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/self-alignment/place-self-shorthand-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/self-alignment/place-self-shorthand-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/self-alignment/place-self-shorthand-006.html"], "git_node": "db85fce74dd3806eb820bf7a1a416b8249f61106", "git_parents": ["5b95a4442af08516002ee5c9ca7e05811d169e11"], "node": "58f89eff5b1e53a91a51275dc2bc6d4cd16bab6e", "parents": ["e5108f13cdcf3e5acce5fccb7782ca6178d6f7a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076907 [wpt PR 63116] - [masonry] Add gap decoration tests for grid subgridded into grid-lanes., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] Add gap decoration tests for grid subgridded into grid-lanes.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: Ic05524eb48c63eb9b4250bc14b72c5d97c02ae02\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8424354\nReviewed-by: Yanling Wang \u003cyanlingwang@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708243}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e7fe2835166e163b1eefa445521c69e6b28e2076\nwpt-pr: 63116\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-auto-placement-decorations-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-auto-placement-decorations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-empty-decorations-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-empty-decorations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-gap-override-decorations-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-gap-override-decorations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-nested-decorations-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-nested-decorations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-opposite-direction-rule-colors-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-opposite-direction-rule-colors.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-parent-rule-break-none-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-parent-rule-break-none.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-parent-rule-break-normal-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-parent-rule-break-normal.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-rule-break-intersection-inset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-rule-break-intersection-inset.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-rule-visibility-around-parent-between-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-rule-visibility-around-parent-between.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-spanning-item-decorations-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-spanning-item-decorations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-auto-placement-decorations-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-auto-placement-decorations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-empty-decorations-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-empty-decorations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-gap-override-decorations-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-gap-override-decorations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-nested-decorations-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-nested-decorations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-parent-rule-break-none-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-parent-rule-break-none.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-rule-visibility-around-parent-between-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-rule-visibility-around-parent-between.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-rule-visibility-between-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-rule-visibility-between.html"], "git_node": "20a2f4192e3a2d4ab9b32852aa376b2ee283e53e", "git_parents": ["db85fce74dd3806eb820bf7a1a416b8249f61106"], "node": "f341b81af3e82fe7f38b42cc91d45e43e431d55a", "parents": ["58f89eff5b1e53a91a51275dc2bc6d4cd16bab6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076907 [wpt PR 63116] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63116\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-auto-placement-decorations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-empty-decorations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-gap-override-decorations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-nested-decorations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-opposite-direction-rule-colors.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-parent-rule-break-none.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-parent-rule-break-normal.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-rule-break-intersection-inset.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-rule-visibility-around-parent-between.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-subgrid-spanning-item-decorations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-auto-placement-decorations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-empty-decorations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-gap-override-decorations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-nested-decorations.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-parent-rule-break-none.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-rule-visibility-around-parent-between.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-subgrid-rule-visibility-between.html.ini"], "git_node": "3d9d7b1f14b8ee76a7d13e31ce167776d7d676e5", "git_parents": ["20a2f4192e3a2d4ab9b32852aa376b2ee283e53e"], "node": "c2fb980fbba0cf37c26395b3920ee58d7190fb13", "parents": ["f341b81af3e82fe7f38b42cc91d45e43e431d55a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076345 [wpt PR 63030] - CSSPseudoElement: Add scroll-button support., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCSSPseudoElement: Add scroll-button support.\n\nThis adds (experimental) scroll button support for CSSPseudoElement.\n\nR=flackr@chromium.org\n\nChange-Id: If4fd08585d70cfcbfa2fb8bb939bd8407099a7f1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8463604\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708268}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 336cfcec71a274ccc53c124eaa03749c97df3577\nwpt-pr: 63030\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/CSSPseudoElement-scroll-button.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/scroll-button-pseudo-element-click.html"], "git_node": "ead5dd88b4e69f6a86e5bfad24846e2fb438fabc", "git_parents": ["3d9d7b1f14b8ee76a7d13e31ce167776d7d676e5"], "node": "97713996896e1002d3a528a8b2c8e0480a8309b4", "parents": ["c2fb980fbba0cf37c26395b3920ee58d7190fb13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076345 [wpt PR 63030] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63030\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/CSSPseudoElement-scroll-button.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/scroll-button-pseudo-element-click.html.ini"], "git_node": "54072e149a14a6fef23e4925d03023dbb0bb87ca", "git_parents": ["ead5dd88b4e69f6a86e5bfad24846e2fb438fabc"], "node": "f1b70607560bc916b0acc59c4fe4342df68abda8", "parents": ["97713996896e1002d3a528a8b2c8e0480a8309b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Justin Lulejian \u003cjlulejian@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076585 [wpt PR 63071] - [Extensions] Implement runtime.onExtensionLoaded lifecycle event, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Extensions] Implement runtime.onExtensionLoaded lifecycle event\n\nCurrently, extensions have multiple disjoint lifecycle events\n(onInstalled, onStartup, onEnabled) to detect state changes, but no\nsingle unified event that fires whenever an extension becomes active\nalong with the specific reason (install, update, browser_update, enable,\nstartup, or reload).\n\nWith this change, extensions can listen to runtime.onExtensionLoaded,\nwhich fires whenever the extension is loaded into the set of enabled\nextensions, passing details with the specific load reason and optional\nprevious version (when updated).\n\nLow-Coverage-Reason: TRIVIAL_CHANGE extension_registry_observer.h changes are just adding a virtual method.\nBug: 550447466, 41486131\nChange-Id: I058b7ebc1b232d3f78dff89944b35fe11211a4df\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8282026\nAuto-Submit: Justin Lulejian \u003cjlulejian@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Tim \u003ctjudkins@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Justin Lulejian \u003cjlulejian@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708375}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3ba906187e19e4eb9053fb5cabc03364b5e46030\nwpt-pr: 63071\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-extensions/resources/runtime/background.js"], "git_node": "c1746ffc868a8cbc327ef035839b58134c72215e", "git_parents": ["54072e149a14a6fef23e4925d03023dbb0bb87ca"], "node": "61d9d59623336ab07ca682a9549bcc63c653f1d1", "parents": ["f1b70607560bc916b0acc59c4fe4342df68abda8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075201 [wpt PR 62935] - [html-in-canvas] Handle display:contents children, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Handle display:contents children\n\nPreviously, display:contents children of a content=drawable \u003ccanvas\u003e\nwere not skipped when finding the layout parent, could attach non-box or\npseudo-element children (such as anonymous inline wrappers for text)\ndirectly to LayoutHTMLCanvas and crash, and did not invalidate\ndescendant styles when toggling display:contents.\n\nThis change:\n* Restricts LayoutHTMLCanvas children to non-pseudo Element boxes for\n  now (with crbug.com/564820084 tracking pseudo-element support).\n* Replaces FlatTreeTraversal::ParentElementSkippingSlots with\n  LayoutTreeBuilderTraversal::LayoutParentElement (for layout parent\n  checks) and FlatTreeTraversal::ParentElement (for ancestor walks).\n* Tracks IsContentDrawableCanvasChild on ComputedStyle so toggling\n  display:contents under a canvas recalculates descendant styles.\n\nFixed: 563038957\nChange-Id: I54708243b4ae065d750dcf1a8343307c5286c1c9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8421823\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708379}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5cd8e3fa0a6c4ca11fa565f7c0956802c8e0045d\nwpt-pr: 62935\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/display-contents.tentative.html"], "git_node": "5014df5bdd46027a686e789107984017c41eba66", "git_parents": ["c1746ffc868a8cbc327ef035839b58134c72215e"], "node": "5924e29dda427b3a8f955fb8d0ec90eea7d657dd", "parents": ["61d9d59623336ab07ca682a9549bcc63c653f1d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075201 [wpt PR 62935] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62935\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/display-contents.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "ae95a9264717a21bd41a7bb494b2c4e8afd22033", "git_parents": ["5014df5bdd46027a686e789107984017c41eba66"], "node": "36d04ae8642e5643bcf363b30a15a522af4b569b", "parents": ["5924e29dda427b3a8f955fb8d0ec90eea7d657dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077018 [wpt PR 63145] - Add Payment Method Manifest WPTs for manifest validation and origins, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd Payment Method Manifest WPTs for manifest validation and origins\n\nAdd Web Platform Tests covering Payment Method Manifest validation and\nsupported_origins parsing. Tests cover:\n\n   - Valid manifests omitting supported_origins or containing\n     unrecognized members\n   - Invalid default_applications entries (non-string items,\n     unparsable URLs) aborting manifest validation without fetching\n     valid sibling web app manifests\n   - Multiple valid HTTPS origins (including explicit ports) in\n     supported_origins\n   - Non-array supported_origins values (single origin string, wildcard\n     \"*\", null) and empty array ([])\n       - The empty array test fails in Chrome, as ParseSupportedOrigins\n         does not currently reject empty lists - crbug.com/567692130\n   - Invalid supported_origins entries (non-string items, relative URLs,\n     non-HTTPS origins, credentials, paths, queries, and fragments)\n\nBug: 552832440, 567692130\nChange-Id: I514296d646507968d809c7d517050e0ef1c6e43e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464506\nReviewed-by: Xuehui Chen \u003cxuehuichen@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708662}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3bc1b1f07f58a11cb825f9beb7f555b86416b5d7\nwpt-pr: 63145\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/pmm-supported-origins.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/wam-ingestion.https.window.js"], "git_node": "60ce7cd5800030d7ec9d7829b0472c94a7484348", "git_parents": ["ae95a9264717a21bd41a7bb494b2c4e8afd22033"], "node": "fd70fc0f61966880ec7d942321bca171d3b9f085", "parents": ["36d04ae8642e5643bcf363b30a15a522af4b569b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077018 [wpt PR 63145] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63145\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/pmm-supported-origins.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/wam-ingestion.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "3921d310a8b4bb2581d3610c89d51ac1332218cb", "git_parents": ["60ce7cd5800030d7ec9d7829b0472c94a7484348"], "node": "a51422a18ae045d29166796efb1a6cc695481d21", "parents": ["fd70fc0f61966880ec7d942321bca171d3b9f085"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077093 [wpt PR 63162] - [wdspec] Add test for preload script with channel and sandbox, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wdspec] Add test for preload script with channel and sandbox\n\n- Verify that `script.addPreloadScript` with both `arguments` (channel)\n  and `sandbox` emits `script.message` events from the sandbox realm.\n\nBug: 411433988\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: I090142015c6b6d13dc9210355fe372009cc14792\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8488371\nReviewed-by: Alex Rudenko \u003calexrudenko@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Alex Rudenko \u003calexrudenko@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708751}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d093118bf6977bfd2bd0dd6e35d829195b85e76e\nwpt-pr: 63162\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/script/add_preload_script/sandbox.py"], "git_node": "1889df47574c30947506dcd6a950f20126ae3bfb", "git_parents": ["3921d310a8b4bb2581d3610c89d51ac1332218cb"], "node": "e03c3b00d29339d37d307ccfdeb12fa82c908489", "parents": ["a51422a18ae045d29166796efb1a6cc695481d21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077093 [wpt PR 63162] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63162\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/script/add_preload_script/add_preload_script.py.ini"], "git_node": "f0f30bda7ed4d697af4e43844b1e72efbefc9a14", "git_parents": ["1889df47574c30947506dcd6a950f20126ae3bfb"], "node": "9f9c639c58340c34519bb66e5d7a19509538f839", "parents": ["e03c3b00d29339d37d307ccfdeb12fa82c908489"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Misha Nasledov \u003cmisha@nasledov.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077024 [wpt PR 63147] - Skip siblings pending re-attach when finding the next layout sibling, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSkip siblings pending re-attach when finding the next layout sibling\n\nmoveBefore() does not detach the layout tree of the node it moves. The\nnode is marked for a forced re-attach instead, so until the next layout\ntree rebuild its LayoutObject is still a child of its old parent's\nLayoutObject, while in the DOM it is already a sibling of its new\nsiblings.\n\nIf one of those new siblings changes between in-flow and out-of-flow\n(position: absolute/fixed, or float) in the same frame,\nElement::RecalcOwnStyle() removes its LayoutObject and re-inserts it\nbefore LayoutTreeBuilderTraversal::NextSiblingLayoutObject(). That\nreturned the moved node's stale LayoutObject, which is not in the\nparent's layout subtree at all. AddChild() then took the\nAddChildBeforeDescendant() path, walked up from the stale object past\nthe LayoutView looking for a child of the parent, and dereferenced\nnull.\n\nmoveBefore() is one way to get there, not the only one: re-slotting a\nshadow host's child marks it for a forced re-attach the same way, and\nClusterFuzz reached the same crash through \u003cselect\u003e's manual slot\nassignment. This change also stops the ClusterFuzz testcase for that\nbug from crashing.\n\nA sibling that is pending re-attach is not a valid insertion point, and\ndoes not need to be one: it is inserted relative to its own siblings\nwhen it is re-attached. Skip such siblings in\nNextSiblingLayoutObjectInternal(), next to the existing skip for\nLayoutObjects that are reparented into the top layer or an overscroll\narea.\n\nFixed: 541682083\nTest: external/wpt/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-out-of-flow-sibling-crash.html\nChange-Id: Ia4fcfef31aa1571d8ea9f73ac29710e1257358e1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8467632\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708754}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2133436b8b01acfda873707cec4815bb4f6f5f12\nwpt-pr: 63147\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-out-of-flow-sibling-crash.html"], "git_node": "72df4e0a5fa5f939cd8e6ad8ab44ff8696e08f77", "git_parents": ["f0f30bda7ed4d697af4e43844b1e72efbefc9a14"], "node": "dc121729b40e81362dbf4dd2c6280aa19321dace", "parents": ["9f9c639c58340c34519bb66e5d7a19509538f839"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077089 [wpt PR 63159] - [masonry] Implement `flow-start/end` capabilities for placement reversals, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] Implement `flow-start/end` capabilities for placement reversals\n\nThis change allows `flow-start/end` to indicate the placement start and\nend when `fill-reverse` and `track-reverse` are present in grid-lanes.\n\nBug: 343257585, 555299635\nChange-Id: I4228219344ece140e0c89c9af25ed858b4d6a9c6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8462483\nCommit-Queue: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708791}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6fa18a46660efb5df326fb4f0648075db9aa8d6c\nwpt-pr: 63159\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-align-items-017-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-align-items-017.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-fill-reverse-align-content-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-fill-reverse-align-content-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-fill-reverse-align-content-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-fill-reverse-align-content-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-justify-items-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-justify-items-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-track-reverse-justify-content-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-track-reverse-justify-content-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-track-reverse-justify-items-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-track-reverse-justify-items-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-track-reverse-justify-items-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-track-reverse-justify-items-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-fill-reverse-justify-content-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-fill-reverse-justify-content-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-fill-reverse-justify-content-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-fill-reverse-justify-content-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-fill-reverse-justify-content-indefinite-size-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-fill-reverse-justify-content-indefinite-size-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-justify-items-016-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-justify-items-016.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-track-reverse-align-content-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-track-reverse-align-content-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-track-reverse-align-items-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-track-reverse-align-items-001.html"], "git_node": "6422d4ba784b424401c2d9e8bd3a6208eb403276", "git_parents": ["72df4e0a5fa5f939cd8e6ad8ab44ff8696e08f77"], "node": "080d3c484742aed7303f1090941c6553526ff80e", "parents": ["dc121729b40e81362dbf4dd2c6280aa19321dace"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077089 [wpt PR 63159] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63159\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-fill-reverse-align-content-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-justify-items-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-track-reverse-justify-content-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-track-reverse-justify-items-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/column-track-reverse-justify-items-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-fill-reverse-justify-content-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-track-reverse-align-content-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/alignment/row-track-reverse-align-items-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "799953320e37018383f4944bad959276b3cb2abb", "git_parents": ["6422d4ba784b424401c2d9e8bd3a6208eb403276"], "node": "5ecef540fa0863f2f166e602d4f27f36d465d4ea", "parents": ["080d3c484742aed7303f1090941c6553526ff80e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076784 [wpt PR 63104] - [chromium-bidi] Include request cookies and headers when paused, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[chromium-bidi] Include request cookies and headers when paused\n\n- Include request cookies and `Fetch.requestPaused` headers in\n  `network.beforeRequestSent` events when a request is intercepted.\n- When a request is paused in the `beforeRequestSent` phase via\n  `Fetch.requestPaused`, CDP only emits\n  `Network.requestWillBeSentExtraInfo` after `Fetch.continueRequest` is\n  called, leaving `request.cookies` empty and omitting headers from\n  `Fetch.requestPaused`.\n- Merge `Fetch.requestPaused` headers into the request headers, query\n  `Network.getCookies` filtered by the paused `Cookie` header, and\n  enqueue the event as a promise so async cookie resolution preserves\n  event ordering.\n\nBug: 480081339\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: I06e1edc165c686ad2f77132e9a38355a5f8c8b1c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8482134\nReviewed-by: Alex Rudenko \u003calexrudenko@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708828}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7f439c226694df407f6ae71b7a86a3794cc67776\nwpt-pr: 63104\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/before_request_sent/before_request_sent.py"], "git_node": "b5ee836e35f2b98f0a6c7fc011deef5467bc1b90", "git_parents": ["799953320e37018383f4944bad959276b3cb2abb"], "node": "1510a32189cc8bb1b5edc25f2cad58b19675a303", "parents": ["5ecef540fa0863f2f166e602d4f27f36d465d4ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076809 [wpt PR 63109] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325799, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nOrigin-Agent-Cluster should be ignored in non-secure contexts\n\nA document can only request an origin-keyed agent cluster when the reserved\nenvironment of its navigation is a secure context, which depends on the\nenvironment's top-level creation URL. We only checked the response URL, so an\nHTTPS document in an HTTP page was origin-keyed when it asked for it:\nwindow.originAgentCluster returned true while window.isSecureContext returned\nfalse, and document.domain did nothing.\n\nWith site isolation, a document that loads in another process is created in\nthe WebFrame's provisional frame, which WebFrame::didReceivePolicyDecision()\nskipped, so it was never origin-keyed.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325799\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d1be42980512f3ceea0c903723a69b00d2412e70\nwpt-pr: 63109\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/1-iframe/parent-no-child-yes-cross-site.sub.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/insecure-http-opener-https-openee.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/insecure-http-parent-https-children.sub.html"], "git_node": "b5059c77fdd50c7367099c4170350b33ad6813d3", "git_parents": ["b5ee836e35f2b98f0a6c7fc011deef5467bc1b90"], "node": "78231ddcde506793547aa78f89b9e65c804e82c1", "parents": ["1510a32189cc8bb1b5edc25f2cad58b19675a303"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076809 [wpt PR 63109] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63109\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/insecure-http-parent-https-children.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/popups-crash.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "bcc9ab45570bf3e2e0d4e98b83a76f9737188236", "git_parents": ["b5059c77fdd50c7367099c4170350b33ad6813d3"], "node": "c48f1bf1e9475b82c87cec36d0e959eb2b672457", "parents": ["78231ddcde506793547aa78f89b9e65c804e82c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076731 [wpt PR 63091] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325465, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake sure two customizable select tests wait for their timeout\n\nselect-size-change.html and select-multiple-removed.html changed the select after their test had already finished.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325465\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7d3ef357cb1658fc015f54eaaf0dfa154cb2c473\nwpt-pr: 63091\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-multiple-removed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-size-change.html"], "git_node": "762cbbe907db9781cc33155654bbd24ea8e8659b", "git_parents": ["bcc9ab45570bf3e2e0d4e98b83a76f9737188236"], "node": "ba9ad2d9d92835cb6be2afb7309db8ed579a2e28", "parents": ["c48f1bf1e9475b82c87cec36d0e959eb2b672457"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnoamr@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076746 [wpt PR 63095] - Test that unrendered image with sizes=auto doesn't cause unnecessary fetches, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest that unrendered image with sizes=auto doesn't cause unnecessary fetches\n\nOnce an image is rendered, it should retain its last rendered size until it is removed\nor re-rendered.\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13004\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 90ecc630ac832689cca10268830bb54980993e10\nwpt-pr: 63095\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-auto-unrendered.html"], "git_node": "a157824731e528f24306c1994dcf4ba080f110d3", "git_parents": ["762cbbe907db9781cc33155654bbd24ea8e8659b"], "node": "1fcfd0e1a34ef8ba5ec26452fa0e07339fffd643", "parents": ["ba9ad2d9d92835cb6be2afb7309db8ed579a2e28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076746 [wpt PR 63095] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63095\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-auto-unrendered.html.ini"], "git_node": "cab05bfce0e9024f0d3f5949980563bd5de955a9", "git_parents": ["a157824731e528f24306c1994dcf4ba080f110d3"], "node": "e6a73ee465636886e1265d892c6ef9450ca13e05", "parents": ["1fcfd0e1a34ef8ba5ec26452fa0e07339fffd643"], "tags": []}, {"author": "youennf \u003cyouennf@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075735 [wpt PR 62966] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324804, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSupport WebCodecs HEVC annexB encoder (#62966)\n\nWe add support for the HevcEncoderConfig so that web pages can turn on annexB HEVC encoding.\nWe add a few enumerations to AvcBitstreamFormat and HevcBitstreamFormat so that we get better casing for avec, hevc and annexb enumeration values.\n\nCovered by updated WPT test.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324804\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0364154f9175aa87045a6647869641901b2efceb\nwpt-pr: 62966\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/full-cycle-test.https.any.js"], "git_node": "0b73eb160a25ee8dab2f16edc74edb2ec29b595c", "git_parents": ["cab05bfce0e9024f0d3f5949980563bd5de955a9"], "node": "886b12ea936f3888c7b0faf019f23b9c7d53808d", "parents": ["e6a73ee465636886e1265d892c6ef9450ca13e05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077530 - [wpt-sync] Update web-platform-tests to 0364154f9175aa87045a6647869641901b2efceb, a=testonly\n\nMANUAL PUSH: wpt sync bot\n\nwpt-head: 0364154f9175aa87045a6647869641901b2efceb\nwpt-type: landing\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/ai/language-model/language-model-create-sampling-mode.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-valid-color-mix-function.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-valid-hsl.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-valid-hwb.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-valid-relative-color.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-image-animation/image-animation-img-running-to-normal.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/mask-image/backdrop-filter-bad-mask-image.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/input-security-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/input-security-none-sensitive-text-input.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/input-security-parsing.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/document-picture-in-picture/returns-window-with-document.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/events/scrolling/scrollend-event-fired-after-layout-clamping.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/security/dangling-markup/dangling-markup-mitigation-allowed-apis.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/window-open-defaults.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/moved-webgl-canvas.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/nested-canvas-scale.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-iframe-post-tree-order.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-post-tree-order.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/render-blocking/parser-inserted-stylesheet-link.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/render-blocking/remove-attr-style-keeps-blocking.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/ready-states/autoplay-hidden.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-auto-unrendered.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/webappapis/dynamic-markup-insertion/opening-the-input-stream/url.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mozilla-sync", "testing/web-platform/meta/picture-in-picture/picture-in-picture-element.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/pointerevents/pointerevent_after_target_removed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/pointerevents/pointerlock/pointerevent_coordinates_when_locked.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/content-type-minimization.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/delivery-type.tentative.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speech-api/idlharness.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-extensions/browser.runtime.extension.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-unconnected-outputs.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/interop/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/declarative/document-domain-enabled.sub.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/document-domain-enabled.sub.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-events.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "427403c038e2942ef4fef5a9448ae0280db436bd", "git_parents": ["0b73eb160a25ee8dab2f16edc74edb2ec29b595c"], "node": "8eb8c987e79b056a710238a20786c91bba089a33", "parents": ["886b12ea936f3888c7b0faf019f23b9c7d53808d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 1: Unify the hint charset handling between the script preload and regular script load. r=bthrall,dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nStore the hint charset attribute into the ScriptLoadRequest field, both for the\npreload and the regular load, so that the remaining part of the preload and\nthe cache handling doesn't have to distinguish between them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324186\n", "files": ["dom/script/ModuleLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.cpp", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.h", "dom/workers/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/loader/ModuleLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/script-charset-03.html.ini"], "git_node": "17feeab75893d24cbb6b18260d832850f074ce8b", "git_parents": ["427403c038e2942ef4fef5a9448ae0280db436bd"], "node": "eed31b2caf672bdc2640b46407e404c41449f480", "parents": ["8eb8c987e79b056a710238a20786c91bba089a33"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 2: Include the hint charset into the cache key string for the ChromeUtils.getCachedJavaScriptSource. r=bthrall,devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314577\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/network-monitor/network-event-actor.js", "devtools/server/actors/resources/network-events-content.js", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.cpp", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.h", "dom/chrome-webidl/ChromeUtils.webidl", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.cpp", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.h", "remote/shared/NetworkResponse.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "9860ed0966e36e22d89369b446b5e043e9a00c35", "git_parents": ["17feeab75893d24cbb6b18260d832850f074ce8b"], "node": "d485e274feae74a5be521a99b7d04066cd14a83c", "parents": ["eed31b2caf672bdc2640b46407e404c41449f480"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 3: Move the alignment handling out of LoadedScript methods and clarify the input/output. r=bthrall\n\nThe later patch will put an extra section between the SRI+padding and the\nserialized stencil.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324187\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/loader/LoadedScript.h"], "git_node": "305059a36b6e13a0182f787fb11c4cd0de132b24", "git_parents": ["9860ed0966e36e22d89369b446b5e043e9a00c35"], "node": "c819f2a20a601b0341be4452ff226762a3451712", "parents": ["d485e274feae74a5be521a99b7d04066cd14a83c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 4: Add ScriptLoader::GetClassicScriptFallbackEncoding. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324188\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h"], "git_node": "3e9e75e9edc5ff18f0809b3b4bb528a6c228b097", "git_parents": ["305059a36b6e13a0182f787fb11c4cd0de132b24"], "node": "e6042da0a2fe2c6fcce6cb9b9989adde074e8fff", "parents": ["c819f2a20a601b0341be4452ff226762a3451712"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 5: Put the encoding into the serialized stencil. r=bthrall\n\nThe encoding becomes a part of the cached value.\nWhen encoding doesn't match, the cache is treated in the same way as corrupted,\nand the load restarted, bypassing the cache.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324189\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h", "js/loader/LoadedScript.cpp", "js/loader/LoadedScript.h"], "git_node": "58ef47fa022e19d595d21c0325e81b3752f9120a", "git_parents": ["3e9e75e9edc5ff18f0809b3b4bb528a6c228b097"], "node": "7ba231aca958fef0cdaee01dfceab2013df60b68", "parents": ["e6042da0a2fe2c6fcce6cb9b9989adde074e8fff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 6: Validate the script preload with fallback encoding. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330332\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h"], "git_node": "430b7bd57fdf39649f8937a79ce45a6b8b29f524", "git_parents": ["58ef47fa022e19d595d21c0325e81b3752f9120a"], "node": "cc05796129c610510d3db33d618c7756615eae8f", "parents": ["7ba231aca958fef0cdaee01dfceab2013df60b68"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 7: Use the encoding when looking up the in-memory script cache. r=bthrall\n\nCompare the hint encoding also for the in-memory cache, but only when the\nhint encoding was actually used.\n\nFor script preloads, the document's encoding may not have been settled yet,\nand in that case, the check is performed when the actual script load is\nlooking up the preload.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324190\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "dddfed0f0e1701c376c51e830b487596b27592fa", "git_parents": ["430b7bd57fdf39649f8937a79ce45a6b8b29f524"], "node": "36d00d156020a6ceee0e7cd7fb8f4659ea4ed35b", "parents": ["cc05796129c610510d3db33d618c7756615eae8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056134 - Part 8: Add tests. r=bthrall,perftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314581\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/browser_script_loader_js_cache_charset.js", "dom/base/test/file_js_cache_charset_html.sjs", "dom/base/test/file_js_cache_charset_js.sjs", "dom/base/test/head.js"], "git_node": "72d70e11bf17af1d89af33f6f064646c68d686a1", "git_parents": ["dddfed0f0e1701c376c51e830b487596b27592fa"], "node": "7d2df81199a3f6a46c2396724dfaefcc4c2ecfb0", "parents": ["36d00d156020a6ceee0e7cd7fb8f4659ea4ed35b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072070 - Bypass SharedSubResourceCache if any Vary header is present. r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331101\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/tests/browser/browser_scriptCache_responseHeaders.js", "dom/tests/browser/responseHeaders_server.sjs"], "git_node": "895a259b4c4bd473cf10b11b1848ac47df4a34af", "git_parents": ["72d70e11bf17af1d89af33f6f064646c68d686a1"], "node": "0ab824be91325189041be7c02845faa1431d6cec", "parents": ["7d2df81199a3f6a46c2396724dfaefcc4c2ecfb0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988531 - Part 1. Use the MediaCodec NDK via ffmpeg by default for Android isolated process. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nThe Java MediaCodec decoders are unavailable when content runs in an isolated\nprocess, so codecs without an ffvpx software decoder, such as H.264, have no\ndecoder at all. Default isolated process builds to decoding and encoding with\nthe MediaCodec NDK via ffmpeg in the RDD process instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329523\n", "files": ["taskcluster/test_configs/variants.yml"], "git_node": "e0286afb5f6836d607a3f218a527db69979c0bbd", "git_parents": ["895a259b4c4bd473cf10b11b1848ac47df4a34af"], "node": "e61462d1798b6724ffae2d900abbb2611cb85242", "parents": ["0ab824be91325189041be7c02845faa1431d6cec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988531 - Part 2. Run media related WPT and mochitests for Android isolated process. r=media-playback-reviewers,jolin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329524\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml"], "git_node": "76481521655f285e1f78ce94b5493a1321f147c2", "git_parents": ["e0286afb5f6836d607a3f218a527db69979c0bbd"], "node": "b01cadf9a719927d176783a39eed7086917861ee", "parents": ["e61462d1798b6724ffae2d900abbb2611cb85242"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988531 - Part 3. Update media test annotations for Android isolated process. r=media-playback-reviewers,webrtc-reviewers,pehrsons,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329525\n", "files": ["dom/media/autoplay/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/mediasession/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/mediasource/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/mediasource/test/mochitest_compat.toml", "dom/media/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/test/mochitest_background_video.toml", "dom/media/test/mochitest_bugs.toml", "dom/media/test/mochitest_compat.toml", "dom/media/test/mochitest_seek.toml", "dom/media/test/mochitest_stream.toml", "dom/media/webaudio/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webaudio/test/mochitest_media.toml", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/mochitest_datachannel.toml", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/mochitest_peerconnection.toml", "dom/media/webvtt/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-close.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCIceTransport.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-addTransceiver.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCRtpReceiver-video-anyCodec.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCRtpSender-replaceTrack.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/protocol/h264-profile-levels.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/protocol/rtp-demuxing.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/simulcast/h264.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "fa8ca72860ba455cef6e522ab3344a8516a6d720", "git_parents": ["76481521655f285e1f78ce94b5493a1321f147c2"], "node": "3489633ca367bd4b4fbca7a8f9e9bac39ad954b2", "parents": ["b01cadf9a719927d176783a39eed7086917861ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078073 - Fold a Not of an integer comparison into the negated comparison. r=jandem\n\n`!(a \u003c b)` on int32 operands and `!!x` on an int32 (including a string, whose\ntruthiness becomes a test of its length during type analysis) materialized the\ninner boolean and then flipped it with an xor, e.g. on arm64:\n\n  cmp  w0, #0\n  cset x0, eq\n  eor  w0, w0, #1\n\nand on x86-64:\n\n  test  %eax, %eax\n  setz  %al\n  movzx %al, %eax\n  xor   $0x1, %eax\n\nFold Not(Compare) of an integer comparison into the comparison with the\nnegated operator, and Not(Not(int32)) into a comparison against zero, when the\ninner instruction has no other uses. The result is then computed directly, with\n`cset ne` on arm64 and `setnz` without the `xor` on x86-64.\n\nOn a JetStream 3 run on arm64 the cset + eor pair occurred at 1,006 Ion sites,\n783 of them a comparison against zero.\n\nFound with armlint.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330645\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/not-compare-fold.js", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp"], "git_node": "448f537844cbae9236e18fea38b497b5161873dc", "git_parents": ["fa8ca72860ba455cef6e522ab3344a8516a6d720"], "node": "85f324482a5c9a2f369f476f89c65290ee2c900d", "parents": ["3489633ca367bd4b4fbca7a8f9e9bac39ad954b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076979 - Release EGL context when AndroidImageReaderImage::BuildSurfaceDescriptorBuffer() ends r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nAndroidImageReaderImage::BuildSurfaceDescriptorBuffer() is called in RemoteMediaManagerParent's ManagerThread. But the ManagerThread is actually TaskQueue of SharedThreadPool 4 threads.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330634\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/AndroidImageReader.cpp"], "git_node": "a06476cf539c15fe2b3e27db16fabe424c242490", "git_parents": ["448f537844cbae9236e18fea38b497b5161873dc"], "node": "37ec4a3add3e62595c60ffe147377734bafb7095", "parents": ["85f324482a5c9a2f369f476f89c65290ee2c900d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045134 - Part 1: Remove unnecessary virtual keyword from nsHTMLContentSerializer::SerializeHTMLAttributes; r=masayuki\n\nThis patch doesn't change behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310402\n", "files": ["dom/serializers/nsHTMLContentSerializer.h"], "git_node": "f99f3258dfed652941e004e55da49bbd20c58e63", "git_parents": ["a06476cf539c15fe2b3e27db16fabe424c242490"], "node": "79c87b5ce7d34b8ebbfd239f96198e16cedcba5b", "parents": ["37ec4a3add3e62595c60ffe147377734bafb7095"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045134 - Part 2: Remove unused arguments from nsHTMLContentSerializer::SerializeHTMLAttributes; r=masayuki\n\nThis patch doesn't change behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310403\n", "files": ["dom/serializers/nsHTMLContentSerializer.cpp", "dom/serializers/nsHTMLContentSerializer.h"], "git_node": "ae50df358d75e4a76d65029f2a7809edf0c45d81", "git_parents": ["f99f3258dfed652941e004e55da49bbd20c58e63"], "node": "eacbdfb8b9cd6ab31d17ece04765b35fbbe0d797", "parents": ["79c87b5ce7d34b8ebbfd239f96198e16cedcba5b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045134 - Part 3: Use uint32_t for attribute count and index in nsHTMLContentSerializer::SerializeHTMLAttributes; r=masayuki\n\nThis patch doesn't change behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310404\n", "files": ["dom/serializers/nsHTMLContentSerializer.cpp"], "git_node": "23d70d44616546c5b344edde1684eac7b9f86632", "git_parents": ["ae50df358d75e4a76d65029f2a7809edf0c45d81"], "node": "6d0d8fcb017ddefc428b006edcfb2853d9d41f04", "parents": ["eacbdfb8b9cd6ab31d17ece04765b35fbbe0d797"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045134 - Part 4: Remove unnecessary local variable from nsHTMLContentSerializer::SerializeHTMLAttributes. r=masayuki\n\nThis patch doesn't change behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310405\n", "files": ["dom/serializers/nsHTMLContentSerializer.cpp"], "git_node": "02347d7dd88fc600536650fd53f26be66705cc05", "git_parents": ["23d70d44616546c5b344edde1684eac7b9f86632"], "node": "85ca2c1927cbb5716415b26dce212ec6db14abc9", "parents": ["6d0d8fcb017ddefc428b006edcfb2853d9d41f04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078221 - Add telemetry for user activation for each geolocation requests r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nThis should help us decide on https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2077926.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330787\n", "files": ["dom/geolocation/Geolocation.cpp", "dom/geolocation/metrics.yaml", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/geolocation-API/user-activation-glean.https.window.js"], "git_node": "597a9b6036628896b8c6986b9b974f7eabf1fcc4", "git_parents": ["02347d7dd88fc600536650fd53f26be66705cc05"], "node": "e6da2a41d920fde1a816e06be77ac1f79696139c", "parents": ["85ca2c1927cbb5716415b26dce212ec6db14abc9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2045134 - Part 4: Remove unnecessary local variable from nsHTMLContentSerializer::SerializeHTMLAttributes. r=masayuki\" for causing build bustages @ nsHTMLContentSerializer\n\nThis reverts commit 02347d7dd88fc600536650fd53f26be66705cc05.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2045134 - Part 3: Use uint32_t for attribute count and index in nsHTMLContentSerializer::SerializeHTMLAttributes; r=masayuki\"\n\nThis reverts commit 23d70d44616546c5b344edde1684eac7b9f86632.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2045134 - Part 2: Remove unused arguments from nsHTMLContentSerializer::SerializeHTMLAttributes; r=masayuki\"\n\nThis reverts commit ae50df358d75e4a76d65029f